window.CHENHUA_TODAY_NOTES = {"gu-kaizhi-admonitions-scroll-400": {"note": "《女史箴图》是现存最早的中国人物画手卷之一，一般认为是唐代摹本，原作作者是顾恺之。画中以九个存留下来的场景描绘了张华《女史箴》里的十二段故事：冯女护驾熊袭、班女辞帝车，以及宫女梳妆或坐着聊天下棋。衣纹轻盈飘动，线条细腻连贯，就像蚕丝般柔顺。\n\n画中没有透视和阴影，但通过线条的节奏、人物间的距离以及空白处来组织叙事。这幅作品既是道德教材，也像是一幅宫廷女性生活的影像史。它在1900年义和团事件后流入英国，现在收藏于大英博物馆。", "note_en": "Admonitions of the Instructress to the Court Ladies is among the earliest surviving Chinese handscrolls of figure painting, generally regarded as a Tang-dynasty copy after Gu Kaizhi. It illustrates twelve passages from Zhang Hua's Admonitions in the form of nine surviving scenes: Lady Feng shielding the emperor from a bear, Lady Ban declining the imperial carriage, and court ladies at their toilet or seated in conversation. Draperies lift and flow; lines are fine and unbroken, like silk spun by a silkworm.\n\nThere is no perspective and no shadow, yet rhythm of line, distance between figures and blank space organise the narrative. It is both a moral textbook and an image-history of palace women's lives. It entered Britain after the Boxer upheaval in 1900 and is now in the British Museum.", "note_html": "《女史箴图》是现存最早的中国人物画手卷之一，一般认为是唐代摹本，原作作者是顾恺之。画中以九个存留下来的场景描绘了张华《女史箴》里的十二段故事：冯女护驾熊袭、班女辞帝车，以及宫女梳妆或坐着聊天下棋。衣纹轻盈飘动，线条细腻连贯，就像蚕丝般柔顺。\n\n画中没有透视和阴影，但通过线条的节奏、人物间的距离以及空白处来组织叙事。这幅作品既是道德教材，也像是一幅宫廷女性生活的影像史。它在1900年义和团事件后流入英国，现在收藏于大英博物馆。"}, "mural-fragment-with-elite-male-and-maguey-cactus-leaves-500": {"note": "这位衣着华丽的精英男性属于一排相同的形象，他们沿着特奥蒂瓦坎一处富人公寓院落的庭院墙壁列队行进。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "This richly dressed elite male belonged to a row of identical figures who processed along the walls of a patio in one of Teotihuacán’s wealthy apartment compounds.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "这位衣着华丽的精英男性属于一排相同的形象，他们沿着特奥蒂瓦坎一处富人公寓院落的庭院墙壁列队行进。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "fragment-with-a-head-of-bodhisattva-600": {"note": "菩萨头像残片，600–650年。中亚，克孜尔。壁画；图像：16.8 x 15.5厘米（6 5/8 x 6 1/8英寸）；整体：23.2 x 20.6厘米（9 1/8 x 8 1/8英寸）。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。", "note_en": "Fragment with a Head of Bodhisattva, 600–650. Central Asia, Kizil. Fresco; image: 16.8 x 15.5 cm (6 5/8 x 6 1/8 in.); overall: 23.2 x 20.6 cm (9 1/8 x 8 1/8 in.).\n\nThe work arranges sacred figures inside a legible composition: bodies, gestures, objects and borders prescribe the order of looking. Read the centre first, then the sides and the lower edge; the image becomes a reusable language of faith.", "note_html": "菩萨头像残片，600–650年。中亚，克孜尔。壁画；图像：16.8 x 15.5厘米（6 5/8 x 6 1/8英寸）；整体：23.2 x 20.6厘米（9 1/8 x 8 1/8英寸）。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。"}, "buddha-in-the-preaching-attitude-618": {"note": "说法图佛像，618–1279年。中国，唐朝（618-907）-宋朝（960-1279）。壁画；整体尺寸：49 x 35厘米（19 5/16 x 13 3/4英寸）。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。", "note_en": "Buddha in the Preaching Attitude, 618–1279. China, Tang dynasty (618-907) - Song dynasty (960-1279). Fresco; overall: 49 x 35 cm (19 5/16 x 13 3/4 in.).\n\nThe work arranges sacred figures inside a legible composition: bodies, gestures, objects and borders prescribe the order of looking. Read the centre first, then the sides and the lower edge; the image becomes a reusable language of faith.", "note_html": "说法图佛像，618–1279年。中国，唐朝（618-907）-宋朝（960-1279）。壁画；整体尺寸：49 x 35厘米（19 5/16 x 13 3/4英寸）。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。"}, "shakyamuni-triad-buddha-attended-by-manjushri-and-samantabhadr-850": {"note": "普贤菩萨骑着一头六牙白象，文殊菩萨则端坐在狮子背上。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。", "note_en": "Samantabhadra rides a six-tusked white elephant, while Manjusri is seated upon a lion.\n\nThe work arranges sacred figures inside a legible composition: bodies, gestures, objects and borders prescribe the order of looking. Read the centre first, then the sides and the lower edge; the image becomes a reusable language of faith.", "note_html": "普贤菩萨骑着一头六牙白象，文殊菩萨则端坐在狮子背上。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。"}, "barbarian-royalty-worshiping-the-buddha-900": {"note": "这幅画从右侧开始，15个人跟随着一位戴着双雉羽头饰的威严人物。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。", "note_en": "This painting begins on the right with 15 people following a dignified figure wearing headgear with twin pheasant feathers.\n\nThe work arranges sacred figures inside a legible composition: bodies, gestures, objects and borders prescribe the order of looking. Read the centre first, then the sides and the lower edge; the image becomes a reusable language of faith.", "note_html": "这幅画从右侧开始，15个人跟随着一位戴着双雉羽头饰的威严人物。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。"}, "buddhist-retreat-by-stream-and-mountains-960": {"note": "巨然僧曾在南京的南唐（937–975年）皇室任职，师从董源（活跃于930–960年代）。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "Monk Juran served the Southern Tang (937–75) imperial house in Nanjing, where he studied with Dong Yuan (active 930s–60s).\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "巨然僧曾在南京的南唐（937–975年）皇室任职，师从董源（活跃于930–960年代）。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "juran-buddhist-retreat-975": {"note": "960–85，中国 五代北宋。巨然的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。", "note_en": "960–85, China. 巨然; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1959.348. This is a painting (绢本水墨).", "note_html": "960–85，中国 五代北宋。巨然的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。"}, "seven-leaves-from-a-manuscript-of-the-gandavyuha-sutra-scriptu-1000": {"note": "这些书页来自一本长长的横向书籍，共包含355片棕榈叶，现已分散在许多收藏中。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "These pages come from a long horizontal book of 355 palm leaves, now dispersed among many collections.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "这些书页来自一本长长的横向书籍，共包含355片棕榈叶，现已分散在许多收藏中。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "palace-landscape-1000": {"note": "《宫苑图》，11世纪。中国，北宋（960–1127）。册页；绢本设色、水墨、金彩；整体尺寸：33 x 41.6厘米（13 x 16 3/8英寸）。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "Palace Landscape, 1000s. China, Northern Song dynasty (960–1127). Album leaf; ink, color, and gold on silk; overall: 33 x 41.6 cm (13 x 16 3/8 in.).\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "《宫苑图》，11世纪。中国，北宋（960–1127）。册页；绢本设色、水墨、金彩；整体尺寸：33 x 41.6厘米（13 x 16 3/8英寸）。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "votive-initiation-card-tsakali-with-preaching-buddha-shakyamun-1000": {"note": "佛教于7世纪传入西藏，但9世纪和10世纪随之而来的迫害摧毁了该时期的所有文物。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。", "note_en": "Buddhism was introduced to Tibet in the 7th century, but the persecution that followed in the 9th and 10th centuries destroyed all artifacts of the period.\n\nThe work arranges sacred figures inside a legible composition: bodies, gestures, objects and borders prescribe the order of looking. Read the centre first, then the sides and the lower edge; the image becomes a reusable language of faith.", "note_html": "佛教于7世纪传入西藏，但9世纪和10世纪随之而来的迫害摧毁了该时期的所有文物。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。"}, "fan-kuan-travelers-1025": {"note": "《溪山行旅图》是北宋山水画的巅峰之作。一座巨大的中央山峰向前凸出，山顶隐没在雾中；右侧有瀑布垂下，山脚下有一条小路，驮驴队和两个旅人正沿路前行。人物几乎看不见，被放在画面下方，以衬托山的高大。\n\n范宽用密集的“雨点”皴法堆砌岩石的重量，通过层层叠墨，让山体看起来仿佛真能挡住道路。他追求的不是风景如画的效果，而是那种山就在那里、沉重逼人的气势。", "note_en": "Travelers Among Mountains and Streams is the summit of Northern Song landscape. A vast central peak presses forward, its summit lost in mist; a waterfall falls at the right, and at the foot a path carries a train of pack donkeys and two travelers. The figures are almost invisible, placed low in the picture to measure the mountain's height.\n\nFan Kuan builds the weight of rock from dense \"raindrop\" texture strokes, layering ink until the mass feels like something that would actually block the road. He seeks not the picturesque but the pressure of a mountain that is simply there.", "note_html": "《溪山行旅图》是北宋山水画的巅峰之作。一座巨大的中央山峰向前凸出，山顶隐没在雾中；右侧有瀑布垂下，山脚下有一条小路，驮驴队和两个旅人正沿路前行。人物几乎看不见，被放在画面下方，以衬托山的高大。\n\n范宽用密集的“雨点”皴法堆砌岩石的重量，通过层层叠墨，让山体看起来仿佛真能挡住道路。他追求的不是风景如画的效果，而是那种山就在那里、沉重逼人的气势。"}, "cle-1968-190-1095": {"note": "拉丁圣经圣路加细密画，1095年。欧洲。蛋彩；Sheet: 17.3 x 16.1 cm (6 13/16 x 6 5/16 in.); Framed: 44.5 x 34.3 cm (17 1/2 x 13 1/2 in.); Matted: 40.6 x 30.5 cm (16 x 12 in.)。\n\n以极小尺度承载密集叙事，近看才有细节，远看才见结构。", "note_en": "Miniature from a Latin Bible: Saint Luke, c. 1100. France, Burgundy, Abbey of Cluny. Ink, tempera, and gold on vellum; sheet: 17.3 x 16.1 cm (6 13/16 x 6 5/16 in.); framed: 44.5 x 34.3 cm (17 1/2 x 13 1/2 in.); matted: 40.6 x 30.5 cm (16 x 12 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Purchase from the J. H. Wade Fund, 1968.190\n\nWithin “Material and Technique”, under “细密画”: A tiny scale carries dense narrative: detail up close, structure from afar.", "note_html": "拉丁圣经圣路加细密画，1095年。欧洲。蛋彩；Sheet: 17.3 x 16.1 cm (6 13/16 x 6 5/16 in.); Framed: 44.5 x 34.3 cm (17 1/2 x 13 1/2 in.); Matted: 40.6 x 30.5 cm (16 x 12 in.)。\n\n以极小尺度承载密集叙事，近看才有细节，远看才见结构。"}, "cle-1939-507-1100": {"note": "《古兰经》双面叶，1100年。西亚·北非。纸本设色；Sheet: 32 x 21.3 cm (12 5/8 x 8 3/8 in.)。\n\n让书页、字体与装帧一起进入图像，文字本身也是被观看的对象。", "note_en": "Double-Sided Leaf from a Qur'an, 1100s. Seljuk Iran. Opaque watercolor, ink, and gold on paper; sheet: 32 x 21.3 cm (12 5/8 x 8 3/8 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Purchase from the J. H. Wade Fund, 1939.507\n\nWithin “Faith and Image”, under “经典与书”: Treats page, script and binding as one image; the word itself is meant to be looked at.", "note_html": "《古兰经》双面叶，1100年。西亚·北非。纸本设色；Sheet: 32 x 21.3 cm (12 5/8 x 8 3/8 in.)。\n\n让书页、字体与装帧一起进入图像，文字本身也是被观看的对象。"}, "dwelling-in-the-longmian-sleeping-dragon-mountains-1100": {"note": "《龙眠山庄图》，12-13世纪。李公麟（中国，约1049–1106年）。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "Dwelling in the Longmian (\"Sleeping Dragon\") Mountains, 1100s-1200s. Li Gonglin (Chinese, c. 1049–1106).\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "《龙眠山庄图》，12-13世纪。李公麟（中国，约1049–1106年）。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "zhang-zeduan-qingming-scroll-1100": {"note": "《清明上河图》展示了北宋首都汴京在清明时节的全景。这幅卷从城外的柳树和运货队伍开始，经过汴河上的虹桥，进入城门和集市：船夫、挑夫、小贩、说书人、轿子、骆驼、酒馆、药铺——数百个人物，每个人都有动作，甚至桥边小贩的伞都画得栩栩如生。\n\n张择端画的不是宫廷，而是城市的运作：粮食运输、税收、消费、交通与娱乐。虹桥是高潮：一只大船正在降低桅杆以通过桥下，而桥上的人群喊叫观看。这既是一幅风俗画，也是一份十一世纪城市生活的社会记录。", "note_en": "Along the River During the Qingming Festival presents a panoramic view of the Northern Song capital Bianjing at the Qingming season. The scroll begins in willows and pack teams outside the city, passes the Rainbow Bridge over the Bian River, and enters gates and markets: boatmen, porters, vendors, storytellers, sedan chairs, camels, taverns, pharmacies — hundreds of figures, each with an action, down to the parasols of bridge-side hawkers.\n\nZhang Zeduan paints not the court but how a city works: grain transport, taxation, consumption, traffic and entertainment. The Rainbow Bridge is the climax: a large boat is lowering its mast to pass beneath while crowds on the bridge shout and watch. It is both a genre painting and a social record of eleventh-century urban life.", "note_html": "《清明上河图》展示了北宋首都汴京在清明时节的全景。这幅卷从城外的柳树和运货队伍开始，经过汴河上的虹桥，进入城门和集市：船夫、挑夫、小贩、说书人、轿子、骆驼、酒馆、药铺——数百个人物，每个人都有动作，甚至桥边小贩的伞都画得栩栩如生。\n\n张择端画的不是宫廷，而是城市的运作：粮食运输、税收、消费、交通与娱乐。虹桥是高潮：一只大船正在降低桅杆以通过桥下，而桥上的人群喊叫观看。这既是一幅风俗画，也是一份十一世纪城市生活的社会记录。"}, "one-hundred-children-at-play-1100": {"note": "以“百子”为主题的绘画通常描绘了许多儿童，即使不是正好100个。\n\n日常场景把城市、室内或劳作变成画面。器物、动作与衣饰这些细节，比情节更能说明当时的生活秩序。", "note_en": "Paintings on the “one hundred children” theme usually have numerous, if not exactly 100, children.\n\nA scene of daily life turns a city, an interior or labour into a picture. Objects, actions and clothes tell us more about the order of life than the anecdote does.", "note_html": "以“百子”为主题的绘画通常描绘了许多儿童，即使不是正好100个。\n\n日常场景把城市、室内或劳作变成画面。器物、动作与衣饰这些细节，比情节更能说明当时的生活秩序。"}, "wang-ximeng-thousand-li-1113": {"note": "《千里江山图》是北宋青绿山水的巅峰之作。王希孟画这幅画时才十八岁；画卷近十二米长，层层涂抹着蓝铜矿和孔雀石，山川、村落、桥梁和渔船在矿物色泽中徐徐展开。画面没有单一的焦点，视线沿着水面慢慢游走。\n\n青绿不是对自然的模仿，而是理想化的国土：蓝色闪耀，绿色透亮。它把“江山”变成一个可以游览和治理的空间，同时是绘画也是政治想象。", "note_en": "A Thousand Li of Rivers and Mountains is the peak of Northern Song blue-and-green landscape. Wang Ximeng was only eighteen when he painted it; the scroll runs nearly twelve metres, layered with azurite and malachite so that mountains, rivers, villages, bridges and fishing boats unfold in mineral light. There is no single focus; the eye travels slowly along the water.\n\nThe blue-green is not an imitation of nature but an idealised country: blue that shines, green that is transparent. It turns \"rivers and mountains\" into a space that can be toured and governed, at once painting and political imagination.", "note_html": "《千里江山图》是北宋青绿山水的巅峰之作。王希孟画这幅画时才十八岁；画卷近十二米长，层层涂抹着蓝铜矿和孔雀石，山川、村落、桥梁和渔船在矿物色泽中徐徐展开。画面没有单一的焦点，视线沿着水面慢慢游走。\n\n青绿不是对自然的模仿，而是理想化的国土：蓝色闪耀，绿色透亮。它把“江山”变成一个可以游览和治理的空间，同时是绘画也是政治想象。"}, "cottages-in-a-misty-grove-in-autumn-1117": {"note": "这幅作品是自900年代以来发展起来的水景风光画新模式的早期范例。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "This leaf is an early example of a new mode in landscape painting expressed in vistas of water-rich scenery that developed since the 900s.\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "这幅作品是自900年代以来发展起来的水景风光画新模式的早期范例。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "watching-the-deer-by-a-pine-shaded-stream-1127": {"note": "《松溪观鹿图》，1127–1279年。马远（中国，约1150年—1255年后）。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "Watching the Deer by a Pine Shaded Stream (松溪觀鹿圖), 1127–1279. Ma Yuan (Chinese, c. 1150–after 1255).\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "《松溪观鹿图》，1127–1279年。马远（中国，约1150年—1255年后）。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "bamboo-and-ducks-by-a-rushing-stream-1127": {"note": "《竹溪试浴》，1127–1279年。马远（中国，约1150年—1255年后）。挂轴；绢本水墨浅设色；整体尺寸：61 x 37厘米（24 x 14 9\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "Bamboo and Ducks by a Rushing Stream (竹溪試浴), 1127–1279. Ma Yuan (Chinese, c. 1150–after 1255). Hanging scroll; ink and light color on silk; overall: 61 x 37 cm (24 x 14 9/16 in.).\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "《竹溪试浴》，1127–1279年。马远（中国，约1150年—1255年后）。挂轴；绢本水墨浅设色；整体尺寸：61 x 37厘米（24 x 14 9\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "birds-on-a-tree-above-a-cataract-1127": {"note": "《宿禽激湍图》，1127–1279年。李迪（中国，约1100年—约1192年）。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。", "note_en": "Birds on a Tree above a Cataract (宿禽激湍圖), 1127–1279. Li Di (Chinese, c. 1100-c. 1192).\n\nThe work arranges sacred figures inside a legible composition: bodies, gestures, objects and borders prescribe the order of looking. Read the centre first, then the sides and the lower edge; the image becomes a reusable language of faith.", "note_html": "《宿禽激湍图》，1127–1279年。李迪（中国，约1100年—约1192年）。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。"}, "buffalo-and-boy-in-autumnal-landscape-1127": {"note": "《秋景牛童图》，1127–1279年。燕肃平（中国，活跃于1164–1187年）。册页；绢本水墨浅设色；画心：23 x 21厘米（9 1/16 x 8 1/4英寸）。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "Buffalo and Boy in Autumnal Landscape, 1127–1279. Yan Ciping (Chinese, active 1164–1187). Album leaf; ink and light color on silk; image: 23 x 21 cm (9 1/16 x 8 1/4 in.).\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "《秋景牛童图》，1127–1279年。燕肃平（中国，活跃于1164–1187年）。册页；绢本水墨浅设色；画心：23 x 21厘米（9 1/16 x 8 1/4英寸）。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "man-buffalo-and-calf-1145": {"note": "在这里，一位牧童正照看一头带着小牛的母牛，他坐在树下，身边是他的宠物八哥。这幅画可以被解读为一幅田园风光。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "Here, a herdboy tending a cow with a calf is sitting beneath a tree with his pet myna bird. The painting can be read as a pastoral scene.\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "在这里，一位牧童正照看一头带着小牛的母牛，他坐在树下，身边是他的宠物八哥。这幅画可以被解读为一幅田园风光。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "listening-to-the-qin-zither-1150": {"note": "《听琴图》再现了伯牙为钟子期鼓琴的故事。伯牙是一位喜欢弹琴（七弦琴）的琴师，而钟子期则是一位善于鉴赏的听众。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "Listening to the Qin recalls the story of Bo Ya, a musician who loved to play the qin (a seven-stringed zither) for Zhong Ziqi, who was a discerning listener.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "《听琴图》再现了伯牙为钟子期鼓琴的故事。伯牙是一位喜欢弹琴（七弦琴）的琴师，而钟子期则是一位善于鉴赏的听众。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "cle-1978-68-1150": {"note": "城门口西湖泊船，1150年。中国。绢本设色；Image: 25.3 x 19.2 cm (9 15/16 x 7 9/16 in.); with mat: 33.3 x 40.5 cm (13 1/8 x 15 15/16 in.)。\n\n把街巷当作舞台：行走、相遇与冲突都在同一段路发生。", "note_en": "Boats at Anchor on West Lake at the City Gate (早秋夜泊圖), 1150–1200. China, Southern Song dynasty (1127-1279). Album leaf; ink and color on silk; image: 25.3 x 19.2 cm (9 15/16 x 7 9/16 in.); with mat: 33.3 x 40.5 cm (13 1/8 x 15 15/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, John L. Severance Fund, 1978.68\n\nWithin “City and Everyday Life”, under “街道”: The street is a stage: walking, meeting and conflict share one route.", "note_html": "城门口西湖泊船，1150年。中国。绢本设色；Image: 25.3 x 19.2 cm (9 15/16 x 7 9/16 in.); with mat: 33.3 x 40.5 cm (13 1/8 x 15 15/16 in.)。\n\n把街巷当作舞台：行走、相遇与冲突都在同一段路发生。"}, "cle-1989-104-1150": {"note": "大日如来（金刚萨埵相），1150年。南亚。蛋彩；Overall: 111 x 73 cm (43 11/16 x 28 3/4 in.)。\n\n把神圣形象放回具体信仰：先看脸、手势与光环，再读教义。", "note_en": "Tantric Buddha Vairochana as Vajrasattva, c. 1150–1200. Central Tibet. Gum tempera, ink, and gold on cloth; overall: 111 x 73 cm (43 11/16 x 28 3/4 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Mr. and Mrs. William H. Marlatt Fund, 1989.104\n\nWithin “Faith and Image”, under “神圣人物”: Puts sacred figures back into a specific faith: face, gesture and halo first, doctrine second.", "note_html": "大日如来（金刚萨埵相），1150年。南亚。蛋彩；Overall: 111 x 73 cm (43 11/16 x 28 3/4 in.)。\n\n把神圣形象放回具体信仰：先看脸、手势与光环，再读教义。"}, "swinging-gibbon-1180": {"note": "《猿戏图》，12世纪末至13世纪初。传为夏圭（中国，活跃于约1209–约 1243年左右）。册页；绢本水墨设色；画心：24.8 x 26.5厘米（9 3/4 x 10 7/16英寸）\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "Swinging Gibbon, late 1100s–early 1200s. Attributed to Xia Gui (Chinese, active c. 1209–c. 1243). Album leaf; ink and color on silk; image: 24.8 x 26.5 cm (9 3/4 x 10 7/16 in.).\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "《猿戏图》，12世纪末至13世纪初。传为夏圭（中国，活跃于约1209–约 1243年左右）。册页；绢本水墨设色；画心：24.8 x 26.5厘米（9 3/4 x 10 7/16英寸）\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "cle-1938-422-1185": {"note": "药师如来与十二神将，1185年。东亚。绢本设色；Image: 151.2 x 84.1 cm (59 1/2 x 33 1/8 in.); Overall: 261 x 106.6 cm (102 3/4 x 41 15/16 in.); with knobs: 261 x 113.3 cm (102 3/4 x 44 5/8 in.)。\n\n把神圣形象放回具体信仰：先看脸、手势与光环，再读教义。", "note_en": "Medicine Master Buddha and the Twelve Divine Generals (薬師如来及び十二神将像), 1200s. Japan, Kamakura period (1185–1333). Hanging scroll painting; ink, color, gold, and silver on silk; image: 151.2 x 84.1 cm (59 1/2 x 33 1/8 in.); overall: 261 x 106.6 cm (102 3/4 x 41 15/16 in.); with knobs: 261 x 113.3 cm (102 3/4 x 44 5/8 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Edward L. Whittemore Fund, 1938.422\n\nWithin “Faith and Image”, under “神圣人物”: Puts sacred figures back into a specific faith: face, gesture and halo first, doctrine second.", "note_html": "药师如来与十二神将，1185年。东亚。绢本设色；Image: 151.2 x 84.1 cm (59 1/2 x 33 1/8 in.); Overall: 261 x 106.6 cm (102 3/4 x 41 15/16 in.); with knobs: 261 x 113.3 cm (102 3/4 x 44 5/8 in.)。\n\n把神圣形象放回具体信仰：先看脸、手势与光环，再读教义。"}, "drinking-in-the-moonlight-1189": {"note": "待到月上中天，酒尽杯空，或许这位微醺的躺卧君子会回到石桌旁，那里摆着墨、纸和毛笔。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "Once the moon rises and the wine is finished, perhaps the reclined tipsy gentleman will return to the stone table, where ink, paper, and brush can be seen.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "待到月上中天，酒尽杯空，或许这位微醺的躺卧君子会回到石桌旁，那里摆着墨、纸和毛笔。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "the-football-players-1189": {"note": "《蹴鞠图》，约1100年代末至1200年代初。传为马远（中国，约1150年—1255年后）所作。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "The Football Players (蹴鞠圖), c. late 1100s–1st quarter 1200s. Attributed to Ma Yuan (Chinese, c. 1150–after 1255).\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "《蹴鞠图》，约1100年代末至1200年代初。传为马远（中国，约1150年—1255年后）所作。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "bamboo-and-insects-1190": {"note": "吴炳是平江人，深得李皇后宠幸，在绍熙年间（1190–94年）在杭州宫廷担任侍画。\n\n日常场景把城市、室内或劳作变成画面。器物、动作与衣饰这些细节，比情节更能说明当时的生活秩序。", "note_en": "Wu Bing, a native of Piling, gained Empress Li’s favor and served as a painter-in-attendance at the court in Hangzhou during the Shaoxi reign (1190–94).\n\nA scene of daily life turns a city, an interior or labour into a picture. Objects, actions and clothes tell us more about the order of life than the anecdote does.", "note_html": "吴炳是平江人，深得李皇后宠幸，在绍熙年间（1190–94年）在杭州宫廷担任侍画。\n\n日常场景把城市、室内或劳作变成画面。器物、动作与衣饰这些细节，比情节更能说明当时的生活秩序。"}, "the-autumn-hunt-1196": {"note": "骑马和狩猎在中国东北边境生活的契丹族和女真族中尤为盛行。\n\n日常场景把城市、室内或劳作变成画面。器物、动作与衣饰这些细节，比情节更能说明当时的生活秩序。", "note_en": "Equestrian pursuits and hunting were particularly popular among the Khitan (also spelled “Qidan”) and Jurchen, ethnic groups who lived along China’s northeastern border.\n\nA scene of daily life turns a city, an interior or labour into a picture. Objects, actions and clothes tell us more about the order of life than the anecdote does.", "note_html": "骑马和狩猎在中国东北边境生活的契丹族和女真族中尤为盛行。\n\n日常场景把城市、室内或劳作变成画面。器物、动作与衣饰这些细节，比情节更能说明当时的生活秩序。"}, "cle-1961-423-1200": {"note": "五秘密菩萨，1200年。东亚。绢本设色；Image: 78.1 x 63.5 cm (30 3/4 x 25 in.); Overall: 163.2 x 83.8 cm (64 1/4 x 33 in.)。\n\n把神圣形象放回具体信仰：先看脸、手势与光环，再读教义。", "note_en": "The Secret Five Bodhisattvas (Gohimitsu Bosatsu) (五秘密菩薩像), 1200s. Japan, Kamakura period (1185–1333). Hanging scroll; ink, color, gold, and silver on silk; image: 78.1 x 63.5 cm (30 3/4 x 25 in.); overall: 163.2 x 83.8 cm (64 1/4 x 33 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Mr. and Mrs. William H. Marlatt Fund, 1961.423\n\nWithin “Faith and Image”, under “神圣人物”: Puts sacred figures back into a specific faith: face, gesture and halo first, doctrine second.", "note_html": "五秘密菩萨，1200年。东亚。绢本设色；Image: 78.1 x 63.5 cm (30 3/4 x 25 in.); Overall: 163.2 x 83.8 cm (64 1/4 x 33 in.)。\n\n把神圣形象放回具体信仰：先看脸、手势与光环，再读教义。"}, "magpies-and-wild-rabbits-1200": {"note": "《喜鹊与野兔》，13世纪。李泳（中国，活跃于13世纪）。册页，绢本水墨淡彩；画芯：25 x 24.5厘米（9 13/16 x 9 5/8英寸）。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "Magpies and Wild Rabbits, 1200s. Li Yong (Chinese, active 1200s). Album leaf, ink and light color on silk; painting only: 25 x 24.5 cm (9 13/16 x 9 5/8 in.).\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "《喜鹊与野兔》，13世纪。李泳（中国，活跃于13世纪）。册页，绢本水墨淡彩；画芯：25 x 24.5厘米（9 13/16 x 9 5/8英寸）。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "cle-1987-37-1200": {"note": "月下山景，1200年。中国。绢本水墨；Image: 54.3 x 36 cm (21 3/8 x 14 3/16 in.); Overall: 139.6 x 41.4 cm (54 15/16 x 16 5/16 in.)。\n\n以山体、路径与雾气组织观看，山不是背景，而是叙事的主体。", "note_en": "Mountain Landscape in Moonlight, 1200s. China, Southern Song dynasty (1127–1279) to Yuan dynasty (1271–1368). Hanging scroll; ink on silk; image: 54.3 x 36 cm (21 3/8 x 14 3/16 in.); overall: 139.6 x 41.4 cm (54 15/16 x 16 5/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Mr. and Mrs. William H. Marlatt Fund, 1987.37\n\nWithin “Landscape and Nature”, under “山”: Organises looking through mass, path and mist; the mountain is the subject, not the backdrop.", "note_html": "月下山景，1200年。中国。绢本水墨；Image: 54.3 x 36 cm (21 3/8 x 14 3/16 in.); Overall: 139.6 x 41.4 cm (54 15/16 x 16 5/16 in.)。\n\n以山体、路径与雾气组织观看，山不是背景，而是叙事的主体。"}, "waterfowl-and-reeds-1200": {"note": "这幅册页现已装裱成挂轴，被认为是13世纪艺术家梁楷的作品。梁楷曾短暂地在南宋朝廷担任宫廷画家。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "This album leaf now mounted as a hanging scroll is attributed to the 13th-century artist Liang Kai, who served for a time in the Southern Song court as a court painter.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "这幅册页现已装裱成挂轴，被认为是13世纪艺术家梁楷的作品。梁楷曾短暂地在南宋朝廷担任宫廷画家。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "cle-1974-35-1200": {"note": "阿弥陀佛与二胁侍菩萨，1200年。中国。绢本设色；Painting: 134 x 79.7 cm (52 3/4 x 31 3/8 in.); Overall with knobs: 224.5 x 101.5 cm (88 3/8 x 39 15/16 in.)。\n\n把神圣形象放回具体信仰：先看脸、手势与光环，再读教义。", "note_en": "Buddha Amitābha with Two Attending Bodhisattvas, 1200s. China, Southern Song dynasty (1127–1279). Hanging scroll; ink and color on silk; painting: 134 x 79.7 cm (52 3/4 x 31 3/8 in.); overall with knobs: 224.5 x 101.5 cm (88 3/8 x 39 15/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Leonard C. Hanna Jr. Fund, 1974.35\n\nWithin “Faith and Image”, under “神圣人物”: Puts sacred figures back into a specific faith: face, gesture and halo first, doctrine second.", "note_html": "阿弥陀佛与二胁侍菩萨，1200年。中国。绢本设色；Painting: 134 x 79.7 cm (52 3/4 x 31 3/8 in.); Overall with knobs: 224.5 x 101.5 cm (88 3/8 x 39 15/16 in.)。\n\n把神圣形象放回具体信仰：先看脸、手势与光环，再读教义。"}, "full-sail-on-the-misty-river-1200": {"note": "《烟江帆影图》，13 世纪。夏旉（中国，活跃于13世纪）协助。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "Full Sail on the Misty River (煙江颿景圖), 1200s. Assisted by Xia Sheng (Chinese, active 1200s).\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "《烟江帆影图》，13 世纪。夏旉（中国，活跃于13世纪）协助。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "the-knickknack-peddler-1212": {"note": "杭州宫廷画家李嵩擅长细腻地描绘儿童、小贩及其各种商品。\n\n日常场景把城市、室内或劳作变成画面。器物、动作与衣饰这些细节，比情节更能说明当时的生活秩序。", "note_en": "The court artist Li Song from Hangzhou excelled in meticulous depictions of children, peddlers, and their various goods.\n\nA scene of daily life turns a city, an interior or labour into a picture. Objects, actions and clothes tell us more about the order of life than the anecdote does.", "note_html": "杭州宫廷画家李嵩擅长细腻地描绘儿童、小贩及其各种商品。\n\n日常场景把城市、室内或劳作变成画面。器物、动作与衣饰这些细节，比情节更能说明当时的生活秩序。"}, "the-crucifixion-of-st-andrew-with-st-francis-and-st-paul-below-1225": {"note": "这幅小型祭坛画专为家居内饰或私人小教堂而作，由三块画板组成，可折叠并便于携带。\n\n日常场景把城市、室内或劳作变成画面。器物、动作与衣饰这些细节，比情节更能说明当时的生活秩序。", "note_en": "This small altarpiece, intended for a domestic interior or private chapel, consists of three panels, allowing it to be folded and easily transported.\n\nA scene of daily life turns a city, an interior or labour into a picture. Objects, actions and clothes tell us more about the order of life than the anecdote does.", "note_html": "这幅小型祭坛画专为家居内饰或私人小教堂而作，由三块画板组成，可折叠并便于携带。\n\n日常场景把城市、室内或劳作变成画面。器物、动作与衣饰这些细节，比情节更能说明当时的生活秩序。"}, "virgin-and-child-with-saints-1225": {"note": "这幅小型祭坛画专为家居内饰或私人小教堂而作，由三块画板组成，可折叠并便于携带。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。", "note_en": "This small altarpiece, intended for a domestic interior or private chapel, consists of three panels, allowing it to be folded and easily transported.\n\nThe work arranges sacred figures inside a legible composition: bodies, gestures, objects and borders prescribe the order of looking. Read the centre first, then the sides and the lower edge; the image becomes a reusable language of faith.", "note_html": "这幅小型祭坛画专为家居内饰或私人小教堂而作，由三块画板组成，可折叠并便于携带。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。"}, "crucifix-with-scenes-of-the-passion-1225": {"note": "这些大型彩绘十字架的历史可追溯至12世纪和13世纪，是现存最早的意大利板画之一。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "Large painted crucifixes dating from the 1100s and 1200s are among the earliest surviving Italian panel paintings.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "这些大型彩绘十字架的历史可追溯至12世纪和13世纪，是现存最早的意大利板画之一。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "christ-in-a-mandorla-with-the-instruments-of-the-passion-with--1225": {"note": "这幅小型祭坛画专为家居内饰或私人小教堂而作，由三块画板组成，可折叠并便于携带。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。", "note_en": "This small altarpiece, intended for a domestic interior or private chapel, consists of three panels, allowing it to be folded and easily transported.\n\nThe work arranges sacred figures inside a legible composition: bodies, gestures, objects and borders prescribe the order of looking. Read the centre first, then the sides and the lower edge; the image becomes a reusable language of faith.", "note_html": "这幅小型祭坛画专为家居内饰或私人小教堂而作，由三块画板组成，可折叠并便于携带。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。"}, "willow-and-magpie-1225": {"note": "《柳荫下喜鹊》的创作灵感源于一种思维方式，它将对鸟类（尤其是喜鹊）的细致观察与使用\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "The Willow and Magpie is the product of a mindset that combines knowledgeable observation of birds in general and magpies in particular with an image-making process using a sophist\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "《柳荫下喜鹊》的创作灵感源于一种思维方式，它将对鸟类（尤其是喜鹊）的细致观察与使用\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "swallow-and-lotus-1225": {"note": "一只燕子展开双翼翱翔，飞越一朵翠绿的莲花，莲花从两片宽大的叶子和草芽中亭亭玉立。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "A swallow with wings spread in flight soars above a lush lotus blossom, which rises above two broad leaves and grassy shoots.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "一只燕子展开双翼翱翔，飞越一朵翠绿的莲花，莲花从两片宽大的叶子和草芽中亭亭玉立。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "landscape-with-flying-geese-1225": {"note": "这幅极简主义风景画将大多数具象元素置于右下方的前景中。一位独行的绅士沿着水边的曲折小径漫步。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "This minimalist landscape places most of the representational elements in the lower right foreground. A lone gentleman strolls along a zigzagging path by the water.\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "这幅极简主义风景画将大多数具象元素置于右下方的前景中。一位独行的绅士沿着水边的曲折小径漫步。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "folio-22-from-a-yoga-shastra-of-hemachandra-jain-monk-with-dis-1250": {"note": "这幅画出自后来的一篇关于瑜伽和冥想的梵文文献，描绘了教义的传承。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "This painting, from later in a Sanskrit text on yoga and meditation, shows the transmission of the teaching.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "这幅画出自后来的一篇关于瑜伽和冥想的梵文文献，描绘了教义的传承。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "folio-2-from-a-kalpa-sutra-a-monk-preaching-recto-text-verso-1250": {"note": "第2页，出自《劫世经》：僧侣布道（正面）；文字（背面），约 1275年。印度西部，古吉拉特邦。棕榈叶上的胶质蛋彩画和墨水；整体尺寸：5.7 x 18.4厘米（2 1/4 x 7\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "Folio 2, from a Kalpa-sutra: A Monk Preaching (recto); Text (verso), c. 1275. Western India, Gujarat. Gum tempera and ink on palm leaf; overall: 5.7 x 18.4 cm (2 1/4 x 7 1/4 in.).\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "第2页，出自《劫世经》：僧侣布道（正面）；文字（背面），约 1275年。印度西部，古吉拉特邦。棕榈叶上的胶质蛋彩画和墨水；整体尺寸：5.7 x 18.4厘米（2 1/4 x 7\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "herdboys-and-buffalo-in-landscape-1250": {"note": "牧牛男孩在蜿蜒小溪旁的田园风光中照看水牛。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "Herdboys tend their buffalo in a bucolic landscape by a winding stream.\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "牧牛男孩在蜿蜒小溪旁的田园风光中照看水牛。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "green-tara-1250": {"note": "对于藏族人来说，绿度母是他们佛教信仰中最杰出的形象之一，是一位光芒四射的救世主，体现了完美、开明心灵的女性形象。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。", "note_en": "For Tibetans, Green Tara is one of the preeminent figures of their Buddhist faith, a radiant savioress who embodies the female form of the perfect, enlightened mind.\n\nThe work arranges sacred figures inside a legible composition: bodies, gestures, objects and borders prescribe the order of looking. Read the centre first, then the sides and the lower edge; the image becomes a reusable language of faith.", "note_html": "对于藏族人来说，绿度母是他们佛教信仰中最杰出的形象之一，是一位光芒四射的救世主，体现了完美、开明心灵的女性形象。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。"}, "bamboo-in-the-wind-1250": {"note": "竹子是一种常绿植物，不会因积雪的重量或风力而折断，因此成为文人画和禅宗佛教中的常见主题。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "Bamboo is an evergreen plant that does not break under the weight of snow or the force of the wind, and thus became a favorite motif in literati painting and Chan Buddhism as a met\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "竹子是一种常绿植物，不会因积雪的重量或风力而折断，因此成为文人画和禅宗佛教中的常见主题。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "herdboys-and-buffalo-in-landscapes-1250": {"note": "牧牛男孩在蜿蜒小溪旁的田园风光中照看水牛。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "Herdboys tend their buffalo in a bucolic landscape by a winding stream.\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "牧牛男孩在蜿蜒小溪旁的田园风光中照看水牛。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "dragon-tiger-1250": {"note": "龙和虎与阴阳的哲学概念紧密相连，阴阳描述的是相互对立但又相互补充的力量。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "The dragon and tiger are tied to the philosophical concept of yin and yang, which describes opposite but complementary forces.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "龙和虎与阴阳的哲学概念紧密相连，阴阳描述的是相互对立但又相互补充的力量。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "scholar-reclining-and-watching-rising-clouds-poem-by-wang-wei-1251": {"note": "诗与画曾被装裱在一把扇子上，体现了皇室赞助者与宫廷画师之间的合作。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "Poem and painting, once mounted together as one fan, exemplify the collaboration between imperial patron and court painter.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "诗与画曾被装裱在一把扇子上，体现了皇室赞助者与宫廷画师之间的合作。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "muqi-dragon-1260": {"note": "c. 1250–79，中国 南宋。牧溪（法常）的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。", "note_en": "c. 1250–79, China. 牧溪（法常）; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1958.427.1. This is a painting (绢本水墨).", "note_html": "c. 1250–79，中国 南宋。牧溪（法常）的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。"}, "cle-1924-427-1265": {"note": "诗篇集圣母诞生细密画，1265年。欧洲。蛋彩；Sheet: 9.5 x 12.2 cm (3 3/4 x 4 13/16 in.)。\n\n以极小尺度承载密集叙事，近看才有细节，远看才见结构。", "note_en": "Miniature Excised from a Psalter: The Nativity, c. 1270. England, London(?), 13th century. Ink, tempera, and gold on vellum; sheet: 9.5 x 12.2 cm (3 3/4 x 4 13/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift from J. H. Wade, 1924.427\n\nWithin “Material and Technique”, under “细密画”: A tiny scale carries dense narrative: detail up close, structure from afar.", "note_html": "诗篇集圣母诞生细密画，1265年。欧洲。蛋彩；Sheet: 9.5 x 12.2 cm (3 3/4 x 4 13/16 in.)。\n\n以极小尺度承载密集叙事，近看才有细节，远看才见结构。"}, "monk-preaching-to-a-disciple-with-a-lay-audience-folio-2-recto-1270": {"note": "一位年长的僧侣正在教导他的弟子，这一场景强调了口头传承故事和知识的重要性。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "The scene of a senior monk teaching his disciple emphasizes the importance of oral transmission of stories and knowledge.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "一位年长的僧侣正在教导他的弟子，这一场景强调了口头传承故事和知识的重要性。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "folio-2-from-a-parshvanatha-charitra-life-and-stories-of-lord--1270": {"note": "这张叶片来自一份手稿的开头，手稿讲述的是倒数第二位耆那（耆那教中的解脱者）帕什瓦（Parshva）的一生和九世前生。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "This leaf comes from the beginning of a manuscript about the life and nine past lives of the penultimate Jina (liberated being in the Jain religion), known as Parshva.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "这张叶片来自一份手稿的开头，手稿讲述的是倒数第二位耆那（耆那教中的解脱者）帕什瓦（Parshva）的一生和九世前生。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "text-folio-2-verso-from-a-parshvanatha-charitra-life-and-stori-1270": {"note": "本页上的九行文字以天成文书写。这些文字从左至右阅读，每行文字贯穿整页。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "The nine lines of text on this page are written in Devanagari script. They are read from left to right, with each line of text spanning the entire length of the page.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "本页上的九行文字以天成文书写。这些文字从左至右阅读，每行文字贯穿整页。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "folio-167-from-a-kalpa-sutra-and-story-of-kalakacharya-two-nun-1278": {"note": "本页来自一份手稿的末尾，其中包含两篇通常成对出现的文本：《劫经》（Kalpa-sutra）和《迦罗迦遮那的故事》（Story of Kalakacharya）。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "This page is from the end of a manuscript, which contains two texts often paired together, the Kalpa-sutra and Story of Kalakacharya .\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "本页来自一份手稿的末尾，其中包含两篇通常成对出现的文本：《劫经》（Kalpa-sutra）和《迦罗迦遮那的故事》（Story of Kalakacharya）。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "folio-from-a-kalpa-sutra-and-story-of-kalakacharya-of-devachan-1279": {"note": "本页出自《迦拉迦的故事》的结尾，讲述迦拉迦因绝食而死。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "This page is from the end of the Story of Kalakacharya, when Kalaka dies by fasting.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "本页出自《迦拉迦的故事》的结尾，讲述迦拉迦因绝食而死。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "folio-2-from-a-kalpa-sutra-and-story-of-kalakacharya-of-devach-1279": {"note": "第2页，选自《劫世经》和《德瓦钱德拉的卡拉卡查雅故事》：坐于宝座上的僧侣乔达摩（正面）；文字（背面），1279年。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "Folio 2, from a Kalpa-sutra and Story of Kalakacharya of Devachandra: Enthroned Monk Gautama (recto); Text (verso), 1279.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "第2页，选自《劫世经》和《德瓦钱德拉的卡拉卡查雅故事》：坐于宝座上的僧侣乔达摩（正面）；文字（背面），1279年。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "folio-141-from-a-kalpa-sutra-and-story-of-kalakacharya-text-re-1286": {"note": "在15世纪之前，棕榈叶是印度神圣经文的首选材料。这里的文本通常附在耆那教最神圣的经典《劫经》（Kalpa-sutra）之后。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "Palm leaf was the preferred material for sacred texts before the 1400s in India. The text here was often appended to the Kalpa-sutra, the most sacred book of Jainism.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "在15世纪之前，棕榈叶是印度神圣经文的首选材料。这里的文本通常附在耆那教最神圣的经典《劫经》（Kalpa-sutra）之后。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "folio-2-from-a-kalpa-sutra-and-story-of-kalakacharya-monk-hold-1286": {"note": "该文本描述了摩诃毗罗从天上降临到婆罗门女子提婆南陀的子宫中。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "The text describes the descent of Mahavira from heaven into the womb of the Brahman woman Devananda.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "该文本描述了摩诃毗罗从天上降临到婆罗门女子提婆南陀的子宫中。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "cle-1983-73-1290": {"note": "《启示录》抄本细密画，1290年。欧洲。蛋彩；Sheet: 10.2 x 14.7 cm (4 x 5 13/16 in.); Framed: 52.4 x 39.7 cm (20 5/8 x 15 5/8 in.); Matted: 48.9 x 36.2 cm (19 1/4 x 14 1/4 in.)。\n\n让抄写、插图与装帧互相解释，书是一件被使用的整体。", "note_en": "Miniatures from a Manuscript of the Apocalypse, c. 1295. France, Lorraine. Ink, tempera, and gold on vellum; sheet: 10.2 x 14.7 cm (4 x 5 13/16 in.); framed: 52.4 x 39.7 cm (20 5/8 x 15 5/8 in.); matted: 48.9 x 36.2 cm (19 1/4 x 14 1/4 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Mr. and Mrs. William H. Marlatt Fund, 1983.73\n\nWithin “Word and Looking”, under “手抄本”: Writing, illumination and binding explain one another; the book is a used object.", "note_html": "《启示录》抄本细密画，1290年。欧洲。蛋彩；Sheet: 10.2 x 14.7 cm (4 x 5 13/16 in.); Framed: 52.4 x 39.7 cm (20 5/8 x 15 5/8 in.); Matted: 48.9 x 36.2 cm (19 1/4 x 14 1/4 in.)。\n\n让抄写、插图与装帧互相解释，书是一件被使用的整体。"}, "cle-1951-314-1295": {"note": "供养人戈鲁斯·福奇跪拜基督（唱经本首字母），1295年。欧洲。蛋彩；Sheet: 13.4 x 13.4 cm (5 1/4 x 5 1/4 in.)。\n\n把出资者放进神圣叙事，让信仰与社会位置同时可见。", "note_en": "Historiated Initial (O) Excised from an Antiphonary: The Donor, Gorus Fucci, Kneels before Christ, c. 1300–1350. Italy, Arezzo(?). Ink, tempera, and gold on parchment; sheet: 13.4 x 13.4 cm (5 1/4 x 5 1/4 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Purchase from the J. H. Wade Fund, 1951.314\n\nWithin “Portrait and Self”, under “供养人”: Places the patron inside the sacred narrative, making faith and social position visible together.", "note_html": "供养人戈鲁斯·福奇跪拜基督（唱经本首字母），1295年。欧洲。蛋彩；Sheet: 13.4 x 13.4 cm (5 1/4 x 5 1/4 in.)。\n\n把出资者放进神圣叙事，让信仰与社会位置同时可见。"}, "river-village-fisherman-s-joy-1298": {"note": "这幅青绿山水画的作者赵孟頫是南方人，精通书法、鉴赏等文人雅士的各种爱好。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "The artist of this blue-green–style landscape, Zhao Mengfu, was a southerner, versed in all fields of literati pursuits, such as calligraphy and connoisseurship.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "这幅青绿山水画的作者赵孟頫是南方人，精通书法、鉴赏等文人雅士的各种爱好。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "landscape-ink-play-1300": {"note": "画家巧妙地将宁静航行的船只与背景中高耸山脉的汹涌澎湃形成鲜明对比，营造出一种矛盾的并置效果。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "The painter created a paradoxical juxtaposition of the boat serenely sailing against the turbulent onrushing movement of the towering mountains in the background.\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "画家巧妙地将宁静航行的船只与背景中高耸山脉的汹涌澎湃形成鲜明对比，营造出一种矛盾的并置效果。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "a-prunus-in-the-moonlight-1300": {"note": "梅花在南方温暖的气候中盛开，直到六朝时期（公元220–589年），这一主题才开始受到南方艺术家的青睐。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "The plum flourishes in the mild climate of the south, and it was not before the Six Dynasties period (220– 589 CE) that the motif began to be appreciated by southern artists, many\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "梅花在南方温暖的气候中盛开，直到六朝时期（公元220–589年），这一主题才开始受到南方艺术家的青睐。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "plum-blossoms-in-moonlight-1300": {"note": "《月梅图》，14 世纪上半叶。颜辉（中国，活跃于1270–1310年）。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "Plum Blossoms in Moonlight (月梅圖), first half of the 1300s. Yan Hui (Chinese, active 1270–1310).\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "《月梅图》，14 世纪上半叶。颜辉（中国，活跃于1270–1310年）。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "fishermen-hermits-in-stream-and-mountain-1300": {"note": "在这幅典型的南方河流分隔两岸的构图中，两位渔夫分别坐在各自带顶棚的船屋船尾，将鱼钩抛入漩涡般的水流中。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "In this typical southern two shores divided by a river composition, two fishermen, each seated in the stern of his covered houseboat, troll their hooks in the swirling water, holdi\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "在这幅典型的南方河流分隔两岸的构图中，两位渔夫分别坐在各自带顶棚的船屋船尾，将鱼钩抛入漩涡般的水流中。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "bamboo-rock-and-tall-tree-1300": {"note": "《筠石乔柯》，约14世纪。倪瓒（中国，1301–1374）。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "Bamboo, Rock, and Tall Tree (筠石喬柯), c. 1300s. Ni Zan (Chinese, 1301–1374).\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "《筠石乔柯》，约14世纪。倪瓒（中国，1301–1374）。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "flowers-and-birds-1300": {"note": "《花鸟》，14世纪上半叶。钱选（中国，1235–1307）的风格。册页；纸本水墨设色；画心：29.4 x 28.8厘米（11 9/16 x 11 5/16英寸）\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "Flowers and Birds, first half of the 14th Century. Style of Qian Xuan (Chinese, 1235–1307). Album leaf; ink and color on paper; image: 29.4 x 28.8 cm (11 9/16 x 11 5/16 in.).\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "《花鸟》，14世纪上半叶。钱选（中国，1235–1307）的风格。册页；纸本水墨设色；画心：29.4 x 28.8厘米（11 9/16 x 11 5/16英寸）\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "cle-1982-25-1300": {"note": "释迦牟尼与二侍者，1300年。中国。绢本设色；Overall: 293.5 x 136 cm (115 9/16 x 53 9/16 in.); Painting only: 218.4 x 112.8 cm (86 x 44 7/16 in.); with knobs: 293.5 x 144.2 cm (115 9/16 x 56 3/4 in.)。\n\n以绢、纸的吸墨与反光，决定线条和颜色的呼吸。", "note_en": "Shakyamuni with two attendants, 1300s. China, Yuan (1271-1368) or early Ming dynasty (1368-1644). Hanging scroll; ink, color, and gold on silk; overall: 293.5 x 136 cm (115 9/16 x 53 9/16 in.); painting only: 218.4 x 112.8 cm (86 x 44 7/16 in.); with knobs: 293.5 x 144.2 cm (115 9/16 x 56 3/4 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, John L. Severance Fund, 1982.25\n\nWithin “Material and Technique”, under “绢纸”: Silk and paper decide how ink and colour breathe.", "note_html": "释迦牟尼与二侍者，1300年。中国。绢本设色；Overall: 293.5 x 136 cm (115 9/16 x 53 9/16 in.); Painting only: 218.4 x 112.8 cm (86 x 44 7/16 in.); with knobs: 293.5 x 144.2 cm (115 9/16 x 56 3/4 in.)。\n\n以绢、纸的吸墨与反光，决定线条和颜色的呼吸。"}, "nagarjuna-c-150-250-ce-with-a-buddhist-master-1300": {"note": "来自印度南部的佛教哲学家龙树（Nagarjuna）坐在与他同名的红黑双蛇（即那伽）之上。与他交谈的人可能是他的弟子龙树。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "Nagarjuna, the Buddhist philosopher from southern India, sits on his eponymous red and black serpents, or naga . His interlocutor may be his disciple Aryadeva.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "来自印度南部的佛教哲学家龙树（Nagarjuna）坐在与他同名的红黑双蛇（即那伽）之上。与他交谈的人可能是他的弟子龙树。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "writing-books-under-the-pine-trees-1303": {"note": "王蒙出生于浙江省吴兴（今湖州）的一个显赫家族，是赵孟頫（1254–1322）的外孙。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "Wang Meng, born into a distinguished family in Wuxing (modern Huzhou), Zhejiang province, was the maternal grandson of Zhao Mengfu (1254–1322).\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "王蒙出生于浙江省吴兴（今湖州）的一个显赫家族，是赵孟頫（1254–1322）的外孙。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "giotto-lamentation-1305": {"note": "在帕多瓦的斯克罗维尼教堂，乔托把拜占庭的圣像变成了有重量、有呼吸的身体。玛丽靠近基督的脸，约翰张开双臂，抹大拉的玛利亚握着他的脚；一个斜斜的岩石台阶把目光引向死去的身体，把整个场景压在左下角。在天空中，天使在哭泣，他们的悲伤几乎可见。\n\n乔托把场景放在灰蓝色的岩石和土地上，而不是金色背景里，用体积感、空间深度和可识别的表情代替了象征性的秩序。衣服有了厚度，脸上有了阴影，悲伤也有了不同的层次。艺术史上通常把这一刻视为西方绘画从圣像走向自然的转折点。", "note_en": "In the Scrovegni Chapel in Padua, Giotto turned the Byzantine icon into bodies that weigh and breathe. Mary bends close to Christ's face, John throws his arms wide, Mary Magdalene holds the feet; a diagonal rock ledge drives the eye down to the dead figure and presses the whole group into the lower left corner. In the sky, angels weep, their grief almost visible.\n\nGiotto set the scene on grey-blue rock and earth rather than against a gold ground, replacing symbolic order with volume, spatial depth and recognisable expression. Drapery acquires thickness, faces acquire shadow, and grief acquires different degrees. Art history often treats this moment as the point where Western painting turns from icon towards nature.", "note_html": "在帕多瓦的斯克罗维尼教堂，乔托把拜占庭的圣像变成了有重量、有呼吸的身体。玛丽靠近基督的脸，约翰张开双臂，抹大拉的玛利亚握着他的脚；一个斜斜的岩石台阶把目光引向死去的身体，把整个场景压在左下角。在天空中，天使在哭泣，他们的悲伤几乎可见。\n\n乔托把场景放在灰蓝色的岩石和土地上，而不是金色背景里，用体积感、空间深度和可识别的表情代替了象征性的秩序。衣服有了厚度，脸上有了阴影，悲伤也有了不同的层次。艺术史上通常把这一刻视为西方绘画从圣像走向自然的转折点。"}, "duccio-maesta-1308": {"note": "《威严》是杜乔为锡耶纳大教堂创作的双面祭坛画的正面板，于1311年像圣物一样被抬过街道。圣母端坐在宝座上，怀抱基督儿童，周围环绕着圣人和天使；金色的背景将人群压缩到一个发光的平面上。杜乔并没有放弃拜占庭式的威严——蓝色的披肩、修长的手指和仪式般的对称都是从东方继承而来——但他让人物转身、低语和倾斜，使衣纹在膝部显得有真实重量，并在宝座后面开辟了一个浅浅的空间。\n\n结果是一幅开始有呼吸感的神圣图像。它表明文艺复兴并非只出现在佛罗伦萨：在锡耶纳，宗教绘画早已成为展示人体动作的舞台。", "note_en": "*Maestà* was the front panel of Duccio's double-sided altarpiece for Siena Cathedral, carried through the streets in 1311 like a relic. The Virgin sits on a throne with the Christ Child, surrounded by saints and angels; the gold ground compresses the crowd into a luminous plane. Duccio does not abandon Byzantine majesty — the blue mantle, long fingers and ceremonial symmetry are inherited from the East — but he lets figures turn, whisper and lean, gives drapery real weight at the knee, and opens a shallow space behind the throne.\n\nThe result is a sacred image that begins to breathe. It shows that the Renaissance did not appear only in Florence: in Siena, devotional painting had already become a stage for human gesture.", "note_html": "《威严》是杜乔为锡耶纳大教堂创作的双面祭坛画的正面板，于1311年像圣物一样被抬过街道。圣母端坐在宝座上，怀抱基督儿童，周围环绕着圣人和天使；金色的背景将人群压缩到一个发光的平面上。杜乔并没有放弃拜占庭式的威严——蓝色的披肩、修长的手指和仪式般的对称都是从东方继承而来——但他让人物转身、低语和倾斜，使衣纹在膝部显得有真实重量，并在宝座后面开辟了一个浅浅的空间。\n\n结果是一幅开始有呼吸感的神圣图像。它表明文艺复兴并非只出现在佛罗伦萨：在锡耶纳，宗教绘画早已成为展示人体动作的舞台。"}, "travelers-in-autumn-mountains-1310": {"note": "画家的款识大多已被刮掉，因此只有“盛”字清晰可辨。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "Most of the signature of the artist has been scraped away, so that only the character \"Sheng\" is legible.\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "画家的款识大多已被刮掉，因此只有“盛”字清晰可辨。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "ramblers-over-a-winding-stream-1320": {"note": "这幅册页是罗钦顺为数不多的存世画作之一。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "This album leaf is one of few surviving paintings by Luo Zichuan.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "这幅册页是罗钦顺为数不多的存世画作之一。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "the-second-coming-of-the-fifth-patriarch-1325": {"note": "一个小男孩在母亲的陪同下，双手合十向一位老僧人行礼，老僧人身后站着一位年轻的侍者。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "A small boy, accompanied by his mother, is closing his hands in greeting to an old monk who has a young attendant standing behind him.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "一个小男孩在母亲的陪同下，双手合十向一位老僧人行礼，老僧人身后站着一位年轻的侍者。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "old-trees-by-a-cool-spring-1326": {"note": "《清泉乔木图》，1326 年。李士行（中国，1283–1328）。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "Old Trees by a Cool Spring (清泉喬木圖), 1326. Li Shixing (Chinese, 1283–1328).\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "《清泉乔木图》，1326 年。李士行（中国，1283–1328）。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "cle-2025-138-1336": {"note": "阿弥陀佛来迎图，1336年。东亚。绢本设色；Painting: 164.5 x 137.7 cm (64 3/4 x 54 3/16 in.); Mounted: 255 x 166.6 cm (100 3/8 x 65 9/16 in.)。\n\n把神圣形象放回具体信仰：先看脸、手势与光环，再读教义。", "note_en": "Welcoming Descent of Amida with Twenty-Five Bodhisattvas (阿弥陀二十五菩薩来迎図), mid-1300s. Japan, Nanbokuchō period (1336–92). Hanging scroll; ink, color, gold, silver, and cut gold on silk; painting: 164.5 x 137.7 cm (64 3/4 x 54 3/16 in.); mounted: 255 x 166.6 cm (100 3/8 x 65 9/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Leonard C. Hanna Jr. Fund, 2025.138\n\nWithin “Faith and Image”, under “神圣人物”: Puts sacred figures back into a specific faith: face, gesture and halo first, doctrine second.", "note_html": "阿弥陀佛来迎图，1336年。东亚。绢本设色；Painting: 164.5 x 137.7 cm (64 3/4 x 54 3/16 in.); Mounted: 255 x 166.6 cm (100 3/8 x 65 9/16 in.)。\n\n把神圣形象放回具体信仰：先看脸、手势与光环，再读教义。"}, "cle-1968-206-1345": {"note": "圣母子登座，1345年。欧洲。蛋彩；Framed: 122.5 x 61 x 7.5 cm (48 1/4 x 24 x 2 15/16 in.); Unframed: 113.7 x 54 cm (44 3/4 x 21 1/4 in.)。\n\n把神圣形象放回具体信仰：先看脸、手势与光环，再读教义。", "note_en": "Madonna and Child Enthroned, c. 1350. Master of San Lucchese (Italian, c. 1335–1380). Tempera and gold on poplar panel; framed: 122.5 x 61 x 7.5 cm (48 1/4 x 24 x 2 15/16 in.); unframed: 113.7 x 54 cm (44 3/4 x 21 1/4 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Leonard C. Hanna Jr. Fund, 1968.206\n\nWithin “Faith and Image”, under “神圣人物”: Puts sacred figures back into a specific faith: face, gesture and halo first, doctrine second.", "note_html": "圣母子登座，1345年。欧洲。蛋彩；Framed: 122.5 x 61 x 7.5 cm (48 1/4 x 24 x 2 15/16 in.); Unframed: 113.7 x 54 cm (44 3/4 x 21 1/4 in.)。\n\n把神圣形象放回具体信仰：先看脸、手势与光环，再读教义。"}, "quails-and-sparrows-in-an-autumn-scene-1347": {"note": "这里的花鸟题材以工笔手法描绘，呼应了学院派的传统，但将惯常的彩色图像转化为纯粹的单色。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "The flower-and-bird subjects here are depicted in a meticulous manner, echoing the academic tradition but translating the customarily colored images to plain monochrome.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "这里的花鸟题材以工笔手法描绘，呼应了学院派的传统，但将惯常的彩色图像转化为纯粹的单色。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "huang-gongwang-summer-mountains-1350": {"note": "1290–1354，中国 元。黄公望的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。", "note_en": "1290–1354, China. 黄公望; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1992.1. This is a painting (绢本设色).", "note_html": "1290–1354，中国 元。黄公望的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。"}, "huang-gongwang-fuchun-1350": {"note": "黄公望在七十九岁开始创作《富春山居图》，历时数年完成。淡墨干笔描绘富春江畔的山峦、村落、松林和渔船；笔触松散，像重复呼吸的痕迹。群山不压，人水不喧；整幅画卷仿佛是一段漫长的漫步。\n\n清初，一位收藏家因随葬需将画卷焚毁。幸被救出后，画卷被分为两部分：前段《剩山图》收藏于浙江省博物馆；后段《无用师卷》收藏于台北故宫博物院。它的命运成为中国画史上最著名的“断简之美”。", "note_en": "Dwelling in the Fuchun Mountains was begun when Huang Gongwang was seventy-nine and completed over several years. Pale ink and dry brush describe mountains, villages, pine groves and fishing boats along the Fuchun River; the strokes are loose, like traces of repeated breathing. Mountains do not press, water does not clamour; the whole scroll is an extended walk.\n\nIn the early Qing, a collector had the scroll burned to accompany him in death. Rescued, it was split in two: the first section, Remaining Mountain, is in the Zhejiang Provincial Museum; the later section, the Wuyongshi scroll, is in the National Palace Museum, Taipei. Its fate became the most famous \"beauty of the fragment\" in Chinese painting.", "note_html": "黄公望在七十九岁开始创作《富春山居图》，历时数年完成。淡墨干笔描绘富春江畔的山峦、村落、松林和渔船；笔触松散，像重复呼吸的痕迹。群山不压，人水不喧；整幅画卷仿佛是一段漫长的漫步。\n\n清初，一位收藏家因随葬需将画卷焚毁。幸被救出后，画卷被分为两部分：前段《剩山图》收藏于浙江省博物馆；后段《无用师卷》收藏于台北故宫博物院。它的命运成为中国画史上最著名的“断简之美”。"}, "wang-meng-writing-books-1350": {"note": "c. 1308–1385，中国 元。王蒙的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。", "note_en": "c. 1308–1385, China. 王蒙; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1997.94. This is a painting (纸本设色).", "note_html": "c. 1308–1385，中国 元。王蒙的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。"}, "ni-zan-bamboo-rock-1350": {"note": "c. 1300s，中国 元。倪瓒的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。", "note_en": "c. 1300s, China. 倪瓒; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1978.65. This is a painting (纸本水墨).", "note_html": "c. 1300s，中国 元。倪瓒的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。"}, "cle-2009-342-2-1350": {"note": "释迦三尊：文殊与普贤，1350年。中国。绢本设色；Painting: 107 x 46.6 cm (42 1/8 x 18 3/8 in.); Overall with knobs: 192.4 x 66.7 cm (75 3/4 x 26 1/4 in.)。\n\n把神圣形象放回具体信仰：先看脸、手势与光环，再读教义。", "note_en": "Shakyamuni Triad: Buddha Attended by Manjushri and Samantabhadra (Buddha) (釋迦三尊：釋迦摩尼與文殊菩薩普賢菩薩), late 1300s. China, Fuzhou, Fujian Province, Yuan dynasty (1271-1368). Hanging scroll; ink and color on silk; painting: 107 x 46.6 cm (42 1/8 x 18 3/8 in.); overall with knobs: 192.4 x 66.7 cm (75 3/4 x 26 1/4 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Purchase from the J. H. Wade Fund, 2009.342.2\n\nWithin “Faith and Image”, under “神圣人物”: Puts sacred figures back into a specific faith: face, gesture and halo first, doctrine second.", "note_html": "释迦三尊：文殊与普贤，1350年。中国。绢本设色；Painting: 107 x 46.6 cm (42 1/8 x 18 3/8 in.); Overall with knobs: 192.4 x 66.7 cm (75 3/4 x 26 1/4 in.)。\n\n把神圣形象放回具体信仰：先看脸、手势与光环，再读教义。"}, "ni-zan-woods-valleys-1355": {"note": "《玉山林谷》是倪瓒典型的“一江两岸”构图：前景中几棵稀疏的树和一片岩石坡，中央是一片宽阔空旷的水面，远处是低矮的山丘。没有人，也没有船，只有简约的墨迹和一首诗。倪瓒用干笔侧锋，线条轻而粗糙，就像呼吸留在纸上的痕迹。\n\n这种极端的空旷不是不完整，而是他的选择：他把世界缩减到树、石、水和一条天际。晚元的动荡和一个人孤高的纯净都被压进了那个空白中。", "note_en": "Woods and Valleys of Mount Yu is Ni Zan's typical \"one river, two banks\" composition: a few sparse trees and a rocky slope in the foreground, a broad empty expanse of water in the middle, low hills in the distance. There are no people and no boats, only minimal ink and a poem. Ni Zan uses a dry side-tipped brush; lines are light and rough, like breath left on paper.\n\nThis extreme emptiness is not incompletion but choice: he reduces the world to trees, rock, water and a strip of sky. The turmoil of the late Yuan and one man's solitary purity are pressed into that void.", "note_html": "《玉山林谷》是倪瓒典型的“一江两岸”构图：前景中几棵稀疏的树和一片岩石坡，中央是一片宽阔空旷的水面，远处是低矮的山丘。没有人，也没有船，只有简约的墨迹和一首诗。倪瓒用干笔侧锋，线条轻而粗糙，就像呼吸留在纸上的痕迹。\n\n这种极端的空旷不是不完整，而是他的选择：他把世界缩减到树、石、水和一条天际。晚元的动荡和一个人孤高的纯净都被压进了那个空白中。"}, "cle-1950-374-1360": {"note": "《马里戈拉》鞭刑细密画，1360年。欧洲。蛋彩；Sheet: 29.5 x 21 cm (11 5/8 x 8 1/4 in.)。\n\n以极小尺度承载密集叙事，近看才有细节，远看才见结构。", "note_en": "Miniature from a Mariegola: The Flagellation, c. 1365–75. Lorenzo Veneziano (Italian), and Workshop. Tempera and gold on parchment; sheet: 29.5 x 21 cm (11 5/8 x 8 1/4 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Purchase from the J. H. Wade Fund, 1950.374\n\nWithin “Material and Technique”, under “细密画”: A tiny scale carries dense narrative: detail up close, structure from afar.", "note_html": "《马里戈拉》鞭刑细密画，1360年。欧洲。蛋彩；Sheet: 29.5 x 21 cm (11 5/8 x 8 1/4 in.)。\n\n以极小尺度承载密集叙事，近看才有细节，远看才见结构。"}, "the-woodcutter-of-luofu-1366": {"note": "这幅山水画展现了中国画的传统性：虽然笔法新颖，但构图仍以早期的宋代（960-1127年）范本为基础。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "This landscape illustrates the traditionalism of Chinese painting: while the brush manner is novel, the composition is based on early Song dynasty (960-1127) models.\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "这幅山水画展现了中国画的传统性：虽然笔法新颖，但构图仍以早期的宋代（960-1127年）范本为基础。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "landscape-in-the-style-of-juran-1368": {"note": "左下方的悬岩下有一处极小的伪造款识。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "There is a tiny apocryphal signature under the overhanging rocks on the lower left side.\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "左下方的悬岩下有一处极小的伪造款识。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "fan-shaped-album-painting-1368": {"note": "扇形册页画，1368–1644年。范宽（中国，活跃于约990–约 1030年左右）。绢本水墨设色；整体尺寸：27.9 x 23厘米（11 x 9 1/16英寸）。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "Fan-shaped Album Painting, 1368–1644. Copy after Fan Kuan (Chinese, active c. 990–c. 1030). Ink and slight color on silk; overall: 27.9 x 23 cm (11 x 9 1/16 in.).\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "扇形册页画，1368–1644年。范宽（中国，活跃于约990–约 1030年左右）。绢本水墨设色；整体尺寸：27.9 x 23厘米（11 x 9 1/16英寸）。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "narcissus-and-rocks-1368": {"note": "《兰石图》，1368–1644年。陆天枢（中国，15世纪上半叶）。绢本水墨立轴；整体尺寸：66.8 x 42.8厘米（26 5/16 x 16 7/8英寸）。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "Narcissus and Rocks (蘭石圖), 1368–1644. Lu Tianru (Chinese, first half of 1400s). Hanging scroll, ink on silk; overall: 66.8 x 42.8 cm (26 5/16 x 16 7/8 in.).\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "《兰石图》，1368–1644年。陆天枢（中国，15世纪上半叶）。绢本水墨立轴；整体尺寸：66.8 x 42.8厘米（26 5/16 x 16 7/8英寸）。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "leaping-carp-1368": {"note": "这幅作品以细腻的墨线和层次分明的晕染，栩栩如生地描绘了游动迅捷的鲤鱼，体现了明代宫廷画家刘珏作品的高超品质。\n\n日常场景把城市、室内或劳作变成画面。器物、动作与衣饰这些细节，比情节更能说明当时的生活秩序。", "note_en": "With a fine ink line and graded wash, the life-like depiction of these swiftly moving carp is representative of the high quality of works by Liu Jie, a Ming dynasty court painter k\n\nA scene of daily life turns a city, an interior or labour into a picture. Objects, actions and clothes tell us more about the order of life than the anecdote does.", "note_html": "这幅作品以细腻的墨线和层次分明的晕染，栩栩如生地描绘了游动迅捷的鲤鱼，体现了明代宫廷画家刘珏作品的高超品质。\n\n日常场景把城市、室内或劳作变成画面。器物、动作与衣饰这些细节，比情节更能说明当时的生活秩序。"}, "twenty-three-deity-nairatma-mandala-1370": {"note": "曼荼罗是觉悟众生世界的图示。这幅曼荼罗描绘的是无我（Nairatma）的宫殿，无我在中央起舞。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。", "note_en": "A mandala is a diagram of a realm of enlightened beings. This mandala depicts the palace of Nairatma, who dances in the center.\n\nThe work arranges sacred figures inside a legible composition: bodies, gestures, objects and borders prescribe the order of looking. Read the centre first, then the sides and the lower edge; the image becomes a reusable language of faith.", "note_html": "曼荼罗是觉悟众生世界的图示。这幅曼荼罗描绘的是无我（Nairatma）的宫殿，无我在中央起舞。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。"}, "cle-1924-1012-1370": {"note": "圣母子（唱经本首字母），1370年。欧洲。蛋彩；Sheet: 16 x 13 cm (6 5/16 x 5 1/8 in.)。\n\n把神圣形象放回具体信仰：先看脸、手势与光环，再读教义。", "note_en": "Initial S[alve sancta parens]  from a Gradual: Madonna and Child, c. 1370–74. Don Silvestro dei Gherarducci (Italian, 1339–1399). Ink, tempera, and gold on vellum; sheet: 16 x 13 cm (6 5/16 x 5 1/8 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift from J. H. Wade, 1924.1012\n\nWithin “Faith and Image”, under “神圣人物”: Puts sacred figures back into a specific faith: face, gesture and halo first, doctrine second.", "note_html": "圣母子（唱经本首字母），1370年。欧洲。蛋彩；Sheet: 16 x 13 cm (6 5/16 x 5 1/8 in.)。\n\n把神圣形象放回具体信仰：先看脸、手势与光环，再读教义。"}, "streams-and-mountains-1372": {"note": "与元末明初的许多文人一样，徐贲也深陷王朝更迭的动荡与仕途沉浮的困扰之中。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "Like many literati of the late Yuan and early Ming dynasties, Xu Ben was entangled with the perils of dynastic change as well as the ups and downs of his official career.\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "与元末明初的许多文人一样，徐贲也深陷王朝更迭的动荡与仕途沉浮的困扰之中。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "cle-1963-500-1375": {"note": "谦卑圣母，1375年。欧洲。蛋彩；Framed: 91.5 x 70 x 4 cm (36 x 27 9/16 x 1 9/16 in.); Unframed: 79.6 x 54.6 cm (31 5/16 x 21 1/2 in.)。\n\n把神圣形象放回具体信仰：先看脸、手势与光环，再读教义。", "note_en": "Madonna of Humility, late 1370s. Caterino Veneziano (Italian, active 1362–82). Tempera and gold on wood panel; framed: 91.5 x 70 x 4 cm (36 x 27 9/16 x 1 9/16 in.); unframed: 79.6 x 54.6 cm (31 5/16 x 21 1/2 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of Dr. Rudolf J. Heinemann, 1963.500\n\nWithin “Faith and Image”, under “神圣人物”: Puts sacred figures back into a specific faith: face, gesture and halo first, doctrine second.", "note_html": "谦卑圣母，1375年。欧洲。蛋彩；Framed: 91.5 x 70 x 4 cm (36 x 27 9/16 x 1 9/16 in.); Unframed: 79.6 x 54.6 cm (31 5/16 x 21 1/2 in.)。\n\n把神圣形象放回具体信仰：先看脸、手势与光环，再读教义。"}, "cle-1936-496-1395": {"note": "圣母之死，1395年。欧洲。油画；Image: 66 x 53.3 cm (26 x 21 in.); Framed: 74 x 61.5 x 4.5 cm (29 1/8 x 24 3/16 x 1 3/4 in.); Unframed: 71 x 54 cm (27 15/16 x 21 1/4 in.)。\n\n以遗体、葬礼与纪念物，把失去变成可共享的图像。", "note_en": "Death of the Virgin, c. 1400. Master of Heiligenkreuz (Austrian). Tempera and oil with gold on panel; image: 66 x 53.3 cm (26 x 21 in.); framed: 74 x 61.5 x 4.5 cm (29 1/8 x 24 3/16 x 1 3/4 in.); unframed: 71 x 54 cm (27 15/16 x 21 1/4 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of the Friends of The Cleveland Museum of Art in memory of John Long Severance, 1936.496\n\nWithin “Portrait and Self”, under “死亡与记忆”: Body, funeral and memorial turn loss into a shareable image.", "note_html": "圣母之死，1395年。欧洲。油画；Image: 66 x 53.3 cm (26 x 21 in.); Framed: 74 x 61.5 x 4.5 cm (29 1/8 x 24 3/16 x 1 3/4 in.); Unframed: 71 x 54 cm (27 15/16 x 21 1/4 in.)。\n\n以遗体、葬礼与纪念物，把失去变成可共享的图像。"}, "cle-1927-197-1400": {"note": "主教圣人与供养人，1400年。欧洲。蛋彩；Framed: 191.4 x 127.3 x 14 cm (75 3/8 x 50 1/8 x 5 1/2 in.); Painted surface: 171.5 x 107 cm (67 1/2 x 42 1/8 in.); Panel: 178 x 117.2 cm (70 1/16 x 46 1/8 in.)。\n\n把出资者放进神圣叙事，让信仰与社会位置同时可见。", "note_en": "A Bishop Saint with a Donor (Saint Louis of Toulouse?), early 1400s. Spain, Catalonia, early 15th century. Tempera with raised and gilded gesso on wood; framed: 191.4 x 127.3 x 14 cm (75 3/8 x 50 1/8 x 5 1/2 in.); painted surface: 171.5 x 107 cm (67 1/2 x 42 1/8 in.); panel: 178 x 117.2 cm (70 1/16 x 46 1/8 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of the Friends of The Cleveland Museum of Art, 1927.197\n\nWithin “Portrait and Self”, under “供养人”: Places the patron inside the sacred narrative, making faith and social position visible together.", "note_html": "主教圣人与供养人，1400年。欧洲。蛋彩；Framed: 191.4 x 127.3 x 14 cm (75 3/8 x 50 1/8 x 5 1/2 in.); Painted surface: 171.5 x 107 cm (67 1/2 x 42 1/8 in.); Panel: 178 x 117.2 cm (70 1/16 x 46 1/8 in.)。\n\n把出资者放进神圣叙事，让信仰与社会位置同时可见。"}, "a-hundred-birds-and-the-three-friends-1400": {"note": "在这幅挂轴中，鸟儿在松、竹、梅花（“岁寒三友”）之间栖息嬉戏。由于它们在冬季的耐寒性，它们象征着\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "In this hanging scroll birds rest and frolic among pines, bamboo, and flowering plum, plants known as “the three friends.” Due to their endurance in winter, they symbolize persever\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "在这幅挂轴中，鸟儿在松、竹、梅花（“岁寒三友”）之间栖息嬉戏。由于它们在冬季的耐寒性，它们象征着\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "cle-1985-132-1400": {"note": "藤袴物语场景，1400年。东亚。纸本水墨；Image: 16.2 x 33 cm (6 3/8 x 13 in.); Overall: 105.4 x 57.2 cm (41 1/2 x 22 1/2 in.)。\n\n从衣褶、发型与身体姿态，读出性别、阶层与时代。", "note_en": "Scene from the Tale of the Wisteria Robe (藤の衣物語絵巻断簡), 1400s. Japan, Muromachi period (1392–1573). Section of a handscroll mounted as a hanging scroll; ink on paper; image: 16.2 x 33 cm (6 3/8 x 13 in.); overall: 105.4 x 57.2 cm (41 1/2 x 22 1/2 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, John L. Severance Fund, 1985.132\n\nWithin “Portrait and Self”, under “身体与服饰”: Fold, hair and posture reveal gender, class and period.", "note_html": "藤袴物语场景，1400年。东亚。纸本水墨；Image: 16.2 x 33 cm (6 3/8 x 13 in.); Overall: 105.4 x 57.2 cm (41 1/2 x 22 1/2 in.)。\n\n从衣褶、发型与身体姿态，读出性别、阶层与时代。"}, "the-hermit-xu-you-resting-by-a-stream-1400": {"note": "许由是一位隐士，他拒绝了传说中的尧帝所赐的王位，而是选择在箕山耕田。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "Xu You, a recluse who refused the throne offered to him by legendary Emperor Yao, chose instead to farm on Mount Ji.\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "许由是一位隐士，他拒绝了传说中的尧帝所赐的王位，而是选择在箕山耕田。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "cle-2001-76-1420": {"note": "基督升天（时祷书叶），1420年。欧洲。蛋彩；Overall: 15.9 x 11.6 cm (6 1/4 x 4 9/16 in.)。\n\n用时钟、月份与雨季，把抽象时间落到日常动作上。", "note_en": "The Ascension: Leaf from a Book of Hours (4 of 6 Excised Leaves), c. 1420–30. Henri d'Orquevaulx (French), or Workshop. Ink, tempera, silver, and gold on vellum; overall: 15.9 x 11.6 cm (6 1/4 x 4 9/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, The Jeanne Miles Blackburn Collection, 2001.76\n\nWithin “City and Everyday Life”, under “时间与日常”: Clocks, months and rain turn abstract time into everyday action.", "note_html": "基督升天（时祷书叶），1420年。欧洲。蛋彩；Overall: 15.9 x 11.6 cm (6 1/4 x 4 9/16 in.)。\n\n用时钟、月份与雨季，把抽象时间落到日常动作上。"}, "cle-2010-154-1420": {"note": "慈悲圣母像，1420年。西亚·北非。蛋彩；Unframed: 96 x 70 cm (37 13/16 x 27 9/16 in.)。\n\n把图像放回它被使用、被围绕的空间，而不是只看单幅画面。", "note_en": "Icon of the Mother of God and Infant Christ (Virgin Eleousa), c. 1425–50. Attributed to Angelos Akotantos (Cretan, died 1450). Tempera and gold on wood; unframed: 96 x 70 cm (37 13/16 x 27 9/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Leonard C. Hanna Jr. Fund, 2010.154\n\nWithin “Faith and Image”, under “仪式空间”: Restores the image to the space where it was used and surrounded, not an isolated panel.", "note_html": "慈悲圣母像，1420年。西亚·北非。蛋彩；Unframed: 96 x 70 cm (37 13/16 x 27 9/16 in.)。\n\n把图像放回它被使用、被围绕的空间，而不是只看单幅画面。"}, "sleeping-bird-on-a-prunus-branch-1426": {"note": "《梅花喜鹊图》，15世纪。边文进（中国，约1354–1428）。册页；绢本水墨；整体尺寸：24.3 x 21厘米（9 9/16 x 8 1/4英寸）。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "Sleeping Bird on a Prunus Branch, 1400s. Bian Wenjin (Chinese, about 1354–1428). Album leaf; ink on silk; overall: 24.3 x 21 cm (9 9/16 x 8 1/4 in.).\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "《梅花喜鹊图》，15世纪。边文进（中国，约1354–1428）。册页；绢本水墨；整体尺寸：24.3 x 21厘米（9 9/16 x 8 1/4英寸）。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "cbl-per-119-3-1427": {"note": "《夜宴果园：诗人与友人》，1427年。中亚。纸本、墨、颜料与金箔；散页；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「中亚」区域页：《夜宴果园：诗人与友人》以1427年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。", "note_en": "The poet with his friends in the orchard at night, from Prince Baysunghur’s Rose Garden (Gulistan).  \nThe prologue of the Gulistan tells how one night the middle-aged poet was feeling anxious about his life's achievements so far, when his friend called in and began to cheer him up. They went out, and sat in another friend's orchard, enjoying the spring flowers and the night air. Heading home at dawn, Sa`di resolved (to his friend's delight) that he would write a book called the Rose Garden (Gulistan), with chapters on friendship, good conversation, happiness, youth and age, education, kingship and piety.  \nDetached folio, ink, pigments and gold on paper, Persian text in nasta`liq calligraphy, with blue and gold headings, illumination panels and full-page painting (on verso), calligraphy by Ja`far al-Baysunghuri, from a manuscript dedicated to Timurid prince Baysunghur, Herat, Afghanistan, dated 830H, 1427.\nSa`di (d.1290) of Shiraz is one of Iran's greatest classical poets. Pithy as well as ethical, the distinctive lines of the Rose Garden (Gulistan) combine prose tales (hikayat) with inserted poetry (bayt), and have been admired for centuries. This beautiful illustrated manuscript was produced in Herat, at the court of the Timurid prince Baysunghur (d. 1433), a renowned book-lover, art patron and bon vivant. The Persian text was copied out (and signed) by Baysunghur's head librarian, the master-calligrapher Farid al-Din Ja`far al-Tabrizi (known as Ja`far al-Baysunghuri). The illustrations and the illuminated panels are the work of several different court painters: Amir Khalil, Khwaja Ghiyathuddin, Khwaja Ata and Mawlana Shihab. Although they have not signed their work in this manuscript, a separate court document (written by Ja`far to prince Baysunghur, c. 1430) reported that these specific artists were currently finishing a copy of the Gulistan: for example Amir Khalil was completing \"two sea scenes of the Gulistan\", surely referring to the two such paintings in this manuscript (Per 119.15 and Per 119.29).\n\nBuilds the regional page for Central Asia: The poet with his friends in the orchard at night, from Prince Baysunghur's Rose Garden (Gulistan) by Sa`di enters at 1427 with a verifiable date and medium.", "note_html": "《夜宴果园：诗人与友人》，1427年。中亚。纸本、墨、颜料与金箔；散页；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「中亚」区域页：《夜宴果园：诗人与友人》以1427年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。"}, "cbl-per-119-14-1427": {"note": "《摔跤比赛：〈古丽斯坦〉插图》，1427年。中亚。纸本、墨、颜料与金箔；散页；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「中亚」区域页：《摔跤比赛：〈古丽斯坦〉插图》以1427年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。", "note_en": "The wrestling match, from Prince Baysunghur's Rose Garden (Gulistan) by Sa`di.  \nThe overconfident young wrestler challenges his teacher, and the king organises a match to settle the matter. Once on the field, the older man uses the one wrestling move he has never taught his student, and defeats him easily.  \nDetached folio, ink, pigments and gold on paper, Persian text in nasta`liq calligraphy, with gold headings, illumination panels and full-page painting (on recto), calligraphy by Ja`far al-Baysunghuri, from a manuscript dedicated to Timurid prince Baysunghur, Herat, Afghanistan, dated 830H, 1427.  \nSa`di (d.1290) of Shiraz is one of Iran's greatest classical poets. Pithy as well as ethical, the distinctive lines of the Rose Garden (Gulistan) combine prose tales (hikayat) with inserted poetry (bayt), and have been admired for centuries. This beautiful illustrated manuscript was produced in Herat, at the court of the Timurid prince Baysunghur (d. 1433), a renowned book-lover, art patron and bon vivant. The Persian text was copied out (and signed) by Baysunghur's head librarian, the master-calligrapher Farid al-Din Ja`far al-Tabrizi (known as Ja`far al-Baysunghuri). The illustrations and the illuminated panels are the work of several different court painters: Amir Khalil, Khwaja Ghiyathuddin, Khwaja Ata and Mawlana Shihab. Although they have not signed their work in this manuscript, a separate court document (written by Ja`far to prince Baysunghur, c. 1430) reported that these specific artists were currently finishing a copy of the Gulistan: for example Amir Khalil was completing \"two sea scenes of the Gulistan\", surely referring to the two such paintings in this manuscript (Per 119.15 and Per 119.29).\n\nBuilds the regional page for Central Asia: The wrestling match, from Prince Baysunghur's Rose Garden (Gulistan) by Sa`di. enters at 1427 with a verifiable date and medium.", "note_html": "《摔跤比赛：〈古丽斯坦〉插图》，1427年。中亚。纸本、墨、颜料与金箔；散页；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「中亚」区域页：《摔跤比赛：〈古丽斯坦〉插图》以1427年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。"}, "cbl-per-119-15-1427": {"note": "《海上获救：〈古丽斯坦〉插图》，1427年。中亚。纸本、墨、颜料与金箔；散页；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「中亚」区域页：《海上获救：〈古丽斯坦〉插图》以1427年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。", "note_en": "The rescue at sea, from Prince Baysunghur's Rose Garden (Gulistan) by Sa`di.  A sailor dived into the waters, sent to rescue two brothers after their ship has sunk. When he rescued one but not the other, it was revealed that he saved the man who once did him a good turn, and not the one who had whipped him as a child.  \nDetached folio, ink, pigments and gold on paper, Persian text in nasta`liq calligraphy, with gold headings, illumination panels and full-page painting (on verso), calligraphy by Ja`far al-Baysunghuri, painting by Amir Khalil, from a manuscript dedicated to Timurid prince Baysunghur, Herat, Afghanistan, dated 830H, 1427.  \nSa`di (d.1290) of Shiraz is one of Iran's greatest classical poets. Pithy as well as ethical, the distinctive lines of the Rose Garden (Gulistan) combine prose tales (hikayat) with inserted poetry (bayt), and have been admired for centuries. This beautiful illustrated manuscript was produced in Herat, at the court of the Timurid prince Baysunghur (d. 1433), a renowned book-lover, art patron and bon vivant. The Persian text was copied out (and signed) by Baysunghur's head librarian, the master-calligrapher Farid al-Din Ja`far al-Tabrizi (known as Ja`far al-Baysunghuri). The illustrations and the illuminated panels are the work of several different court painters: Amir Khalil, Khwaja Ghiyathuddin, Khwaja Ata and Mawlana Shihab. Although they have not signed their work in this manuscript, a separate court document (written by Ja`far to prince Baysunghur, c. 1430) reported that these specific artists were currently finishing a copy of the Gulistan: for example Amir Khalil was completing \"two sea scenes of the Gulistan\", surely referring to the two such paintings in this manuscript (Per 119.15 and Per 119.29).\n\nBuilds the regional page for Central Asia: The rescue at sea, from Prince Baysunghur's Rose Garden (Gulistan) by Sa`di enters at 1427 with a verifiable date and medium.", "note_html": "《海上获救：〈古丽斯坦〉插图》，1427年。中亚。纸本、墨、颜料与金箔；散页；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「中亚」区域页：《海上获救：〈古丽斯坦〉插图》以1427年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。"}, "cbl-per-119-36-1427": {"note": "《贵妇向萨迪奉上冷饮》，1427年。中亚。纸本、墨、颜料与金箔；散页；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「中亚」区域页：《贵妇向萨迪奉上冷饮》以1427年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。", "note_en": "A lady offers a cool drink to the poet, from Prince Baysunghur's Rose Garden (Gulistan) by Sa`di.  The poet recalled an extremely hot day in his youth, when he was walking down a street at noon, thirsty and weak. A beautiful woman came out of a house, and handed him an iced drink. Refreshed from his physical thirst, he found himself longing instead for the kind stranger.  \nDetached folio, ink, pigments and gold on paper, Persian text in nasta`liq calligraphy, with blue and gold headings, illumination panels and full-page painting (on verso), calligraphy by Ja`far al-Baysunghuri, from a manuscript dedicated to Timurid prince Baysunghur, Herat, Afghanistan, dated 830H, 1427.  \nSa`di (d.1291) of Shiraz is one of Iran's greatest classical poets. Pithy as well as ethical, the distinctive lines of the Rose Garden (Gulistan) combine prose tales (hikayat) with inserted poetry (bayt), and have been admired for centuries. This beautiful illustrated manuscript was produced in Herat, at the court of the Timurid prince Baysunghur (d. 1433), a renowned book-lover, art patron and bon vivant. The Persian text was copied out (and signed) by Baysunghur's head librarian, the master-calligrapher Farid al-Din Ja`far al-Tabrizi (known as Ja`far al-Baysunghuri). The illustrations and the illuminated panels are the work of several different court painters: Amir Khalil, Khwaja Ghiyathuddin, Khwaja Ata and Mawlana Shihab. Although they have not signed their work in this manuscript, a separate court document (written by Ja`far to prince Baysunghur, c. 1430) reported that these specific artists were currently finishing a copy of the Gulistan: for example Amir Khalil was completing \"two sea scenes of the Gulistan\", surely referring to the two such paintings in this manuscript (Per 119.15 and Per 119.29).\n\nBuilds the regional page for Central Asia: A lady offers a cool drink to the poet Sa'di, from Prince Baysunghur's Rose Garden (Gulistan) by Sa`di enters at 1427 with a verifiable date and medium.", "note_html": "《贵妇向萨迪奉上冷饮》，1427年。中亚。纸本、墨、颜料与金箔；散页；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「中亚」区域页：《贵妇向萨迪奉上冷饮》以1427年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。"}, "masaccio-expulsion-1427": {"note": "在佛罗伦萨的布兰恰奇礼拜堂，马萨乔把羞耻表现为身体的重量。亚当和夏娃赤裸，从右侧被驱赶出去；夏娃抬起头，张开嘴，手遮住私处，而亚当低下头，把脸藏在手臂后面，双脚踏在真实的阴影里。几乎没有背景景观，只有一个拱门和一小块地面，但解剖学、透视缩短和强烈的明暗对比让场景异常具体。\n\n它常被称为第一幅真正把人体置于中心的文艺复兴画作：天使的剑向外指去，但真正打动观众的是这两个人物找不到放手和脚的位置。马萨乔在三十岁前去世，但这幅壁画后来成为列奥纳多和米开朗基罗的回归之作。", "note_en": "In the Brancacci Chapel in Florence, Masaccio made shame a matter of bodily weight. Adam and Eve, naked, are driven out from the right; Eve lifts her head and opens her mouth, her hands covering her sex, while Adam bows and hides his face behind his arm, his feet planted in real shadow. There is almost no landscape, only an archway and a strip of ground, yet anatomy, foreshortening and strong chiaroscuro make the scene unusually concrete.\n\nIt is often called the first Renaissance image to place the human figure truly at its centre: the angel's sword points outward, but what pierces the viewer is the way the two figures can find nowhere to put their hands and feet. Masaccio died before he was thirty, yet this fresco became a point of return for Leonardo and Michelangelo after him.", "note_html": "在佛罗伦萨的布兰恰奇礼拜堂，马萨乔把羞耻表现为身体的重量。亚当和夏娃赤裸，从右侧被驱赶出去；夏娃抬起头，张开嘴，手遮住私处，而亚当低下头，把脸藏在手臂后面，双脚踏在真实的阴影里。几乎没有背景景观，只有一个拱门和一小块地面，但解剖学、透视缩短和强烈的明暗对比让场景异常具体。\n\n它常被称为第一幅真正把人体置于中心的文艺复兴画作：天使的剑向外指去，但真正打动观众的是这两个人物找不到放手和脚的位置。马萨乔在三十岁前去世，但这幅壁画后来成为列奥纳多和米开朗基罗的回归之作。"}, "van-eyck-arnolfini-1434": {"note": "扬·范·艾克把一个婚姻变成了一个密闭的房间。这对夫妇手牵手站在中央，女人把裙子拉在肚子上；光线从左上方照进来，黄铜吊灯、橘子、床幔、拖鞋以及脚边的小狗都被同等细致地描绘出来。在他们之间的后墙上挂着一面凸面镜，反射着房间和两位见证人；镜子上方的字写着“Johannes de eyck fuit hic”——扬·范·艾克在此。\n\n油画颜料被用到了极致：布料、金属和皮肤几乎可以触摸。关于这幅画是记录婚礼、订婚还是纪念，至今仍有争议；但可以确定的是，画家把自己也写进了这个私密空间。", "note_en": "Jan van Eyck turns a marriage into an airtight room. The couple stand hand in hand at the centre, the woman gathering her skirt over her belly; light falls from the upper left, and the brass chandelier, oranges, bed hangings, slippers and the dog at their feet are each rendered with equal attention. On the back wall between them hangs a convex mirror reflecting the room and two witnesses; above it, the inscription reads \"Johannes de eyck fuit hic\" — Jan van Eyck was here.\n\nOil paint is pushed to its limit: fabric, metal and skin seem almost tactile. Whether the image records a wedding, a betrothal or a memorial is still debated; what is certain is that the painter has written himself into this private space.", "note_html": "扬·范·艾克把一个婚姻变成了一个密闭的房间。这对夫妇手牵手站在中央，女人把裙子拉在肚子上；光线从左上方照进来，黄铜吊灯、橘子、床幔、拖鞋以及脚边的小狗都被同等细致地描绘出来。在他们之间的后墙上挂着一面凸面镜，反射着房间和两位见证人；镜子上方的字写着“Johannes de eyck fuit hic”——扬·范·艾克在此。\n\n油画颜料被用到了极致：布料、金属和皮肤几乎可以触摸。关于这幅画是记录婚礼、订婚还是纪念，至今仍有争议；但可以确定的是，画家把自己也写进了这个私密空间。"}, "weyden-descent-from-cross-1435": {"note": "罗吉耶·范·德·魏登把下十字架的场景压缩在一个浅浅的金色盒子里。基督的身体像弓一样弯曲，几乎与昏倒的圣母平行；亚利马太的约瑟和尼哥底母支撑着他的手臂和腿，约翰在右边哭泣，抹大拉的马利亚拧着手。人物被安排在浮雕般的空间里，每一滴泪水、衣褶和伤口都画得锐利入画。\n\n这一构图将悲伤表现到极致，成为北方文艺复兴宗教绘画的范本。它不追求深远的空间感；它不给观者退路，只留下正视哀悼的责任。", "note_en": "Rogier van der Weyden compresses the descent from the cross into a shallow golden box. Christ's body curves like a bow, almost parallel to the swooning Virgin; Joseph of Arimathea and Nicodemus support his arms and legs, John weeps on the right, and Mary Magdalene wrings her hands. The figures are arranged in a relief-like enclosure, every tear, fold and wound drawn with a cutting edge.\n\nThis composition, which pushes grief to an extreme, became a model for religious painting in the Northern Renaissance. It does not seek deep space; it leaves the viewer no exit, only the obligation to face the mourning head-on.", "note_html": "罗吉耶·范·德·魏登把下十字架的场景压缩在一个浅浅的金色盒子里。基督的身体像弓一样弯曲，几乎与昏倒的圣母平行；亚利马太的约瑟和尼哥底母支撑着他的手臂和腿，约翰在右边哭泣，抹大拉的马利亚拧着手。人物被安排在浮雕般的空间里，每一滴泪水、衣褶和伤口都画得锐利入画。\n\n这一构图将悲伤表现到极致，成为北方文艺复兴宗教绘画的范本。它不追求深远的空间感；它不给观者退路，只留下正视哀悼的责任。"}, "cle-2011-59-1435": {"note": "时祷书圣雅各叶，1435年。欧洲。蛋彩；Leaf: 14.9 x 11.2 cm (5 7/8 x 4 7/16 in.)。\n\n让金光参与构图，材料本身承担神圣性与奢华感。", "note_en": "Leaf from a Book of Hours: Saint James the Greater, c. 1440–1450. Master of the Gold Scrolls (Belgian). Ink, tempera and gold on vellum; leaf: 14.9 x 11.2 cm (5 7/8 x 4 7/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, The Jeanne Miles Blackburn Collection, 2011.59\n\nWithin “Material and Technique”, under “金箔”: Gold participates in composition; material carries sanctity and luxury.", "note_html": "时祷书圣雅各叶，1435年。欧洲。蛋彩；Leaf: 14.9 x 11.2 cm (5 7/8 x 4 7/16 in.)。\n\n让金光参与构图，材料本身承担神圣性与奢华感。"}, "cle-1999-212-1440": {"note": "福音书圣路加像单叶，1440年。撒哈拉以南非洲。蛋彩；Sheet: 37 x 25 cm (14 9/16 x 9 13/16 in.)。\n\n让抄写、插图与装帧互相解释，书是一件被使用的整体。", "note_en": "Single Leaf from a Gospel Book with a  Portrait of Saint Luke, c. 1440–80. Empire of Ethiopia, Tigray region (Ethiopia). Ink and tempera on vellum; sheet: 37 x 25 cm (14 9/16 x 9 13/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Purchase from the J. H. Wade Fund, 1999.212\n\nWithin “Word and Looking”, under “手抄本”: Writing, illumination and binding explain one another; the book is a used object.", "note_html": "福音书圣路加像单叶，1440年。撒哈拉以南非洲。蛋彩；Sheet: 37 x 25 cm (14 9/16 x 9 13/16 in.)。\n\n让抄写、插图与装帧互相解释，书是一件被使用的整体。"}, "birds-and-flowers-1440": {"note": "这是两幅可能出自雪舟等杨之手的画作之一。它们曾与一幅描绘水墨山水的中央卷轴并列。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "This is one of two paintings possibly by Sesshū Tōyō. They once flanked a central scroll with an ink landscape.\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "这是两幅可能出自雪舟等杨之手的画作之一。它们曾与一幅描绘水墨山水的中央卷轴并列。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "four-seated-masters-1445": {"note": "这幅画中描绘了西藏佛教萨迦派的创始人和著名大师，他们是传承其知识的传承上师的一部分。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "Founders and prominent masters of the Sakya order of Buddhism in Tibet are featured in this painting as part of the lineage of teachers who transmitted knowledge of their fundament\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "这幅画中描绘了西藏佛教萨迦派的创始人和著名大师，他们是传承其知识的传承上师的一部分。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "the-haven-of-the-peach-blossom-spring-1445": {"note": "这幅小品画的灵感源自《桃花源记》，描绘了隐士诗人陶渊明（公元365–427年）所著的著名故事，故事中一位渔夫\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "A miniature inspired by the “Peach Blossom Spring,” this painting illustrates the well-known tale written by the poet-recluse Tao Yuanming (365–427 CE), in which a fisherman accide\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "这幅小品画的灵感源自《桃花源记》，描绘了隐士诗人陶渊明（公元365–427年）所著的著名故事，故事中一位渔夫\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "vajradhara-nairatmya-and-mahasiddhas-virupa-and-kanha-1445": {"note": "这幅画是描绘传承成佛之道教义的大师系列画作中的第一幅，从左上角的深蓝色金刚手开始，\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "The first in a series depicting the masters who transmitted the teachings on how to reach enlightenment, this painting begins at the upper left with the dark blue Vajradhara, who r\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "这幅画是描绘传承成佛之道教义的大师系列画作中的第一幅，从左上角的深蓝色金刚手开始，\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "landscape-of-the-four-seasons-1450": {"note": "李松云被认为是于1424年20岁时移居日本的朝鲜画家。这对屏风是艺术家在这方面最重要的作品。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "Yi Sumun is believed to have been a Korean painter who migrated to Japan in 1424 at the age of 20. This pair of screens is the artist’s most important composition in this format.\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "李松云被认为是于1424年20岁时移居日本的朝鲜画家。这对屏风是艺术家在这方面最重要的作品。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "cle-1944-490-b-1450": {"note": "波斯诗句书法（另面），1450年。西亚·北非。纸本设色；。\n\n把笔迹、留白与边框当成图像，阅读节奏就是视觉节奏。", "note_en": "Calligraphy, Persian Verses (verso), 1400s. Iran, Timurid period (1370-1501). Opaque watercolor, ink, and gold on paper. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Edward L. Whittemore Fund, 1944.490.b\n\nWithin “Word and Looking”, under “书法”: Hand, blank space and border are image; reading rhythm is visual rhythm.", "note_html": "波斯诗句书法（另面），1450年。西亚·北非。纸本设色；。\n\n把笔迹、留白与边框当成图像，阅读节奏就是视觉节奏。"}, "cle-1947-70-1455": {"note": "圣司提反葬礼，1455年。欧洲。手抄本；Sheet: 24.9 x 19.3 cm (9 13/16 x 7 5/8 in.); Secondary Support: 24.9 x 19.3 cm (9 13/16 x 7 5/8 in.)。\n\n以遗体、葬礼与纪念物，把失去变成可共享的图像。", "note_en": "The Funeral of Saint Stephen, c. 1460. Fra Filippo Lippi (Italian, c. 1406–1469). Pen and brown ink with brush and brown wash with traces of stylus over traces of black chalk; sheet: 24.9 x 19.3 cm (9 13/16 x 7 5/8 in.); secondary support: 24.9 x 19.3 cm (9 13/16 x 7 5/8 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, John L. Severance Fund, 1947.70\n\nWithin “Portrait and Self”, under “死亡与记忆”: Body, funeral and memorial turn loss into a shareable image.", "note_html": "圣司提反葬礼，1455年。欧洲。手抄本；Sheet: 24.9 x 19.3 cm (9 13/16 x 7 5/8 in.); Secondary Support: 24.9 x 19.3 cm (9 13/16 x 7 5/8 in.)。\n\n以遗体、葬礼与纪念物，把失去变成可共享的图像。"}, "cle-1964-150-1458": {"note": "三联板：天使长米迦勒与圣安东尼，1458年。欧洲。蛋彩；Framed: 94 x 40 x 6.5 cm (37 x 15 3/4 x 2 9/16 in.); Unframed: 81.3 x 29.8 x 3 cm (32 x 11 3/4 x 1 3/16 in.)。\n\n把木纹、拼缝与颜料层一起看成画面的一部分。", "note_en": "Pair of Panels from a Triptych: The Archangel Michael and St. Anthony Abbot, 1458. Fra Filippo Lippi (Italian, c. 1406–1469). Tempera on wood panel; framed: 94 x 40 x 6.5 cm (37 x 15 3/4 x 2 9/16 in.); unframed: 81.3 x 29.8 x 3 cm (32 x 11 3/4 x 1 3/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Leonard C. Hanna Jr. Fund, 1964.150\n\nWithin “Material and Technique”, under “木板”: Grain, joins and paint layers are part of the picture.", "note_html": "三联板：天使长米迦勒与圣安东尼，1458年。欧洲。蛋彩；Framed: 94 x 40 x 6.5 cm (37 x 15 3/4 x 2 9/16 in.); Unframed: 81.3 x 29.8 x 3 cm (32 x 11 3/4 x 1 3/16 in.)。\n\n把木纹、拼缝与颜料层一起看成画面的一部分。"}, "tarocchi-luna-1460": {"note": "卢娜手持新月、驾双马战车越过地景；这是前望远镜时代对月亮的图像化理解。\n\n在「山水与自然」的「太空」线索里，月亮被写成驾车穿越天空的女神，夜空有了可叙述的角色。", "note_en": "before 1467, Europe. E 系列塔罗奇大师; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1924.432.41. This is a print (铜版画).", "note_html": "卢娜手持新月、驾双马战车越过地景；这是前望远镜时代对月亮的图像化理解。\n\n在「山水与自然」的「太空」线索里，月亮被写成驾车穿越天空的女神，夜空有了可叙述的角色。"}, "tarocchi-mercury-1460": {"note": "墨丘利以赫尔墨斯形象出现：翼帽、翼鞋、蛇杖与公鸡，把水星放进可辨认的神话叙事。\n\n在「山水与自然」的「太空」线索里，行星不是抽象点，而是带着信使身份、动物与器物的完整人物。", "note_en": "before 1467, Europe. E 系列塔罗奇大师; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1924.432.42. This is a print (铜版画).", "note_html": "墨丘利以赫尔墨斯形象出现：翼帽、翼鞋、蛇杖与公鸡，把水星放进可辨认的神话叙事。\n\n在「山水与自然」的「太空」线索里，行星不是抽象点，而是带着信使身份、动物与器物的完整人物。"}, "budai-1460": {"note": "禅僧宗难悦哲被记载为京都东山�ō福寺的第183任住持，该寺是日本最早、最有影响力的禅宗寺院之一。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。", "note_en": "The Zen monk Jonan Etetsu is recorded as the 183rd abbot of Tō fuku-ji temple in the eastern hills of Kyoto, one of the earliest and most influential Zen institutions in medieval J\n\nThe work arranges sacred figures inside a legible composition: bodies, gestures, objects and borders prescribe the order of looking. Read the centre first, then the sides and the lower edge; the image becomes a reusable language of faith.", "note_html": "禅僧宗难悦哲被记载为京都东山�ō福寺的第183任住持，该寺是日本最早、最有影响力的禅宗寺院之一。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。"}, "emperor-minghuang-teaching-yang-gueifei-to-play-the-flute-1460": {"note": "唐朝（618-906）的著名皇帝明皇及其妃子杨贵妃，在中国后来的文化中激发了许多传奇、绘画和诗歌。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "Minghuang, a prominent emperor of Tang (618-906) China and his consort, Yang Gueifei, have inspired many legends, paintings, and poetry in later Chinese culture.\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "唐朝（618-906）的著名皇帝明皇及其妃子杨贵妃，在中国后来的文化中激发了许多传奇、绘画和诗歌。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "the-poet-lin-bu-wandering-in-the-moonlight-1460": {"note": "林逋（967–1028）是北宋（960–1127）时期的一位诗人兼隐士，隐居于杭州西湖，以梅为妻，以鹤为友。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "Lin Bu (967–1028), a Northern Song (960–1127) poet and hermit who lived at the West Lake in Hangzhou, was known for having plum trees for his female companions and cranes for his c\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "林逋（967–1028）是北宋（960–1127）时期的一位诗人兼隐士，隐居于杭州西湖，以梅为妻，以鹤为友。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "tarocchi-jupiter-1460": {"note": "朱庇特戴冠、坐在双彩虹上，鹰与孩童分列上下；周围地景躺倒的士兵提示行星之下的命运。\n\n在「山水与自然」的「太空」线索里，木星坐在双彩虹与杏仁形光环里，权力、天空与死亡同处一图。", "note_en": "before 1467, Europe. E 系列塔罗奇大师; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1924.432.46. This is a print (铜版画).", "note_html": "朱庇特戴冠、坐在双彩虹上，鹰与孩童分列上下；周围地景躺倒的士兵提示行星之下的命运。\n\n在「山水与自然」的「太空」线索里，木星坐在双彩虹与杏仁形光环里，权力、天空与死亡同处一图。"}, "kingfisher-perched-above-a-stream-1460": {"note": "《栖息在溪流上方的翠鸟》是东亚 late 1400s 的一件纸本水墨作品，现藏于克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以视觉经验为主题，适合放在“早期绘画”这条线索里看。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "Kingfisher Perched above a Stream, late 1400s. Kenkō Shōkei (Japanese, active 1478–1506).\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "《栖息在溪流上方的翠鸟》是东亚 late 1400s 的一件纸本水墨作品，现藏于克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以视觉经验为主题，适合放在“早期绘画”这条线索里看。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "tarocchi-mars-1460": {"note": "玛尔斯坐在战车式宝座上，盔甲、剑与狼把火星固定为战争与冲突的化身。\n\n在「山水与自然」的「太空」线索里，火星是披甲、持剑、带着狼的战士，行星被写成性格。", "note_en": "before 1467, Europe. E 系列塔罗奇大师; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1924.432.45. This is a print (铜版画).", "note_html": "玛尔斯坐在战车式宝座上，盔甲、剑与狼把火星固定为战争与冲突的化身。\n\n在「山水与自然」的「太空」线索里，火星是披甲、持剑、带着狼的战士，行星被写成性格。"}, "tarocchi-sun-1460": {"note": "塔罗奇《天球》系列把古典天文学的七颗行星人格化；太阳乘四马战车，越过想象的地景。\n\n在「山水与自然」的「太空」线索里，把太阳人格化为驾车的神，天球因此成为一张可读的图像。", "note_en": "before 1467, Europe. E 系列塔罗奇大师; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1924.432.44. This is a print (铜版画).", "note_html": "塔罗奇《天球》系列把古典天文学的七颗行星人格化；太阳乘四马战车，越过想象的地景。\n\n在「山水与自然」的「太空」线索里，把太阳人格化为驾车的神，天球因此成为一张可读的图像。"}, "tarocchi-venus-1460": {"note": "维纳斯在河水中沐浴，丘比特与三美神围绕；天文学图像同时承担道德与神话解释。\n\n在「山水与自然」的「太空」线索里，金星被写成沐浴的女神，行星与爱欲、自然和神话绑在一起。", "note_en": "before 1467, Europe. E 系列塔罗奇大师; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1924.432.43. This is a print (铜版画).", "note_html": "维纳斯在河水中沐浴，丘比特与三美神围绕；天文学图像同时承担道德与神话解释。\n\n在「山水与自然」的「太空」线索里，金星被写成沐浴的女神，行星与爱欲、自然和神话绑在一起。"}, "shen-zhou-loft-mount-lu-1467": {"note": "高耸的庐山是沈周为他的老师陈寬七十岁生日所画的。山几乎高出画面的顶端，用麻织纹理的笔触和由深到淡的墨色描绘；山脚下有一条溪流、几棵松树和一个仰望瀑布的人。右侧题款说明这幅画是为老师的生日所作。\n\n沈周把庐山作为知识和美德的象征，而不仅仅是风景。吴门画派的文人趣味在这里体现为温和却坚定的秩序：山高、水长、人小——但仍在凝视。", "note_en": "Lofty Mount Lu was painted by Shen Zhou for his teacher Chen Kuan's seventieth birthday. The mountain rises almost beyond the top of the picture, built with hemp-fibre texture strokes and ink graded from dark to pale; at its foot are a stream, pines and a figure gazing up at a waterfall. The inscription at the right states that the painting is for a teacher's birthday.\n\nShen Zhou makes Mount Lu a symbol of knowledge and virtue, not merely scenery. The literati taste of the Wu School appears here as a gentle but firm order: mountain high, water long, person small — but still looking.", "note_html": "高耸的庐山是沈周为他的老师陈寬七十岁生日所画的。山几乎高出画面的顶端，用麻织纹理的笔触和由深到淡的墨色描绘；山脚下有一条溪流、几棵松树和一个仰望瀑布的人。右侧题款说明这幅画是为老师的生日所作。\n\n沈周把庐山作为知识和美德的象征，而不仅仅是风景。吴门画派的文人趣味在这里体现为温和却坚定的秩序：山高、水长、人小——但仍在凝视。"}, "cle-1932-119-1470": {"note": "《劫波经》抄本与二十四幅插图，1470年。南亚。蛋彩；Overall: 12.5 x 25.7 cm (4 15/16 x 10 1/8 in.)。\n\n让抄写、插图与装帧互相解释，书是一件被使用的整体。", "note_en": "Kalpa-sutra manuscript with 24 illuminations, c. 1475–1500. Western India, Gujarat. Gum tempera, ink, and gold on paper; overall: 12.5 x 25.7 cm (4 15/16 x 10 1/8 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Edward L. Whittemore Fund, 1932.119\n\nWithin “Word and Looking”, under “手抄本”: Writing, illumination and binding explain one another; the book is a used object.", "note_html": "《劫波经》抄本与二十四幅插图，1470年。南亚。蛋彩；Overall: 12.5 x 25.7 cm (4 15/16 x 10 1/8 in.)。\n\n让抄写、插图与装帧互相解释，书是一件被使用的整体。"}, "hotei-1475": {"note": "布袋和尚是一位半传奇人物，可能生活在9世纪末至10世纪初。后来，他在禅宗（日语：禅）佛教文献中声名鹊起。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "Hotei is a semilegendary figure who may have lived from the late 800s to the early 900s. He later became prominent in Chan (Japanese: Zen) Buddhist literature.\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "布袋和尚是一位半传奇人物，可能生活在9世纪末至10世纪初。后来，他在禅宗（日语：禅）佛教文献中声名鹊起。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "river-village-in-a-rainstorm-1475": {"note": "在这个场景中，狂风暴雨肆虐村庄，巧妙的构图捕捉到了大自然的力量。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "In this scene, windswept rain pelting a village captures the power of nature in a masterful composition.\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "在这个场景中，狂风暴雨肆虐村庄，巧妙的构图捕捉到了大自然的力量。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "cle-1944-490-1475": {"note": "皇家营地外景与波斯书法（双页左幅），1475年。中亚。纸本设色；。\n\n把笔迹、留白与边框当成图像，阅读节奏就是视觉节奏。", "note_en": "Left side of a double-page album folio: Outside a Royal Encampment (recto) and Calligraphy, Persian Verses (verso), c. 1485. Style of Bihzad (Iranian, active 1470–1506). Opaque watercolor, ink, and gold on paper. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Edward L. Whittemore Fund, 1944.490\n\nWithin “Word and Looking”, under “书法”: Hand, blank space and border are image; reading rhythm is visual rhythm.", "note_html": "皇家营地外景与波斯书法（双页左幅），1475年。中亚。纸本设色；。\n\n把笔迹、留白与边框当成图像，阅读节奏就是视觉节奏。"}, "chinese-literatus-in-an-autumn-landscape-1475": {"note": "在这幅画中，雪舟等杨的弟子宗恩描绘了一位骑在驴背上的中国士大夫，其随从跟在身后。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "In this painting, Sesshū Tōyō’s disciple Sōen depicts a Chinese scholar-official astride a donkey with his attendant behind.\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "在这幅画中，雪舟等杨的弟子宗恩描绘了一位骑在驴背上的中国士大夫，其随从跟在身后。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "portrait-of-pope-sixtus-iv-della-rovere-1476": {"note": "西班牙艺术家佩德罗·贝鲁盖特（Pedro Berruguete）在1470年代和1480年代在意大利度过了十年，其中有一段时间是在罗马度过的，他在这段时间里为教宗西斯笃四世·德拉·罗韦雷（Sixtus IV della Rovere）画了肖像。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "Spanish artist Pedro Berruguete spent a decade in Italy in the 1470s and 1480s, including a period in Rome during which he painted Pope Sixtus IV della Rovere from life.\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "西班牙艺术家佩德罗·贝鲁盖特（Pedro Berruguete）在1470年代和1480年代在意大利度过了十年，其中有一段时间是在罗马度过的，他在这段时间里为教宗西斯笃四世·德拉·罗韦雷（Sixtus IV della Rovere）画了肖像。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "view-of-xiao-xiang-1478": {"note": "这幅画描绘了著名的“潇湘八景”主题。我们收藏的其他画作中也有描绘这一主题的作品。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "This scene illustrates the famous theme of Eight Views of the Xiao-Xiang River. This subject is also depicted in other paintings in our collection.\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "这幅画描绘了著名的“潇湘八景”主题。我们收藏的其他画作中也有描绘这一主题的作品。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "botticelli-primavera-1480": {"note": "《春》像一个半开的剧院在慢慢展开。在右边，西风追逐仙女，弗洛拉在画面上撒满鲜花；中央，维纳斯举手祝福，蒙眼的丘比特瞄准她的上方；左边，三美神成圈起舞，而墨丘利背对着我们站在远端。橘树把深色的背景围住，草地上点缀着成百上千种可以辨认的花朵。\n\n波提切利把异教神话、春天的寓意和美第奇宫廷的审美融入到一幅横向叙事画中。画面没有一个中心焦点，但目光、动作和衣饰的节奏把整个构图紧密联系起来。与《维纳斯的诞生》一起，它构成了文艺复兴时期对古代神话最完整、最优雅的诠释。", "note_en": "Primavera unfolds like a half-open theatre. On the right, Zephyr pursues a nymph and Flora scatters flowers across the panel; at the centre Venus raises a hand in blessing while blindfolded Cupid aims above her; on the left the Three Graces dance in a ring, with Mercury, his back to us, at the far edge. Orange trees close the dark background, and the grass is studded with hundreds of identifiable flowers.\n\nBotticelli braids pagan myth, spring allegory and Medici court taste into a single horizontal narrative. There is no central focus, yet gaze, gesture and the rhythm of drapery hold the composition together. With The Birth of Venus, it forms the Renaissance's most complete and elegant translation of ancient myth.", "note_html": "《春》像一个半开的剧院在慢慢展开。在右边，西风追逐仙女，弗洛拉在画面上撒满鲜花；中央，维纳斯举手祝福，蒙眼的丘比特瞄准她的上方；左边，三美神成圈起舞，而墨丘利背对着我们站在远端。橘树把深色的背景围住，草地上点缀着成百上千种可以辨认的花朵。\n\n波提切利把异教神话、春天的寓意和美第奇宫廷的审美融入到一幅横向叙事画中。画面没有一个中心焦点，但目光、动作和衣饰的节奏把整个构图紧密联系起来。与《维纳斯的诞生》一起，它构成了文艺复兴时期对古代神话最完整、最优雅的诠释。"}, "portrait-of-a-youth-as-saint-sebastian-1485": {"note": "塞巴斯蒂安是古罗马皇帝戴克里先的侍卫，因信仰基督教而被射箭，最终被淹死。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。", "note_en": "Sebastian, a bodyguard for the ancient Roman emperor Diocletian, was shot with arrows and was eventually drowned for his commitment to Christianity.\n\nThe work arranges sacred figures inside a legible composition: bodies, gestures, objects and borders prescribe the order of looking. Read the centre first, then the sides and the lower edge; the image becomes a reusable language of faith.", "note_html": "塞巴斯蒂安是古罗马皇帝戴克里先的侍卫，因信仰基督教而被射箭，最终被淹死。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。"}, "portrait-of-a-woman-possibly-a-novice-of-san-secondo-1485": {"note": "最近，学者们推测，这幅作品实际上描绘的并不是修女，尽管自1543年以来它一直被描述为修女像。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "Scholars have recently speculated that this work does not actually depict a nun, although it has been described as such since 1543.\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "最近，学者们推测，这幅作品实际上描绘的并不是修女，尽管自1543年以来它一直被描述为修女像。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "botticelli-birth-of-venus-1485": {"note": "维纳斯站在巨大的贝壳上从海中升起，被西风和一位微风女神吹到岸边，而一位时辰女神正等着，手里拿着一件绣着花纹的披肩。波提切利摒弃了中世纪的金色背景，让海水和岸边融入淡蓝和绿色；女神的重量偏向右边，她的头发和衣裳被吹成连续的曲线。解剖学规则被打破：身体被拉长和倾斜，轮廓像雕刻浮雕一样清晰。\n\n这种“非正确的优雅”就是早期文艺复兴时期的理想美，比例来自诗意而非测量。这幅画属于美第奇家族收藏，把异教神话带进了佛罗伦萨的居室，同时也是西方艺术中最常被复制的美的形象之一。", "note_en": "Venus rises from the sea on a vast shell, blown ashore by Zephyr and a breeze goddess, while one of the Horae waits with an embroidered mantle. Botticelli abandons the medieval gold ground and lets sea and shore dissolve into pale blue and green; the goddess's weight sits to the right, her hair and drapery blown into continuous curves. Anatomy is not obeyed: the body is stretched and tilted, its outline as crisp as a carved relief.\n\nThis \"incorrect elegance\" is the ideal beauty of the early Renaissance, proportion derived from poetry rather than measurement. The panel belonged to the Medici collection, carried pagan myth into Florentine rooms, and remains one of the most reproduced images of beauty in Western art.", "note_html": "维纳斯站在巨大的贝壳上从海中升起，被西风和一位微风女神吹到岸边，而一位时辰女神正等着，手里拿着一件绣着花纹的披肩。波提切利摒弃了中世纪的金色背景，让海水和岸边融入淡蓝和绿色；女神的重量偏向右边，她的头发和衣裳被吹成连续的曲线。解剖学规则被打破：身体被拉长和倾斜，轮廓像雕刻浮雕一样清晰。\n\n这种“非正确的优雅”就是早期文艺复兴时期的理想美，比例来自诗意而非测量。这幅画属于美第奇家族收藏，把异教神话带进了佛罗伦萨的居室，同时也是西方艺术中最常被复制的美的形象之一。"}, "cle-1932-227-1488": {"note": "圣家族与施洗约翰、圣玛格丽特，1488年。欧洲。木板油画；Framed: 184 x 186 x 9.5 cm (72 7/16 x 73 1/4 x 3 3/4 in.); Diameter: 153 cm (60 1/4 in.)。\n\n把神圣形象放回具体信仰：先看脸、手势与光环，再读教义。", "note_en": "The Holy Family with Saint John the Baptist and Saint Margaret, c. 1488–93. Filippino Lippi (Italian, c. 1457–1504). Tempera and oil on wood; framed: 184 x 186 x 9.5 cm (72 7/16 x 73 1/4 x 3 3/4 in.); diameter: 153 cm (60 1/4 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, The Delia E. Holden Fund and a fund donated as a memorial to Mrs. Holden by her children: Guerdon S. Holden, Delia Holden White, Roberta Holden Bole, Emery Holden Greenough, Gertrude Holden McGinley, 1932.227\n\nWithin “Faith and Image”, under “神圣人物”: Puts sacred figures back into a specific faith: face, gesture and halo first, doctrine second.", "note_html": "圣家族与施洗约翰、圣玛格丽特，1488年。欧洲。木板油画；Framed: 184 x 186 x 9.5 cm (72 7/16 x 73 1/4 x 3 3/4 in.); Diameter: 153 cm (60 1/4 in.)。\n\n把神圣形象放回具体信仰：先看脸、手势与光环，再读教义。"}, "ink-plum-1488": {"note": "描绘早春盛开的梅树等应季绘画作品，被用于装饰文人的书房或宅邸内的其他室内空间。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "Seasonal paintings, including those depicting flowering plum trees in early spring, furnished scholars’ studios or other interior spaces in the house.\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "描绘早春盛开的梅树等应季绘画作品，被用于装饰文人的书房或宅邸内的其他室内空间。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "inp-voronet-1488": {"note": "《沃罗内茨修道院：最后的审判》，1488年。欧洲。湿壁画（外墙）；壁画现场；照片像素见图像著录。\n\n补足「欧洲」区域页：《沃罗内茨修道院：最后的审判》以1488年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。", "note_en": "Mânăstirea Voroneț, denumită și \"Capela Sixtină a Estului\", se află la 36 de km de municipiul Suceava. Este una dintre cele mai valoroase ctitorii ale domnitorului Moldovei, Ștefan cel Mare, tocmai prin frescele care îmbracă fațadele, în culori vii de albastru și verde. Pe fațada vestică a mânăstirii, se regăsește Judecata de apoi, a adevărată sinteză a Apocalipsei Sf. Ioan Teologul, într-un tablou alcătuit din patru registre dispuse orizontal. Pentru mai multe detalii asupra mânăstirii, inclusă în patrimoniul UNESCO, dar și asupra artei religioase, accesați link-uri: https://doxologia.ro/judecata-de-apoi-surprinsa-detaliu-la-manastirea-voronet; https://www.manastireavoronet.ro/prezentare-generala-manastirea-voronet/.\n\nBuilds the regional page for Europe: Biserica Voroneț (sec XV) - Fresca: Judecata de apoi enters at 1488 with a verifiable date and medium.", "note_html": "《沃罗内茨修道院：最后的审判》，1488年。欧洲。湿壁画（外墙）；壁画现场；照片像素见图像著录。\n\n补足「欧洲」区域页：《沃罗内茨修道院：最后的审判》以1488年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。"}, "water-moon-kannon-1490": {"note": "这幅画描绘的是观音，她是佛教中慈悲为怀的多相神祇。这幅画被认为是著名禅僧月翁宗久的作品，他擅长水墨画。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。", "note_en": "This painting of Kannon, a Buddhist deity of mercy and compassion with many forms. is attributed to Gakuō Zōkyū, a well-known Zen monk who specialized in ink painting.\n\nThe work arranges sacred figures inside a legible composition: bodies, gestures, objects and borders prescribe the order of looking. Read the centre first, then the sides and the lower edge; the image becomes a reusable language of faith.", "note_html": "这幅画描绘的是观音，她是佛教中慈悲为怀的多相神祇。这幅画被认为是著名禅僧月翁宗久的作品，他擅长水墨画。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。"}, "the-thousand-acres-of-clouds-from-twelve-views-of-tiger-hill-s-1491": {"note": "《虎丘图》描绘的是位于苏州西北方几英里处的一处历史遗迹。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "Views of Tiger Hill depicts a historic site a few miles northwest of Suzhou.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "《虎丘图》描绘的是位于苏州西北方几英里处的一处历史遗迹。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "the-pine-retreat-from-twelve-views-of-tiger-hill-suzhou-1491": {"note": "《虎丘图》描绘的是位于苏州西北方几英里处的一处历史遗迹。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "Views of Tiger Hill depicts a historic site a few miles northwest of Suzhou.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "《虎丘图》描绘的是位于苏州西北方几英里处的一处历史遗迹。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "the-enlightened-stone-retreat-from-twelve-views-of-tiger-hill--1491": {"note": "《虎丘图》描绘的是位于苏州西北方几英里处的一处历史遗迹。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "Views of Tiger Hill depicts a historic site a few miles northwest of Suzhou.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "《虎丘图》描绘的是位于苏州西北方几英里处的一处历史遗迹。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "distant-view-of-tiger-hill-from-the-canal-mooring-from-twelve--1491": {"note": "《虎丘图》描绘的是位于苏州西北方几英里处的一处历史遗迹。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "Views of Tiger Hill depicts a historic site a few miles northwest of Suzhou.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "《虎丘图》描绘的是位于苏州西北方几英里处的一处历史遗迹。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "tiger-flight-spring-at-the-back-gate-from-twelve-views-of-tige-1491": {"note": "《虎丘图》描绘的是位于苏州西北方几英里处的一处历史遗迹。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "Views of Tiger Hill depicts a historic site a few miles northwest of Suzhou.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "《虎丘图》描绘的是位于苏州西北方几英里处的一处历史遗迹。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "the-nodding-stone-terrace-tiger-hill-and-the-thousand-man-seat-1491": {"note": "《虎丘图》描绘的是位于苏州西北方几英里处的一处历史遗迹。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "Views of Tiger Hill depicts a historic site a few miles northwest of Suzhou.\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "《虎丘图》描绘的是位于苏州西北方几英里处的一处历史遗迹。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "cloud-climbing-pavilion-from-twelve-views-of-tiger-hill-suzhou-1491": {"note": "《虎丘图》描绘的是位于苏州西北方几英里处的一处历史遗迹。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "Views of Tiger Hill depicts a historic site a few miles northwest of Suzhou.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "《虎丘图》描绘的是位于苏州西北方几英里处的一处历史遗迹。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "the-five-sages-terrace-from-twelve-views-of-tiger-hill-suzhou-1491": {"note": "《虎丘图》描绘的是位于苏州西北方几英里处的一处历史遗迹。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "Views of Tiger Hill depicts a historic site a few miles northwest of Suzhou.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "《虎丘图》描绘的是位于苏州西北方几英里处的一处历史遗迹。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "the-thousand-buddha-hall-and-the-pagoda-of-the-cloudy-cliff-mo-1491": {"note": "《虎丘图》描绘的是位于苏州西北方几英里处的一处历史遗迹。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。", "note_en": "Views of Tiger Hill depicts a historic site a few miles northwest of Suzhou.\n\nThe work arranges sacred figures inside a legible composition: bodies, gestures, objects and borders prescribe the order of looking. Read the centre first, then the sides and the lower edge; the image becomes a reusable language of faith.", "note_html": "《虎丘图》描绘的是位于苏州西北方几英里处的一处历史遗迹。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。"}, "bamboo-pavilion-tiger-hill-from-twelve-views-of-tiger-hill-suz-1491": {"note": "《虎丘图》描绘的是位于苏州西北方几英里处的一处历史遗迹。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "Views of Tiger Hill depicts a historic site a few miles northwest of Suzhou.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "《虎丘图》描绘的是位于苏州西北方几英里处的一处历史遗迹。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "the-sword-spring-tiger-hill-from-twelve-views-of-tiger-hill-su-1491": {"note": "《虎丘图》描绘的是位于苏州西北方几英里处的一处历史遗迹。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "Views of Tiger Hill depicts a historic site a few miles northwest of Suzhou.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "《虎丘图》描绘的是位于苏州西北方几英里处的一处历史遗迹。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "the-fool-s-spring-from-twelve-views-of-tiger-hill-suzhou-1491": {"note": "《虎丘图》描绘的是位于苏州西北方几英里处的一处历史遗迹。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "Views of Tiger Hill depicts a historic site a few miles northwest of Suzhou.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "《虎丘图》描绘的是位于苏州西北方几英里处的一处历史遗迹。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "twelve-views-of-tiger-hill-1491": {"note": "《虎丘图》描绘的是位于苏州西北方几英里处的一处历史遗迹。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "Views of Tiger Hill depicts a historic site a few miles northwest of Suzhou.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "《虎丘图》描绘的是位于苏州西北方几英里处的一处历史遗迹。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "virgin-and-child-1495": {"note": "圣母与圣子以半身像的形式出现，倚靠在深色墙壁上。圣婴的身体笼罩在阴影中，他回头看着母亲。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。", "note_en": "Madonna and Child appear in half-length, seated against a dark wall. The Child's body is covered in shadow as he looks over his shoulder at his mother.\n\nThe work arranges sacred figures inside a legible composition: bodies, gestures, objects and borders prescribe the order of looking. Read the centre first, then the sides and the lower edge; the image becomes a reusable language of faith.", "note_html": "圣母与圣子以半身像的形式出现，倚靠在深色墙壁上。圣婴的身体笼罩在阴影中，他回头看着母亲。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。"}, "virgin-and-child-with-john-the-baptist-and-angels-1495": {"note": "圣母子与施洗约翰和天使，约 1500年左右。彼得罗·德尔·东泽洛（意大利，1452–1509）。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。", "note_en": "Virgin and Child with John the Baptist and Angels, c. 1500. Pietro del Donzello (Italian, 1452–1509).\n\nThe work arranges sacred figures inside a legible composition: bodies, gestures, objects and borders prescribe the order of looking. Read the centre first, then the sides and the lower edge; the image becomes a reusable language of faith.", "note_html": "圣母子与施洗约翰和天使，约 1500年左右。彼得罗·德尔·东泽洛（意大利，1452–1509）。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。"}, "leonardo-last-supper-1495": {"note": "在米兰圣玛利亚感恩教堂的食堂墙上，列奥纳多用一点透视法布置了《最后的晚餐》。十二位使徒被分成四组，每组三个人，从中心向外延展。基督刚说过：“你们中有一个将背叛我”；他的双手摊开在桌上，而犹大在阴影中抓着钱包，身体向后倾。消失点位于基督的头部，长桌的线条将每一个声音都引向中心。\n\n因为列奥纳多使用干蛋彩和油画而非真正的湿壁画，这幅画完成不久后就开始剥落。现在所保存的是一幅被时间不断修补的图像；其中的人类心理编排仍然是西方叙事绘画的入门课。", "note_en": "On the refectory wall of Santa Maria delle Grazie in Milan, Leonardo stages the Last Supper in a room built by one-point perspective. The twelve apostles are arranged in four groups of three, rippling outward from the centre. Christ has just said, \"One of you will betray me\"; his hands lie open on the table, while Judas, in shadow, clutches his purse and leans back. The vanishing point sits at Christ's head, and the long table lines gather every voice towards the centre.\n\nBecause Leonardo worked in dry tempera and oil rather than true fresco, the painting began to flake soon after completion. What survives is an image endlessly patched by time; its choreography of human psychology remains a primer of Western narrative painting.", "note_html": "在米兰圣玛利亚感恩教堂的食堂墙上，列奥纳多用一点透视法布置了《最后的晚餐》。十二位使徒被分成四组，每组三个人，从中心向外延展。基督刚说过：“你们中有一个将背叛我”；他的双手摊开在桌上，而犹大在阴影中抓着钱包，身体向后倾。消失点位于基督的头部，长桌的线条将每一个声音都引向中心。\n\n因为列奥纳多使用干蛋彩和油画而非真正的湿壁画，这幅画完成不久后就开始剥落。现在所保存的是一幅被时间不断修补的图像；其中的人类心理编排仍然是西方叙事绘画的入门课。"}, "cle-2006-13-a-1495": {"note": "猿猎野猪（时祷书叶），1495年。欧洲。蛋彩；Each leaf: 18.1 x 12.9 cm (7 1/8 x 5 1/16 in.)。\n\n让猎犬、马与猎物进入权力场景，动物也是身份道具。", "note_en": "Leaf from a Book of Hours: Ape Hunting Wild Boars (recto), c. 1500–1510. France, Paris or Rouen, 16th century. Ink, tempera and liquid gold on vellum; each leaf: 18.1 x 12.9 cm (7 1/8 x 5 1/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, The Jeanne Miles Blackburn Collection, 2006.13.a\n\nWithin “Landscape and Nature”, under “动物与宫廷”: Hounds, horses and prey enter a scene of power; animals are also status props.", "note_html": "猿猎野猪（时祷书叶），1495年。欧洲。蛋彩；Each leaf: 18.1 x 12.9 cm (7 1/8 x 5 1/16 in.)。\n\n让猎犬、马与猎物进入权力场景，动物也是身份道具。"}, "cle-1977-207-1495": {"note": "花鸟鹿纹边饰中的波斯书法，1495年。南亚。蛋彩；Overall: 36.8 x 25.2 cm (14 1/2 x 9 15/16 in.)。\n\n把笔迹、留白与边框当成图像，阅读节奏就是视觉节奏。", "note_en": "Persian calligraphy framed by an ornamental border of flowers, birds, and deer, from the Late Shah Jahan Album, calligraphy: c. 1500–1540; border: c. 1630–40. Mir 'Ali Haravi (Persian, active in Herat, Afghanistan, died c. 1550). Gum tempera, gold, and ink on paper; overall: 36.8 x 25.2 cm (14 1/2 x 9 15/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of Herbert F. Leisy in memory of his wife, Helen Stamp Leisy, 1977.207\n\nWithin “Word and Looking”, under “书法”: Hand, blank space and border are image; reading rhythm is visual rhythm.", "note_html": "花鸟鹿纹边饰中的波斯书法，1495年。南亚。蛋彩；Overall: 36.8 x 25.2 cm (14 1/2 x 9 15/16 in.)。\n\n把笔迹、留白与边框当成图像，阅读节奏就是视觉节奏。"}, "cle-1985-191-b-1495": {"note": "金刚乘尊神图像稿（另面），1495年。南亚。手抄本；Overall: 20.3 x 12.7 cm (8 x 5 in.)。\n\n保留修改与犹豫的痕迹，让创作过程进入成品。", "note_en": "Iconographic Drawings: Chakrashamvara with Vajravarahi, Hevajra with Nairatmya, and Yamantaka (verso), c. 1500. Tibet. Ink and watercolor on cotton; overall: 20.3 x 12.7 cm (8 x 5 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Delia E. Holden Fund, 1985.191.b\n\nWithin “Material and Technique”, under “素描”: Corrections and hesitation remain visible; process enters the finished work.", "note_html": "金刚乘尊神图像稿（另面），1495年。南亚。手抄本；Overall: 20.3 x 12.7 cm (8 x 5 in.)。\n\n保留修改与犹豫的痕迹，让创作过程进入成品。"}, "bosch-garden-earthly-delights-1500": {"note": "《人间乐园》是一幅三联画。左边的画板是伊甸园，上帝把夏娃介绍给亚当；中间是一个挤满成千上万裸体人物的花园，他们在水果、池塘、鸟类和野兽之间玩耍；右边是一个黑暗的地狱，乐器变成折磨人的工具，怪物吞噬人身。合上时，外翼显示的是灰色的创造，世界被包裹在透明球体中。\n\n博斯把中世纪的道德寓言、炼金术符号和民间谚语都塞进了一个视觉机器里，使得快乐与惩罚连成一体。不管这是警告、讽刺，还是对某种被压抑事物的投射，一直没有定论；正是这种难以解读性，使它在五个世纪后仍然吸引观众。", "note_en": "The Garden of Earthly Delights is a triptych. The left panel is Eden, where God presents Eve to Adam; the centre is a garden crowded with thousands of naked figures sporting among fruit, pools, birds and beasts; the right is a dark hell where musical instruments become instruments of torture and monsters devour bodies. Closed, the outer wings show a grey creation, the world enclosed in a transparent sphere.\n\nBosch packs medieval moral allegory, alchemical signs and folk proverb into one visual machine, so that pleasure and punishment follow nose to tail. Whether it is warning, satire or the projection of something repressed has never been settled; that very resistance to decoding is why it still holds viewers five centuries later.", "note_html": "《人间乐园》是一幅三联画。左边的画板是伊甸园，上帝把夏娃介绍给亚当；中间是一个挤满成千上万裸体人物的花园，他们在水果、池塘、鸟类和野兽之间玩耍；右边是一个黑暗的地狱，乐器变成折磨人的工具，怪物吞噬人身。合上时，外翼显示的是灰色的创造，世界被包裹在透明球体中。\n\n博斯把中世纪的道德寓言、炼金术符号和民间谚语都塞进了一个视觉机器里，使得快乐与惩罚连成一体。不管这是警告、讽刺，还是对某种被压抑事物的投射，一直没有定论；正是这种难以解读性，使它在五个世纪后仍然吸引观众。"}, "adoration-of-the-magi-1500": {"note": "这幅画充满了写实的细节，例如骑手们努力让马和骡子保持不动，还有一只小狗在梁上撒尿。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "This painting is filled with naturalistic details such as the riders who struggle to keep their horses and mules still and a small dog who urinates on a beam.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "这幅画充满了写实的细节，例如骑手们努力让马和骡子保持不动，还有一只小狗在梁上撒尿。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "cle-1924-746-1500": {"note": "《古兰经》手抄本页，1500年。中亚。纸本设色；Sheet: 28 x 17.4 cm (11 x 6 7/8 in.)。\n\n让书页、字体与装帧一起进入图像，文字本身也是被观看的对象。", "note_en": "Qur'an Manuscript Folio, 1500s. Afghanistan, Herat, Safavid period (1501–1722). Ink, gold, and colors on paper; sheet: 28 x 17.4 cm (11 x 6 7/8 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Purchase from the J. H. Wade Fund, 1924.746\n\nWithin “Faith and Image”, under “经典与书”: Treats page, script and binding as one image; the word itself is meant to be looked at.", "note_html": "《古兰经》手抄本页，1500年。中亚。纸本设色；Sheet: 28 x 17.4 cm (11 x 6 7/8 in.)。\n\n让书页、字体与装帧一起进入图像，文字本身也是被观看的对象。"}, "virgin-and-child-1500": {"note": "《圣母与圣子》，16世纪。归于贝尔纳迪诺·卢伊尼（意大利，约1480-约1532）。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。", "note_en": "Virgin and Child, 1500s. Attributed to Bernardino Luini (Italian, c. 1480-c. 1532).\n\nThe work arranges sacred figures inside a legible composition: bodies, gestures, objects and borders prescribe the order of looking. Read the centre first, then the sides and the lower edge; the image becomes a reusable language of faith.", "note_html": "《圣母与圣子》，16世纪。归于贝尔纳迪诺·卢伊尼（意大利，约1480-约1532）。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。"}, "virgin-and-child-with-angels-1500": {"note": "《圣母子与天使》，16世纪初。霍尔登圆形画大师（意大利）。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。", "note_en": "Virgin and Child with Angels, early 1500s. Master of the Holden Tondo (Italian).\n\nThe work arranges sacred figures inside a legible composition: bodies, gestures, objects and borders prescribe the order of looking. Read the centre first, then the sides and the lower edge; the image becomes a reusable language of faith.", "note_html": "《圣母子与天使》，16世纪初。霍尔登圆形画大师（意大利）。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。"}, "cle-2015-517-1500": {"note": "山市晴岚，1500年。东亚。绢本水墨；Painting: 115.3 x 60 cm (45 3/8 x 23 5/8 in.); Overall: 179 x 70.7 cm (70 1/2 x 27 13/16 in.); Overall with knobs and cord: 181.8 x 77 cm (71 9/16 x 30 5/16 in.)。\n\n用货物、叫卖与人群，把交换变成可见的城市节奏。", "note_en": "Mountain Market, Clear with Rising Mist (산시청람도 [山市晴嵐圖]), early 1500s. Korea, Joseon dynasty (1392–1910). Hanging scroll; ink on silk; painting: 115.3 x 60 cm (45 3/8 x 23 5/8 in.); overall: 179 x 70.7 cm (70 1/2 x 27 13/16 in.); overall with knobs and cord: 181.8 x 77 cm (71 9/16 x 30 5/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift from the Collection of George Gund III, 2015.517\n\nWithin “City and Everyday Life”, under “市场”: Goods, calls and crowds turn exchange into the visible rhythm of the city.", "note_html": "山市晴岚，1500年。东亚。绢本水墨；Painting: 115.3 x 60 cm (45 3/8 x 23 5/8 in.); Overall: 179 x 70.7 cm (70 1/2 x 27 13/16 in.); Overall with knobs and cord: 181.8 x 77 cm (71 9/16 x 30 5/16 in.)。\n\n用货物、叫卖与人群，把交换变成可见的城市节奏。"}, "cle-1989-67-1500": {"note": "文殊菩萨像，1500年。中国。绢本设色；Painting: 124.8 x 107.3 cm (49 1/8 x 42 1/4 in.); Overall: 314.2 x 111.2 cm (123 11/16 x 43 3/4 in.); Overall with knobs: 314.2 x 122.8 cm (123 11/16 x 48 3/8 in.)。\n\n把神圣形象放回具体信仰：先看脸、手势与光环，再读教义。", "note_en": "Manjushri (文殊菩薩), c. 1500–1550. China, Ming dynasty (1368–1644). Hanging scroll, ink, color and gold on silk; painting: 124.8 x 107.3 cm (49 1/8 x 42 1/4 in.); overall: 314.2 x 111.2 cm (123 11/16 x 43 3/4 in.); overall with knobs: 314.2 x 122.8 cm (123 11/16 x 48 3/8 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Mr. and Mrs. William H. Marlatt Fund, 1989.67\n\nWithin “Faith and Image”, under “神圣人物”: Puts sacred figures back into a specific faith: face, gesture and halo first, doctrine second.", "note_html": "文殊菩萨像，1500年。中国。绢本设色；Painting: 124.8 x 107.3 cm (49 1/8 x 42 1/4 in.); Overall: 314.2 x 111.2 cm (123 11/16 x 43 3/4 in.); Overall with knobs: 314.2 x 122.8 cm (123 11/16 x 48 3/8 in.)。\n\n把神圣形象放回具体信仰：先看脸、手势与光环，再读教义。"}, "squirrel-on-a-pine-branch-1500": {"note": "这幅画捕捉到一只松鼠在行动中的样子，它在爬行时分了神，扭过头来看着右边的一只小虫子。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "This painting captures a squirrel in action, distracted and twisting its head while climbing and looking at a little bug to the right.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "这幅画捕捉到一只松鼠在行动中的样子，它在爬行时分了神，扭过头来看着右边的一只小虫子。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "durer-self-portrait-1500": {"note": "1500年，丢勒正面、对称地画了自己，目光直视观者：长发和胡须垂落在两侧，像一位基督形象，右手放在胸前。黑色的背景让面部和金发显得格外明亮，毛皮衣领一根根细致描绘。他在右侧署了拉丁铭文和“AD”字母组合，标注了新世纪的起点。\n\n丢勒借用了基督形象的正面构图，并将艺术家的自我意识提升到接近神圣的高度。这被解读为北方文艺复兴肖像的宣言：画家不再只是一个普通工匠，而是获得上帝认可的创造者。", "note_en": "In 1500 Dürer painted himself frontally, symmetrically, staring directly at the viewer: long hair and beard falling to either side like a Christ figure, his right hand laid across his chest. The black ground makes face and golden hair luminous, and the fur collar is painted hair by hair. The Latin inscription and his \"AD\" monogram appear at the right, dated at the threshold of a new century.\n\nDürer borrows the frontal composition of Christ imagery and raises the artist's self-awareness to something close to sacred. It is read as a manifesto of the Northern Renaissance portrait: the painter is no longer a mere craftsman but a creator sanctioned by God.", "note_html": "1500年，丢勒正面、对称地画了自己，目光直视观者：长发和胡须垂落在两侧，像一位基督形象，右手放在胸前。黑色的背景让面部和金发显得格外明亮，毛皮衣领一根根细致描绘。他在右侧署了拉丁铭文和“AD”字母组合，标注了新世纪的起点。\n\n丢勒借用了基督形象的正面构图，并将艺术家的自我意识提升到接近神圣的高度。这被解读为北方文艺复兴肖像的宣言：画家不再只是一个普通工匠，而是获得上帝认可的创造者。"}, "calligraphy-of-chaghatai-turkish-poems-in-praise-of-wine-verso-1500": {"note": "这页来自莫卧儿帝国之前的精美彩绘书法被装裱进了一本莫卧儿帝国时期的画册中。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "This page of delicately illuminated calligraphy from the pre-Mughal period was mounted into a Mughal album.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "这页来自莫卧儿帝国之前的精美彩绘书法被装裱进了一本莫卧儿帝国时期的画册中。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "the-crucifixion-1500": {"note": "《耶稣受难》，16世纪。索多玛的追随者（意大利，1477–1549）。布面油画；带框：72 x 59 x 4厘米（28 3/8 x 23 1/4 x 1 9/16英寸）；不带框：59 x 47厘米（23 1/4 x 18 1\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "The Crucifixion, 1500s. Follower of Sodoma (Italian, 1477–1549). Oil on canvas; framed: 72 x 59 x 4 cm (28 3/8 x 23 1/4 x 1 9/16 in.); unframed: 59 x 47 cm (23 1/4 x 18 1/2 in.).\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "《耶稣受难》，16世纪。索多玛的追随者（意大利，1477–1549）。布面油画；带框：72 x 59 x 4厘米（28 3/8 x 23 1/4 x 1 9/16英寸）；不带框：59 x 47厘米（23 1/4 x 18 1\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "cle-2015-512-1500": {"note": "雨中行路的中国侍者，1500年。东亚。纸本水墨；Mounted: 131.8 x 44.2 cm (51 7/8 x 17 3/8 in.)。\n\n把侍者、工匠与路人放回画面中心，追问谁被记录、谁被省略。", "note_en": "Chinese Servant Walking in the Rain, 1500s. Attributed to Gakuō Zōkyū (Japanese, active about 1482–1514). Hanging scroll; ink on paper; mounted: 131.8 x 44.2 cm (51 7/8 x 17 3/8 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift from the Collection of George Gund III, 2015.512\n\nWithin “Portrait and Self”, under “无名者”: Puts servants, artisans and passers-by at the centre, asking who is recorded and who is omitted.", "note_html": "雨中行路的中国侍者，1500年。东亚。纸本水墨；Mounted: 131.8 x 44.2 cm (51 7/8 x 17 3/8 in.)。\n\n把侍者、工匠与路人放回画面中心，追问谁被记录、谁被省略。"}, "winter-landscape-1500": {"note": "这幅冬景图是理想主义巨幅绘画的生动范例：水墨晕染与勾勒轮廓的笔触形成鲜明对比；岩石轮廓的大胆勾勒\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "This wintry vista is a vivid example of idealistic monumental painting: the strong contrasts of ink washes and contouring brush lines; the bold outlining of rock shapes and tree tr\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "这幅冬景图是理想主义巨幅绘画的生动范例：水墨晕染与勾勒轮廓的笔触形成鲜明对比；岩石轮廓的大胆勾勒\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "leonardo-mona-lisa-1503": {"note": "留给观众的不是微笑，而是不确定感：她没有眉毛，眼角和嘴角的轮廓模糊得无法分辨；她身后的地平线两边高度不同，路和水远远延伸。达·芬奇的烟雾法让形态在空气中消散，同时将观众的注意力锁定在脸上。据说她是佛罗伦萨商人的妻子丽莎·杰拉尔迪尼，但她的身份从未得到确切确认。\n\n这幅画在1911年被盗后成为全球知名的画作，现在是卢浮宫参观人数最多的作品。它真正的革命之处在于，一幅肖像不再只是外貌的记录，而是一个似乎会思考、会回望的人。", "note_en": "What stays with the viewer is not the smile but the uncertainty: there are no eyebrows, and the corners of the eyes and mouth are blurred past definition; the horizon behind her sits at different heights on either side, roads and water receding into distance. Leonardo's sfumato lets form dissolve into air while pinning the viewer's attention to the face. She is said to be the wife of a Florentine merchant, Lisa Gherardini, though her identity has never been settled.\n\nThe painting became a global image after its theft in 1911 and is now the most visited work in the Louvre. Its real revolution is that a portrait ceases to be a record of appearance and becomes a person who seems to think and to look back.", "note_html": "留给观众的不是微笑，而是不确定感：她没有眉毛，眼角和嘴角的轮廓模糊得无法分辨；她身后的地平线两边高度不同，路和水远远延伸。达·芬奇的烟雾法让形态在空气中消散，同时将观众的注意力锁定在脸上。据说她是佛罗伦萨商人的妻子丽莎·杰拉尔迪尼，但她的身份从未得到确切确认。\n\n这幅画在1911年被盗后成为全球知名的画作，现在是卢浮宫参观人数最多的作品。它真正的革命之处在于，一幅肖像不再只是外貌的记录，而是一个似乎会思考、会回望的人。"}, "cle-2020-228-1504": {"note": "圣维罗妮卡木刻匣，1504年。欧洲。木刻；Overall: 28 x 18.5 x 10 cm (11 x 7 5/16 x 3 15/16 in.); Sheet with print: 29 x 19 cm (11 7/16 x 7 1/2 in.)。\n\n以刀痕与黑白对比，把复制技术的限制变成风格。", "note_en": "Coffret with Woodcut of Saint Veronica's Vernicle, Coffret: c. 1515; Woodcut: c. 1509. Woodcuts by Hans Burgkmair the Elder (German, 1473–1531). Wood, leather, iron, textile, woodcut with stenciled coloring; overall: 28 x 18.5 x 10 cm (11 x 7 5/16 x 3 15/16 in.); sheet with print: 29 x 19 cm (11 7/16 x 7 1/2 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Purchase from the J. H. Wade Fund, 2020.228\n\nWithin “Material and Technique”, under “木刻”: Knife marks and black-white contrast turn the limits of reproduction into style.", "note_html": "圣维罗妮卡木刻匣，1504年。欧洲。木刻；Overall: 28 x 18.5 x 10 cm (11 x 7 5/16 x 3 15/16 in.); Sheet with print: 29 x 19 cm (11 7/16 x 7 1/2 in.)。\n\n以刀痕与黑白对比，把复制技术的限制变成风格。"}, "children-at-play-1508": {"note": "十六个儿童参与学术、宗教和军事活动，代表了表达对子嗣昌盛、成功愿望的流行主题“百子图”。\n\n日常场景把城市、室内或劳作变成画面。器物、动作与衣饰这些细节，比情节更能说明当时的生活秩序。", "note_en": "Sixteen children engage in scholarly, religious, and military activities, representing the popular “one hundred boys” theme expressing the wish for abundant, successful male offspr\n\nA scene of daily life turns a city, an interior or labour into a picture. Objects, actions and clothes tell us more about the order of life than the anecdote does.", "note_html": "十六个儿童参与学术、宗教和军事活动，代表了表达对子嗣昌盛、成功愿望的流行主题“百子图”。\n\n日常场景把城市、室内或劳作变成画面。器物、动作与衣饰这些细节，比情节更能说明当时的生活秩序。"}, "virgin-and-child-with-saints-and-donors-1510": {"note": "这件作品重新诠释了文艺复兴艺术中最常见的主题——圣母与圣子。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。", "note_en": "This work reinterprets the most common subject in Renaissance art—the Madonna and Child.\n\nThe work arranges sacred figures inside a legible composition: bodies, gestures, objects and borders prescribe the order of looking. Read the centre first, then the sides and the lower edge; the image becomes a reusable language of faith.", "note_html": "这件作品重新诠释了文艺复兴艺术中最常见的主题——圣母与圣子。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。"}, "portrait-of-a-man-1510": {"note": "这位年轻人可能是斯福尔扎家族的一员，该家族是文艺复兴时期米兰的统治家族。他的帽子上佩戴着一块小饰牌，表明了他的贵族身份。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "This young man is possibly a member of the Sforza household, the ruling family of Milan during the Renaissance. He wears a plaquette on his hat indicating his nobility and status.\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "这位年轻人可能是斯福尔扎家族的一员，该家族是文艺复兴时期米兰的统治家族。他的帽子上佩戴着一块小饰牌，表明了他的贵族身份。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "michelangelo-creation-of-adam-1511": {"note": "米开朗基罗将创造的行为压缩到即将触碰的两只手上。亚当半睡半醒地躺在绿色的土地上，他的身体刚刚被点燃；上帝穿过云层飞奔而来，他的斗篷像帆一样鼓起，天使和风围绕着他。在指尖之间留有一条微小的空隙，这条空隙赋予了整个天花板生命力。\n\n通过雕塑般的裸体、剧烈的扭曲和几乎没有背景，米开朗基罗将“按上帝的形象造的人”转化为肉体与精神之间的紧张关系。亚当的目光慵懒而模糊；上帝的目光则急切而专注。在这一瞬间，创作者与被创造者绝不是平等的。", "note_en": "Michelangelo compresses the act of creation into two hands about to touch. Adam lies half-awake on green earth, his body only just kindled; God rushes forward through cloud, his mantle swelling like a sail, angels and wind packed around him. A tiny gap remains between the fingertips, and that gap is what charges the whole ceiling.\n\nWith sculptural nudity, violent torsion and almost no setting, Michelangelo turns \"man made in God's image\" into a tension between flesh and spirit. Adam's gaze is languid and unfocused; God's is urgent and intent. In this instant, creator and created are anything but equal.", "note_html": "米开朗基罗将创造的行为压缩到即将触碰的两只手上。亚当半睡半醒地躺在绿色的土地上，他的身体刚刚被点燃；上帝穿过云层飞奔而来，他的斗篷像帆一样鼓起，天使和风围绕着他。在指尖之间留有一条微小的空隙，这条空隙赋予了整个天花板生命力。\n\n通过雕塑般的裸体、剧烈的扭曲和几乎没有背景，米开朗基罗将“按上帝的形象造的人”转化为肉体与精神之间的紧张关系。亚当的目光慵懒而模糊；上帝的目光则急切而专注。在这一瞬间，创作者与被创造者绝不是平等的。"}, "raphael-school-of-athens-1511": {"note": "在《署名室》中，拉斐尔描绘了一个理想的古代学术场景。柏拉图和亚里士多德站在中央拱门下，一个指向天堂，另一个指向地球；苏格拉底、毕达哥拉斯、欧几里得和托勒密分别分布在两侧，有的在辩论，有的在计算，有的在倾听。建筑呈现出巴拉曼特式的中央空间，它的透视效果将人群引入深邃的大厅。\n\n拉斐尔把人文主义者对古代知识的想象变成了一场有序的对话，同时允许他的同时代人以不同的形象出现在画面中。平衡并非静止不变：它在手势、目光和身体方向中不断交换。", "note_en": "In the Stanza della Segnatura, Raphael painted an ideal academy of antiquity. Plato and Aristotle stand beneath the central arch, one pointing to heaven, the other to earth; Socrates, Pythagoras, Euclid and Ptolemy are distributed to either side, arguing, calculating or listening. The architecture opens as a Bramante-like centralised space, its perspective drawing the crowd into a deep hall.\n\nRaphael turned the humanists' image of ancient knowledge into an ordered conversation, and allowed his own contemporaries to enter the scene under different guises. The balance is not static: it is continually exchanged through gesture, gaze and the direction of bodies.", "note_html": "在《署名室》中，拉斐尔描绘了一个理想的古代学术场景。柏拉图和亚里士多德站在中央拱门下，一个指向天堂，另一个指向地球；苏格拉底、毕达哥拉斯、欧几里得和托勒密分别分布在两侧，有的在辩论，有的在计算，有的在倾听。建筑呈现出巴拉曼特式的中央空间，它的透视效果将人群引入深邃的大厅。\n\n拉斐尔把人文主义者对古代知识的想象变成了一场有序的对话，同时允许他的同时代人以不同的形象出现在画面中。平衡并非静止不变：它在手势、目光和身体方向中不断交换。"}, "cle-1960-30-1512": {"note": "法国王与福伊尔艾森王之战，1512年。欧洲。木刻；Sheet: 22.1 x 19.7 cm (8 11/16 x 7 3/4 in.)。\n\n不美化冲突，先看阵列、火光与逃散，再看胜利叙事如何被书写。", "note_en": "Der Weisskunig (The White King): How the French King made war on the King of Feuereisen in his realm and how the King of Feuereisen died in the battle, 1512–16. Hans Burgkmair (German, 1473–1531). Woodcut; sheet: 22.1 x 19.7 cm (8 11/16 x 7 3/4 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Dudley P. Allen Fund, 1960.30\n\nWithin “City and Everyday Life”, under “战争与灾难”: No glorification: formation, fire and flight first, then the writing of victory.", "note_html": "法国王与福伊尔艾森王之战，1512年。欧洲。木刻；Sheet: 22.1 x 19.7 cm (8 11/16 x 7 3/4 in.)。\n\n不美化冲突，先看阵列、火光与逃散，再看胜利叙事如何被书写。"}, "portrait-of-a-woman-1513": {"note": "弗朗索瓦一世对意大利文艺复兴文化的浓厚兴趣不仅体现在收藏重要艺术作品上，还体现在他将知名建筑师、\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "King Francis I’s deep interest in Italian Renaissance culture manifested itself not only through acquiring important works of art but also by bringing leading architects, scholars,\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "弗朗索瓦一世对意大利文艺复兴文化的浓厚兴趣不仅体现在收藏重要艺术作品上，还体现在他将知名建筑师、\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "durer-melencolia-i-1514": {"note": "丢勒把几何、工具、天平与一只缩着的狗放在同一个画面里；忧郁不是情绪，而是一种被工具包围的思考状态。", "note_en": "1514, Europe. 阿尔布雷希特·丢勒; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1926.211. This is a print.", "note_html": "丢勒把几何、工具、天平与一只缩着的狗放在同一个画面里；忧郁不是情绪，而是一种被工具包围的思考状态。"}, "met-451285-1515": {"note": "伊斯兰画册中的一页，约创作于1515年；纸本水墨、不透明水彩和金彩，现藏于大都会艺术博物馆。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "A leaf from an Islamic album, dated about 1515; Ink, opaque watercolor, and gold on paper, in the collection of the Metropolitan Museum of Art.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "伊斯兰画册中的一页，约创作于1515年；纸本水墨、不透明水彩和金彩，现藏于大都会艺术博物馆。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "titian-submersion-pharaoh-1549": {"note": "提香1514—15年设计这幅木刻，1549年由多梅尼科·达莱·格雷凯印成；红海分开，法老的军队在右侧被水吞没。", "note_en": "1514–15, printed 1549, Europe. 提香（及多梅尼科·达莱·格雷凯）; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1952.296. This is a print.", "note_html": "提香1514—15年设计这幅木刻，1549年由多梅尼科·达莱·格雷凯印成；红海分开，法老的军队在右侧被水吞没。"}, "cle-1958-117-1519": {"note": "市集上的农民，1519年。欧洲。铜版；。\n\n用货物、叫卖与人群，把交换变成可见的城市节奏。", "note_en": "The Peasants at Market, 1519. Albrecht Dürer (German, 1471–1528). Engraving. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Bequest of Leonard C. Hanna Jr., 1958.117\n\nWithin “City and Everyday Life”, under “市场”: Goods, calls and crowds turn exchange into the visible rhythm of the city.", "note_html": "市集上的农民，1519年。欧洲。铜版；。\n\n用货物、叫卖与人群，把交换变成可见的城市节奏。"}, "titian-adoration-magi-1520": {"note": "1500s，意大利 威尼斯。提香（及工作室）的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。", "note_en": "1500s, Europe. 提香（及工作室）; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1957.15. This is a painting (oil painting).", "note_html": "1500s，意大利 威尼斯。提香（及工作室）的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。"}, "holy-family-with-a-shepherd-1520": {"note": "在这幅圣家像中，若瑟和玛利亚俯身欣赏圣婴，一位牧羊人倚在拐杖上注视着他们。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。", "note_en": "In this image of the Holy Family, Joseph and Mary lean in to admire the Christ Child while a shepherd looks on, leaning on his staff.\n\nThe work arranges sacred figures inside a legible composition: bodies, gestures, objects and borders prescribe the order of looking. Read the centre first, then the sides and the lower edge; the image becomes a reusable language of faith.", "note_html": "在这幅圣家像中，若瑟和玛利亚俯身欣赏圣婴，一位牧羊人倚在拐杖上注视着他们。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。"}, "madonna-and-child-in-a-niche-1520": {"note": "这幅圣母玛利亚抱着圣婴的画作经过多次修复，面貌已大为改观。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。", "note_en": "This image of Madonna with the Christ Child on her lap has been extensively altered by restoration.\n\nThe work arranges sacred figures inside a legible composition: bodies, gestures, objects and borders prescribe the order of looking. Read the centre first, then the sides and the lower edge; the image becomes a reusable language of faith.", "note_html": "这幅圣母玛利亚抱着圣婴的画作经过多次修复，面貌已大为改观。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。"}, "christ-with-joseph-of-arimathea-1520": {"note": "耶稣被钉十字架后，亚利马太的约瑟获得许可，将基督的遗体安葬在自己的坟墓中。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。", "note_en": "After the Crucifixion, Joseph of Arimathea obtained permission to bury Christ’s body in Joseph’s own tomb.\n\nThe work arranges sacred figures inside a legible composition: bodies, gestures, objects and borders prescribe the order of looking. Read the centre first, then the sides and the lower edge; the image becomes a reusable language of faith.", "note_html": "耶稣被钉十字架后，亚利马太的约瑟获得许可，将基督的遗体安葬在自己的坟墓中。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。"}, "cle-1971-171-1520": {"note": "黑天与牧女在朱木拿河（《薄伽梵往世书》），1520年。南亚。蛋彩；Overall: 16.5 x 22.2 cm (6 1/2 x 8 3/4 in.)。\n\n让河流、瀑布与岸边人物共同构成时间感，水线就是画面的节拍。", "note_en": "Krishna sporting with the gopis in the Jumna River, from a Bhagavata Purana, c. 1525–40. Northern India. Gum tempera and ink on paper; overall: 16.5 x 22.2 cm (6 1/2 x 8 3/4 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of Mr. and Mrs. Alvin N. Haas, 1971.171\n\nWithin “Landscape and Nature”, under “水”: River, waterfall and shore figures create time; the waterline sets the rhythm.", "note_html": "黑天与牧女在朱木拿河（《薄伽梵往世书》），1520年。南亚。蛋彩；Overall: 16.5 x 22.2 cm (6 1/2 x 8 3/4 in.)。\n\n让河流、瀑布与岸边人物共同构成时间感，水线就是画面的节拍。"}, "the-sacrifice-of-isaac-1522": {"note": "在旧约《创世记》中这场对信仰的严峻考验中，亚伯拉罕遵照上帝的旨意同意献祭自己的儿子以撒。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "In this dramatic test of faith from the Old Testament book of Genesis, Abraham agrees to slay his son Isaac on God’s command.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "在旧约《创世记》中这场对信仰的严峻考验中，亚伯拉罕遵照上帝的旨意同意献祭自己的儿子以撒。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "portrait-of-an-old-man-1525": {"note": "坎皮是北意大利著名画家家族的一员，他笔下的肖像对象面容并不完美，以精心观察的皱纹为主。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "Part of a distinguished family of Northern northern Italian painters, Campi depicts his sitter with an unidealized face dominated by carefully observed wrinkles.\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "坎皮是北意大利著名画家家族的一员，他笔下的肖像对象面容并不完美，以精心观察的皱纹为主。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "portrait-of-a-young-man-1525": {"note": "与多西画室的其他画作一样，这幅作品传达了肖像人物的社会地位和自信心。他手里拿着一封皱巴巴的意大利文信。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "Like other paintings from the Dossi workshop, this work conveys the sitter's social status and self-confidence. He holds a crumpled letter written in Italian.\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "与多西画室的其他画作一样，这幅作品传达了肖像人物的社会地位和自信心。他手里拿着一封皱巴巴的意大利文信。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "terminus-the-device-of-erasmus-1527": {"note": "本着意大利文艺复兴的精神，伊拉斯谟·罗特丹（约\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "In the spirit of the Italian Renaissance, Erasmus of Rotterdam (c.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "本着意大利文艺复兴的精神，伊拉斯谟·罗特丹（约\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "cbl-per-194-1527": {"note": "《迷醉之书：球与马球杆》，1527年。中亚。纸本、墨、颜料与金箔；写本；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「中亚」区域页：《迷醉之书：球与马球杆》以1527年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。", "note_en": "Book of Ecstasy (Ḥālnāma), or The Ball and the Polo Mallet (Gūy o Chūgān), by Maḥmūd ibn Muḥammad al-`Ārifī.  \nCodex, ink, colours and gold on gold-sprinkled paper, lacquer painted book covers, 24 folios, Persian text in nasta`liq script, with illuminated heading (sarlawh, fol. 1v), colophon (fol. 24r) and borders throughout, the Book of Ecstasy (Ḥālnāma), or The Ball and the Polo Mallet (Gūy-o-Chūgān), by Maḥmūd ibn Muḥammad al-`Ārifī, first composed 1438 for Timurid prince Mīrzā Sulṭān-Muḥammad ibn Baysunghur, copied by `Alī al-Ḥusaynī al-Kātib (possibly Mīr `Alī al-Haravī), Herat, Afghanistan, dated 934H, 1527-1528.\n\nBuilds the regional page for Central Asia: Book of Ecstasy (Ḥālnāma), or The Ball and the Polo Mallet (Gūy o Chūgān), by Maḥmūd ibn Muḥammad al-`Ārifī enters at 1527 with a verifiable date and medium.", "note_html": "《迷醉之书：球与马球杆》，1527年。中亚。纸本、墨、颜料与金箔；写本；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「中亚」区域页：《迷醉之书：球与马球杆》以1527年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。"}, "parmigianino-entombment-1529": {"note": "1529–30，意大利 帕尔马。帕米贾尼诺的版画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。这是一件版画作品，线条与印痕记录了图像被复制的路径。", "note_en": "1529–30, Europe. 帕米贾尼诺; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1985.1. This is a print.", "note_html": "1529–30，意大利 帕尔马。帕米贾尼诺的版画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。这是一件版画作品，线条与印痕记录了图像被复制的路径。"}, "cle-1984-71-1529": {"note": "命运三女神服饰设计，1529年。欧洲。铜版；Sheet: 25.5 x 42.6 cm (10 1/16 x 16 3/4 in.)。\n\n从衣褶、发型与身体姿态，读出性别、阶层与时代。", "note_en": "The Three Fates, Costume Designs, c. 1534. Pierre Milan (French), after Rosso Fiorentino (Italian, 1494–1540). Engraving; sheet: 25.5 x 42.6 cm (10 1/16 x 16 3/4 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of The Print Club of Cleveland, 1984.71\n\nWithin “Portrait and Self”, under “身体与服饰”: Fold, hair and posture reveal gender, class and period.", "note_html": "命运三女神服饰设计，1529年。欧洲。铜版；Sheet: 25.5 x 42.6 cm (10 1/16 x 16 3/4 in.)。\n\n从衣褶、发型与身体姿态，读出性别、阶层与时代。"}, "the-baptism-of-christ-1530": {"note": "克拉纳赫的这幅宏伟画作以细腻的笔触描绘，其中包含了16世纪德国艺术中典型的风景元素：郁郁葱葱的森林、山顶上的城市和远处的山脉。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。", "note_en": "Painted in minute detail, Cranach’s majestic scene includes elements characteristic of landscapes in 16th-century German art: verdant forest, hilltop city, and distant mountains.\n\nThe work arranges sacred figures inside a legible composition: bodies, gestures, objects and borders prescribe the order of looking. Read the centre first, then the sides and the lower edge; the image becomes a reusable language of faith.", "note_html": "克拉纳赫的这幅宏伟画作以细腻的笔触描绘，其中包含了16世纪德国艺术中典型的风景元素：郁郁葱葱的森林、山顶上的城市和远处的山脉。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。"}, "portrait-of-a-man-possibly-girolamo-rosati-1533": {"note": "这位衣着优雅的男士的姿态令人费解。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "The gesture of the elegantly dressed man is a mystery.\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "这位衣着优雅的男士的姿态令人费解。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "parmigianino-madonna-long-neck-1535": {"note": "《长颈圣母》把圣母、圣婴和一群天使安排在一个不确定的空间里。圣母坐在中央，脖子拉得异常长，右手触碰着圣婴，但她的身体似乎随时会滑出画框；圣婴体型偏大，睡着的姿势几乎像古代雕塑。右侧一排纤细的柱子没有柱头，背景看起来既像舞台布景又像未完成的建筑。\n\n帕尔米贾尼诺故意打破比例和透视，把优雅推向失衡的边缘。这种美学后来被称为“矫饰主义”，它不再依赖文艺复兴的测量标准，而是依赖线条、姿态以及观者的微妙不适感。", "note_en": "Madonna with the Long Neck stages the Virgin, Child and a crowd of angels in an uncertain space. The Virgin sits at the centre, her neck stretched impossibly long, her right hand touching the Child while her body seems ready to slide out of the frame; the Child is oversized, his sleeping pose almost like an antique sculpture. A row of slender columns at the right lacks capitals, and the background reads as both stage set and unfinished architecture.\n\nParmigianino deliberately violates proportion and perspective, pushing grace to the edge of imbalance. This aesthetic, later called Mannerism, no longer trusts Renaissance measurement; it trusts line, pose and the viewer's unease.", "note_html": "《长颈圣母》把圣母、圣婴和一群天使安排在一个不确定的空间里。圣母坐在中央，脖子拉得异常长，右手触碰着圣婴，但她的身体似乎随时会滑出画框；圣婴体型偏大，睡着的姿势几乎像古代雕塑。右侧一排纤细的柱子没有柱头，背景看起来既像舞台布景又像未完成的建筑。\n\n帕尔米贾尼诺故意打破比例和透视，把优雅推向失衡的边缘。这种美学后来被称为“矫饰主义”，它不再依赖文艺复兴的测量标准，而是依赖线条、姿态以及观者的微妙不适感。"}, "landscape-with-saint-john-the-baptist-1535": {"note": "这幅画是所谓“世界风景画”的一个范例，这个术语由艺术史学家创造，用于描述一种具有广阔全景的北方风景画。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。", "note_en": "This picture is an example of the so-called world landscape, a term coined by art historians to characterize a type of Northern landscape painting with a vast panorama and a narrat\n\nThe work arranges sacred figures inside a legible composition: bodies, gestures, objects and borders prescribe the order of looking. Read the centre first, then the sides and the lower edge; the image becomes a reusable language of faith.", "note_html": "这幅画是所谓“世界风景画”的一个范例，这个术语由艺术史学家创造，用于描述一种具有广阔全景的北方风景画。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。"}, "cle-1991-157-1537": {"note": "克雷坦诗抄卷首画：两女之争，1537年。欧洲。蛋彩；Sheet: 27.1 x 20.1 cm (10 11/16 x 7 15/16 in.)。\n\n让抄写、插图与装帧互相解释，书是一件被使用的整体。", "note_en": "Frontispiece Miniature from the Manuscript of a Poem by Guillaume Crétin: Debate Between Two Women, c. 1537–1540. Master of Francis I (French). Ink, tempera, and liquid gold on vellum; sheet: 27.1 x 20.1 cm (10 11/16 x 7 15/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, John L. Severance Fund, 1991.157\n\nWithin “Word and Looking”, under “手抄本”: Writing, illumination and binding explain one another; the book is a used object.", "note_html": "克雷坦诗抄卷首画：两女之争，1537年。欧洲。蛋彩；Sheet: 27.1 x 20.1 cm (10 11/16 x 7 15/16 in.)。\n\n让抄写、插图与装帧互相解释，书是一件被使用的整体。"}, "inp-moldovita-1537": {"note": "《摩尔多维察修道院南墙：君士坦丁堡之围》，1537年。欧洲。湿壁画（外墙）；壁画现场；照片像素见图像著录。\n\n补足「欧洲」区域页：《摩尔多维察修道院南墙：君士坦丁堡之围》以1537年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。", "note_en": "Mânăstirea Moldovița, situată în comuna Vatra Moldoviței, reprezintă una dintre cele mai vechi așezări călugărești, un reper al artei vechi moldovenești, inclusă în patrimoniul UNESCO. Mânăstirea de maici poartă hramul Buna Vestire și a fost ctitorită de domnitorul Petru Rareș în 1532. Pictura exterioară este un element inovativ, cu un caracter realist, narativ, bogat cromatic și imagistic, total diferită de sursa de inspirație, și anume cultura religioasă bizantină. Se consideră că pictura de la Moldovița a fost realizată de Toma de la Suceava, pictorul de curte al lui Petru Rareș. Pentru mai multe detalii, accesați link-uri: https://www.radioromaniacultural.ro/sectiuni-articole/calatorii/manastirea-moldovita-bijuterie-a-spiritualitatii-si-artei-vechi-moldovenesti-id5331.html; https://patrimoniu.revistasinteza.ro/2017/03/27/moldovita-poveste-cu-final-neasteptat/.\n\nBuilds the regional page for Europe: Mânăstirea Moldovița. Peretele din sud. Jos: Asediul Constantinopolului enters at 1537 with a verifiable date and medium.", "note_html": "《摩尔多维察修道院南墙：君士坦丁堡之围》，1537年。欧洲。湿壁画（外墙）；壁画现场；照片像素见图像著录。\n\n补足「欧洲」区域页：《摩尔多维察修道院南墙：君士坦丁堡之围》以1537年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。"}, "portrait-of-a-prelate-1540": {"note": "来自费拉拉的宫廷艺术家吉罗拉莫·达·卡尔皮（Girolamo da Carpi）受到了意大利风格主义艺术中优雅和理性人为性的影响，这体现在\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "Girolamo da Carpi, a court artist from Ferrara, was influenced by the grace and intellectual artificiality found in Italian Mannerist art, seen in the flowing S-curve of the sitter\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "来自费拉拉的宫廷艺术家吉罗拉莫·达·卡尔皮（Girolamo da Carpi）受到了意大利风格主义艺术中优雅和理性人为性的影响，这体现在\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "hunting-near-hartenfels-castle-1540": {"note": "这幅生动的狩猎场景画作是由萨克森的新教统治者委托创作的，背景中可以看到他们的住所——位于德国东部的哈滕费尔斯城堡。\n\n日常场景把城市、室内或劳作变成画面。器物、动作与衣饰这些细节，比情节更能说明当时的生活秩序。", "note_en": "The Protestant rulers of Saxony commissioned this animated hunt scene, set near their residence seen in the background, Hartenfels Castle (in eastern Germany).\n\nA scene of daily life turns a city, an interior or labour into a picture. Objects, actions and clothes tell us more about the order of life than the anecdote does.", "note_html": "这幅生动的狩猎场景画作是由萨克森的新教统治者委托创作的，背景中可以看到他们的住所——位于德国东部的哈滕费尔斯城堡。\n\n日常场景把城市、室内或劳作变成画面。器物、动作与衣饰这些细节，比情节更能说明当时的生活秩序。"}, "portrait-of-a-woman-1540": {"note": "科尔内耶·德·里昂（Corneille de Lyon）曾为法国宫廷和富商创作肖像。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "Corneille de Lyon worked both for the French court and wealthy merchants.\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "科尔内耶·德·里昂（Corneille de Lyon）曾为法国宫廷和富商创作肖像。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "portrait-of-machtelt-suijs-1540": {"note": "马尔滕·范·海姆斯克（Maerten van Heemskerck）在罗马生活了四年（1532–1536年），深受这座城市的艺术和古迹的影响。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "Maerten van Heemskerck lived in Rome for four years (1532–36) and was deeply affected by the city's art and antiquities.\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "马尔滕·范·海姆斯克（Maerten van Heemskerck）在罗马生活了四年（1532–1536年），深受这座城市的艺术和古迹的影响。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "lazarus-and-the-rich-man-1545": {"note": "圣经中关于拉撒路和财主的比喻（路加福音16:19-21）讲述了一个人每天大宴豪饮，而一个名叫拉撒路的乞丐却饿着肚子坐在附近。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "The Biblical parable of Lazarus and the Rich Man (Luke 16:19-21) tells of a man who feasted and celebrated every day, while a beggar named Lazarus sat starving nearby.\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "圣经中关于拉撒路和财主的比喻（路加福音16:19-21）讲述了一个人每天大宴豪饮，而一个名叫拉撒路的乞丐却饿着肚子坐在附近。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "portrait-of-maria-kitscher-frau-von-freyberg-1545": {"note": "玛丽亚·冯·弗莱贝格（Maria von Freyberg）曾在巴伐利亚公爵阿尔布雷希特五世（Albert V）的宫廷任职。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "Maria von Freyberg was in the court of Albert V, Duke of Bavaria.\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "玛丽亚·冯·弗莱贝格（Maria von Freyberg）曾在巴伐利亚公爵阿尔布雷希特五世（Albert V）的宫廷任职。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "cle-1982-170-1550": {"note": "哀悼基督，1550年。欧洲。木刻；。\n\n以刀痕与黑白对比，把复制技术的限制变成风格。", "note_en": "Lamentation over the Body of Christ, late 1500s–early 1600s. Giuseppe Scolari (Italian). Woodcut. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of The Print Club of Cleveland, 1982.170\n\nWithin “Material and Technique”, under “木刻”: Knife marks and black-white contrast turn the limits of reproduction into style.", "note_html": "哀悼基督，1550年。欧洲。木刻；。\n\n以刀痕与黑白对比，把复制技术的限制变成风格。"}, "holy-family-with-the-mystic-marriage-of-saint-catherine-1550": {"note": "这幅画中描绘的婚姻被称为“神秘婚姻”，因为它纯粹是象征性的。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。", "note_en": "The marriage shown in this painting is called “mystic” because it was a purely symbolic.\n\nThe work arranges sacred figures inside a legible composition: bodies, gestures, objects and borders prescribe the order of looking. Read the centre first, then the sides and the lower edge; the image becomes a reusable language of faith.", "note_html": "这幅画中描绘的婚姻被称为“神秘婚姻”，因为它纯粹是象征性的。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。"}, "bronzino-portrait-woman-1550": {"note": "c. 1550，意大利 佛罗伦萨。阿尼奥洛·布龙齐诺的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。", "note_en": "c. 1550, Europe. 阿尼奥洛·布龙齐诺; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1972.121. This is a painting (oil painting).", "note_html": "c. 1550，意大利 佛罗伦萨。阿尼奥洛·布龙齐诺的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。"}, "portrait-of-a-woman-1550": {"note": "勃龙齐诺是佛罗伦萨公爵科西莫一世·德·美第奇的宫廷画家。虽然无法确切辨认出这位女性的身份，但她很可能与美第奇宫廷有关系。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "Bronzino was court painter to Cosimo I de’Medici, the Duke of Florence. Though the woman cannot be definitively identified, she was likely affiliated with the Medici court.\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "勃龙齐诺是佛罗伦萨公爵科西莫一世·德·美第奇的宫廷画家。虽然无法确切辨认出这位女性的身份，但她很可能与美第奇宫廷有关系。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "hunting-with-falcons-in-a-landscape-recto-1553": {"note": "莫卧儿王朝的王子们骑着马，带着猎鹰去打猎。狩猎队伍会骑马进入野外，将猎物从灌木丛中驱赶出来。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "Mughal princes hunted on horseback with falcons. The hunting party would ride out into the wild and flush the prey from the brush.\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "莫卧儿王朝的王子们骑着马，带着猎鹰去打猎。狩猎队伍会骑马进入野外，将猎物从灌木丛中驱赶出来。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "hunting-with-falcons-in-a-landscape-verso-calligraphy-of-chagh-1553": {"note": "莫卧儿人骑着马，带着猎鹰去狩猎。狩猎队伍会骑马进入野外，驱赶猎物。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "The Mughals hunted on horseback with falcons. The hunting party would ride out into the wild and flush the prey.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "莫卧儿人骑着马，带着猎鹰去狩猎。狩猎队伍会骑马进入野外，驱赶猎物。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "cle-1962-279-129-b-1555": {"note": "假曼苏尔受审逐城（《鹦鹉故事》），1555年。南亚。蛋彩；Overall: 20.3 x 14 cm (8 x 5 1/2 in.); Painting only: 11.7 x 10 cm (4 5/8 x 3 15/16 in.)。\n\n把街巷当作舞台：行走、相遇与冲突都在同一段路发生。", "note_en": "The false Mansur punished before the judge and expelled from the city, from a Tuti-nama (Tales of a Parrot): Seventeenth Night, c. 1560. Mughal India, court of Akbar (reigned 1556–1605). Gum tempera, ink, and gold on paper; overall: 20.3 x 14 cm (8 x 5 1/2 in.); painting only: 11.7 x 10 cm (4 5/8 x 3 15/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of Mrs. A. Dean Perry, 1962.279.129.b\n\nWithin “City and Everyday Life”, under “街道”: The street is a stage: walking, meeting and conflict share one route.", "note_html": "假曼苏尔受审逐城（《鹦鹉故事》），1555年。南亚。蛋彩；Overall: 20.3 x 14 cm (8 x 5 1/2 in.); Painting only: 11.7 x 10 cm (4 5/8 x 3 15/16 in.)。\n\n把街巷当作舞台：行走、相遇与冲突都在同一段路发生。"}, "the-astrologer-predicts-a-calamity-for-the-newly-born-prince-i-1555": {"note": "鹦鹉第八夜的故事以一位印度国王为开端，这位国王在晚年终于有了一个儿子。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "The parrot’s tale on the eighth night begins with a king in India who finally had a son late in life.\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "鹦鹉第八夜的故事以一位印度国王为开端，这位国王在晚年终于有了一个儿子。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "cle-1962-279-30-a-1555": {"note": "厨娘扮侍女求恕（《鹦鹉故事》），1555年。南亚。蛋彩；Painting only: 5.2 x 10.5 cm (2 1/16 x 4 1/8 in.); Overall: 20 x 14.7 cm (7 7/8 x 5 13/16 in.)。\n\n从衣褶、发型与身体姿态，读出性别、阶层与时代。", "note_en": "The two erring cooks, dressed as maidservants, fall at the prince’s feet and beg forgiveness, from a Tuti-nama (Tales of the Parrot): Fourth Night, c. 1560. Mughal India, court of Akbar (reigned 1556–1605). Gum tempera, ink, and gold on paper; painting only: 5.2 x 10.5 cm (2 1/16 x 4 1/8 in.); overall: 20 x 14.7 cm (7 7/8 x 5 13/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of Mrs. A. Dean Perry, 1962.279.30.a\n\nWithin “Portrait and Self”, under “身体与服饰”: Fold, hair and posture reveal gender, class and period.", "note_html": "厨娘扮侍女求恕（《鹦鹉故事》），1555年。南亚。蛋彩；Painting only: 5.2 x 10.5 cm (2 1/16 x 4 1/8 in.); Overall: 20 x 14.7 cm (7 7/8 x 5 13/16 in.)。\n\n从衣褶、发型与身体姿态，读出性别、阶层与时代。"}, "the-wounded-monkey-bites-the-hand-of-the-prince-his-chessmate--1555": {"note": "这幅画描绘了鹦鹉妈妈向幼崽讲述的一个寓言故事的场景，她告诫幼崽，像它们与狐狸幼崽这样的跨物种友谊是\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "This painting depicts a scene from the cautionary tale the mother parrot tells her young to warn them that interspecies friendships, like theirs with the fox cubs, are a bad idea.\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "这幅画描绘了鹦鹉妈妈向幼崽讲述的一个寓言故事的场景，她告诫幼崽，像它们与狐狸幼崽这样的跨物种友谊是\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "portrait-of-a-woman-as-saint-catherine-1555": {"note": "亚历山大的圣凯瑟琳是一位基督徒，因拒绝按照异教罗马皇帝马克森提乌斯的旨意向偶像献祭而被殉道。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。", "note_en": "Saint Catherine of Alexandria, a Christian, was martyred for refusing to make sacrifices to idols as decreed by the pagan Roman emperor Maxentius.\n\nThe work arranges sacred figures inside a legible composition: bodies, gestures, objects and borders prescribe the order of looking. Read the centre first, then the sides and the lower edge; the image becomes a reusable language of faith.", "note_html": "亚历山大的圣凯瑟琳是一位基督徒，因拒绝按照异教罗马皇帝马克森提乌斯的旨意向偶像献祭而被殉道。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。"}, "the-handmaiden-again-pleads-for-the-death-of-the-prince-from-a-1555": {"note": "这幅描绘莫卧儿王朝早期宫廷场景的画作是该系列的最后一幅，画中侍女撒谎说王子强奸了她，并威胁说如果王子不娶她，她就自焚而亡。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "This early Mughal court scene is the last of the series in which the handmaiden lies about how the prince raped her, and she threatens to burn herself to death if he is not execute\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "这幅描绘莫卧儿王朝早期宫廷场景的画作是该系列的最后一幅，画中侍女撒谎说王子强奸了她，并威胁说如果王子不娶她，她就自焚而亡。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "the-wife-of-the-son-of-the-vizier-brings-the-magic-wooden-parr-1555": {"note": "宰相儿子的妻子与僧侣有染，僧侣坐在虎皮上，身着苦行僧的蓝色长袍。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "The wife of the vizier’s son is having an affair with the monk, who is seated on tiger skins and wearing the blue robes of a dervish.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "宰相儿子的妻子与僧侣有染，僧侣坐在虎皮上，身着苦行僧的蓝色长袍。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "the-young-prince-is-crowned-and-the-wicked-handmaiden-is-execu-1555": {"note": "在鹦鹉故事第八夜的结尾插图中，王子在音乐号角的伴奏下登基，位于构图的顶端。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "In the concluding illustration to the parrot's story on the eighth night, the prince is enthroned at the top of the composition to the accompaniment of musical fanfare.\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "在鹦鹉故事第八夜的结尾插图中，王子在音乐号角的伴奏下登基，位于构图的顶端。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "the-young-prince-recounts-his-experiences-to-his-father-the-ki-1555": {"note": "七天后，年轻的王子结束了沉默的誓言，终于能够开口说话，为自己辩护，驳斥女仆对他殴打的诬告。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "After seven days the young prince’s vow of silence has come to an end, and he is finally able to speak and defend himself against false charges of assault by the handmaiden.\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "七天后，年轻的王子结束了沉默的誓言，终于能够开口说话，为自己辩护，驳斥女仆对他殴打的诬告。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "cle-1962-279-328-a-1555": {"note": "弃妻于沙漠（《鹦鹉故事》），1555年。南亚。蛋彩；Overall: 20.3 x 14 cm (8 x 5 1/2 in.); Painting only: 7.4 x 10.3 cm (2 15/16 x 4 1/16 in.)。\n\n用空旷、行列与远行，把荒凉变成一种心理尺度。", "note_en": "King Bahram, who has married Khassa’s daughter, has her tied to a camel to be abandoned in the desert as a result of false accusations made by Khulasa, from a Tuti-nama (Tales of a Parrot): Fifty-first Night, c. 1560. Mughal India, court of Akbar (reigned 1556–1605). Gum tempera, ink, and gold on paper; overall: 20.3 x 14 cm (8 x 5 1/2 in.); painting only: 7.4 x 10.3 cm (2 15/16 x 4 1/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of Mrs. A. Dean Perry, 1962.279.328.a\n\nWithin “Landscape and Nature”, under “沙漠”: Emptiness, procession and distance give desolation a psychological scale.", "note_html": "弃妻于沙漠（《鹦鹉故事》），1555年。南亚。蛋彩；Overall: 20.3 x 14 cm (8 x 5 1/2 in.); Painting only: 7.4 x 10.3 cm (2 15/16 x 4 1/16 in.)。\n\n用空旷、行列与远行，把荒凉变成一种心理尺度。"}, "cle-1962-279-200-b-1555": {"note": "弃家入林遇豹的女子（《鹦鹉故事》），1555年。南亚。蛋彩；Overall: 20.3 x 14 cm (8 x 5 1/2 in.); Painting only: 15.6 x 10.2 cm (6 1/8 x 4 in.)。\n\n从姿态、服饰与手中物件，看女性如何被看见、也被规训。", "note_en": "A woman with two children, having abandoned her home, goes into the forest where she encounters a leopard, from a Tuti-nama (Tales of a Parrot): Thirtieth Night, c. 1560. Mughal India, court of Akbar (reigned 1556–1605). Gum tempera, ink, and gold on paper; overall: 20.3 x 14 cm (8 x 5 1/2 in.); painting only: 15.6 x 10.2 cm (6 1/8 x 4 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of Mrs. A. Dean Perry, 1962.279.200.b\n\nWithin “Portrait and Self”, under “女性”: Pose, dress and objects show how women were seen, and also regulated.", "note_html": "弃家入林遇豹的女子（《鹦鹉故事》），1555年。南亚。蛋彩；Overall: 20.3 x 14 cm (8 x 5 1/2 in.); Painting only: 15.6 x 10.2 cm (6 1/8 x 4 in.)。\n\n从姿态、服饰与手中物件，看女性如何被看见、也被规训。"}, "the-donkey-in-a-tiger-s-skin-reveals-his-identity-by-braying-a-1555": {"note": "这幅画讲述了一位商人拥有一头驴，但没有足够的钱来喂养它的故事。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "This painting illustrates a story about a merchant who owned a donkey but did not have enough money to feed him.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "这幅画讲述了一位商人拥有一头驴，但没有足够的钱来喂养它的故事。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "the-hunter-offers-the-mother-parrot-to-the-king-of-kamarupa-fr-1555": {"note": "卡马拉帕国王患有麻风病，而“卡马拉帕”的字面意思讽刺地是“情欲之躯”。猎人将捕获的母鹦鹉带给国王，向他保证这只鸟知道如何治愈他的疾病。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "The king of Kamarupa, which ironically means “body of erotic love,” had leprosy. The hunter brought the captured mother parrot to the king, assuring him that the bird knew a cure.\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "卡马拉帕国王患有麻风病，而“卡马拉帕”的字面意思讽刺地是“情欲之躯”。猎人将捕获的母鹦鹉带给国王，向他保证这只鸟知道如何治愈他的疾病。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "the-monkey-slain-his-blood-to-be-used-as-medicine-for-the-aili-1555": {"note": "被下棋的猴子咬伤后，王子的手越来越感染。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "Wounded by the chess-playing monkey’s bite, the prince’s hand became increasingly infected.\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "被下棋的猴子咬伤后，王子的手越来越感染。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "the-prince-s-ordeal-continues-he-is-ordered-away-to-be-execute-1555": {"note": "狡诈的女仆向登基的国王申诉，诬告年轻的王子侵犯了她。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "The deceptive handmaiden appeals her case to the enthroned king, falsely claiming that the young prince has assaulted her.\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "狡诈的女仆向登基的国王申诉，诬告年轻的王子侵犯了她。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "cle-1962-279-45-a-1555": {"note": "苦行僧以金象为聘（《鹦鹉故事》），1555年。南亚。蛋彩；Overall: 20.3 x 14 cm (8 x 5 1/2 in.); Painting only: 4.2 x 9.9 cm (1 5/8 x 3 7/8 in.)。\n\n让金光参与构图，材料本身承担神圣性与奢华感。", "note_en": "The dervish brings in as dowry an elephant laden with gold, from a Tuti-nama (Tales of a Parrot): Seventh Night, c. 1560. Mughal India, court of Akbar (reigned 1556–1605). Gum tempera, ink, and gold on paper; overall: 20.3 x 14 cm (8 x 5 1/2 in.); painting only: 4.2 x 9.9 cm (1 5/8 x 3 7/8 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of Mrs. A. Dean Perry, 1962.279.45.a\n\nWithin “Material and Technique”, under “金箔”: Gold participates in composition; material carries sanctity and luxury.", "note_html": "苦行僧以金象为聘（《鹦鹉故事》），1555年。南亚。蛋彩；Overall: 20.3 x 14 cm (8 x 5 1/2 in.); Painting only: 4.2 x 9.9 cm (1 5/8 x 3 7/8 in.)。\n\n让金光参与构图，材料本身承担神圣性与奢华感。"}, "cle-1962-279-97-a-1555": {"note": "街吏树下遭窃（《鹦鹉故事》），1555年。南亚。蛋彩；Overall: 20.3 x 14 cm (8 x 5 1/2 in.); Painting only: 10.5 x 10.4 cm (4 1/8 x 4 1/8 in.)。\n\n把街巷当作舞台：行走、相遇与冲突都在同一段路发生。", "note_en": "The street cleaner, on his way to meet King Bhojaraja, sleeps under a tree where four thieves disguised as fellow travelers deprive him of a priceless pearl, from a Tuti-nama (Tales of a Parrot): Twelfth Night, c. 1560. Mughal India, court of Akbar (reigned 1556–1605). Gum tempera, ink, and gold on paper; overall: 20.3 x 14 cm (8 x 5 1/2 in.); painting only: 10.5 x 10.4 cm (4 1/8 x 4 1/8 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of Mrs. A. Dean Perry, 1962.279.97.a\n\nWithin “City and Everyday Life”, under “街道”: The street is a stage: walking, meeting and conflict share one route.", "note_html": "街吏树下遭窃（《鹦鹉故事》），1555年。南亚。蛋彩；Overall: 20.3 x 14 cm (8 x 5 1/2 in.); Painting only: 10.5 x 10.4 cm (4 1/8 x 4 1/8 in.)。\n\n把街巷当作舞台：行走、相遇与冲突都在同一段路发生。"}, "portrait-of-a-kneeling-holy-man-from-the-prince-salim-album-1555": {"note": "跪着的人物是一位江湖术士，身着苏菲派神秘主义者的蓝色长袍。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "The kneeling figure is a charlatan holy man who wears the blue robe of a Sufi mystic.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "跪着的人物是一位江湖术士，身着苏菲派神秘主义者的蓝色长袍。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "cle-1962-279-240-b-1555": {"note": "马赫鲁萨嫁城尹（《鹦鹉故事》），1555年。南亚。蛋彩；Overall: 20.3 x 14 cm (8 x 5 1/2 in.); Painting only: 9.7 x 10.1 cm (3 13/16 x 4 in.)。\n\n把街巷当作舞台：行走、相遇与冲突都在同一段路发生。", "note_en": "Mahrusa’s marriage to the prefect of the city, from a Tuti-nama (Tales of a Parrot): Thirty-sixth Night, c. 1560. Mughal India, court of Akbar (reigned 1556–1605). Gum tempera, ink, and gold on paper; overall: 20.3 x 14 cm (8 x 5 1/2 in.); painting only: 9.7 x 10.1 cm (3 13/16 x 4 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of Mrs. A. Dean Perry, 1962.279.240.b\n\nWithin “City and Everyday Life”, under “街道”: The street is a stage: walking, meeting and conflict share one route.", "note_html": "马赫鲁萨嫁城尹（《鹦鹉故事》），1555年。南亚。蛋彩；Overall: 20.3 x 14 cm (8 x 5 1/2 in.); Painting only: 9.7 x 10.1 cm (3 13/16 x 4 in.)。\n\n把街巷当作舞台：行走、相遇与冲突都在同一段路发生。"}, "the-parrot-mother-cautions-her-young-on-the-danger-of-playing--1555": {"note": "有一天晚上，鹦鹉图提告诉胡贾斯塔，他希望她与新情人的关系不会像国王的医疗一样，最终不了了之。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "One night the parrot Tuti tells Khujasta that he hopes her relationship with her new lover does not wind up being only half-baked, like the medical treatment of the king of Kamarup\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "有一天晚上，鹦鹉图提告诉胡贾斯塔，他希望她与新情人的关系不会像国王的医疗一样，最终不了了之。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "the-tale-of-the-three-men-trapped-in-a-cave-by-a-rolling-bould-1555": {"note": "三个男人跪在一个黑暗洞穴的深处，他们在寻找隐藏的宝藏时被困在这里。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "Three men kneel in the bowels of a dark cave where they have been trapped while seeking hidden treasure.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "三个男人跪在一个黑暗洞穴的深处，他们在寻找隐藏的宝藏时被困在这里。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "the-deceitful-wife-ejects-the-procuress-after-blackening-her-f-1555": {"note": "这位不忠妻子的情人派了一名女信使来安排他们的幽会。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "The lover of the unfaithful wife sent a female messenger to arrange for their rendezvous.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "这位不忠妻子的情人派了一名女信使来安排他们的幽会。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "the-parrot-addresses-khujasta-at-the-beginning-of-the-eleventh-1555": {"note": "当海洋的爱人——太阳——进入其在西方的归宿，而星辰的爱人——月亮——从新娘在东方的居所走出时，胡吉\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "When the lover of the ocean—the sun—entered his place of retirement in the west and the beloved of the stars— the moon—came out of the bride’s apartment in the east, Khujasta with\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "当海洋的爱人——太阳——进入其在西方的归宿，而星辰的爱人——月亮——从新娘在东方的居所走出时，胡吉\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "the-parrot-addresses-khujasta-at-the-beginning-of-the-tenth-ni-1555": {"note": "聪明的鹦鹉图提开始向胡贾斯塔讲述一个寓意深刻的故事，故事的主角是一位商人、一位宰相的儿子和一只神奇的木制鹦鹉。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "Tuti the wise parrot begins to tell Khujasta a moralizing tale of a merchant, the son of a vizier, and a magical, wooden parrot.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "聪明的鹦鹉图提开始向胡贾斯塔讲述一个寓意深刻的故事，故事的主角是一位商人、一位宰相的儿子和一只神奇的木制鹦鹉。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "the-deceitful-wife-returns-to-her-terrace-after-caressing-her--1555": {"note": "为了说服国王不要仅仅因为女仆的指控就处死王子，国王的七位大臣各自讲述了一个故事。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "In order to convince the king that he should not have the prince executed solely on the basis of the handmaiden's accusation, the king's seven viziers each tell a story about the a\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "为了说服国王不要仅仅因为女仆的指控就处死王子，国王的七位大臣各自讲述了一个故事。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "bruegel-tower-of-babel-1563": {"note": "老彼得·勃鲁盖尔将圣经中的巴别塔描绘成一个建筑工地：塔螺旋向上，拱廊、楼梯和脚手架层层叠叠，像蚁穴一样繁忙；顶部还未封闭，红砖和灰石交替出现。在左下方，弥诺陶国王骑着马带着随从到来，而工人们还在搬运石块。老彼得·勃鲁盖尔在这座象征人类傲慢的纪念碑中填满了佛兰德日常细节，让它映射出十六世纪安特卫普的商业狂热和语言分裂的恐惧。塔像切开的一段历史：壮丽，但注定要毁灭。", "note_en": "Bruegel paints the biblical Tower of Babel as a building site: the tower spirals upward, its tiers of arcades, stairs and scaffolding swarming like an anthill; the top has not closed, and red brick alternates with grey stone. At the lower left, King Nimrod rides in with his retinue while workmen still haul blocks.\n\nBruegel fills this monument to human hubris with Flemish everyday detail, and lets it shadow the commercial fever and fear of linguistic division in sixteenth-century Antwerp. The tower is cut open like a section through history: magnificent, and doomed.", "note_html": "老彼得·勃鲁盖尔将圣经中的巴别塔描绘成一个建筑工地：塔螺旋向上，拱廊、楼梯和脚手架层层叠叠，像蚁穴一样繁忙；顶部还未封闭，红砖和灰石交替出现。在左下方，弥诺陶国王骑着马带着随从到来，而工人们还在搬运石块。老彼得·勃鲁盖尔在这座象征人类傲慢的纪念碑中填满了佛兰德日常细节，让它映射出十六世纪安特卫普的商业狂热和语言分裂的恐惧。塔像切开的一段历史：壮丽，但注定要毁灭。"}, "bruegel-hunters-in-snow-1565": {"note": "《雪中猎人》是老彼得·勃鲁盖尔一年十二个月系列中最寒冷、最宁静的一幅画。猎人和猎狗从右侧山脊下行，他们的足迹在雪地上拖出一条斜线；左边的村庄屋顶被雪压得下沉，远处的池塘上有人滑冰，灰蓝色的山脉封住了天际线。画面没有中心人物，但视线会沿着山脊、树线和冰面一直延伸到远方。\n\n老彼得·勃鲁盖尔描绘的北方冬日空气仿佛可以呼吸：铅灰色的天空、黑色的树木、脏雪。人类的形象只是风景的一部分，这种“小人物、大自然”的视角在后来的荷兰风景画和浪漫主义中得到了呼应。", "note_en": "Hunters in the Snow is the coldest and quietest panel of Bruegel's series of the months. Hunters and dogs descend a ridge from the right, their tracks dragging a diagonal line through the snow; village roofs sag under snow on the left, skaters circle a pond beyond, and grey-blue mountains close the horizon. There is no central figure, yet the eye is led along ridge, treeline and ice into the distance.\n\nBruegel paints northern winter air as something breathable: leaden sky, black trees, dirty snow. The human figures are only part of the landscape, and this \"small people, large nature\" view echoes later through Dutch landscape painting and Romanticism.", "note_html": "《雪中猎人》是老彼得·勃鲁盖尔一年十二个月系列中最寒冷、最宁静的一幅画。猎人和猎狗从右侧山脊下行，他们的足迹在雪地上拖出一条斜线；左边的村庄屋顶被雪压得下沉，远处的池塘上有人滑冰，灰蓝色的山脉封住了天际线。画面没有中心人物，但视线会沿着山脊、树线和冰面一直延伸到远方。\n\n老彼得·勃鲁盖尔描绘的北方冬日空气仿佛可以呼吸：铅灰色的天空、黑色的树木、脏雪。人类的形象只是风景的一部分，这种“小人物、大自然”的视角在后来的荷兰风景画和浪漫主义中得到了呼应。"}, "cle-1939-508-1570": {"note": "亭中授业园景，1570年。西亚·北非。纸本设色；Image: 19.8 x 13.3 cm (7 13/16 x 5 1/4 in.); Overall: 21.2 x 13.3 cm (8 3/8 x 5 1/4 in.)。\n\n把园林当作被安排的自然：亭、树、路径与视线都在说话。", "note_en": "Garden Scene with a Master Instructing a Student in a Pavilion, c. 1570–1590s. Iran, Qazvin, Safavid period (1501-1722). Opaque watercolor and ink on paper; image: 19.8 x 13.3 cm (7 13/16 x 5 1/4 in.); overall: 21.2 x 13.3 cm (8 3/8 x 5 1/4 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Purchase from the J. H. Wade Fund, 1939.508\n\nWithin “Landscape and Nature”, under “园林”: A garden is arranged nature: pavilion, tree, path and sightline all speak.", "note_html": "亭中授业园景，1570年。西亚·北非。纸本设色；Image: 19.8 x 13.3 cm (7 13/16 x 5 1/4 in.); Overall: 21.2 x 13.3 cm (8 3/8 x 5 1/4 in.)。\n\n把园林当作被安排的自然：亭、树、路径与视线都在说话。"}, "met-822698-1570": {"note": "伊斯兰画册中的一页，约创作于1570年；纸上不透明水彩和金彩，现藏于大都会艺术博物馆。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "A leaf from an Islamic album, dated about 1570; Opaque watercolor and gold on paper, in the collection of the Metropolitan Museum of Art.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "伊斯兰画册中的一页，约创作于1570年；纸上不透明水彩和金彩，现藏于大都会艺术博物馆。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "cle-2013-294-1570": {"note": "莫卧儿廷臣，1570年。南亚。蛋彩；。\n\n以礼仪、队列与身体距离，画出权力如何被日常表演。", "note_en": "A Mughal courtier, c. 1575; border added probably 1700s. Mughal India, court of Akbar (reigned 1556–1605). Gum tempera and gold on paper, mounted with gold-sprinkled borders. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift in honor of Madeline Neves Clapp; Gift of Mrs. Henry White Cannon by exchange; Bequest of Louise T. Cooper; Leonard C. Hanna Jr. Fund; From the Catherine and Ralph Benkaim Collection, 2013.294\n\nWithin “Portrait and Self”, under “宫廷人物”: Ceremony, rank and bodily distance show power performed as everyday life.", "note_html": "莫卧儿廷臣，1570年。南亚。蛋彩；。\n\n以礼仪、队列与身体距离，画出权力如何被日常表演。"}, "cle-1928-16-1571": {"note": "阿戈斯蒂诺·巴尔巴里戈肖像，1571年。欧洲。油画；Framed: 136.2 x 136.2 x 12.1 cm (53 5/8 x 53 5/8 x 4 3/4 in.); Unframed: 102.2 x 104.2 cm (40 1/4 x 41 in.)。\n\n不只看像不像，更看服饰、姿态与目光如何制造身份。", "note_en": "Portrait of Agostino Barbarigo, after c. 1571. Paolo Veronese (Italian, 1528–1588). Oil on canvas; framed: 136.2 x 136.2 x 12.1 cm (53 5/8 x 53 5/8 x 4 3/4 in.); unframed: 102.2 x 104.2 cm (40 1/4 x 41 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of Mrs. L. E. Holden, Mr. and Mrs. Guerdon S. Holden, and the L. E. Holden Fund, 1928.16\n\nWithin “Portrait and Self”, under “肖像”: Not only likeness: dress, pose and gaze manufacture identity.", "note_html": "阿戈斯蒂诺·巴尔巴里戈肖像，1571年。欧洲。油画；Framed: 136.2 x 136.2 x 12.1 cm (53 5/8 x 53 5/8 x 4 3/4 in.); Unframed: 102.2 x 104.2 cm (40 1/4 x 41 in.)。\n\n不只看像不像，更看服饰、姿态与目光如何制造身份。"}, "met-451967-1575": {"note": "伊斯兰画册中的一页，约作于1575年；纸本水墨、不透明水彩和金彩，现藏于大都会艺术博物馆。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "A leaf from an Islamic album, dated about 1575; Ink, opaque watercolor, and gold on paper, in the collection of the Metropolitan Museum of Art.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "伊斯兰画册中的一页，约作于1575年；纸本水墨、不透明水彩和金彩，现藏于大都会艺术博物馆。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "met-451969-1575": {"note": "伊斯兰画册中的一页，约作于1575年；纸本水墨、不透明水彩和金彩，现藏于大都会艺术博物馆。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "A leaf from an Islamic album, dated about 1575; Ink, opaque watercolor, and gold on paper, in the collection of the Metropolitan Museum of Art.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "伊斯兰画册中的一页，约作于1575年；纸本水墨、不透明水彩和金彩，现藏于大都会艺术博物馆。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "cle-2015-480-1575": {"note": "文人赴山寺，1575年。东亚。纸本设色；。\n\n以山体、路径与雾气组织观看，山不是背景，而是叙事的主体。", "note_en": "Chinese Literatus Traveling to a Mountain Temple, late 1500s. Kano Hidemasa (Japanese, active late 1500s). Hanging scroll; ink and light color on paper. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift from the Collection of George Gund III, 2015.480\n\nWithin “Landscape and Nature”, under “山”: Organises looking through mass, path and mist; the mountain is the subject, not the backdrop.", "note_html": "文人赴山寺，1575年。东亚。纸本设色；。\n\n以山体、路径与雾气组织观看，山不是背景，而是叙事的主体。"}, "cle-1944-494-a-1575": {"note": "波斯双联句与书法，1575年。西亚·北非。纸本设色；Overall: 31.6 x 20.4 cm (12 7/16 x 8 1/16 in.); Text area: 21 x 12.4 cm (8 1/4 x 4 7/8 in.)。\n\n把笔迹、留白与边框当成图像，阅读节奏就是视觉节奏。", "note_en": "Persian Couplets (recto), Calligraphy, Persian Verses; Single Page Manuscript, late 1500s–early 1600s. Iran, Isfahan, Safavid period (1501-1722). Ink, gold, and opaque watercolor on paper; overall: 31.6 x 20.4 cm (12 7/16 x 8 1/16 in.); text area: 21 x 12.4 cm (8 1/4 x 4 7/8 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Purchase from the J. H. Wade Fund, 1944.494.a\n\nWithin “Word and Looking”, under “书法”: Hand, blank space and border are image; reading rhythm is visual rhythm.", "note_html": "波斯双联句与书法，1575年。西亚·北非。纸本设色；Overall: 31.6 x 20.4 cm (12 7/16 x 8 1/16 in.); Text area: 21 x 12.4 cm (8 1/4 x 4 7/8 in.)。\n\n把笔迹、留白与边框当成图像，阅读节奏就是视觉节奏。"}, "met-457782-1575": {"note": "伊斯兰画册中的一页，约创作于1575年；纸本不透明水彩、墨和金，现藏于大都会艺术博物馆。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。", "note_en": "A leaf from an Islamic album, dated about 1575; Opaque watercolor, ink, and gold on paper, in the collection of the Metropolitan Museum of Art.\n\nThe work arranges sacred figures inside a legible composition: bodies, gestures, objects and borders prescribe the order of looking. Read the centre first, then the sides and the lower edge; the image becomes a reusable language of faith.", "note_html": "伊斯兰画册中的一页，约创作于1575年；纸本不透明水彩、墨和金，现藏于大都会艺术博物馆。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。"}, "su-dongpo-riding-a-donkey-1575": {"note": "苏东坡（1037–1101）是宋代杰出的诗人兼艺术家。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "Su Dongpo 蘇東坡 (1037–1101) was the leading Song dynasty poet and artist.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "苏东坡（1037–1101）是宋代杰出的诗人兼艺术家。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "met-451964-1575": {"note": "伊斯兰画册中的一页，约作于1575年；纸上不透明水彩和金彩，现藏于大都会艺术博物馆。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "A leaf from an Islamic album, dated about 1575; Opaque watercolor and gold on paper, in the collection of the Metropolitan Museum of Art.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "伊斯兰画册中的一页，约作于1575年；纸上不透明水彩和金彩，现藏于大都会艺术博物馆。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "lions-and-fox-in-a-rugged-landscape-1576": {"note": "《崎岖山景中的狮子和狐狸》，1576–1637年。罗兰·萨弗里（佛兰德斯，1576–1639）。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "Lions and Fox in a Rugged Landscape, 1576–1637. Roelant Savery (Flemish, 1576–1639).\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "《崎岖山景中的狮子和狐狸》，1576–1637年。罗兰·萨弗里（佛兰德斯，1576–1639）。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "cle-1925-985-1580": {"note": "圣母子、圣人与供养人，1580年。欧洲。木刻；。\n\n把出资者放进神圣叙事，让信仰与社会位置同时可见。", "note_en": "The Virgin and Child with Saints and a Donor (after a drawing by Girolamo da Treviso), c. 1610. Andrea Andreani (Italian, about 1558–1610), Alessandro Gandini (Italian). Chiaroscuro woodcut. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of The Print Club of Cleveland, 1925.985\n\nWithin “Portrait and Self”, under “供养人”: Places the patron inside the sacred narrative, making faith and social position visible together.", "note_html": "圣母子、圣人与供养人，1580年。欧洲。木刻；。\n\n把出资者放进神圣叙事，让信仰与社会位置同时可见。"}, "xu-wei-grapes-1580": {"note": "《墨葡萄》是徐渭大写意花鸟画的代表作。一串葡萄悬挂在藤蔓上，墨色从深到淡，笔触狂放，甚至每颗葡萄的边界几乎消失；叶子用大笔一挥，像被风撕开的纸。在右边，有一首诗：“半生坎坷，如今老矣；独坐书斋，对着晚风长啸。笔下明珠无处卖——随意抛入野葡萄藤里。”\n\n徐渭的一生波折不断：入狱、发疯、杀妻。他画葡萄是“无人要的珍珠”，也把自己画进了墨里。大写意不只是技法，更是一种把生命赌在纸上的表达。", "note_en": "Ink Grapes is the representative work of Xu Wei's grand xieyi flower painting. A cluster of grapes hangs from a vine, ink running from dark to pale, the brush wild until individual grapes almost lose their edges; leaves are swept with a broad brush like paper torn by wind. At the right, a poem: \"Half a life in failure, now an old man; alone in my study I howl at the evening wind. The bright pearls under my brush have nowhere to be sold — tossed idly into the wild vines.\"\n\nXu Wei's life was turbulent: imprisonment, madness, the killing of his wife. He painted grapes as \"pearls no one wants\" and painted himself into that ink. Grand xieyi becomes more than technique: an expression that stakes a life on paper.", "note_html": "《墨葡萄》是徐渭大写意花鸟画的代表作。一串葡萄悬挂在藤蔓上，墨色从深到淡，笔触狂放，甚至每颗葡萄的边界几乎消失；叶子用大笔一挥，像被风撕开的纸。在右边，有一首诗：“半生坎坷，如今老矣；独坐书斋，对着晚风长啸。笔下明珠无处卖——随意抛入野葡萄藤里。”\n\n徐渭的一生波折不断：入狱、发疯、杀妻。他画葡萄是“无人要的珍珠”，也把自己画进了墨里。大写意不只是技法，更是一种把生命赌在纸上的表达。"}, "cle-1940-1197-1580": {"note": "岩景中的狩猎王子，1580年。南亚。纸本设色；Image: 26.4 x 15.8 cm (10 3/8 x 6 1/4 in.); Overall: 40.5 x 26 cm (15 15/16 x 10 1/4 in.)。\n\n以山体、路径与雾气组织观看，山不是背景，而是叙事的主体。", "note_en": "Princes hunting in a rocky landscape, c. 1580–85; borders added c. 1700s. India, Mughal, 16th century. Ink, slight color, and gold on paper; image: 26.4 x 15.8 cm (10 3/8 x 6 1/4 in.); overall: 40.5 x 26 cm (15 15/16 x 10 1/4 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Edward L. Whittemore Fund, 1940.1197\n\nWithin “Landscape and Nature”, under “山”: Organises looking through mass, path and mist; the mountain is the subject, not the backdrop.", "note_html": "岩景中的狩猎王子，1580年。南亚。纸本设色；Image: 26.4 x 15.8 cm (10 3/8 x 6 1/4 in.); Overall: 40.5 x 26 cm (15 15/16 x 10 1/4 in.)。\n\n以山体、路径与雾气组织观看，山不是背景，而是叙事的主体。"}, "wild-geese-1580": {"note": "在日本，鹅的形象通常以水墨画的形式出现，始于13世纪。后来，它们出现在插图手卷的色彩斑斓的山水画中。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "Depictions of geese usually appear as ink paintings in Japan during the 1200s. They later show up in the colorful landscapes of illustrated handscrolls.\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "在日本，鹅的形象通常以水墨画的形式出现，始于13世纪。后来，它们出现在插图手卷的色彩斑斓的山水画中。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "cle-2013-298-1580": {"note": "金链公羊，1580年。南亚。蛋彩；。\n\n让金光参与构图，材料本身承担神圣性与奢华感。", "note_en": "A royal ram with a gold chain, c. 1585; border added probably 1700s. India, Mughal. Gum tempera and gold on paper. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift in honor of Madeline Neves Clapp; Gift of Mrs. Henry White Cannon by exchange; Bequest of Louise T. Cooper; Leonard C. Hanna Jr. Fund; From the Catherine and Ralph Benkaim Collection, 2013.298\n\nWithin “Material and Technique”, under “金箔”: Gold participates in composition; material carries sanctity and luxury.", "note_html": "金链公羊，1580年。南亚。蛋彩；。\n\n让金光参与构图，材料本身承担神圣性与奢华感。"}, "eighteen-views-of-huzhou-1583": {"note": "到了 16 世纪，人们对长江下游三角洲历史名胜和风景名胜的游览，推动了图文并茂的游记书籍的出版。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "By the 1500s, visits to historic and scenic sites in the lower Yangzi delta stimulated an increase of printed illustrated travel books.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "到了 16 世纪，人们对长江下游三角洲历史名胜和风景名胜的游览，推动了图文并茂的游记书籍的出版。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "cle-1998-78-5-1583": {"note": "董山（石窟山），1583年。中国。绢本设色；Sheet: 26.4 x 28.4 cm (10 3/8 x 11 3/16 in.)。\n\n以山体、路径与雾气组织观看，山不是背景，而是叙事的主体。", "note_en": "Eighteen Views of Huzhou (湖州十八景圖): Mt. Dong (Grotto Mountain) (洞山), c. 1588. Song Xu (Chinese, 1525-c. 1606). Album leaf; ink and color on silk; sheet: 26.4 x 28.4 cm (10 3/8 x 11 3/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, The Severance and Greta Millikin Purchase Fund, 1998.78.5\n\nWithin “Landscape and Nature”, under “山”: Organises looking through mass, path and mist; the mountain is the subject, not the backdrop.", "note_html": "董山（石窟山），1583年。中国。绢本设色；Sheet: 26.4 x 28.4 cm (10 3/8 x 11 3/16 in.)。\n\n以山体、路径与雾气组织观看，山不是背景，而是叙事的主体。"}, "baoyang-lake-1583": {"note": "这本山水画册描绘了中国东南部吴兴市及其周边地区的著名风景区。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "This album of landscape paintings depicts the famous scenic areas located in and around the city of Wuxing in southeastern China.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "这本山水画册描绘了中国东南部吴兴市及其周边地区的著名风景区。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "snowscape-with-figures-1584": {"note": "这幅挂轴是早期朝鲜王朝绘画中罕见的存世作品。画家金狮（1481–1537）是贵族阶层的一员，即高官显贵。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "This hanging scroll is a rare surviving example of early Joseon period painting. The painter Kim Si (1481–1537) was a member of the aristocracy, or high-ranking men.\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "这幅挂轴是早期朝鲜王朝绘画中罕见的存世作品。画家金狮（1481–1537）是贵族阶层的一员，即高官显贵。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "inp-sucevita-1586": {"note": "《苏切维察修道院：德行之梯（局部）》，1586年。欧洲。湿壁画（外墙）；壁画现场；照片像素见图像著录。\n\n补足「欧洲」区域页：《苏切维察修道院：德行之梯（局部）》以1586年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。", "note_en": "\"Istoria mânăstirii Sucevița, cunoscută prin tradiție și confirmată de cercetările arheologice, este puternic legată de numele familiei Movileștilor. Avându-și începutul într-un modest schit de lemn, atribuit călugărului Pahomie, așezarea monahală ce astăzi poartă numele de Sucevița, ia ființă printr-o biserică din zid ridicată la sfârșitul secolului al XVI-lea de Gheorghe Movilă. Cel mai mare dintre frații Movilă, acesta îmbracă haina călugărească la mânăstirea Probota, ajungând mitropolit al Moldovei. Întregul complex pe care îl reprezintă mânăstirea Sucevița impresionează prin îmbinarea armonioasă dintre arhitectură (religioasă, de apărare și civilă), pictură, sculptură (în piatră și lemn) și exemple ale artei decorative religioase. Astfel, mânăstirea face dovada continuității tradiției autohtone a veacurilor XV și XVI, reprezentând un simbol al dăinuirii în timp.\" (https://manastirea-sucevita.ro/despre/).\n\nBuilds the regional page for Europe: Mânăstirea Sucevița (sec. XVI). Scara Virtuților (detaliu) enters at 1586 with a verifiable date and medium.", "note_html": "《苏切维察修道院：德行之梯（局部）》，1586年。欧洲。湿壁画（外墙）；壁画现场；照片像素见图像著录。\n\n补足「欧洲」区域页：《苏切维察修道院：德行之梯（局部）》以1586年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。"}, "cle-1971-89-1590": {"note": "欧洲服饰场景，1590年。南亚。蛋彩；Image: 21.5 x 13.4 cm (8 7/16 x 5 1/4 in.)。\n\n从衣褶、发型与身体姿态，读出性别、阶层与时代。", "note_en": "European Costume Scene, c. 1590–1595. India, Mughal Dynasty (1526-1756). Gum tempera and gold on paper; image: 21.5 x 13.4 cm (8 7/16 x 5 1/4 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Andrew R. and Martha Holden Jennings Fund, 1971.89\n\nWithin “Portrait and Self”, under “身体与服饰”: Fold, hair and posture reveal gender, class and period.", "note_html": "欧洲服饰场景，1590年。南亚。蛋彩；Image: 21.5 x 13.4 cm (8 7/16 x 5 1/4 in.)。\n\n从衣褶、发型与身体姿态，读出性别、阶层与时代。"}, "winter-and-summer-flowers-1595": {"note": "在这幅作品中，右侧屏风后方一棵大松树下盛开着白色山茶花，左侧屏风上则有蓝色牵牛花攀附在竹子上。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "White camellias bloom behind a large pine in the right screen and blue morning glories creep through bamboo in the left screen of this composition.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "在这幅作品中，右侧屏风后方一棵大松树下盛开着白色山茶花，左侧屏风上则有蓝色牵牛花攀附在竹子上。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "jain-ascetic-walking-along-a-riverbank-1595": {"note": "这位身着白袍的耆那教僧侣左臂下夹着一本红色封面的手稿，暗示着他的智慧。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "Alluding to his wisdom, this white-clad Jain monk carries a manuscript under his left arm, bound with a red cover.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "这位身着白袍的耆那教僧侣左臂下夹着一本红色封面的手稿，暗示着他的智慧。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "a-mounted-prince-hunting-lion-in-a-rocky-landscape-1595": {"note": "一位莫卧儿王子在荒野中遇到了一只狮子，他镇定自若，一剑将其斩杀。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "A Mughal prince encounters a lion in the wilderness and, maintaining his composure, dispatches it with a single blow of his sword.\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "一位莫卧儿王子在荒野中遇到了一只狮子，他镇定自若，一剑将其斩杀。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "akbar-supervising-the-capture-of-wild-elephants-at-malwa-in-15-1596": {"note": "这幅画出自阿克巴去世前不久创作的一部传记。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "This painting is from a biography of Akbar made shortly before his death.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "这幅画出自阿克巴去世前不久创作的一部传记。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "caravaggio-judith-1599": {"note": "卡拉瓦乔将圣经中的刺杀变成了床边的谋杀。朱迪思站在右侧，一手抓着荷罗孚尼斯的头发，另一只手握着剑;她的脸皱起，眉头紧锁，厌恶与恐惧交织在一起。将军的身体在床上扭转，嘴巴张开，鲜血从脖子喷射到白色床单上。女仆阿布拉在左侧等着，手提包，神情紧张。\n\n卡拉瓦乔拒绝美化这一英雄行为：朱迪思不是寓言，而是一个施展力量、感到恐惧的女性。极端明暗对比将背景压入黑色，仅留下皮肤、亚麻布和血迹在光线中。", "note_en": "Caravaggio turns the biblical assassination into a murder at the bedside. Judith stands on the right, one hand gripping Holofernes' hair, the other holding the sword; her face recoils, brows knitted, disgust and fear together. The general's body twists on the bed, mouth open, blood jetting from the neck onto white sheets. The maid Abra waits at the left, bag in hand, tense.\n\nCaravaggio refuses to beautify the heroic act: Judith is not an allegory but a woman exerting force and feeling afraid. Extreme chiaroscuro presses the background into black, leaving only skin, linen and blood in the light.", "note_html": "卡拉瓦乔将圣经中的刺杀变成了床边的谋杀。朱迪思站在右侧，一手抓着荷罗孚尼斯的头发，另一只手握着剑;她的脸皱起，眉头紧锁，厌恶与恐惧交织在一起。将军的身体在床上扭转，嘴巴张开，鲜血从脖子喷射到白色床单上。女仆阿布拉在左侧等着，手提包，神情紧张。\n\n卡拉瓦乔拒绝美化这一英雄行为：朱迪思不是寓言，而是一个施展力量、感到恐惧的女性。极端明暗对比将背景压入黑色，仅留下皮肤、亚麻布和血迹在光线中。"}, "a-courtier-possibly-khan-alam-holding-a-spinel-and-a-deccan-sw-1600": {"note": "据阿克巴的宫廷史官记载，皇帝下令为帝国的大臣们绘制肖像。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "According to Akbar's court historian, the emperor ordered likenesses to be taken of the grandees of his realm.\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "据阿克巴的宫廷史官记载，皇帝下令为帝国的大臣们绘制肖像。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "met-825727-1600": {"note": "伊斯兰画册中的一页，约创作于1600年；纸上不透明水彩、金银颜料，现藏于大都会艺术博物馆。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "A leaf from an Islamic album, dated about 1600; Opaque watercolor, gold silver paint on paper, in the collection of the Metropolitan Museum of Art.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "伊斯兰画册中的一页，约创作于1600年；纸上不透明水彩、金银颜料，现藏于大都会艺术博物馆。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "met-453272-1600": {"note": "伊斯兰画册中的一页，约创作于1600年；纸上墨彩、不透明水彩和金彩，现藏于大都会艺术博物馆。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "A leaf from an Islamic album, dated about 1600; Ink, opaque watercolor, and gold on paper, in the collection of the Metropolitan Museum of Art.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "伊斯兰画册中的一页，约创作于1600年；纸上墨彩、不透明水彩和金彩，现藏于大都会艺术博物馆。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "page-from-the-mirror-of-holiness-mir-at-al-quds-1600": {"note": "据阿克巴的宫廷史官记载，皇帝下令为帝国的大臣们绘制肖像。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "According to Akbar's court historian, the emperor ordered likenesses to be taken of the grandees of his realm.\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "据阿克巴的宫廷史官记载，皇帝下令为帝国的大臣们绘制肖像。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "caravaggio-calling-of-matthew-1600": {"note": "《圣马太的召唤》发生在一个昏暗的罗马税吏室中。基督从右侧进入，举起手；一道光束随着他的手势，穿过桌子照在马太身上。马太坐在桌子后面，指着自己，好像在问：“是我吗？”他身旁的一个年轻人正在数钱，另外两个人继续交谈。桌子、凳子、钱袋和羽毛笔都被画得很普通。\n\n卡拉瓦乔把这个神圣的时刻置于最世俗的房间里，让光线而不是构图完成召唤。光束照亮了马太，在桌子上划出一条不可回头的线。", "note_en": "The Calling of Saint Matthew takes place in a dim Roman tax collector's room. Christ enters from the right and raises a hand; a shaft of light follows the gesture, crossing the table and landing on Matthew. Seated behind the table, Matthew points at himself as if asking, \"Who, me?\" A young man beside him counts coins, two others continue talking. Table, stool, money bag and quill are painted as ordinary objects.\n\nCaravaggio places the sacred moment in the most worldly of rooms and lets light, rather than composition, perform the calling. The beam illuminates Matthew and draws a line at the table from which there is no turning back.", "note_html": "《圣马太的召唤》发生在一个昏暗的罗马税吏室中。基督从右侧进入，举起手；一道光束随着他的手势，穿过桌子照在马太身上。马太坐在桌子后面，指着自己，好像在问：“是我吗？”他身旁的一个年轻人正在数钱，另外两个人继续交谈。桌子、凳子、钱袋和羽毛笔都被画得很普通。\n\n卡拉瓦乔把这个神圣的时刻置于最世俗的房间里，让光线而不是构图完成召唤。光束照亮了马太，在桌子上划出一条不可回头的线。"}, "crossing-at-sano-1600": {"note": "与俵屋工坊（一家位于京都的画室，经营着俵屋画廊）的许多画作一样，这幅画也是用墨、矿物颜料和金箔绘制而成，在形式上让人回想起\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "Like many paintings from the Sōtatsu studio, a Kyoto-based atelier that ran the shop Tawaraya, this one is done in ink, mineral colors, and gold, and is formally reminiscent of 12t\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "与俵屋工坊（一家位于京都的画室，经营着俵屋画廊）的许多画作一样，这幅画也是用墨、矿物颜料和金箔绘制而成，在形式上让人回想起\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "met-454343-1600": {"note": "伊斯兰画册中的一页，约创作于1600年；剪纸贴于纸上，不透明水彩和金箔，现藏于大都会艺术博物馆。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "A leaf from an Islamic album, dated about 1600; Cut paper on paper, opaque watercolor, and gold, in the collection of the Metropolitan Museum of Art.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "伊斯兰画册中的一页，约创作于1600年；剪纸贴于纸上，不透明水彩和金箔，现藏于大都会艺术博物馆。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "cle-1961-35-c-1600": {"note": "弗拉基米尔圣母像三联板，1600年。欧洲。绘画；Unframed: 6.2 x 6 x 0.5 cm (2 7/16 x 2 3/8 x 3/16 in.); Closed: 7.3 x 6.9 x 3.4 cm (2 7/8 x 2 11/16 x 1 5/16 in.); Open and extended: 7 x 19.1 cm (2 3/4 x 7 1/2 in.)。\n\n把图像放回它被使用、被围绕的空间，而不是只看单幅画面。", "note_en": "Portable Triptych Icon: Adoration of the Miracle-Working Icon of the Vladimir Mother of God, 1600s. Byzantium, Russia, Moscow?, Byzantine period, 17th century. Painted wood panel within enameled brass frame; unframed: 6.2 x 6 x 0.5 cm (2 7/16 x 2 3/8 x 3/16 in.); closed: 7.3 x 6.9 x 3.4 cm (2 7/8 x 2 11/16 x 1 5/16 in.); open and extended: 7 x 19.1 cm (2 3/4 x 7 1/2 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of Mrs. Harry F. Stratton, 1961.35.c\n\nWithin “Faith and Image”, under “仪式空间”: Restores the image to the space where it was used and surrounded, not an isolated panel.", "note_html": "弗拉基米尔圣母像三联板，1600年。欧洲。绘画；Unframed: 6.2 x 6 x 0.5 cm (2 7/16 x 2 3/8 x 3/16 in.); Closed: 7.3 x 6.9 x 3.4 cm (2 7/8 x 2 11/16 x 1 5/16 in.); Open and extended: 7 x 19.1 cm (2 3/4 x 7 1/2 in.)。\n\n把图像放回它被使用、被围绕的空间，而不是只看单幅画面。"}, "el-greco-view-of-toledo-1600": {"note": "埃尔·格列柯的《托莱多的景色》没有描绘城市最显眼的地标——大教堂，而是画出一座被风暴围困的城市。阿尔卡萨尔坐落在左侧的小山上，房顶和尖塔挤满了画面的中间，而塔霍河绕到右侧。天空占据了大部分画布，呈铅灰色和绿色翻滚，一道闪电划破天际。\n\n这更像是一幅内心的风景画，而不是地理肖像。埃尔·格列柯舍弃了意大利式的纵深感，让城市漂浮在黑夜中；建筑被拉长和扭曲，边缘模糊不清。托莱多不再是单纯的地理地点，而是信仰与衰败的象征。", "note_en": "El Greco's View of Toledo omits the city's most obvious landmark, the cathedral, and paints instead a city besieged by storm. The alcázar sits on a hill at the left, roofs and spires crowd the middle, and the Tagus bends around the right. Sky occupies most of the canvas, rolling in lead and green, a lightning bolt cracking through it.\n\nThis is less a topographic portrait than an inner landscape. El Greco abandons Italianate depth and lets the city float in night; buildings are stretched and twisted, their edges uncertain. Toledo becomes not geography but a symbol of faith and decline together.", "note_html": "埃尔·格列柯的《托莱多的景色》没有描绘城市最显眼的地标——大教堂，而是画出一座被风暴围困的城市。阿尔卡萨尔坐落在左侧的小山上，房顶和尖塔挤满了画面的中间，而塔霍河绕到右侧。天空占据了大部分画布，呈铅灰色和绿色翻滚，一道闪电划破天际。\n\n这更像是一幅内心的风景画，而不是地理肖像。埃尔·格列柯舍弃了意大利式的纵深感，让城市漂浮在黑夜中；建筑被拉长和扭曲，边缘模糊不清。托莱多不再是单纯的地理地点，而是信仰与衰败的象征。"}, "thangka-with-amitayus-1600": {"note": "这幅唐卡包含一系列来自拉贾斯坦邦的印度教俗家信徒的捐赠者肖像，他们为一座佛教寺庙赞助了这幅画。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。", "note_en": "This thangka includes a series of donor portraits of Hindu laypeople from Rajasthan, who sponsored this painting for a Buddhist temple.\n\nThe work arranges sacred figures inside a legible composition: bodies, gestures, objects and borders prescribe the order of looking. Read the centre first, then the sides and the lower edge; the image becomes a reusable language of faith.", "note_html": "这幅唐卡包含一系列来自拉贾斯坦邦的印度教俗家信徒的捐赠者肖像，他们为一座佛教寺庙赞助了这幅画。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。"}, "cle-1944-494-b-1600": {"note": "沉睡少年（单页写本插图），1600年。西亚·北非。纸本设色；Image: 21 x 12.4 cm (8 1/4 x 4 7/8 in.); Overall: 31.6 x 20.4 cm (12 7/16 x 8 1/16 in.)。\n\n让抄写、插图与装帧互相解释，书是一件被使用的整体。", "note_en": "Sleeping Youth (verso), Illustration from a Single Page Manuscript, early 1600s. Style of Riza-yi Abbasi (Iranian). Opaque watercolor and gold on paper; image: 21 x 12.4 cm (8 1/4 x 4 7/8 in.); overall: 31.6 x 20.4 cm (12 7/16 x 8 1/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Purchase from the J. H. Wade Fund, 1944.494.b\n\nWithin “Word and Looking”, under “手抄本”: Writing, illumination and binding explain one another; the book is a used object.", "note_html": "沉睡少年（单页写本插图），1600年。西亚·北非。纸本设色；Image: 21 x 12.4 cm (8 1/4 x 4 7/8 in.); Overall: 31.6 x 20.4 cm (12 7/16 x 8 1/16 in.)。\n\n让抄写、插图与装帧互相解释，书是一件被使用的整体。"}, "landscape-with-fishermen-1600": {"note": "一位渔夫身穿草编雨披，头戴宽檐帽，坐在小船上。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "Clad in a straw rain poncho and wide-brimmed hat, a fisherman is seated in a small boat.\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "一位渔夫身穿草编雨披，头戴宽檐帽，坐在小船上。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "lohan-immortal-1600": {"note": "罗汉（仙人），17世纪。西藏，汉藏风格，17世纪。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "Lohan (Immortal), 1600s. Tibet, Sino-Tibetan style, 17th century.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "罗汉（仙人），17世纪。西藏，汉藏风格，17世纪。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "christ-on-the-cross-1600": {"note": "埃尔·格列柯（西班牙语意为“希腊人”）在其故乡克里特岛接受了小幅宗教画（圣像）的绘画训练。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。", "note_en": "El Greco (Spanish for \"the Greek\") was trained on his native island, Crete, as a painter of small-scale devotional images (icons).\n\nThe work arranges sacred figures inside a legible composition: bodies, gestures, objects and borders prescribe the order of looking. Read the centre first, then the sides and the lower edge; the image becomes a reusable language of faith.", "note_html": "埃尔·格列柯（西班牙语意为“希腊人”）在其故乡克里特岛接受了小幅宗教画（圣像）的绘画训练。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。"}, "cle-2013-319-1600": {"note": "花鸟动物幻境（瓦格瓦格），1600年。南亚。蛋彩；Page: 37.6 x 26.6 cm (14 13/16 x 10 1/2 in.)。\n\n让花、鸟、兽与人物共享一张画面，观察自然如何被编排。", "note_en": "A floral fantasy of animals and birds (Waq-waq), early 1600s. Mughal India. Gum tempera and gold on paper; page: 37.6 x 26.6 cm (14 13/16 x 10 1/2 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift in honor of Madeline Neves Clapp; Gift of Mrs. Henry White Cannon by exchange; Bequest of Louise T. Cooper; Leonard C. Hanna Jr. Fund; From the Catherine and Ralph Benkaim Collection, 2013.319\n\nWithin “Landscape and Nature”, under “动植物”: Flowers, birds, beasts and people share one field; nature is edited, not copied.", "note_html": "花鸟动物幻境（瓦格瓦格），1600年。南亚。蛋彩；Page: 37.6 x 26.6 cm (14 13/16 x 10 1/2 in.)。\n\n让花、鸟、兽与人物共享一张画面，观察自然如何被编排。"}, "su-shi-so-shoku-and-pan-lang-han-r-1600": {"note": "这组屏风描绘了宋代著名诗人苏轼（公元十一世纪）和周代官员潘郎（公元十世纪）的故事片段。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "This pair of screens depicts episodes from the stories of famed Song-dynasty poets Su Shi of the 1000s and Zhou-dynasty official Pan Lang of the 900s.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "这组屏风描绘了宋代著名诗人苏轼（公元十一世纪）和周代官员潘郎（公元十世纪）的故事片段。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "isfandiyar-slays-arjasp-the-king-of-turan-from-a-shah-nama-boo-1600": {"note": "这幅插图描绘的场景发生在伊斯凡迪亚尔故事的早期，他注定要成为波斯国王，而鲁斯塔姆则是他的勇士。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "This illustrated scene occurs early in the narrative of Isfandiyar, who is destined to serve as king of Iran with Rustam as his champion.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "这幅插图描绘的场景发生在伊斯凡迪亚尔故事的早期，他注定要成为波斯国王，而鲁斯塔姆则是他的勇士。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "circumcision-ceremony-for-akbar-s-sons-painting-126-from-an-ak-1600": {"note": "本页出自一份阿克巴传记的副本，该传记于1605年阿克巴去世前不久完成。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "This page is from a copy of the biography of Akbar that was completed not long before his death in 1605.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "本页出自一份阿克巴传记的副本，该传记于1605年阿克巴去世前不久完成。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "cle-1915-680-1600": {"note": "骑马狩猎，1600年。中国。绢本设色；Painting: 276 x 147.5 cm (108 11/16 x 58 1/16 in.); Overall with knobs: 380 x 184 cm (149 5/8 x 72 7/16 in.)。\n\n让猎犬、马与猎物进入权力场景，动物也是身份道具。", "note_en": "Hunting on Horses (騎馬狩獵), c. 1600s–1700s. China, Ming dynasty (1368–1644) to Qing dynasty (1644–1911). Hanging scroll; ink and color on silk; painting: 276 x 147.5 cm (108 11/16 x 58 1/16 in.); overall with knobs: 380 x 184 cm (149 5/8 x 72 7/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of the John Huntington Art and Polytechnic Trust, 1915.680\n\nWithin “Landscape and Nature”, under “动物与宫廷”: Hounds, horses and prey enter a scene of power; animals are also status props.", "note_html": "骑马狩猎，1600年。中国。绢本设色；Painting: 276 x 147.5 cm (108 11/16 x 58 1/16 in.); Overall with knobs: 380 x 184 cm (149 5/8 x 72 7/16 in.)。\n\n让猎犬、马与猎物进入权力场景，动物也是身份道具。"}, "the-judgment-of-paris-1602": {"note": "特洛伊王子帕里斯被要求评判哪位女神最美。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "The Trojan prince Paris was asked to determine which goddess was the most beautiful.\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "特洛伊王子帕里斯被要求评判哪位女神最美。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "antelope-and-deer-hunt-1602": {"note": "莫卧儿王朝的人们在野外狩猎时会使用训练有素的猎豹（如这只戴着红色项圈的猎豹）来捕捉猎物。\n\n日常场景把城市、室内或劳作变成画面。器物、动作与衣饰这些细节，比情节更能说明当时的生活秩序。", "note_en": "The Mughals used trained cheetahs, such as this one wearing a red collar, to capture prey during hunting expeditions in the wilderness.\n\nA scene of daily life turns a city, an interior or labour into a picture. Objects, actions and clothes tell us more about the order of life than the anecdote does.", "note_html": "莫卧儿王朝的人们在野外狩猎时会使用训练有素的猎豹（如这只戴着红色项圈的猎豹）来捕捉猎物。\n\n日常场景把城市、室内或劳作变成画面。器物、动作与衣饰这些细节，比情节更能说明当时的生活秩序。"}, "illuminated-page-verso-from-a-panj-ganj-five-treasures-of-abd--1603": {"note": "这段文字摘自贾米（Jami）的诗作《优素福与祖莱哈》（Joseph and Zulaykha），以斜体书写在页边空白处，描述了祖莱哈（Zulaykha）宅邸的美景，她打算在那里勾引优素福。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "This section of text from Jami’s poem of Joseph and Zulaykha, written diagonally in the margins, describes the beauties of Zulaykha’s house, in which she intends to seduce Joseph.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "这段文字摘自贾米（Jami）的诗作《优素福与祖莱哈》（Joseph and Zulaykha），以斜体书写在页边空白处，描述了祖莱哈（Zulaykha）宅邸的美景，她打算在那里勾引优素福。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "zulaykha-in-her-palace-and-as-an-old-woman-with-joseph-from-a--1603": {"note": "这张册页的正面描绘了《优素福与祖莱卡的故事》中的两个情节。在第一幕中，祖莱卡在她为他们建造的房子里等待着约瑟。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "The recto of this album leaf illustrates two episodes from the story of Joseph and Zulaykha. In the first, Zulaykha awaits Joseph in the house she has built for them.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "这张册页的正面描绘了《优素福与祖莱卡的故事》中的两个情节。在第一幕中，祖莱卡在她为他们建造的房子里等待着约瑟。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "zulaykha-in-her-palace-and-as-an-elderly-woman-with-joseph-rec-1603": {"note": "画作底部中央的金罐中盛放着白色水仙花，预示着左侧倚靠在拐杖上的祖莱卡即将恢复青春，\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "The golden pot of white narcissus flowers at the bottom center of the painting signals that Zulaykha, leaning on her staff to the left, will imminently have her youth and beauty re\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "画作底部中央的金罐中盛放着白色水仙花，预示着左侧倚靠在拐杖上的祖莱卡即将恢复青春，\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "a-european-couple-1605": {"note": "这幅描绘一对欧洲夫妇的画作似乎源于对外国人的细致观察和记录其相貌的愿望。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "This painting of a European couple seems to be based on close observation and a desire to record the appearance of foreigners.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "这幅描绘一对欧洲夫妇的画作似乎源于对外国人的细致观察和记录其相貌的愿望。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "el-greco-christ-cross-1600": {"note": "c. 1600–1610，西班牙 托莱多。埃尔·格列柯的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。", "note_en": "c. 1600–1610, Europe. 埃尔·格列柯; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1952.222. This is a painting (oil painting).", "note_html": "c. 1600–1610，西班牙 托莱多。埃尔·格列柯的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。"}, "met-457804-1605": {"note": "伊斯兰画册中的一页，约作于1605年；黑色纸上的水粉画，带有彩色和白色拼贴，现藏于大都会艺术博物馆。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "A leaf from an Islamic album, dated about 1605; Gouache on black paper with colored and white decoupage, in the collection of the Metropolitan Museum of Art.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "伊斯兰画册中的一页，约作于1605年；黑色纸上的水粉画，带有彩色和白色拼贴，现藏于大都会艺术博物馆。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "vabhruvahana-approaches-arjuna-page-from-the-khan-khanan-s-raz-1605": {"note": "文本块的左侧是一棵树，树干呈奇特的薄荷绿色，上面栖息着鸟儿和筑有鸟蛋的鸟巢。文本块中以佩尔语描述了下方的动作。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "A tree with a whimsically mint-green trunk populated with birds and nests with eggs appears to the left of the block of text, in which the action below is described in Persian.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "文本块的左侧是一棵树，树干呈奇特的薄荷绿色，上面栖息着鸟儿和筑有鸟蛋的鸟巢。文本块中以佩尔语描述了下方的动作。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "an-ambassador-before-humayun-1605": {"note": "印度第二任莫卧儿皇帝胡马雍是巴布尔之子、阿克巴之父，他正于户外皇家营地登基。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "Humayun, the second Mughal emperor of India, son of Babur and father of Akbar, is enthroned in an outdoor royal encampment.\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "印度第二任莫卧儿皇帝胡马雍是巴布尔之子、阿克巴之父，他正于户外皇家营地登基。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "cle-2019-81-1605": {"note": "误认牛为死神的老妇（《智慧之灯》），1605年。南亚。蛋彩；Painting: 19.7 x 10.2 cm (7 3/4 x 4 in.); Framed: 38.1 x 26.7 cm (15 x 10 1/2 in.)。\n\n以遗体、葬礼与纪念物，把失去变成可共享的图像。", "note_en": "A woman mistakes a cow for the Angel of Death, from a Lights of Canopus (Anwar-i Suhaili) of Kashifi (Iranian, d. 1504), c. 1610. Mughal India, court of Jahangir (1605–1627). Gum tempera on paper; painting: 19.7 x 10.2 cm (7 3/4 x 4 in.); framed: 38.1 x 26.7 cm (15 x 10 1/2 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of Michael Silver and Deborah Lader in memory of Rabbi Daniel Jeremy Silver, 2019.81\n\nWithin “Portrait and Self”, under “死亡与记忆”: Body, funeral and memorial turn loss into a shareable image.", "note_html": "误认牛为死神的老妇（《智慧之灯》），1605年。南亚。蛋彩；Painting: 19.7 x 10.2 cm (7 3/4 x 4 in.); Framed: 38.1 x 26.7 cm (15 x 10 1/2 in.)。\n\n以遗体、葬礼与纪念物，把失去变成可共享的图像。"}, "akbar-mounting-his-horse-page-from-the-chester-beatty-akbar-na-1605": {"note": "在“nim qalam”绘画中（波斯语的字面意思是“半支笔”），构图的大部分采用单色晕染，只有少数区域采用鲜艳的色彩或点缀以\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "In nim qalam drawings, literally \"half pen\" in Persian, most of the composition is done with monochrome washes, with only a few areas brightly colored or embellished with gold.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "在“nim qalam”绘画中（波斯语的字面意思是“半支笔”），构图的大部分采用单色晕染，只有少数区域采用鲜艳的色彩或点缀以\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "cle-1945-171-1605": {"note": "马努奇赫尔与图尔之战（《列王纪》），1605年。南亚。蛋彩；Image: 12.4 x 11 cm (4 7/8 x 4 5/16 in.); Overall: 34.6 x 22.9 cm (13 5/8 x 9 in.)。\n\n不美化冲突，先看阵列、火光与逃散，再看胜利叙事如何被书写。", "note_en": "Battle between Manuchihr and Tur, from a Shah-nama (Book of Kings) of Firdausi (Persian, c. 934–1020), c. 1610. Mughal India, court of Jahangir (reigned 1605–27). Gum tempera, ink, and gold on paper; image: 12.4 x 11 cm (4 7/8 x 4 5/16 in.); overall: 34.6 x 22.9 cm (13 5/8 x 9 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Edward L. Whittemore Fund, 1945.171\n\nWithin “City and Everyday Life”, under “战争与灾难”: No glorification: formation, fire and flight first, then the writing of victory.", "note_html": "马努奇赫尔与图尔之战（《列王纪》），1605年。南亚。蛋彩；Image: 12.4 x 11 cm (4 7/8 x 4 5/16 in.); Overall: 34.6 x 22.9 cm (13 5/8 x 9 in.)。\n\n不美化冲突，先看阵列、火光与逃散，再看胜利叙事如何被书写。"}, "the-crucifixion-of-saint-andrew-1606": {"note": "公元一世纪，圣安德烈传播基督教至希腊的努力遭到了当地当局的敌视。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。", "note_en": "Saint Andrew’s efforts to introduce Christianity to Greece in the first century CE were met with hostility from local authorities.\n\nThe work arranges sacred figures inside a legible composition: bodies, gestures, objects and borders prescribe the order of looking. Read the centre first, then the sides and the lower edge; the image becomes a reusable language of faith.", "note_html": "公元一世纪，圣安德烈传播基督教至希腊的努力遭到了当地当局的敌视。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。"}, "poem-card-from-the-shinkokin-wakashu-new-collection-of-japanes-1606": {"note": "俵屋宗达和本阿弥光悦都与日本绘画的琳派的创立有关。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "Tawaraya Sotatsu and Hon’ami Koetsu are both associated with the founding of the Rimpa school of Japanese painting.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "俵屋宗达和本阿弥光悦都与日本绘画的琳派的创立有关。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "flowers-in-a-glass-1606": {"note": "安布罗修斯·博斯哈特是首批专门从事花卉绘画的艺术家之一，他可能受到了家乡植物园和科学收藏品的启发。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "One of the first artists to specialize in flower painting, Ambrosius Bosschaert may have been inspired by the botanical gardens and scientific collections in his hometown of Middel\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "安布罗修斯·博斯哈特是首批专门从事花卉绘画的艺术家之一，他可能受到了家乡植物园和科学收藏品的启发。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "summer-and-winter-landscapes-1607": {"note": "这幅构图疏朗的画作在右侧描绘了夏景，在左侧描绘了冬景。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "This sparse composition depicts a summer scene on the right and a winter scene on the left.\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "这幅构图疏朗的画作在右侧描绘了夏景，在左侧描绘了冬景。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "diana-and-her-nymphs-departing-for-the-hunt-1610": {"note": "罗马狩猎女神狄安娜额头上戴着一弯新月，这也表明她是月神。\n\n日常场景把城市、室内或劳作变成画面。器物、动作与衣饰这些细节，比情节更能说明当时的生活秩序。", "note_en": "Diana, the Roman goddess of the hunt, wears a crescent on her forehead, also identifying her as the moon goddess.\n\nA scene of daily life turns a city, an interior or labour into a picture. Objects, actions and clothes tell us more about the order of life than the anecdote does.", "note_html": "罗马狩猎女神狄安娜额头上戴着一弯新月，这也表明她是月神。\n\n日常场景把城市、室内或劳作变成画面。器物、动作与衣饰这些细节，比情节更能说明当时的生活秩序。"}, "portrait-of-king-louis-xiii-of-france-1611": {"note": "虽然十岁的路易十三已是法国国王，但他的母亲玛丽·德·美第奇仍掌有实权，直到这位少年正式成年。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "Although ten-year-old Louis XIII was king of France, his mother Marie de’ Medici remained in power until the boy officially came of age.\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "虽然十岁的路易十三已是法国国王，但他的母亲玛丽·德·美第奇仍掌有实权，直到这位少年正式成年。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "rubens-descent-from-cross-1614": {"note": "鲁本斯的《基督下十字架》，是为安特卫普大教堂创作的三联画的中央面板，展示了基督的身体沿着十字架斜滑下，被白色布料承托。亚利马太的约瑟夫和尼哥底母从上方拉拽布料，约翰在下方接住双足，圣母、抹大拉的马利亚和其他妇女跪在左侧。人物形成一个旋转的菱形，光线沿着布料和肌肉流动。\n\n鲁本斯将巴洛克的重量感、运动感和血腥感推向极致：这不是安静的哀悼，而是仍在进行中的拉拽。白色布料既是裹尸布也是反光板，让所有视线都集中在身体上。", "note_en": "Rubens's Descent from the Cross, the central panel of a triptych for Antwerp Cathedral, shows Christ's body sliding diagonally from the cross, caught in a white sheet. Joseph of Arimathea and Nicodemus haul the cloth from above, John receives the feet below, and the Virgin, Mary Magdalene and other women kneel at the left. The figures form a rotating diamond, light running along the sheet and across muscle.\n\nRubens pushes Baroque weight, motion and blood to an extreme: this is not quiet mourning but a hauling that is still under way. The white cloth is both shroud and reflector, turning every gaze towards the body.", "note_html": "鲁本斯的《基督下十字架》，是为安特卫普大教堂创作的三联画的中央面板，展示了基督的身体沿着十字架斜滑下，被白色布料承托。亚利马太的约瑟夫和尼哥底母从上方拉拽布料，约翰在下方接住双足，圣母、抹大拉的马利亚和其他妇女跪在左侧。人物形成一个旋转的菱形，光线沿着布料和肌肉流动。\n\n鲁本斯将巴洛克的重量感、运动感和血腥感推向极致：这不是安静的哀悼，而是仍在进行中的拉拽。白色布料既是裹尸布也是反光板，让所有视线都集中在身体上。"}, "the-trinity-1615": {"note": "这幅色彩鲜艳的祭坛画创作于安特卫普，这里是天主教佛兰德斯地区的宗教学习中心。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "This vividly colored altarpiece was made in Antwerp, the center of religious learning in Catholic Flanders.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "这幅色彩鲜艳的祭坛画创作于安特卫普，这里是天主教佛兰德斯地区的宗教学习中心。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "samson-and-delilah-1615": {"note": "为了报复参孙单枪匹马歼灭他们的军队，非利士人贿赂了他的情人大利拉，让她探出参孙力量的源泉：他的头发，自他出生以来从未剪过。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "In retaliation for Samson’s single-handed decimation of their army, the Philistines bribed his lover Delilah to discover the source of his strength: his hair, uncut since birth.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "为了报复参孙单枪匹马歼灭他们的军队，非利士人贿赂了他的情人大利拉，让她探出参孙力量的源泉：他的头发，自他出生以来从未剪过。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "portrait-of-a-man-1615": {"note": "这幅佚名男子的肖像画中，细致地描绘了一把细剑，这种剑通常与便装搭配，用于决斗。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "This portrait of an unknown man includes a detailed representation of a rapier, a sword worn with civilian dress and used in duels.\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "这幅佚名男子的肖像画中，细致地描绘了一把细剑，这种剑通常与便装搭配，用于决斗。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "cle-1985-279-1615": {"note": "节庆场景，1615年。东亚。纸本设色；Overall: 51.1 x 208.9 cm (20 1/8 x 82 1/4 in.)。\n\n让短暂的热闹进入图像，节庆既是娱乐，也是社会秩序的排练。", "note_en": "Festival Scenes, 1615–99. Japan, Edo period (1615–1868). Pair of six-panel folding screens; ink, color, gold, and gold leaf on paper; overall: 51.1 x 208.9 cm (20 1/8 x 82 1/4 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, The Kelvin Smith Collection, given by Mrs. Kelvin Smith, 1985.279\n\nWithin “City and Everyday Life”, under “节庆”: A brief festivity enters the image; celebration is also a rehearsal of social order.", "note_html": "节庆场景，1615年。东亚。纸本设色；Overall: 51.1 x 208.9 cm (20 1/8 x 82 1/4 in.)。\n\n让短暂的热闹进入图像，节庆既是娱乐，也是社会秩序的排练。"}, "cle-1988-16-1615": {"note": "虫祭，1615年。东亚。纸本水墨；Image: 30.7 x 45 cm (12 1/16 x 17 11/16 in.); Overall: 122.5 x 55.9 cm (48 1/4 x 22 in.)。\n\n让短暂的热闹进入图像，节庆既是娱乐，也是社会秩序的排练。", "note_en": "Festival of Insects, c. 1615–1868. After Motsurin Jōtō (Japanese, d. 1492). Hanging scroll; ink on paper; image: 30.7 x 45 cm (12 1/16 x 17 11/16 in.); overall: 122.5 x 55.9 cm (48 1/4 x 22 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Mr. and Mrs. William H. Marlatt Fund, 1988.16\n\nWithin “City and Everyday Life”, under “节庆”: A brief festivity enters the image; celebration is also a rehearsal of social order.", "note_html": "虫祭，1615年。东亚。纸本水墨；Image: 30.7 x 45 cm (12 1/16 x 17 11/16 in.); Overall: 122.5 x 55.9 cm (48 1/4 x 22 in.)。\n\n让短暂的热闹进入图像，节庆既是娱乐，也是社会秩序的排练。"}, "still-life-with-meat-fish-vegetables-and-fruit-1615": {"note": "雅各布·范·胡尔斯东克（Jacob van Hulsdonck）描绘了一系列色彩缤纷的食物和餐具，从陶制餐盘到精致的中国瓷器应有尽有，后者是一种昂贵的奢侈品，\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "Jacob van Hulsdonck depicted a colorful array of foods, and tablewares ranging from an earthenware trencher to delicate Chinese porcelain—an expensive luxury made possible by inter\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "雅各布·范·胡尔斯东克（Jacob van Hulsdonck）描绘了一系列色彩缤纷的食物和餐具，从陶制餐盘到精致的中国瓷器应有尽有，后者是一种昂贵的奢侈品，\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "saint-jerome-1616": {"note": "并非所有主体都容易识别。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。", "note_en": "Not all subjects are easy to identify.\n\nThe work arranges sacred figures inside a legible composition: bodies, gestures, objects and borders prescribe the order of looking. Read the centre first, then the sides and the lower edge; the image becomes a reusable language of faith.", "note_html": "并非所有主体都容易识别。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。"}, "ghatotkacha-and-three-demons-in-his-company-chase-bhagadatta-f-1616": {"note": "骑着大象的红色恶魔是由《战争之书》中一位主角的儿子伽陀德迦（Ghatotkacha）以魔法方式大量制造出来的。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "The red demons riding elephants were magically generated in multiples by Ghatotkacha, the son of one of the protagonists of Book of Wars .\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "骑着大象的红色恶魔是由《战争之书》中一位主角的儿子伽陀德迦（Ghatotkacha）以魔法方式大量制造出来的。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "a-charioteer-riding-through-a-rocky-landscape-with-an-entourag-1616": {"note": "驾驭战车穿越岩石地貌的驭手，随行有步兵和乐师，出自《拉兹姆·纳玛》（《战争之书》）的一页，改编自梵文《摩诃婆罗多》和\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "A charioteer riding through a rocky landscape with an entourage of footmen and musicians, page from a Razm-nama (Book of Wars) adapted from the Sanskrit Mahabharata and translated\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "驾驭战车穿越岩石地貌的驭手，随行有步兵和乐师，出自《拉兹姆·纳玛》（《战争之书》）的一页，改编自梵文《摩诃婆罗多》和\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "dohras-songs-from-the-kitab-i-nauras-of-sultan-ibrahim-adil-sh-1617": {"note": "比贾布尔苏丹易卜拉欣·阿迪勒·沙二世（1570–1627）的《瑙拉斯之书》中的多赫拉（歌曲）；正面：摘自第36首和第40首多赫拉；背面：摘自第40首和第42首多赫拉，1618年。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "Dohras (Songs) from the Kitab-i Nauras of Sultan Ibrahim Adil Shah II of Bijapur (1570–1627); recto: From Dohras 36 and 40; verso: From Dohras 40 and 42, 1618.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "比贾布尔苏丹易卜拉欣·阿迪勒·沙二世（1570–1627）的《瑙拉斯之书》中的多赫拉（歌曲）；正面：摘自第36首和第40首多赫拉；背面：摘自第40首和第42首多赫拉，1618年。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "dana-1618": {"note": "达娜厄的父亲担心一个预言会成真，即他的孙子会杀了他，因此他将女儿关了起来，以保护她免受求婚者的骚扰。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "Danaë’s father feared a prophecy that his grandson would kill him, so he imprisoned his daughter to protect her from suitors.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "达娜厄的父亲担心一个预言会成真，即他的孙子会杀了他，因此他将女儿关了起来，以保护她免受求婚者的骚扰。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "portrait-of-a-woman-possibly-elizabeth-boothby-1619": {"note": "研究表明，这幅肖像画可能描绘的是伊丽莎白·布思比（Elizabeth Boothby，1590–1658），一位伦敦知名商人的女儿。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "Research suggests that this portrait may depict Elizabeth Boothby (1590–1658), daughter of a prominent London merchant.\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "研究表明，这幅肖像画可能描绘的是伊丽莎白·布思比（Elizabeth Boothby，1590–1658），一位伦敦知名商人的女儿。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "portrait-of-isabella-brant-1620": {"note": "伊莎贝拉·勃兰特是鲁本斯的元配。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "Isabella Brant was Rubens’s first wife.\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "伊莎贝拉·勃兰特是鲁本斯的元配。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "portrait-of-a-woman-1620": {"note": "当画作有部分缺失时，该如何进行修复？\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "How do you conserve a painting when portions are missing?\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "当画作有部分缺失时，该如何进行修复？\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "artemisia-judith-1620": {"note": "阿尔特米西亚·詹蒂莱斯基的《朱迪斯斩首荷罗孚尼》比卡拉瓦乔的处理更具身体感和亲密感。朱迪斯站在床边，卷起袖子到肘部，双手用力按住将军的肩膀和头发；女仆阿布拉从上方压住他的身体，两位女性在完成一项必须完成的任务。鲜血顺着床单流下，染红了朱迪斯的袖口。\n\n画家本人在1611年的一次审判中被迫描述了一起强奸事件，这幅画常被解读为复仇之作。不管这种解读是不是有些过头，两个女性共同施力的构图在17世纪的绘画中是极其罕见的。", "note_en": "Artemisia Gentileschi's Judith Beheading Holofernes is more physical and more intimate than Caravaggio's treatment. Judith stands at the bed, sleeves pushed to the elbow, both arms bearing down on the general's shoulder and hair; the maid Abra presses his body from above, the two women completing a task that must be completed. Blood runs down the sheet and stains Judith's cuff.\n\nThe painter herself was forced to describe a rape during a 1611 trial, and the picture is often read as revenge. Whether or not that reading is pressed too far, the composition of two women exerting force together is extremely rare in seventeenth-century painting.", "note_html": "阿尔特米西亚·詹蒂莱斯基的《朱迪斯斩首荷罗孚尼》比卡拉瓦乔的处理更具身体感和亲密感。朱迪斯站在床边，卷起袖子到肘部，双手用力按住将军的肩膀和头发；女仆阿布拉从上方压住他的身体，两位女性在完成一项必须完成的任务。鲜血顺着床单流下，染红了朱迪斯的袖口。\n\n画家本人在1611年的一次审判中被迫描述了一起强奸事件，这幅画常被解读为复仇之作。不管这种解读是不是有些过头，两个女性共同施力的构图在17世纪的绘画中是极其罕见的。"}, "still-life-with-sweets-1622": {"note": "这个大胆的陈设摆放在一个简单的石台上，包括一个木盒、一个深色玻璃瓶、一些核桃、一个精美的威尼斯玻璃杯和几块名为“tur”的糖果。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "Placed on a simple stone ledge, this bold arrangement includes a wooden box, a dark glass bottle, some walnuts, an elaborate Venetian glass, and several sweets called turrones.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "这个大胆的陈设摆放在一个简单的石台上，包括一个木盒、一个深色玻璃瓶、一些核桃、一个精美的威尼斯玻璃杯和几块名为“tur”的糖果。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "a-genoese-lady-with-her-child-1623": {"note": "在17世纪之前，富裕客户的大型全身肖像通常最强调地位的象征，而非其他特质。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "Prior to the 1600s, large, full-length portraits of wealthy clients usually emphasized the trappings of status above any other qualities.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "在17世纪之前，富裕客户的大型全身肖像通常最强调地位的象征，而非其他特质。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "violin-player-with-a-wine-glass-1623": {"note": "巴布伦是乌得勒支的本土画家，他是最早将卡拉瓦乔的革命性风格引入荷兰的画家之一。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "Baburen, a native of Utrecht, was among the first to introduce Caravaggio’s revolutionary style to the Netherlands.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "巴布伦是乌得勒支的本土画家，他是最早将卡拉瓦乔的革命性风格引入荷兰的画家之一。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "rest-on-the-flight-into-egypt-1624": {"note": "乔瓦尼·弗朗切斯科·巴尔比耶里（人称“瓜尔奇诺”）创作了《逃往埃及途中的歇息》，这是一幅圆形画，在十六、十七世纪很少使用这种圆形画布。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "Giovanni Francesco Barbieri (called il Guercino) created Rest on the Flight to Egypt as a tondo, a circular canvas rarely used in the sixteenth and seventeenth centuries except in\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "乔瓦尼·弗朗切斯科·巴尔比耶里（人称“瓜尔奇诺”）创作了《逃往埃及途中的歇息》，这是一幅圆形画，在十六、十七世纪很少使用这种圆形画布。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "travelers-by-a-lake-1625": {"note": "在17世纪初之前，荷兰艺术家通常将风景画成理想化或人为的背景，以装饰更重要的宗教或神话叙事。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "Prior to the early 1600s, Dutch artists typically painted landscapes as idealized or artificial backdrops to decorate the more important religious or mythological narratives they i\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "在17世纪初之前，荷兰艺术家通常将风景画成理想化或人为的背景，以装饰更重要的宗教或神话叙事。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "cle-1970-30-1630": {"note": "岩景猎手，1630年。欧洲。油画；Framed: 159 x 201 x 12 cm (62 5/8 x 79 1/8 x 4 3/4 in.); Unframed: 127 x 175.2 cm (50 x 69 in.)。\n\n以山体、路径与雾气组织观看，山不是背景，而是叙事的主体。", "note_en": "Rocky Landscape with Hunters, c. 1635. Gaspard Dughet (French, 1615–1675). Oil on canvas; framed: 159 x 201 x 12 cm (62 5/8 x 79 1/8 x 4 3/4 in.); unframed: 127 x 175.2 cm (50 x 69 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, John L. Severance Fund, 1970.30\n\nWithin “Landscape and Nature”, under “山”: Organises looking through mass, path and mist; the mountain is the subject, not the backdrop.", "note_html": "岩景猎手，1630年。欧洲。油画；Framed: 159 x 201 x 12 cm (62 5/8 x 79 1/8 x 4 3/4 in.); Unframed: 127 x 175.2 cm (50 x 69 in.)。\n\n以山体、路径与雾气组织观看，山不是背景，而是叙事的主体。"}, "cle-2018-126-1630": {"note": "黑天与牧人跳水（《罗悉迦》），1630年。南亚。蛋彩；Page: 20.6 x 17.8 cm (8 1/8 x 7 in.)。\n\n让河流、瀑布与岸边人物共同构成时间感，水线就是画面的节拍。", "note_en": "Krishna and the Cowherds Dive into the River, from a Rasikapriya, c. 1640. Central India, Madhya Pradesh, Malwa. Gum tempera, ink, and gold on paper; page: 20.6 x 17.8 cm (8 1/8 x 7 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Purchase and partial gift from the Catherine and Ralph Benkaim Collection; Severance and Greta Millikin Purchase Fund, 2018.126\n\nWithin “Landscape and Nature”, under “水”: River, waterfall and shore figures create time; the waterline sets the rhythm.", "note_html": "黑天与牧人跳水（《罗悉迦》），1630年。南亚。蛋彩；Page: 20.6 x 17.8 cm (8 1/8 x 7 in.)。\n\n让河流、瀑布与岸边人物共同构成时间感，水线就是画面的节拍。"}, "velazquez-jester-calabazas-1632": {"note": "卡拉巴萨斯是西班牙宫廷里的弄臣；委拉斯开兹没有把他画成笑话，而是让他坐在光里，手里攥着一只小葫芦。", "note_en": "c. 1631–32, Europe. 迭戈·委拉斯开兹; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1965.15. This is a painting (oil painting).", "note_html": "卡拉巴萨斯是西班牙宫廷里的弄臣；委拉斯开兹没有把他画成笑话，而是让他坐在光里，手里攥着一只小葫芦。"}, "cle-1983-69-1634": {"note": "《熊猎》习作，1634年。欧洲。木板油画；Framed: 70.5 x 40.6 x 7.6 cm (27 3/4 x 16 x 3 in.); Unframed: 26 x 53.7 cm (10 1/4 x 21 1/8 in.)。\n\n让猎犬、马与猎物进入权力场景，动物也是身份道具。", "note_en": "Study for \"The Bear Hunt\" (for the Alcázar, Madrid), c. 1639. Peter Paul Rubens (Flemish, 1577–1640). Oil on wood; framed: 70.5 x 40.6 x 7.6 cm (27 3/4 x 16 x 3 in.); unframed: 26 x 53.7 cm (10 1/4 x 21 1/8 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Leonard C. Hanna Jr. Fund, 1983.69\n\nWithin “Landscape and Nature”, under “动物与宫廷”: Hounds, horses and prey enter a scene of power; animals are also status props.", "note_html": "《熊猎》习作，1634年。欧洲。木板油画；Framed: 70.5 x 40.6 x 7.6 cm (27 3/4 x 16 x 3 in.); Unframed: 26 x 53.7 cm (10 1/4 x 21 1/8 in.)。\n\n让猎犬、马与猎物进入权力场景，动物也是身份道具。"}, "cle-2013-289-b-1635": {"note": "书法，1635年。南亚。蛋彩；Page: 40.5 x 28.9 cm (15 15/16 x 11 3/8 in.)。\n\n把笔迹、留白与边框当成图像，阅读节奏就是视觉节奏。", "note_en": "Calligraphy, c. 1640–60. Western India, Deccan. Gum tempera, ink, and gold on paper; page: 40.5 x 28.9 cm (15 15/16 x 11 3/8 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift in honor of Madeline Neves Clapp; Gift of Mrs. Henry White Cannon by exchange; Bequest of Louise T. Cooper; Leonard C. Hanna Jr. Fund; From the Catherine and Ralph Benkaim Collection, 2013.289.b\n\nWithin “Word and Looking”, under “书法”: Hand, blank space and border are image; reading rhythm is visual rhythm.", "note_html": "书法，1635年。南亚。蛋彩；Page: 40.5 x 28.9 cm (15 15/16 x 11 3/8 in.)。\n\n把笔迹、留白与边框当成图像，阅读节奏就是视觉节奏。"}, "cle-1958-472-1635": {"note": "岩景废墟，1635年。欧洲。油画；Framed: 157.5 x 189.2 x 7 cm (62 x 74 1/2 x 2 3/4 in.); Unframed: 144 x 176.7 cm (56 11/16 x 69 9/16 in.)。\n\n以山体、路径与雾气组织观看，山不是背景，而是叙事的主体。", "note_en": "Ruins in a Rocky Landscape, c. 1640. Salvator Rosa (Italian, 1615–1673). Oil on canvas; framed: 157.5 x 189.2 x 7 cm (62 x 74 1/2 x 2 3/4 in.); unframed: 144 x 176.7 cm (56 11/16 x 69 9/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of Rosenberg & Stiebel, Inc., 1958.472\n\nWithin “Landscape and Nature”, under “山”: Organises looking through mass, path and mist; the mountain is the subject, not the backdrop.", "note_html": "岩景废墟，1635年。欧洲。油画；Framed: 157.5 x 189.2 x 7 cm (62 x 74 1/2 x 2 3/4 in.); Unframed: 144 x 176.7 cm (56 11/16 x 69 9/16 in.)。\n\n以山体、路径与雾气组织观看，山不是背景，而是叙事的主体。"}, "cle-2013-331-1640": {"note": "奥朗则布肖像日轮，1640年。南亚。蛋彩；Page: 40 x 27.7 cm (15 3/4 x 10 7/8 in.)。\n\n让光源、金底与反射参与叙事，光不是效果，而是意义。", "note_en": "Shamsa (sunburst) with portrait of Aurangzeb (1618–1707), from the Emperor's Album (the Kevorkian Album), illumination 1640–55; original portrait c. 1640–50; altered after 1658. Probably by Bichitr (Indian, active c. 1615–50). Gum tempera and gold on paper; page: 40 x 27.7 cm (15 3/4 x 10 7/8 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift in honor of Madeline Neves Clapp; Gift of Mrs. Henry White Cannon by exchange; Bequest of Louise T. Cooper; Leonard C. Hanna Jr. Fund; From the Catherine and Ralph Benkaim Collection, 2013.331\n\nWithin “Material and Technique”, under “光与材料”: Source, gold ground and reflection narrate; light is meaning, not effect.", "note_html": "奥朗则布肖像日轮，1640年。南亚。蛋彩；Page: 40 x 27.7 cm (15 3/4 x 10 7/8 in.)。\n\n让光源、金底与反射参与叙事，光不是效果，而是意义。"}, "rembrandt-night-watch-1642": {"note": "《夜巡》实际上并不是夜晚的场景。一支民兵队伍正从阿姆斯特丹的拱门里出发。队长弗朗斯·班宁克·考克穿着黑色外套，系着红色腰带，正伸手去碰他的中尉威廉·范·鲁伊滕堡的手套，中尉穿着黄色，手指着画框之外的长矛。一些人在打鼓，有些人在升旗，有些人在操纵武器；人群中间被光照到的小女孩格外显眼。\n\n伦勃朗拒绝了传统的按排排列的群像画，而是把整个队伍描绘成一个集结的瞬间。光影在队伍中流动；每个人都在动作中，每个人都被看见。后来被称为“夜巡”，那是因为上过暗色清漆；清洗后才显现出白天出发的场景。", "note_en": "The Night Watch is not actually a night scene. A militia company marches out of an Amsterdam archway. Captain Frans Banninck Cocq, in black with a red sash, reaches towards the glove of his lieutenant, Willem van Ruytenburch, who wears yellow and points a lance beyond the frame. Some men drum, some raise a flag, some handle weapons; a small girl is picked out by light in the middle of the crowd.\n\nRembrandt refuses the conventional row-by-row group portrait and paints the company as a moment of assembly. Light and shadow move through the crowd; everyone is in motion and everyone is seen. The later title \"Night Watch\" came from darkened varnish; cleaning revealed a daytime departure.", "note_html": "《夜巡》实际上并不是夜晚的场景。一支民兵队伍正从阿姆斯特丹的拱门里出发。队长弗朗斯·班宁克·考克穿着黑色外套，系着红色腰带，正伸手去碰他的中尉威廉·范·鲁伊滕堡的手套，中尉穿着黄色，手指着画框之外的长矛。一些人在打鼓，有些人在升旗，有些人在操纵武器；人群中间被光照到的小女孩格外显眼。\n\n伦勃朗拒绝了传统的按排排列的群像画，而是把整个队伍描绘成一个集结的瞬间。光影在队伍中流动；每个人都在动作中，每个人都被看见。后来被称为“夜巡”，那是因为上过暗色清漆；清洗后才显现出白天出发的场景。"}, "cle-1951-454-1645": {"note": "悔悟的圣彼得，1645年。欧洲。油画；Framed: 140.3 x 119.1 x 7 cm (55 1/4 x 46 7/8 x 2 3/4 in.); Unframed: 114 x 95 cm (44 7/8 x 37 3/8 in.)。\n\n把神圣形象放回具体信仰：先看脸、手势与光环，再读教义。", "note_en": "Saint Peter Repentant, 1645. Georges de La Tour (French, 1593–1652). Oil on canvas; framed: 140.3 x 119.1 x 7 cm (55 1/4 x 46 7/8 x 2 3/4 in.); unframed: 114 x 95 cm (44 7/8 x 37 3/8 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of the Hanna Fund, 1951.454\n\nWithin “Faith and Image”, under “神圣人物”: Puts sacred figures back into a specific faith: face, gesture and halo first, doctrine second.", "note_html": "悔悟的圣彼得，1645年。欧洲。油画；Framed: 140.3 x 119.1 x 7 cm (55 1/4 x 46 7/8 x 2 3/4 in.); Unframed: 114 x 95 cm (44 7/8 x 37 3/8 in.)。\n\n把神圣形象放回具体信仰：先看脸、手势与光环，再读教义。"}, "cle-2013-329-1645": {"note": "贾汉吉尔皇帝华盖像（另面书法），1645年。南亚。蛋彩；Page: 35.2 x 22.1 cm (13 7/8 x 8 11/16 in.)。\n\n把笔迹、留白与边框当成图像，阅读节奏就是视觉节奏。", "note_en": "Posthumous portrait of Emperor Jahangir under a canopy (recto); Calligraphy (verso), c. 1650. India, Mughal, 17th century. Gum tempera, ink, and gold on paper; page: 35.2 x 22.1 cm (13 7/8 x 8 11/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift in honor of Madeline Neves Clapp; Gift of Mrs. Henry White Cannon by exchange; Bequest of Louise T. Cooper; Leonard C. Hanna Jr. Fund; From the Catherine and Ralph Benkaim Collection, 2013.329\n\nWithin “Word and Looking”, under “书法”: Hand, blank space and border are image; reading rhythm is visual rhythm.", "note_html": "贾汉吉尔皇帝华盖像（另面书法），1645年。南亚。蛋彩；Page: 35.2 x 22.1 cm (13 7/8 x 8 11/16 in.)。\n\n把笔迹、留白与边框当成图像，阅读节奏就是视觉节奏。"}, "cle-1928-643-1647": {"note": "伦敦新宫院与钟楼，1647年。跨地域。铜版；。\n\n用时钟、月份与雨季，把抽象时间落到日常动作上。", "note_en": "Views of London:  New Palace Yard with Westminster Hall, and the Clock House, 1647. Wenceslaus Hollar (Bohemian, 1607–1677). Etching. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of The Print Club of Cleveland, 1928.643\n\nWithin “City and Everyday Life”, under “时间与日常”: Clocks, months and rain turn abstract time into everyday action.", "note_html": "伦敦新宫院与钟楼，1647年。跨地域。铜版；。\n\n用时钟、月份与雨季，把抽象时间落到日常动作上。"}, "poussin-holy-family-steps-1648": {"note": "1648，法国 巴黎。尼古拉·普桑的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。", "note_en": "1648, Europe. 尼古拉·普桑; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1981.18. This is a painting (oil painting).", "note_html": "1648，法国 巴黎。尼古拉·普桑的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。"}, "bejeweled-buddha-preaching-1648": {"note": "尼泊尔的布面宗教绘画在新瓦尔语中被称为“帕乌巴”（paubha）。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。", "note_en": "Nepalese devotional paintings on cloth are called \"paubha\" in the Newari language.\n\nThe work arranges sacred figures inside a legible composition: bodies, gestures, objects and borders prescribe the order of looking. Read the centre first, then the sides and the lower edge; the image becomes a reusable language of faith.", "note_html": "尼泊尔的布面宗教绘画在新瓦尔语中被称为“帕乌巴”（paubha）。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。"}, "cle-1981-95-1648": {"note": "阿喀琉斯拖曳赫克托耳遗体，1648年。欧洲。铜版；。\n\n从衣褶、发型与身体姿态，读出性别、阶层与时代。", "note_en": "Achilles Dragging the Body of Hector, 1648. Pietro Testa (Italian, 1612–1650). Etching. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of The Print Club of Cleveland, 1981.95\n\nWithin “Portrait and Self”, under “身体与服饰”: Fold, hair and posture reveal gender, class and period.", "note_html": "阿喀琉斯拖曳赫克托耳遗体，1648年。欧洲。铜版；。\n\n从衣褶、发型与身体姿态，读出性别、阶层与时代。"}, "cle-1982-179-34-1650": {"note": "列那狐朝圣，1650年。欧洲。铜版；。\n\n追踪摹本、复制与传教路线，看图像如何换手、换语境。", "note_en": "Reynard the Fox:  Reynard Equipped for his Pilgrimage, 1650–75. Allart van Everdingen (Dutch, 1621–1675). Etching. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of Ellen V. Kloppman in memory of her parents, Mr. and Mrs. Bernard Vixseboxse, 1982.179.34\n\nWithin “Word and Looking”, under “图像如何旅行”: Follows copies, replicas and missions to see images change hands and contexts.", "note_html": "列那狐朝圣，1650年。欧洲。铜版；。\n\n追踪摹本、复制与传教路线，看图像如何换手、换语境。"}, "cle-1943-559-1650": {"note": "地中海港口，1650年。欧洲。铜版；Sheet: 11.5 x 16.3 cm (4 1/2 x 6 7/16 in.); Platemark: 10.7 x 15.7 cm (4 3/16 x 6 3/16 in.)。\n\n以海岸、船只与远处建筑，把贸易与航行变成可看的空间。", "note_en": "A Mediterranean Harbor, 2nd half 1600s. Adrian van der Cabel (Dutch, 1631–1705), Nicolas Robert. Etching; sheet: 11.5 x 16.3 cm (4 1/2 x 6 7/16 in.); platemark: 10.7 x 15.7 cm (4 3/16 x 6 3/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Mr. and Mrs. Lewis B. Williams Collection, 1943.559\n\nWithin “Landscape and Nature”, under “海与港口”: Coast, ships and distant buildings turn trade and navigation into visible space.", "note_html": "地中海港口，1650年。欧洲。铜版；Sheet: 11.5 x 16.3 cm (4 1/2 x 6 7/16 in.); Platemark: 10.7 x 15.7 cm (4 3/16 x 6 3/16 in.)。\n\n以海岸、船只与远处建筑，把贸易与航行变成可看的空间。"}, "velazquez-las-meninas-1656": {"note": "《宫娥》将观众置于国王的视线之中。在画面的中央，小公主玛格丽塔由两位宫女照料；右边站着一个侏儒和一只半睡的狗。左边，委拉斯开兹本人站在一幅巨大的画布后面，手持画笔，胸前佩戴圣地亚哥勋章。背墙的镜子中映出了国王和王后，他们正站在观众所在的位置。\n\n通过镜子、门口和多层视线，委拉斯开兹把“谁在看谁”作为画作的主题。这既是一幅宫廷群像，也是关于绘画的画作：画家在画什么，观众站在哪里，都被留在了画框之外。", "note_en": "Las Meninas puts the viewer inside the king's gaze. At the centre, the young Infanta Margarita is attended by two maids of honour; to the right stand a dwarf and a half-awake dog. On the left, Velázquez himself works behind a huge canvas, brush in hand, the Order of Santiago on his chest. In the mirror on the back wall appear the king and queen, standing exactly where the viewer stands.\n\nWith a mirror, a doorway and several layers of gaze, Velázquez makes \"who is looking at whom\" the subject of the picture. It is at once a court group portrait and a painting about painting: what the painter is painting, and where the viewer stands, are both left outside the frame.", "note_html": "《宫娥》将观众置于国王的视线之中。在画面的中央，小公主玛格丽塔由两位宫女照料；右边站着一个侏儒和一只半睡的狗。左边，委拉斯开兹本人站在一幅巨大的画布后面，手持画笔，胸前佩戴圣地亚哥勋章。背墙的镜子中映出了国王和王后，他们正站在观众所在的位置。\n\n通过镜子、门口和多层视线，委拉斯开兹把“谁在看谁”作为画作的主题。这既是一幅宫廷群像，也是关于绘画的画作：画家在画什么，观众站在哪里，都被留在了画框之外。"}, "vermeer-view-of-delft-1660": {"note": "《代尔夫特的风景》展示了雨后的城市景象。天空占据了画布的大部分，云朵从灰蓝色变化到奶油色，阳光轻轻照在远处的屋顶和尖塔上。前景的运河和码头仍笼罩在阴影中，停靠着船只，几个人站在水边。新城的红砖和老城的灰瓦被一条水线分隔开来。\n\n维米尔用几乎看不见的笔触将光分解：屋顶不是单一的颜色，而是由数百道微小的笔触组成。后来的画家称它为世界上最美的画之一，不是因为宏伟，而是因为它让普通的城市在光影中看起来值得铭记。", "note_en": "View of Delft shows the city after rain. Sky fills most of the canvas, clouds shifting from grey-blue to cream, light touching distant roofs and spires. The canal and quay in the foreground remain in shadow, with boats moored and a few figures standing at the water's edge. Red brick of the new town and grey tile of the old are separated by a line of water.\n\nVermeer atomises light with an almost invisible touch: a roof is not a single colour but hundreds of tiny strokes. Later painters called it one of the most beautiful paintings in the world, not for grandeur but for making an ordinary city seem worth remembering in the light.", "note_html": "《代尔夫特的风景》展示了雨后的城市景象。天空占据了画布的大部分，云朵从灰蓝色变化到奶油色，阳光轻轻照在远处的屋顶和尖塔上。前景的运河和码头仍笼罩在阴影中，停靠着船只，几个人站在水边。新城的红砖和老城的灰瓦被一条水线分隔开来。\n\n维米尔用几乎看不见的笔触将光分解：屋顶不是单一的颜色，而是由数百道微小的笔触组成。后来的画家称它为世界上最美的画之一，不是因为宏伟，而是因为它让普通的城市在光影中看起来值得铭记。"}, "cle-1967-63-1660": {"note": "枯山毛榉下的低瀑，1660年。欧洲。油画；Framed: 123 x 157 x 9.5 cm (48 7/16 x 61 13/16 x 3 3/4 in.); Unframed: 99.2 x 131 cm (39 1/16 x 51 9/16 in.)。\n\n以山体、路径与雾气组织观看，山不是背景，而是叙事的主体。", "note_en": "Low Waterfall in a Wooded Landscape with a Dead Beech Tree, c. 1660–70. Jacob van Ruisdael (Dutch, 1628/29–1682). Oil on canvas; framed: 123 x 157 x 9.5 cm (48 7/16 x 61 13/16 x 3 3/4 in.); unframed: 99.2 x 131 cm (39 1/16 x 51 9/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Mr. and Mrs. William H. Marlatt Fund, 1967.63\n\nWithin “Landscape and Nature”, under “山”: Organises looking through mass, path and mist; the mountain is the subject, not the backdrop.", "note_html": "枯山毛榉下的低瀑，1660年。欧洲。油画；Framed: 123 x 157 x 9.5 cm (48 7/16 x 61 13/16 x 3 3/4 in.); Unframed: 99.2 x 131 cm (39 1/16 x 51 9/16 in.)。\n\n以山体、路径与雾气组织观看，山不是背景，而是叙事的主体。"}, "cle-2025-40-1662": {"note": "战神，1662年。中国。纸本设色；Print only: 107.9 x 54 cm (42 1/2 x 21 1/4 in.)。\n\n不美化冲突，先看阵列、火光与逃散，再看胜利叙事如何被书写。", "note_en": "The God of War (關羽), 1662–1735. China, Qing dynasty (1644–1911), Kangxi reign (1622–1722) to Yongzheng reign (1723–35). Polychrome woodblock print; ink and color on paper; print only: 107.9 x 54 cm (42 1/2 x 21 1/4 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Purchase from the J. H. Wade Fund, 2025.40\n\nWithin “City and Everyday Life”, under “战争与灾难”: No glorification: formation, fire and flight first, then the writing of victory.", "note_html": "战神，1662年。中国。纸本设色；Print only: 107.9 x 54 cm (42 1/2 x 21 1/4 in.)。\n\n不美化冲突，先看阵列、火光与逃散，再看胜利叙事如何被书写。"}, "cle-2025-68-1662": {"note": "西式版画与西文，1662年。中国。纸本水墨；28.5 x 30.3 cm (11 1/4 x 11 15/16 in.)。\n\n从刀线、墨色与复制，看图像如何离开手稿进入流通。", "note_en": "Print in Western Style with Western Text (丁氏仿泰西筆意墨線版畫), 1662–1735. Southeast China, Suzhou, Qing dynasty (1644–1911), Kangxi reign (1662–1722) to Yongzheng reign (1723–35). Woodblock print; ink on paper; 28.5 x 30.3 cm (11 1/4 x 11 15/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Purchase from the J. H. Wade Fund, 2025.68\n\nWithin “Word and Looking”, under “印刷与版画”: Knife line, ink and replication show how images leave the manuscript and circulate.", "note_html": "西式版画与西文，1662年。中国。纸本水墨；28.5 x 30.3 cm (11 1/4 x 11 15/16 in.)。\n\n从刀线、墨色与复制，看图像如何离开手稿进入流通。"}, "vermeer-girl-pearl-earring-1665": {"note": "《戴珍珠耳环的少女》是一幅类型画（类型画），而不是某位特定人物的肖像，更像是对类型和表情的练习。少女回头看向我们，嘴微张；蓝色头巾和黄色衣服形成冷暖对比，珍珠在她的脖子上捕捉到一点高光，就好像它是房间里唯一的光源。背景是一片深色，没有窗户，也没有家具。\n\n维米尔没有赋予她身份；他只呈现了被看到的瞬间，好像她正要开口说话或正要转身离开。正是这种悬而未决，使这幅画在三个多世纪里一直紧绷着观者的视线。", "note_en": "Girl with a Pearl Earring is a tronie, not a portrait of a named sitter but an exercise in type and expression. The girl turns her head back towards us, lips parted; the blue turban and yellow garment set up a cold-warm contrast, and the pearl catches a small highlight at her neck, as if it were the only light source in the room. The background is a dark field with no window, no furniture.\n\nVermeer does not give her an identity; he gives only the instant of being seen, as if she is about to speak or about to turn away. That suspension has kept the picture taut for more than three centuries.", "note_html": "《戴珍珠耳环的少女》是一幅类型画（类型画），而不是某位特定人物的肖像，更像是对类型和表情的练习。少女回头看向我们，嘴微张；蓝色头巾和黄色衣服形成冷暖对比，珍珠在她的脖子上捕捉到一点高光，就好像它是房间里唯一的光源。背景是一片深色，没有窗户，也没有家具。\n\n维米尔没有赋予她身份；他只呈现了被看到的瞬间，好像她正要开口说话或正要转身离开。正是这种悬而未决，使这幅画在三个多世纪里一直紧绷着观者的视线。"}, "cle-2018-194-1665": {"note": "持花王室女子，1665年。南亚。蛋彩；Miniature: 19.7 x 10 cm (7 3/4 x 3 15/16 in.)。\n\n从姿态、服饰与手中物件，看女性如何被看见、也被规训。", "note_en": "Royal Woman Holding a Flower, c. 1670s–80s. Northwestern India, Rajasthan, Rajput Kingdom of Bikaner. Gum tempera and gold on paper; miniature: 19.7 x 10 cm (7 3/4 x 3 15/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Purchase and partial gift from the Catherine and Ralph Benkaim Collection; Severance and Greta Millikin Purchase Fund, 2018.194\n\nWithin “Portrait and Self”, under “女性”: Pose, dress and objects show how women were seen, and also regulated.", "note_html": "持花王室女子，1665年。南亚。蛋彩；Miniature: 19.7 x 10 cm (7 3/4 x 3 15/16 in.)。\n\n从姿态、服饰与手中物件，看女性如何被看见、也被规训。"}, "cle-1955-302-8-1668": {"note": "四季山水册页H，1668年。中国。纸本设色；Overall: 21 x 15.8 cm (8 1/4 x 6 1/4 in.)。\n\n把后来者的字放在画面上，观看变成一场跨时代的对话。", "note_en": "Album of Seasonal Landscapes, Leaf H (previous leaf 8) (山水圖冊), 1668. Xiao Yuncong (Chinese, 1596–1673). Album leaf; ink and light color on paper; overall: 21 x 15.8 cm (8 1/4 x 6 1/4 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, John L. Severance Fund, 1955.302.8\n\nWithin “Word and Looking”, under “题跋”: Later hands enter the picture; looking becomes a conversation across time.", "note_html": "四季山水册页H，1668年。中国。纸本设色；Overall: 21 x 15.8 cm (8 1/4 x 6 1/4 in.)。\n\n把后来者的字放在画面上，观看变成一场跨时代的对话。"}, "rembrandt-self-portrait-1669": {"note": "《双圆自画像》是伦勃朗晚期自画像中最安静的一幅。他坐在画架前，手握画笔和调色板，转向观众；在他身后的墙上，两圈淡色的圆圈像几何练习或未完成的宣言一样被描绘着。脸部有光照，眼角和嘴角向下，皮肤已经不再年轻。\n\n伦勃朗画了数十幅自画像；这幅没有戏剧性的动作，只有一个人在自己的工作室里平静地面对衰老。那两个圆圈的意义从未得到确定；它们像未解的方程一样留在画面上。", "note_en": "Self-Portrait with Two Circles is the quietest of Rembrandt's late self-portraits. He sits at his easel with brush and palette, turning towards the viewer; on the wall behind, two circles are sketched in pale paint, like a geometry exercise or an unfinished manifesto. The face is lit, the corners of eye and mouth drawn down, the skin no longer young.\n\nRembrandt painted dozens of self-portraits; this one has no dramatic action, only a man in his studio facing old age calmly. What the two circles mean has never been settled; they leave the picture like an equation still to be solved.", "note_html": "《双圆自画像》是伦勃朗晚期自画像中最安静的一幅。他坐在画架前，手握画笔和调色板，转向观众；在他身后的墙上，两圈淡色的圆圈像几何练习或未完成的宣言一样被描绘着。脸部有光照，眼角和嘴角向下，皮肤已经不再年轻。\n\n伦勃朗画了数十幅自画像；这幅没有戏剧性的动作，只有一个人在自己的工作室里平静地面对衰老。那两个圆圈的意义从未得到确定；它们像未解的方程一样留在画面上。"}, "cbl-per-276-205-1671": {"note": "《白亭中的巴赫拉姆·古尔与伊朗公主》，1671年。中亚。纸本、墨、颜料与金箔；散页；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「中亚」区域页：《白亭中的巴赫拉姆·古尔与伊朗公主》以1671年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。", "note_en": "Bahram Gur and the Iranian princess in the white pavilion, from Seven Portraits (Haft Paykar), in the anthology of Five Poems (Khamsa), by Nizami.  \nNizami's Seven Portraits tells how prince Bahram marries seven princesses from the seven world regions, and orders a pavilion built for each bride within his palace. Following cosmic order, each world region has a specific colour, virtue, ruling planet and day of the week, and Bahram's seven pavilions are themed accordingly. Each night, he visits one princess, who tells him a story. The week ends in the white pavilion on Friday, when Bahram visits the Iranian princess, attended by her servants and musicians, and listens to her story.  \nFolio, ink, colours and gold on paper, Persian text in nasta`liq script, with painting (unsigned, attributed to Muhammad Muqim, on recto), from Seven Portraits (Haft Paykar), in the anthology Five Poems (Khamsa), by Nizami (1141-1209), copied by Mulla Barqi and Mulla `Arabshah, ordered by librarian (kitabdar) `Abd al-Rahman for Janid ruler ‘Abd al-`Aziz Bahadur Khan (r. 1647-80), Bukhara, Uzbekistan, codex (Per 276, fol. 348v) dated 15 Dhu'l-Hijja 1081, 25 April 1671.\n\nBuilds the regional page for Central Asia: Bahram Gur and the Iranian princess in the white pavilion, from Seven Portraits (Haft Paykar), in the Five Poems (Khamsa), by Nizami enters at 1671 with a verifiable date and medium.", "note_html": "《白亭中的巴赫拉姆·古尔与伊朗公主》，1671年。中亚。纸本、墨、颜料与金箔；散页；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「中亚」区域页：《白亭中的巴赫拉姆·古尔与伊朗公主》以1671年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。"}, "diptych-with-twelve-apostles-st-paul-1675": {"note": "这幅双联画（两幅画板组成的绘画）描绘了13位圣人，其尺寸适合埃塞俄比亚东正教教堂或精英人士的住宅。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。", "note_en": "Depicting 13 holy men, this diptych (two-panel painting) is sized for an Ethiopian Orthodox Christian church or elite home.\n\nThe work arranges sacred figures inside a legible composition: bodies, gestures, objects and borders prescribe the order of looking. Read the centre first, then the sides and the lower edge; the image becomes a reusable language of faith.", "note_html": "这幅双联画（两幅画板组成的绘画）描绘了13位圣人，其尺寸适合埃塞俄比亚东正教教堂或精英人士的住宅。\n\n这件作品把神圣形象放进可读的构图里：人物、手势、器物与边框共同规定观看的顺序。先看中心，再看两侧与下方，图像因而成为一套可以被重复使用的信仰语言。"}, "cle-2013-290-1675": {"note": "女子互换男装，1675年。南亚。纸本设色；Page: 33.5 x 26.7 cm (13 3/16 x 10 1/2 in.); Painting: 23.6 x 16 cm (9 5/16 x 6 5/16 in.)。\n\n从衣褶、发型与身体姿态，读出性别、阶层与时代。", "note_en": "Women playing at cross-dressing, c. 1680–1700; border added 1800s. India, Golconda, Deccan, 17th century. Ink heightened with colors on paper; page: 33.5 x 26.7 cm (13 3/16 x 10 1/2 in.); painting: 23.6 x 16 cm (9 5/16 x 6 5/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift in honor of Madeline Neves Clapp; Gift of Mrs. Henry White Cannon by exchange; Bequest of Louise T. Cooper; Leonard C. Hanna Jr. Fund; From the Catherine and Ralph Benkaim Collection, 2013.290\n\nWithin “Portrait and Self”, under “身体与服饰”: Fold, hair and posture reveal gender, class and period.", "note_html": "女子互换男装，1675年。南亚。纸本设色；Page: 33.5 x 26.7 cm (13 3/16 x 10 1/2 in.); Painting: 23.6 x 16 cm (9 5/16 x 6 5/16 in.)。\n\n从衣褶、发型与身体姿态，读出性别、阶层与时代。"}, "cle-1917-1067-1675": {"note": "廷臣米尔扎·穆伊兹肖像，1675年。南亚。纸本设色；Overall: 22 x 13.4 cm (8 11/16 x 5 1/4 in.)。\n\n以礼仪、队列与身体距离，画出权力如何被日常表演。", "note_en": "Portrait of the Courtier Mirza Muizz, c. 1680–1700. India, Mughal Dynasty (1526-1756). Color on paper; overall: 22 x 13.4 cm (8 11/16 x 5 1/4 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of the John Huntington Art and Polytechnic Trust, 1917.1067\n\nWithin “Portrait and Self”, under “宫廷人物”: Ceremony, rank and bodily distance show power performed as everyday life.", "note_html": "廷臣米尔扎·穆伊兹肖像，1675年。南亚。纸本设色；Overall: 22 x 13.4 cm (8 11/16 x 5 1/4 in.)。\n\n以礼仪、队列与身体距离，画出权力如何被日常表演。"}, "cle-1971-1-1675": {"note": "教堂内部，1675年。欧洲。油画；Framed: 89.5 x 80.5 x 6.5 cm (35 1/4 x 31 11/16 x 2 9/16 in.); Unframed: 62 x 54 cm (24 7/16 x 21 1/4 in.)。\n\n把教堂、剧场与房间当作观看装置，空间本身也在叙事。", "note_en": "Interior of a Church, c. 1680. Emanuel de Witte (Dutch, c. 1617–1692). Oil on canvas; framed: 89.5 x 80.5 x 6.5 cm (35 1/4 x 31 11/16 x 2 9/16 in.); unframed: 62 x 54 cm (24 7/16 x 21 1/4 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Mr. and Mrs. William H. Marlatt Fund, 1971.1\n\nWithin “City and Everyday Life”, under “日常空间”: Church, theatre and room are viewing devices; space itself narrates.", "note_html": "教堂内部，1675年。欧洲。油画；Framed: 89.5 x 80.5 x 6.5 cm (35 1/4 x 31 11/16 x 2 9/16 in.); Unframed: 62 x 54 cm (24 7/16 x 21 1/4 in.)。\n\n把教堂、剧场与房间当作观看装置，空间本身也在叙事。"}, "cle-2018-191-1680": {"note": "比卡内尔王阿努普·辛格接见廷臣，1680年。南亚。蛋彩；Page: 25 x 18.3 cm (9 13/16 x 7 3/16 in.); Miniature: 20 x 14.3 cm (7 7/8 x 5 5/8 in.)。\n\n以礼仪、队列与身体距离，画出权力如何被日常表演。", "note_en": "Maharaja Anup Singh of Bikaner (reigned 1669–98) Receives a Courtier, c. 1690. Ruknuddin (Indian, active c. 1666–97). Ink and gum tempera on paper; page: 25 x 18.3 cm (9 13/16 x 7 3/16 in.); miniature: 20 x 14.3 cm (7 7/8 x 5 5/8 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Purchase and partial gift from the Catherine and Ralph Benkaim Collection; Severance and Greta Millikin Purchase Fund, 2018.191\n\nWithin “Portrait and Self”, under “宫廷人物”: Ceremony, rank and bodily distance show power performed as everyday life.", "note_html": "比卡内尔王阿努普·辛格接见廷臣，1680年。南亚。蛋彩；Page: 25 x 18.3 cm (9 13/16 x 7 3/16 in.); Miniature: 20 x 14.3 cm (7 7/8 x 5 5/8 in.)。\n\n以礼仪、队列与身体距离，画出权力如何被日常表演。"}, "cle-2025-9-1680": {"note": "猴魔之战（《香格里拉罗摩衍那》），1680年。南亚。蛋彩；Page: 22.2 x 32.1 cm (8 3/4 x 12 5/8 in.)。\n\n不美化冲突，先看阵列、火光与逃散，再看胜利叙事如何被书写。", "note_en": "Battle between monkeys and demons, from the “Shangri” Ramayana, c. 1700. Northern India, Pahari kingdoms. Gum tempera and ink on paper; page: 22.2 x 32.1 cm (8 3/4 x 12 5/8 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Sundry Art - Miscellaneous Fund, 2025.9\n\nWithin “City and Everyday Life”, under “战争与灾难”: No glorification: formation, fire and flight first, then the writing of victory.", "note_html": "猴魔之战（《香格里拉罗摩衍那》），1680年。南亚。蛋彩；Page: 22.2 x 32.1 cm (8 3/4 x 12 5/8 in.)。\n\n不美化冲突，先看阵列、火光与逃散，再看胜利叙事如何被书写。"}, "cle-1955-37-6-1684": {"note": "秋山行旅（《山水册》），1684年。中国。纸本设色；Overall: 29.9 x 39.4 cm (11 3/4 x 15 1/2 in.)。\n\n追踪摹本、复制与传教路线，看图像如何换手、换语境。", "note_en": "Landscape Album in Various Styles: Traveling in Autumn Mountains, 1684. Zha Shibiao (Chinese, 1615–1698). Album leaf, ink and light color on paper; overall: 29.9 x 39.4 cm (11 3/4 x 15 1/2 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of Mr. and Mrs. Severance A. Millikin, 1955.37.6\n\nWithin “Word and Looking”, under “图像如何旅行”: Follows copies, replicas and missions to see images change hands and contexts.", "note_html": "秋山行旅（《山水册》），1684年。中国。纸本设色；Overall: 29.9 x 39.4 cm (11 3/4 x 15 1/2 in.)。\n\n追踪摹本、复制与传教路线，看图像如何换手、换语境。"}, "rijks-rp-p-1896-a-19368-655": {"note": "《使节觐见暹罗国王》，1687年。东南亚。铜版画；版画；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「东南亚」区域页：《使节觐见暹罗国王》以1687年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。", "note_en": "Gezant op audientie bij de koning van Siam (Thailand), 1687. Southeast Asia. engraving; print; dimensions not recorded.\n\nBuilds the regional page for Southeast Asia: Gezant op audientie bij de koning van Siam (Thailand) enters at 1687 with a verifiable date and medium.", "note_html": "《使节觐见暹罗国王》，1687年。东南亚。铜版画；版画；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「东南亚」区域页：《使节觐见暹罗国王》以1687年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。"}, "rijks-rp-p-1896-a-19368-659": {"note": "《暹罗亲王御舟》，1687年。东南亚。铜版画；版画；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「东南亚」区域页：《暹罗亲王御舟》以1687年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。", "note_en": "Prent rechtsboven gemerkt: Pag: 184.\n\nBuilds the regional page for Southeast Asia: Prinselijk vaartuig te Siam (Thailand) enters at 1687 with a verifiable date and medium.", "note_html": "《暹罗亲王御舟》，1687年。东南亚。铜版画；版画；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「东南亚」区域页：《暹罗亲王御舟》以1687年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。"}, "rijks-rp-p-1896-a-19368-661": {"note": "《暹罗国王在宫中观测月食》，1687年。东南亚。铜版画；版画；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「东南亚」区域页：《暹罗国王在宫中观测月食》以1687年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。", "note_en": "Prent rechtsboven gemerkt: Pag: 229.\n\nBuilds the regional page for Southeast Asia: Koning van Siam (Thailand) observeert vanuit zijn paleis de maaneclips enters at 1687 with a verifiable date and medium.", "note_html": "《暹罗国王在宫中观测月食》，1687年。东南亚。铜版画；版画；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「东南亚」区域页：《暹罗国王在宫中观测月食》以1687年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。"}, "rijks-rp-p-1896-a-19368-656": {"note": "《暹罗水乡与舟船》，1687年。东南亚。铜版画；版画；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「东南亚」区域页：《暹罗水乡与舟船》以1687年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。", "note_en": "Prent rechtsboven gemerkt: Pag: 148.\n\nBuilds the regional page for Southeast Asia: Landschap in Siam (Thailand) met boten enters at 1687 with a verifiable date and medium.", "note_html": "《暹罗水乡与舟船》，1687年。东南亚。铜版画；版画；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「东南亚」区域页：《暹罗水乡与舟船》以1687年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。"}, "rijks-rp-p-1896-a-19368-658": {"note": "《暹罗百二十桨御舟》，1687年。东南亚。铜版画；版画；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「东南亚」区域页：《暹罗百二十桨御舟》以1687年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。", "note_en": "Prent rechtsboven gemerkt: Pag: 184.\n\nBuilds the regional page for Southeast Asia: Koninklijk vaartuig met 120 roeiers te Siam (Thailand) enters at 1687 with a verifiable date and medium.", "note_html": "《暹罗百二十桨御舟》，1687年。东南亚。铜版画；版画；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「东南亚」区域页：《暹罗百二十桨御舟》以1687年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。"}, "cle-1949-227-1690": {"note": "佛教写本，1690年。南亚。蛋彩；Overall: 6.4 cm (2 1/2 in.)。\n\n让抄写、插图与装帧互相解释，书是一件被使用的整体。", "note_en": "Buddhist Manuscript, c. 1700. Sri Lanka. Covers: Gum tempera on wood; pages: charcoal on palm leaves; overall: 6.4 cm (2 1/2 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Educational Purchase Fund, 1949.227\n\nWithin “Word and Looking”, under “手抄本”: Writing, illumination and binding explain one another; the book is a used object.", "note_html": "佛教写本，1690年。南亚。蛋彩；Overall: 6.4 cm (2 1/2 in.)。\n\n让抄写、插图与装帧互相解释，书是一件被使用的整体。"}, "cbl-w-942-1-1690": {"note": "《基督割礼与西面抱婴（双面单叶）》，1690年。撒哈拉以南非洲。羊皮纸、墨与颜料；双面单叶；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「撒哈拉以南非洲」区域页：《基督割礼与西面抱婴（双面单叶）》以1690年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。", "note_en": "One of two detached folios from an Ethiopian prayer book illustrating, on the recto, the Circumcision of Christ and, on the verso, Simeon in the Temple recognizng Jesus as the messiah, painted and written on parchment in the 17th or beginning of the 18th century in Ethiopia and written in Ge'ez.\n\nBuilds the regional page for Sub-Saharan Africa: The Circumsion of Christ (recto), Simeon and the Infant Jesus (verso) from an Ethiopian prayer book enters at 1690 with a verifiable date and medium.", "note_html": "《基督割礼与西面抱婴（双面单叶）》，1690年。撒哈拉以南非洲。羊皮纸、墨与颜料；双面单叶；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「撒哈拉以南非洲」区域页：《基督割礼与西面抱婴（双面单叶）》以1690年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。"}, "cbl-w-942-2-1690": {"note": "《耶稣受难与复活（双面单叶）》，1690年。撒哈拉以南非洲。羊皮纸、墨与颜料；双面单叶；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「撒哈拉以南非洲」区域页：《耶稣受难与复活（双面单叶）》以1690年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。", "note_en": "One of two detached folios from an Ethiopian prayer book illustrating, on the recto, the Crucifixion and, on the verso, the Resurrection, painted and written on parchment in the 17th or beginning of the 18th century in Ethiopia and written in Ge'ez.\n\nBuilds the regional page for Sub-Saharan Africa: The Crucifixion (recto), The Resurrection (verso) from an Ethiopian prayer book enters at 1690 with a verifiable date and medium.", "note_html": "《耶稣受难与复活（双面单叶）》，1690年。撒哈拉以南非洲。羊皮纸、墨与颜料；双面单叶；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「撒哈拉以南非洲」区域页：《耶稣受难与复活（双面单叶）》以1690年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。"}, "cle-1975-80-1690": {"note": "英国战舰鸣炮，1690年。欧洲。油画；Framed: 91 x 103 x 4 cm (35 13/16 x 40 9/16 x 1 9/16 in.); Unframed: 63.7 x 77.5 cm (25 1/16 x 30 1/2 in.)。\n\n不美化冲突，先看阵列、火光与逃散，再看胜利叙事如何被书写。", "note_en": "English Warship Firing a Salute, 1690. Netherlands. Oil on canvas; framed: 91 x 103 x 4 cm (35 13/16 x 40 9/16 x 1 9/16 in.); unframed: 63.7 x 77.5 cm (25 1/16 x 30 1/2 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of Mr. and Mrs. Noah L. Butkin, 1975.80\n\nWithin “City and Everyday Life”, under “战争与灾难”: No glorification: formation, fire and flight first, then the writing of victory.", "note_html": "英国战舰鸣炮，1690年。欧洲。油画；Framed: 91 x 103 x 4 cm (35 13/16 x 40 9/16 x 1 9/16 in.); Unframed: 63.7 x 77.5 cm (25 1/16 x 30 1/2 in.)。\n\n不美化冲突，先看阵列、火光与逃散，再看胜利叙事如何被书写。"}, "cle-1969-65-1695": {"note": "大象素描，1695年。南亚。纸本水墨；Image: 12.8 x 18.1 cm (5 1/16 x 7 1/8 in.); Overall: 20 x 25.3 cm (7 7/8 x 9 15/16 in.)。\n\n保留修改与犹豫的痕迹，让创作过程进入成品。", "note_en": "Drawing of an Elephant, c. 1700. India, Mughal School, early 18th Century. Ink on paper; image: 12.8 x 18.1 cm (5 1/16 x 7 1/8 in.); overall: 20 x 25.3 cm (7 7/8 x 9 15/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Edward L. Whittemore Fund, 1969.65\n\nWithin “Material and Technique”, under “素描”: Corrections and hesitation remain visible; process enters the finished work.", "note_html": "大象素描，1695年。南亚。纸本水墨；Image: 12.8 x 18.1 cm (5 1/16 x 7 1/8 in.); Overall: 20 x 25.3 cm (7 7/8 x 9 15/16 in.)。\n\n保留修改与犹豫的痕迹，让创作过程进入成品。"}, "album-of-calligraphy-and-paintings-1700": {"note": "画家卞守民以描绘野雁、水和芦苇而闻名。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "The artist Bian Shoumin is known for his depiction of wild geese, water, and reeds.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "画家卞守民以描绘野雁、水和芦苇而闻名。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "landscape-after-jing-hao-and-guan-tong-1700": {"note": "在较低的斜坡上，三个人兴奋地看着瀑布下翻涌的波浪和飞溅的泡沫。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "Three figures on the lower slope excitedly watch the waves and foam rising beneath the waterfall.\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "在较低的斜坡上，三个人兴奋地看着瀑布下翻涌的波浪和飞溅的泡沫。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "cle-1997-305-1700": {"note": "文殊菩萨，1700年。南亚。手抄本；Overall: 57.6 x 42.4 cm (22 11/16 x 16 11/16 in.)。\n\n把神圣形象放回具体信仰：先看脸、手势与光环，再读教义。", "note_en": "Bodhisattva Manjushri, early 1700s. Tibet, 18th century. Ink and slight color on cotton; overall: 57.6 x 42.4 cm (22 11/16 x 16 11/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Bequest of Lillian M. Kern, 1997.305\n\nWithin “Faith and Image”, under “神圣人物”: Puts sacred figures back into a specific faith: face, gesture and halo first, doctrine second.", "note_html": "文殊菩萨，1700年。南亚。手抄本；Overall: 57.6 x 42.4 cm (22 11/16 x 16 11/16 in.)。\n\n把神圣形象放回具体信仰：先看脸、手势与光环，再读教义。"}, "cle-2017-65-1700": {"note": "杨贵妃出浴，1700年。中国。绢本设色；Painting only: 96.5 x 44.1 cm (38 x 17 3/8 in.); Overall with knobs: 231.8 x 73 cm (91 1/4 x 28 3/4 in.)。\n\n以绢、纸的吸墨与反光，决定线条和颜色的呼吸。", "note_en": "Yang Guifei Leaving the Bath (楊貴妃出浴圖), 1700s. China, Qing dynasty (1644–1911). Hanging scroll; ink, colors, and gold on silk; painting only: 96.5 x 44.1 cm (38 x 17 3/8 in.); overall with knobs: 231.8 x 73 cm (91 1/4 x 28 3/4 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of The MCH Foundation, 2017.65\n\nWithin “Material and Technique”, under “绢纸”: Silk and paper decide how ink and colour breathe.", "note_html": "杨贵妃出浴，1700年。中国。绢本设色；Painting only: 96.5 x 44.1 cm (38 x 17 3/8 in.); Overall with knobs: 231.8 x 73 cm (91 1/4 x 28 3/4 in.)。\n\n以绢、纸的吸墨与反光，决定线条和颜色的呼吸。"}, "cle-2025-123-1700": {"note": "《芥子园画传》版画，1700年。中国。纸本设色；25.6 x 32.2 cm (10 1/16 x 12 11/16 in.)。\n\n从刀线、墨色与复制，看图像如何离开手稿进入流通。", "note_en": "Mustard Garden Print (芥子園畫譜), 1700–1750. China, Suzhou, Qing dynasty (1644–1911). Polychrome woodblock print; ink and color on paper; 25.6 x 32.2 cm (10 1/16 x 12 11/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Purchase from the J. H. Wade Fund, 2025.123\n\nWithin “Word and Looking”, under “印刷与版画”: Knife line, ink and replication show how images leave the manuscript and circulate.", "note_html": "《芥子园画传》版画，1700年。中国。纸本设色；25.6 x 32.2 cm (10 1/16 x 12 11/16 in.)。\n\n从刀线、墨色与复制，看图像如何离开手稿进入流通。"}, "shitao-thirty-six-peaks-1705": {"note": "《黄山三十六峰图》是石涛的一幅晚年挂轴作品，凭记忆创作完成。画面层次向上堆叠：前景有松树和茅屋，中景有巨石、溪流和云雾，高峰几乎延伸至画面顶端。干湿笔交替使用，墨色由浓黑到浅灰，如同被雾气冲洗；右上方有一段长款，记载了作画的缘由。\n\n石涛曾多次游历黄山，晚年在扬州凭记忆重绘。他并不描绘某一特定的山峰，而是将山的奇特压缩在一笔之中：山峰转折，云雾破散，树木倾斜。在他的《画语录》中，他提出了“一笔”的理念——世界由一笔开始并由这一笔维系；这幅画就是那“一笔”的可视化。", "note_en": "Thirty-six Peaks of Mount Huang Recollected is a late hanging scroll by Shitao, painted from memory. The composition stacks upward: pines and a thatched hut in the foreground, boulders, stream and cloud in the middle, peak heads receding almost to the top edge. Wet and dry brush alternate, ink running from dense black to pale grey as if washed by mist; a long inscription at the upper right records the occasion.\n\nShitao travelled through Huangshan many times and repainted it from memory in Yangzhou in old age. He does not reproduce a particular peak but compresses the mountain's strangeness into a stroke: mountains turn, clouds break, trees lean. In his Huayulu he proposed \"one-stroke\" — the world begins and is held together by a single brushstroke; this painting is that \"one\" made visible.", "note_html": "《黄山三十六峰图》是石涛的一幅晚年挂轴作品，凭记忆创作完成。画面层次向上堆叠：前景有松树和茅屋，中景有巨石、溪流和云雾，高峰几乎延伸至画面顶端。干湿笔交替使用，墨色由浓黑到浅灰，如同被雾气冲洗；右上方有一段长款，记载了作画的缘由。\n\n石涛曾多次游历黄山，晚年在扬州凭记忆重绘。他并不描绘某一特定的山峰，而是将山的奇特压缩在一笔之中：山峰转折，云雾破散，树木倾斜。在他的《画语录》中，他提出了“一笔”的理念——世界由一笔开始并由这一笔维系；这幅画就是那“一笔”的可视化。"}, "landscape-after-ni-zan-1707": {"note": "王原祁是康熙皇帝（1662–1722年在位）朝廷的官员，出生于一个艺术世家。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "Wang Yuanqi, an official in Emperor Kangxi’s (reigned 1662–1722) court, grew up in an artistic family.\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "王原祁是康熙皇帝（1662–1722年在位）朝廷的官员，出生于一个艺术世家。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "cle-2018-145-1710": {"note": "梅瓦尔王桑格拉姆·辛格二世猎虎，1710年。南亚。蛋彩；Painting: 48.3 x 53.4 cm (19 x 21 in.)。\n\n让猎犬、马与猎物进入权力场景，动物也是身份道具。", "note_en": "Maharana Sangram Singh II of Mewar (r. 1710–34) and Stages a Boar Hunt with Tigers at Sadri, c. 1720. Northwestern India, Rajasthan, Rajput Kingdom of Mewar, Udaipur. Gum tempera, ink, and gold on paper; painting: 48.3 x 53.4 cm (19 x 21 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Purchase and partial gift from the Catherine and Ralph Benkaim Collection; Severance and Greta Millikin Purchase Fund, 2018.145\n\nWithin “Landscape and Nature”, under “动物与宫廷”: Hounds, horses and prey enter a scene of power; animals are also status props.", "note_html": "梅瓦尔王桑格拉姆·辛格二世猎虎，1710年。南亚。蛋彩；Painting: 48.3 x 53.4 cm (19 x 21 in.)。\n\n让猎犬、马与猎物进入权力场景，动物也是身份道具。"}, "cle-1989-246-1713": {"note": "奇幻港口建筑与人物，1713年。欧洲。手抄本；Sheet: 18.4 x 27.2 cm (7 1/4 x 10 11/16 in.)。\n\n以船、货物与外来服饰，呈现城市与远方之间的接口。", "note_en": "Fantastic Harbor Scene with Architecture and Figures, 1713. Isaac de Moucheron (Dutch, 1667–1744). Pen and black ink and brush and gray wash with traces of blue gouache, heightened with white gouache; sheet: 18.4 x 27.2 cm (7 1/4 x 10 11/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Bequest of Mrs. Severance A. Millikin, 1989.246\n\nWithin “City and Everyday Life”, under “港口”: Ships, cargo and foreign dress show the interface between the city and elsewhere.", "note_html": "奇幻港口建筑与人物，1713年。欧洲。手抄本；Sheet: 18.4 x 27.2 cm (7 1/4 x 10 11/16 in.)。\n\n以船、货物与外来服饰，呈现城市与远方之间的接口。"}, "cle-2018-94-1715": {"note": "卡玛坎达拉闻马德瓦死讯，1715年。南亚。蛋彩；Image: 17.6 x 28.5 cm (6 15/16 x 11 1/4 in.); Page: 20.2 x 31 cm (7 15/16 x 12 3/16 in.)。\n\n以遗体、葬礼与纪念物，把失去变成可共享的图像。", "note_en": "Kamakandala dies on hearing the news of Madhava’s death, folio 19 from a Madhavanala-Kamakandala of Alam, c. 1720. Northern India, Pahari kingdoms. Gum tempera and gold on paper; image: 17.6 x 28.5 cm (6 15/16 x 11 1/4 in.); page: 20.2 x 31 cm (7 15/16 x 12 3/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Purchase and partial gift from the Catherine and Ralph Benkaim Collection; Severance and Greta Millikin Purchase Fund, 2018.94\n\nWithin “Portrait and Self”, under “死亡与记忆”: Body, funeral and memorial turn loss into a shareable image.", "note_html": "卡玛坎达拉闻马德瓦死讯，1715年。南亚。蛋彩；Image: 17.6 x 28.5 cm (6 15/16 x 11 1/4 in.); Page: 20.2 x 31 cm (7 15/16 x 12 3/16 in.)。\n\n以遗体、葬礼与纪念物，把失去变成可共享的图像。"}, "portrait-of-an-qi-1715": {"note": "肖像中的人物安岐是来自朝鲜的第二代盐商。他用自己财富的一部分来收藏艺术品。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "An Qi, the subject of the portrait, was a second-generation salt merchant from Korea. He used part of his wealth to collect art.\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "肖像中的人物安岐是来自朝鲜的第二代盐商。他用自己财富的一部分来收藏艺术品。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "watteau-romancer-study-1716": {"note": "这是华托为《说书人》准备的红粉笔习作；人物的姿态先被单独研究，再被放进一幅风俗画的关系里。", "note_en": "c. 1716, Europe. 让-安托万·华托; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1928.661. This is a drawing.", "note_html": "这是华托为《说书人》准备的红粉笔习作；人物的姿态先被单独研究，再被放进一幅风俗画的关系里。"}, "watteau-pilgrimage-cythera-1717": {"note": "《锡特拉的朝圣》描绘了一群恋人准备离开爱情之岛的场景。他们穿着丝绸和丝带，缓慢地穿过花丛和树林，走向岸边的一艘小船；维纳斯的雕像上挂满了花环，而船夫手持长篙做好了准备。人物从右到左呈起伏的线条，有的回头，有的依旧相拥。\n\n瓦托将爱情描绘成一种即将结束的氛围，而不是一个故事。这种题材，被称为“户外雅集”，融合了洛可可的轻盈感和一种难以言喻的忧郁：快乐已经在渐渐远去。", "note_en": "Pilgrimage to Cythera shows a group of lovers preparing to leave the island of love. Dressed in silk and ribbon, they move slowly through flowers and trees towards a boat at the shore; the statue of Venus is garlanded, and a boatman stands ready with his pole. The figures form a rising and falling line from right to left, some turning back, some still embracing.\n\nWatteau paints love as an atmosphere about to end rather than a story. This genre, the fête galante, carries Rococo lightness together with an indefinable melancholy: the pleasure is already receding.", "note_html": "《锡特拉的朝圣》描绘了一群恋人准备离开爱情之岛的场景。他们穿着丝绸和丝带，缓慢地穿过花丛和树林，走向岸边的一艘小船；维纳斯的雕像上挂满了花环，而船夫手持长篙做好了准备。人物从右到左呈起伏的线条，有的回头，有的依旧相拥。\n\n瓦托将爱情描绘成一种即将结束的氛围，而不是一个故事。这种题材，被称为“户外雅集”，融合了洛可可的轻盈感和一种难以言喻的忧郁：快乐已经在渐渐远去。"}, "a-vignette-of-life-on-the-frontier-1717": {"note": "焦秉真是一位主要活跃于康熙帝在位期间的宫廷画家，是这把扇子的首席画家。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。", "note_en": "Jiao Bingzhen, a court painter largely active during the reign of the Kangxi Emperor, was the senior artist on this fan.\n\nThe figure is placed in a readable pose: dress, gesture and gaze together declare an identity. A portrait does not merely record a face; it stages how a person is to be seen.", "note_html": "焦秉真是一位主要活跃于康熙帝在位期间的宫廷画家，是这把扇子的首席画家。\n\n人物被放在一个可读的姿态里：服饰、手势与目光共同说明身份。画像不只是记录长相，也在安排一个人如何被看见。"}, "cle-1982-36-1720": {"note": "圣徒引荐虔诚女子，1720年。欧洲。油画；Framed: 185 x 149 x 6.5 cm (72 13/16 x 58 11/16 x 2 9/16 in.); Unframed: 172 x 135.5 cm (67 11/16 x 53 3/8 in.)。\n\n从姿态、服饰与手中物件，看女性如何被看见、也被规训。", "note_en": "Saints Presenting a Devout Woman to the Virgin and Child, 1720s. Giovanni Battista Pittoni (Italian, 1687–1767). Oil on canvas; framed: 185 x 149 x 6.5 cm (72 13/16 x 58 11/16 x 2 9/16 in.); unframed: 172 x 135.5 cm (67 11/16 x 53 3/8 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Leonard C. Hanna Jr. Fund, 1982.36\n\nWithin “Portrait and Self”, under “女性”: Pose, dress and objects show how women were seen, and also regulated.", "note_html": "圣徒引荐虔诚女子，1720年。欧洲。油画；Framed: 185 x 149 x 6.5 cm (72 13/16 x 58 11/16 x 2 9/16 in.); Unframed: 172 x 135.5 cm (67 11/16 x 53 3/8 in.)。\n\n从姿态、服饰与手中物件，看女性如何被看见、也被规训。"}, "cle-1929-96-1726": {"note": "圣雅各的奇迹，1726年。欧洲。油画；Framed: 129.5 x 107.5 x 10.5 cm (51 x 42 5/16 x 4 1/8 in.); Unframed: 102 x 80.7 cm (40 3/16 x 31 3/4 in.)。\n\n把神圣形象放回具体信仰：先看脸、手势与光环，再读教义。", "note_en": "The Miracles of Saint James the Greater, 1726. Noël Nicolas Coypel (French, 1690–1734). Oil on canvas; framed: 129.5 x 107.5 x 10.5 cm (51 x 42 5/16 x 4 1/8 in.); unframed: 102 x 80.7 cm (40 3/16 x 31 3/4 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of Felix Wildenstein, 1929.96\n\nWithin “Faith and Image”, under “神圣人物”: Puts sacred figures back into a specific faith: face, gesture and halo first, doctrine second.", "note_html": "圣雅各的奇迹，1726年。欧洲。油画；Framed: 129.5 x 107.5 x 10.5 cm (51 x 42 5/16 x 4 1/8 in.); Unframed: 102 x 80.7 cm (40 3/16 x 31 3/4 in.)。\n\n把神圣形象放回具体信仰：先看脸、手势与光环，再读教义。"}, "castiglione-hundred-horses-1728": {"note": "《百马图》是意大利耶稣会士朱塞佩·卡斯蒂廖内在清朝宫廷绘制的手卷。百余匹马分布在草坡、溪流和树林间：有的站立，有的打滚，有的饮水，有的由牧人牵引。它们的身体通过细腻的明暗塑造，而树木、岩石和地面则保留了中国画的质感笔触和留白。\n\n卡斯蒂廖内将欧洲的透视、解剖学和明暗对比引入宫廷画，同时必须与中国的材料和观画习惯妥协。结果是混合的视觉效果：马是立体的，空间却是平面的；写实与装饰在同一卷轴中并存。", "note_en": "One Hundred Horses is a handscroll painted at the Qing court by the Italian Jesuit Giuseppe Castiglione. More than a hundred horses are dispersed across grassy slopes, streams and trees: standing, rolling, drinking, led by herdsmen. Their bodies are modelled with fine light and shade, while trees, rocks and ground retain Chinese texture strokes and reserved space.\n\nCastiglione brought European perspective, anatomy and chiaroscuro into court painting, and was obliged to compromise with Chinese materials and viewing habits. The result is a hybrid vision: horses in the round, space flat; realism and ornament in the same scroll.", "note_html": "《百马图》是意大利耶稣会士朱塞佩·卡斯蒂廖内在清朝宫廷绘制的手卷。百余匹马分布在草坡、溪流和树林间：有的站立，有的打滚，有的饮水，有的由牧人牵引。它们的身体通过细腻的明暗塑造，而树木、岩石和地面则保留了中国画的质感笔触和留白。\n\n卡斯蒂廖内将欧洲的透视、解剖学和明暗对比引入宫廷画，同时必须与中国的材料和观画习惯妥协。结果是混合的视觉效果：马是立体的，空间却是平面的；写实与装饰在同一卷轴中并存。"}, "chardin-the-ray-1728": {"note": "夏尔丹的《鳐鱼》是他于1728年为皇家艺术学院提交的展览作品，也是他对静物画的一种宣言。一条被剖开的鳐鱼挂在钩子上，银色的腹部翻开，红色的内脏溢出；左边有只猫在牡蛎壳间行走，而右边放着瓶子、罐子、刀和一块白布。所有物品都摆放在粗糙的石板上。没有神话，也没有寓意，只有厨房的气味。\n\n夏尔丹用厚重的白色高光表现鱼的湿润皮肤，并用深棕色背景将物体衬托得更突出。他让日常事物值得被注视，为库尔贝和马奈对普通事物的尊重铺平了道路。", "note_en": "Chardin's *The Ray* was his reception piece for the Royal Academy in 1728, and a manifesto for still life. A gutted ray hangs from a hook, its silver belly opened, red entrails spilling; a cat steps among oyster shells on the left, while bottles, a jar, a knife and a white cloth occupy the right. Everything sits on a rough stone ledge. There is no myth and no allegory, only the smell of a kitchen.\n\nChardin uses thick white highlights for the wet skin of the fish and a dark brown ground to push the objects forward. He makes the everyday worth looking at, preparing the way for Courbet and Manet's respect for ordinary things.", "note_html": "夏尔丹的《鳐鱼》是他于1728年为皇家艺术学院提交的展览作品，也是他对静物画的一种宣言。一条被剖开的鳐鱼挂在钩子上，银色的腹部翻开，红色的内脏溢出；左边有只猫在牡蛎壳间行走，而右边放着瓶子、罐子、刀和一块白布。所有物品都摆放在粗糙的石板上。没有神话，也没有寓意，只有厨房的气味。\n\n夏尔丹用厚重的白色高光表现鱼的湿润皮肤，并用深棕色背景将物体衬托得更突出。他让日常事物值得被注视，为库尔贝和马奈对普通事物的尊重铺平了道路。"}, "cbl-w-914-1730": {"note": "《圣母玛利亚的奇迹》，1730年。撒哈拉以南非洲。羊皮纸、墨与颜料；写本；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「撒哈拉以南非洲」区域页：《圣母玛利亚的奇迹》以1730年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。", "note_en": "Parchment codex with leather covers containing the Miracles of the Blessed Virgin Mary (Ta'amara Miriam) in Ge'ez, made in Ethiopian for Heraclius in the 18th century. The manuscript contains 48 full-page and three-quarter page paintings illustrating the various miraculous stories. \n\nThe manuscript was once part of the collection of Lady Valeria Meux (1852–1910). It was later purchased by Chester Beatty at a Sotheby's sale on 14 June 1954 (lot 16).\n\nBuilds the regional page for Sub-Saharan Africa: The Miracles of Mary (Ta'amara Miriam) enters at 1730 with a verifiable date and medium.", "note_html": "《圣母玛利亚的奇迹》，1730年。撒哈拉以南非洲。羊皮纸、墨与颜料；写本；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「撒哈拉以南非洲」区域页：《圣母玛利亚的奇迹》以1730年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。"}, "rijks-rp-p-1909-1648-1730": {"note": "《暹罗寺院风景》，1730年。东南亚。铜版画；版画；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「东南亚」区域页：《暹罗寺院风景》以1730年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。", "note_en": "Gezicht op een Thais landschap met omheind klooster. Links wordt een olifant bereden, rechts op de voorgrond lopen twee figuren met handspiegels(?). Prent rechtsboven gemerkt: II. Deel. Pag. 523.\n\nBuilds the regional page for Southeast Asia: Thais landschap met klooster enters at 1730 with a verifiable date and medium.", "note_html": "《暹罗寺院风景》，1730年。东南亚。铜版画；版画；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「东南亚」区域页：《暹罗寺院风景》以1730年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。"}, "cle-1974-6-1730": {"note": "街头神龛的礼拜者，1730年。欧洲。手抄本；Sheet: 47.7 x 37.2 cm (18 3/4 x 14 5/8 in.)。\n\n把街巷当作舞台：行走、相遇与冲突都在同一段路发生。", "note_en": "Worshippers at a Street Shrine, 1730/40. Alessandro Magnasco (Italian, 1667–1749). Brush and red-brown ink and black chalk, heightened with lead white; sheet: 47.7 x 37.2 cm (18 3/4 x 14 5/8 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Dudley P. Allen Fund, 1974.6\n\nWithin “City and Everyday Life”, under “街道”: The street is a stage: walking, meeting and conflict share one route.", "note_html": "街头神龛的礼拜者，1730年。欧洲。手抄本；Sheet: 47.7 x 37.2 cm (18 3/4 x 14 5/8 in.)。\n\n把街巷当作舞台：行走、相遇与冲突都在同一段路发生。"}, "cle-2018-197-1730": {"note": "阿拜·辛格王观秋千节，1730年。南亚。蛋彩；Painting: 29.9 x 19.4 cm (11 3/4 x 7 5/8 in.)。\n\n让短暂的热闹进入图像，节庆既是娱乐，也是社会秩序的排练。", "note_en": "Maharaja Abhai Singh of Marwar (reigned 1724–49), Equestrian, Watching Girls Swinging at the Teej Festival, c. 1740. Northwestern India, Rajasthan, Marwar region, Rajput kingdom of Jodhpur, court of Abhai Singh (reigned 1702–49). Gum tempera and gold on paper; painting: 29.9 x 19.4 cm (11 3/4 x 7 5/8 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Purchase and partial gift from the Catherine and Ralph Benkaim Collection; Severance and Greta Millikin Purchase Fund, 2018.197\n\nWithin “City and Everyday Life”, under “节庆”: A brief festivity enters the image; celebration is also a rehearsal of social order.", "note_html": "阿拜·辛格王观秋千节，1730年。南亚。蛋彩；Painting: 29.9 x 19.4 cm (11 3/4 x 7 5/8 in.)。\n\n让短暂的热闹进入图像，节庆既是娱乐，也是社会秩序的排练。"}, "chardin-kitchen-utensils-1734": {"note": "c. 1734，法国 巴黎。让-巴蒂斯特-西梅翁·夏尔丹的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。", "note_en": "c. 1734, Europe. 让-巴蒂斯特-西梅翁·夏尔丹; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1980.37. This is a painting (oil painting).", "note_html": "c. 1734，法国 巴黎。让-巴蒂斯特-西梅翁·夏尔丹的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。"}, "cle-1925-1239-5-1735": {"note": "多洛港景，1735年。欧洲。铜版；。\n\n以海岸、船只与远处建筑，把贸易与航行变成可看的空间。", "note_en": "Views:  The Harbor at Dolo, 1735–1746. Antonio Canaletto (Italian, 1697–1768). Etching. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of The Print Club of Cleveland, 1925.1239.5\n\nWithin “Landscape and Nature”, under “海与港口”: Coast, ships and distant buildings turn trade and navigation into visible space.", "note_html": "多洛港景，1735年。欧洲。铜版；。\n\n以海岸、船只与远处建筑，把贸易与航行变成可看的空间。"}, "cle-1920-1967-1735": {"note": "戴察合台帽的女子椭圆肖像，1735年。南亚。蛋彩；Overall: 9.5 x 7.4 cm (3 3/4 x 2 15/16 in.)。\n\n从姿态、服饰与手中物件，看女性如何被看见、也被规训。", "note_en": "Oval portrait of a woman in a Chaghtai hat, c. 1740–50. India, Mughal, 18th century. Gum tempera and gold on paper; overall: 9.5 x 7.4 cm (3 3/4 x 2 15/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of J. H. Wade, 1920.1967\n\nWithin “Portrait and Self”, under “女性”: Pose, dress and objects show how women were seen, and also regulated.", "note_html": "戴察合台帽的女子椭圆肖像，1735年。南亚。蛋彩；Overall: 9.5 x 7.4 cm (3 3/4 x 2 15/16 in.)。\n\n从姿态、服饰与手中物件，看女性如何被看见、也被规训。"}, "cle-1959-310-1738": {"note": "谷仓中更衣的女伶，1738年。欧洲。铜版；Platemark: 45 x 56.5 cm (17 11/16 x 22 1/4 in.); Sheet: 48.8 x 62.6 cm (19 3/16 x 24 5/8 in.)。\n\n从衣褶、发型与身体姿态，读出性别、阶层与时代。", "note_en": "Strolling Actresses Dressing in a Barn, 1738. William Hogarth (British, 1697–1764). Engraving; platemark: 45 x 56.5 cm (17 11/16 x 22 1/4 in.); sheet: 48.8 x 62.6 cm (19 3/16 x 24 5/8 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of Mr. and Mrs. Milton Curtiss Rose, 1959.310\n\nWithin “Portrait and Self”, under “身体与服饰”: Fold, hair and posture reveal gender, class and period.", "note_html": "谷仓中更衣的女伶，1738年。欧洲。铜版；Platemark: 45 x 56.5 cm (17 11/16 x 22 1/4 in.); Sheet: 48.8 x 62.6 cm (19 3/16 x 24 5/8 in.)。\n\n从衣褶、发型与身体姿态，读出性别、阶层与时代。"}, "cle-1916-1154-1740": {"note": "中村剧场内部与市川虾藏，1740年。东亚。绘画；Sheet: 40.2 x 63.7 cm (15 13/16 x 25 1/16 in.)。\n\n把教堂、剧场与房间当作观看装置，空间本身也在叙事。", "note_en": "Perspective View of the Interior of the Nakamura Theater with Ichikawa Ebizo II as Yanone Goro, 1740. Okumura Masanobu (Japanese, 1686–1764). Hand-colored woodblock print; sheet: 40.2 x 63.7 cm (15 13/16 x 25 1/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of Mr. and Mrs. J. H. Wade, 1916.1154\n\nWithin “City and Everyday Life”, under “日常空间”: Church, theatre and room are viewing devices; space itself narrates.", "note_html": "中村剧场内部与市川虾藏，1740年。东亚。绘画；Sheet: 40.2 x 63.7 cm (15 13/16 x 25 1/16 in.)。\n\n把教堂、剧场与房间当作观看装置，空间本身也在叙事。"}, "cbl-w-912-1740": {"note": "《马太与马可福音》，1740年。撒哈拉以南非洲。羊皮纸、墨与颜料；写本；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「撒哈拉以南非洲」区域页：《马太与马可福音》以1740年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。", "note_en": "Gospels of Matthew and Mark, 1740. Sub-Saharan Africa. ink and pigments on vellum; manuscript; dimensions not recorded.\n\nBuilds the regional page for Sub-Saharan Africa: Gospels of Matthew and Mark enters at 1740 with a verifiable date and medium.", "note_html": "《马太与马可福音》，1740年。撒哈拉以南非洲。羊皮纸、墨与颜料；写本；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「撒哈拉以南非洲」区域页：《马太与马可福音》以1740年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。"}, "cle-1996-210-1742": {"note": "服饰、衣袖与手部习作，1742年。欧洲。绘画；Sheet: 24.7 x 18.4 cm (9 3/4 x 7 1/4 in.); Secondary Support: 35 x 27.4 cm (13 3/4 x 10 13/16 in.)。\n\n从衣褶、发型与身体姿态，读出性别、阶层与时代。", "note_en": "Studies of a Costume, Sleeve, and Hand, c. 1747. Pietro Longhi (Italian, 1702–1785). Black chalk (costume) and red chalk (sleeve and hand); sheet: 24.7 x 18.4 cm (9 3/4 x 7 1/4 in.); secondary support: 35 x 27.4 cm (13 3/4 x 10 13/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of the Artemis Group/David Carritt, Ltd., 1996.210\n\nWithin “Portrait and Self”, under “身体与服饰”: Fold, hair and posture reveal gender, class and period.", "note_html": "服饰、衣袖与手部习作，1742年。欧洲。绘画；Sheet: 24.7 x 18.4 cm (9 3/4 x 7 1/4 in.); Secondary Support: 35 x 27.4 cm (13 3/4 x 10 13/16 in.)。\n\n从衣褶、发型与身体姿态，读出性别、阶层与时代。"}, "road-to-shu-1743": {"note": "元代扬州画坊的作品中，很少有像这幅挂轴这样具有如此宏大尺幅的连续构图。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。", "note_en": "Few works by the Yuan workshops in Yangzhou present a continuous composition of such monumental scale as this hanging scroll.\n\nMaterial determines the surface: gold, ink, pigment and paper, silk or panel change how light and colour travel. Look at the material first, then at the brushwork.", "note_html": "元代扬州画坊的作品中，很少有像这幅挂轴这样具有如此宏大尺幅的连续构图。\n\n材料决定画面的表面：金、墨、颜料与纸、绢、板的关系，直接改变光线和颜色的走法。先看材质，再看笔触。"}, "album-of-landscape-paintings-illustrating-old-poems-three-big--1745": {"note": "《山水画册：古诗意境》：三棵大树，溪畔坐着一位老人，1745年。华岩（中国，1682–约1765）。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "Album of Landscape Paintings Illustrating Old Poems: Three Big Trees, a Stream with an Old Man Sitting on the Bank, 1745. Hua Yan (Chinese, 1682–c. 1765).\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "《山水画册：古诗意境》：三棵大树，溪畔坐着一位老人，1745年。华岩（中国，1682–约1765）。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "album-of-landscape-paintings-illustrating-old-poems-man-with-a-1745": {"note": "华岩的《士人赏菊图》让人联想到隐士诗人陶潜（又名陶渊明，公元365年—\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "Hua Yan’s painting of a gentleman admiring orange chrysanthemums evokes a quote from the poem Drinking Wine by poet and recluse Tao Qian (also called Tao Yuanming, AD 365–427): \"I\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "华岩的《士人赏菊图》让人联想到隐士诗人陶潜（又名陶渊明，公元365年—\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "album-of-landscape-paintings-illustrating-old-poems-a-man-recl-1745": {"note": "《山水画册：古诗意境》：倚坐观景图，1745年。华岩（中国，1682–约1765）。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "Album of Landscape Paintings Illustrating Old Poems: A Man Reclining and Enjoying the View, 1745. Hua Yan (Chinese, 1682–c. 1765).\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "《山水画册：古诗意境》：倚坐观景图，1745年。华岩（中国，1682–约1765）。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "album-of-landscape-paintings-illustrating-old-poems-two-women--1745": {"note": "两名正在做针线活的妇女被关在一个室内空间里。这本《华岩册页》中的另外11幅画作描绘了身处大自然的男子。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "Two women doing needlework are confined in an interior space. The other 11 paintings in this Hua Yan album show men in nature.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "两名正在做针线活的妇女被关在一个室内空间里。这本《华岩册页》中的另外11幅画作描绘了身处大自然的男子。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "album-of-landscape-paintings-illustrating-old-poems-children-p-1745": {"note": "华岩是“扬州八怪”之一，他摒弃了正统的绘画观念。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "Hua Yan is one of the Eight Eccentrics of Yangzhou, who rejected orthodox ideas about painting.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "华岩是“扬州八怪”之一，他摒弃了正统的绘画观念。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "album-of-landscape-paintings-illustrating-old-poems-boy-tendin-1745": {"note": "华岩是“扬州八怪”之一，他拒绝接受正统的绘画观念。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "Hua Yan is one of the Eight Eccentrics of Yangzhou, who rejected Orthodox ideas about painting.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "华岩是“扬州八怪”之一，他拒绝接受正统的绘画观念。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "album-of-landscape-paintings-illustrating-old-poems-boy-holdin-1745": {"note": "华岩是“扬州八怪”之一，他摒弃了正统的绘画观念。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "Hua Yan is one of the Eight Eccentrics of Yangzhou, who rejected orthodox ideas about painting.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "华岩是“扬州八怪”之一，他摒弃了正统的绘画观念。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "album-of-landscape-paintings-illustrating-old-poems-man-restin-1745": {"note": "《古诗意山水画册：竹下幽篁图》，1745年。华岩（中国，1682–约1765）。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "Album of Landscape Paintings Illustrating Old Poems: Man Resting under Bamboo, 1745. Hua Yan (Chinese, 1682–c. 1765).\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "《古诗意山水画册：竹下幽篁图》，1745年。华岩（中国，1682–约1765）。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "album-of-landscape-painting-illustrating-old-poems-1745": {"note": "华岩是“扬州八怪”之一，他摒弃了正统的绘画观念。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "Hua Yan is one of the Eight Eccentrics of Yangzhou, who rejected orthodox ideas about painting.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "华岩是“扬州八怪”之一，他摒弃了正统的绘画观念。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "album-of-landscape-paintings-illustrating-old-poems-a-scholar--1745": {"note": "华岩是“扬州八怪”之一，他拒绝接受正统的绘画观念。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "Hua Yan is one of the Eight Eccentrics of Yangzhou, who rejected Orthodox ideas about painting.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "华岩是“扬州八怪”之一，他拒绝接受正统的绘画观念。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "album-of-landscape-paintings-illustrating-old-poems-listening--1745": {"note": "身着粉衣的人物正在弹奏一种七弦琴，即古琴。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "The figure in pink is playing a qin , a seven-stringed zither.\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "身着粉衣的人物正在弹奏一种七弦琴，即古琴。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "album-of-landscape-paintings-illustrating-old-poems-scholar-un-1745": {"note": "《古诗图册·松下高士》，1745年。华岩（中国，1682–约1765）。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "Album of Landscape Paintings Illustrating Old Poems: Scholar under a Pine Tree, 1745. Hua Yan (Chinese, 1682–c. 1765).\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "《古诗图册·松下高士》，1745年。华岩（中国，1682–约1765）。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "album-of-landscape-paintings-illustrating-old-poems-scholar-wa-1745": {"note": "《仿古诗意山水册页：观鱼图》，1745年。华岩（中国，1682–约1765）。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。", "note_en": "Album of Landscape Paintings Illustrating Old Poems: Scholar watching Fish, 1745. Hua Yan (Chinese, 1682–c. 1765).\n\nText and image share one sheet: calligraphy, borders, illustration and blank space press against one another. The order of reading is both verbal and visual.", "note_html": "《仿古诗意山水册页：观鱼图》，1745年。华岩（中国，1682–约1765）。\n\n文字与图像共用同一张纸面：书法、边框、插图与留白互相挤压。阅读的顺序既是文字的，也是图像的。"}, "boucher-music-dance-1740": {"note": "1740s，法国 巴黎。弗朗索瓦·布歇的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。", "note_en": "1740s, Europe. 弗朗索瓦·布歇; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1948.181. This is a painting (oil painting).", "note_html": "1740s，法国 巴黎。弗朗索瓦·布歇的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。"}, "cle-2000-2-1746": {"note": "法国王太子妃玛丽·泰蕾兹葬礼，1746年。欧洲。素描；Sheet: 45 x 30.9 cm (17 11/16 x 12 3/16 in.)。\n\n以遗体、葬礼与纪念物，把失去变成可共享的图像。", "note_en": "Funeral for Marie-Thérèse of Spain, Dauphine of France, in the Church of Nôtre Dame, Paris, on November 24, 1746, c. 1746. Charles-Nicolas Cochin (French, 1715–1790). Pen and black ink and gray wash heightened with white gouache on cream laid paper, incised (with graphite) for transfer; sheet: 45 x 30.9 cm (17 11/16 x 12 3/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, John L. Severance Fund, 2000.2\n\nWithin “Portrait and Self”, under “死亡与记忆”: Body, funeral and memorial turn loss into a shareable image.", "note_html": "法国王太子妃玛丽·泰蕾兹葬礼，1746年。欧洲。素描；Sheet: 45 x 30.9 cm (17 11/16 x 12 3/16 in.)。\n\n以遗体、葬礼与纪念物，把失去变成可共享的图像。"}, "five-pine-trees-1747": {"note": "李山出生于扬州的一个学者和官员之家。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。", "note_en": "Li Shan was born into a family of scholars and officials in Yangzhou.\n\nNature is not a backdrop here but the armature of the picture. The eye follows paths, pauses between foreground and distant peaks, and the landscape becomes a space one can enter.", "note_html": "李山出生于扬州的一个学者和官员之家。\n\n它不把自然当作背景，而是让山、水、树、雾成为画面的骨架。视线沿路径移动，近景与远峰之间留出呼吸，风景因此有了可以进入的空间。"}, "cle-1974-39-1747": {"note": "罗马万神殿内部，1747年。欧洲。油画；Framed: 147.5 x 120 x 5 cm (58 1/16 x 47 1/4 x 1 15/16 in.); Unframed: 127 x 97.8 cm (50 x 38 1/2 in.)。\n\n把教堂、剧场与房间当作观看装置，空间本身也在叙事。", "note_en": "Interior of the Pantheon, Rome, 1747. Giovanni Paolo Panini (Italian, 1691–1765). Oil on canvas; framed: 147.5 x 120 x 5 cm (58 1/16 x 47 1/4 x 1 15/16 in.); unframed: 127 x 97.8 cm (50 x 38 1/2 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Purchase from the J. H. Wade Fund, 1974.39\n\nWithin “City and Everyday Life”, under “日常空间”: Church, theatre and room are viewing devices; space itself narrates.", "note_html": "罗马万神殿内部，1747年。欧洲。油画；Framed: 147.5 x 120 x 5 cm (58 1/16 x 47 1/4 x 1 15/16 in.); Unframed: 127 x 97.8 cm (50 x 38 1/2 in.)。\n\n把教堂、剧场与房间当作观看装置，空间本身也在叙事。"}, "cle-1998-102-1747": {"note": "贾加特·辛格二世狩猎，1747年。南亚。蛋彩；Sheet: 42.5 x 47 cm (16 3/4 x 18 1/2 in.)。\n\n让猎犬、马与猎物进入权力场景，动物也是身份道具。", "note_en": "Maharana Jagat Singh II Hunting, 1747. Jugarsi, son of Jiva (Indian, active mid-1700s). Gum tempera and gold on paper; sheet: 42.5 x 47 cm (16 3/4 x 18 1/2 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, John L. Severance Fund, 1998.102\n\nWithin “Landscape and Nature”, under “动物与宫廷”: Hounds, horses and prey enter a scene of power; animals are also status props.", "note_html": "贾加特·辛格二世狩猎，1747年。南亚。蛋彩；Sheet: 42.5 x 47 cm (16 3/4 x 18 1/2 in.)。\n\n让猎犬、马与猎物进入权力场景，动物也是身份道具。"}, "cbl-w-916-1750": {"note": "《圣母赞歌与赞辞》，1750年。撒哈拉以南非洲。羊皮纸、墨与颜料；写本；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「撒哈拉以南非洲」区域页：《圣母赞歌与赞辞》以1750年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。", "note_en": "Praises of Mary (Weddase Maryam) & Praises and Commendation to the Mother of Adonai (Weddase wa-genay la-Emma Adonay), 1750. Sub-Saharan Africa. ink and pigments on vellum; manuscript; dimensions not recorded.\n\nBuilds the regional page for Sub-Saharan Africa: Praises of Mary (Weddase Maryam) & Praises and Commendation to the Mother of Adonai (Weddase wa-genay la-Emma Adonay) enters at 1750 with a verifiable date and medium.", "note_html": "《圣母赞歌与赞辞》，1750年。撒哈拉以南非洲。羊皮纸、墨与颜料；写本；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「撒哈拉以南非洲」区域页：《圣母赞歌与赞辞》以1750年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。"}, "cle-1915-216-1750": {"note": "溪山风景，1750年。东亚。绢本设色；Painting only: 65.6 x 45.9 cm (25 13/16 x 18 1/16 in.); Overall: 68.5 x 50.7 cm (26 15/16 x 19 15/16 in.)。\n\n以山体、路径与雾气组织观看，山不是背景，而是叙事的主体。", "note_en": "Landscape with Streams and Mountains (계산진경도), late 1700s or early 1800s. Korea, Joseon dynasty (1392–1910). Ink and color on paper with a silk border; painting only: 65.6 x 45.9 cm (25 13/16 x 18 1/16 in.); overall: 68.5 x 50.7 cm (26 15/16 x 19 15/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of the John Huntington Art and Polytechnic Trust, 1915.216\n\nWithin “Landscape and Nature”, under “山”: Organises looking through mass, path and mist; the mountain is the subject, not the backdrop.", "note_html": "溪山风景，1750年。东亚。绢本设色；Painting only: 65.6 x 45.9 cm (25 13/16 x 18 1/16 in.); Overall: 68.5 x 50.7 cm (26 15/16 x 19 15/16 in.)。\n\n以山体、路径与雾气组织观看，山不是背景，而是叙事的主体。"}, "cbl-w-949-1755": {"note": "《圣歌集》，1755年。撒哈拉以南非洲。羊皮纸、墨与颜料；写本；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「撒哈拉以南非洲」区域页：《圣歌集》以1755年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。", "note_en": "Parchment codex with wooden cover (one broken board) containing a collection of Ethiopian hymns to various saints, written in Ge'ez in black and red ink and dated to the 18th century. An ink drawing of a figure is found on the last folio.\n\nBuilds the regional page for Sub-Saharan Africa: Collection of Hymns enters at 1755 with a verifiable date and medium.", "note_html": "《圣歌集》，1755年。撒哈拉以南非洲。羊皮纸、墨与颜料；写本；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「撒哈拉以南非洲」区域页：《圣歌集》以1755年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。"}, "cle-2013-341-1755": {"note": "夜间露台公主与侍从（另面书法），1755年。南亚。蛋彩；Miniature: 25.4 x 19.7 cm (10 x 7 3/4 in.)。\n\n把笔迹、留白与边框当成图像，阅读节奏就是视觉节奏。", "note_en": "A princess on a terrace with attendants at night (recto); Calligraphy (verso), c. 1760. India, Farrukhabad, Mughal, 18th century. Gum tempera, ink, and gold on paper; miniature: 25.4 x 19.7 cm (10 x 7 3/4 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift in honor of Madeline Neves Clapp; Gift of Mrs. Henry White Cannon by exchange; Bequest of Louise T. Cooper; Leonard C. Hanna Jr. Fund; From the Catherine and Ralph Benkaim Collection, 2013.341\n\nWithin “Word and Looking”, under “书法”: Hand, blank space and border are image; reading rhythm is visual rhythm.", "note_html": "夜间露台公主与侍从（另面书法），1755年。南亚。蛋彩；Miniature: 25.4 x 19.7 cm (10 x 7 3/4 in.)。\n\n把笔迹、留白与边框当成图像，阅读节奏就是视觉节奏。"}, "cle-2013-350-1755": {"note": "湿婆夜祭图（另面书法），1755年。南亚。蛋彩；Page: 28.2 x 24.1 cm (11 1/8 x 9 1/2 in.)。\n\n把笔迹、留白与边框当成图像，阅读节奏就是视觉节奏。", "note_en": "A night scene of Shiva puja (recto); Calligraphy (verso), c. 1760–70. Attributed to Muhammad Rizavi Hindi (Indian, active mid-1700s), Ahmad al-Husaini. Gum tempera and gold on paper; page: 28.2 x 24.1 cm (11 1/8 x 9 1/2 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift in honor of Madeline Neves Clapp; Gift of Mrs. Henry White Cannon by exchange; Bequest of Louise T. Cooper; Leonard C. Hanna Jr. Fund; From the Catherine and Ralph Benkaim Collection, 2013.350\n\nWithin “Word and Looking”, under “书法”: Hand, blank space and border are image; reading rhythm is visual rhythm.", "note_html": "湿婆夜祭图（另面书法），1755年。南亚。蛋彩；Page: 28.2 x 24.1 cm (11 1/8 x 9 1/2 in.)。\n\n把笔迹、留白与边框当成图像，阅读节奏就是视觉节奏。"}, "cle-2018-117-1755": {"note": "罗摩与悉多受猴熊军致敬（《战争篇》），1755年。南亚。蛋彩；Overall: 40.7 x 28.9 cm (16 x 11 3/8 in.); Painting: 23.7 x 14.9 cm (9 5/16 x 5 7/8 in.)。\n\n不美化冲突，先看阵列、火光与逃散，再看胜利叙事如何被书写。", "note_en": "Enthroned Rama and Sita receive homage from their monkey and bear Allies, from the Yuddha Kanda (Book of the War) of a Ramayana (Rama’s Journey), c. 1765. Northern India, Pahari kingdoms. Gum tempera and gold on paper; overall: 40.7 x 28.9 cm (16 x 11 3/8 in.); painting: 23.7 x 14.9 cm (9 5/16 x 5 7/8 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Purchase and partial gift from the Catherine and Ralph Benkaim Collection; Severance and Greta Millikin Purchase Fund, 2018.117\n\nWithin “City and Everyday Life”, under “战争与灾难”: No glorification: formation, fire and flight first, then the writing of victory.", "note_html": "罗摩与悉多受猴熊军致敬（《战争篇》），1755年。南亚。蛋彩；Overall: 40.7 x 28.9 cm (16 x 11 3/8 in.); Painting: 23.7 x 14.9 cm (9 5/16 x 5 7/8 in.)。\n\n不美化冲突，先看阵列、火光与逃散，再看胜利叙事如何被书写。"}, "cle-1921-336-1760": {"note": "主妇与女仆，1760年。东亚。绘画；Sheet: 28.3 x 20.9 cm (11 1/8 x 8 1/4 in.)。\n\n把侍者、工匠与路人放回画面中心，追问谁被记录、谁被省略。", "note_en": "Woman and Maid Servant, late 1760s. Suzuki Harunobu (Japanese, 1724–1770). Color woodblock print; sheet: 28.3 x 20.9 cm (11 1/8 x 8 1/4 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift from J. H. Wade, 1921.336\n\nWithin “Portrait and Self”, under “无名者”: Puts servants, artisans and passers-by at the centre, asking who is recorded and who is omitted.", "note_html": "主妇与女仆，1760年。东亚。绘画；Sheet: 28.3 x 20.9 cm (11 1/8 x 8 1/4 in.)。\n\n把侍者、工匠与路人放回画面中心，追问谁被记录、谁被省略。"}, "cle-1916-1030-1761": {"note": "街头歌手与孩子，1761年。欧洲。油画；Framed: 100 x 87.5 x 11 cm (39 3/8 x 34 7/16 x 4 5/16 in.); Unframed: 76.5 x 64.3 cm (30 1/8 x 25 5/16 in.)。\n\n把街巷当作舞台：行走、相遇与冲突都在同一段路发生。", "note_en": "Street Singer and Child, 1700s. John Opie (British, 1761–1807). Oil on canvas; framed: 100 x 87.5 x 11 cm (39 3/8 x 34 7/16 x 4 5/16 in.); unframed: 76.5 x 64.3 cm (30 1/8 x 25 5/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of Mr. and Mrs. J. H. Wade, 1916.1030\n\nWithin “City and Everyday Life”, under “街道”: The street is a stage: walking, meeting and conflict share one route.", "note_html": "街头歌手与孩子，1761年。欧洲。油画；Framed: 100 x 87.5 x 11 cm (39 3/8 x 34 7/16 x 4 5/16 in.); Unframed: 76.5 x 64.3 cm (30 1/8 x 25 5/16 in.)。\n\n把街巷当作舞台：行走、相遇与冲突都在同一段路发生。"}, "cle-1985-309-1765": {"note": "名妓与沉睡侍女，1765年。东亚。绘画；Overall: 28.1 x 20.1 cm (11 1/16 x 7 15/16 in.)。\n\n把侍者、工匠与路人放回画面中心，追问谁被记录、谁被省略。", "note_en": "Courtesan and Sleeping Attendant (遊女と寝る禿), late 1760s. Suzuki Harunobu (Japanese, 1724–1770). Color woodblock print, with embossing; overall: 28.1 x 20.1 cm (11 1/16 x 7 15/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, The Kelvin Smith Collection, given by Mrs. Kelvin Smith, 1985.309\n\nWithin “Portrait and Self”, under “无名者”: Puts servants, artisans and passers-by at the centre, asking who is recorded and who is omitted.", "note_html": "名妓与沉睡侍女，1765年。东亚。绘画；Overall: 28.1 x 20.1 cm (11 1/16 x 7 15/16 in.)。\n\n把侍者、工匠与路人放回画面中心，追问谁被记录、谁被省略。"}, "fragonard-the-swing-1767": {"note": "《荡秋千》将洛可可风格的轻佻发挥到极致。一位年轻女子坐在树荫下的秋千上，裙摆飞扬，一只鞋踢向空中；她的情人从左边的灌木丛中探出身子向上看，而一位年长的男子在右后方拉着绳子，显然浑然不觉。周围是茂密的叶子，光线像舞台灯光一样照在她的粉色裙子上。\n\n弗拉戈纳尔用旋转的构图、飞扬的衣布和偷看者的视角，让画面内容充满戏剧性。这幅画既是18世纪贵族娱乐的记录，也成为最著名、最容易模仿的洛可可艺术形象。", "note_en": "The Swing takes Rococo frivolity to its limit. A young woman sits on a swing in the shade, her skirt flying, one shoe kicked into the air; her lover leans out of the bushes at the left to look up, while an older man pulls the ropes at the right rear, apparently unaware. Foliage encloses the scene, and light falls like stage lighting on the pink dress.\n\nFragonard uses a swirling composition, lifted cloth and a voyeur's gaze to make play the entire content of the picture. It is both a record of eighteenth-century aristocratic amusement and the most famous, most imitable image of Rococo art.", "note_html": "《荡秋千》将洛可可风格的轻佻发挥到极致。一位年轻女子坐在树荫下的秋千上，裙摆飞扬，一只鞋踢向空中；她的情人从左边的灌木丛中探出身子向上看，而一位年长的男子在右后方拉着绳子，显然浑然不觉。周围是茂密的叶子，光线像舞台灯光一样照在她的粉色裙子上。\n\n弗拉戈纳尔用旋转的构图、飞扬的衣布和偷看者的视角，让画面内容充满戏剧性。这幅画既是18世纪贵族娱乐的记录，也成为最著名、最容易模仿的洛可可艺术形象。"}, "cle-1989-52-1769": {"note": "卡德伊德里斯山与马多克河，1769年。欧洲。油画；Framed: 105.5 x 120.5 x 7 cm (41 9/16 x 47 7/16 x 2 3/4 in.); Unframed: 89.8 x 105.5 cm (35 3/8 x 41 9/16 in.)。\n\n让河流、瀑布与岸边人物共同构成时间感，水线就是画面的节拍。", "note_en": "Cader Idris, with the Mawddach River, c. 1774. Richard Wilson (British, 1714–1782). Oil on canvas; framed: 105.5 x 120.5 x 7 cm (41 9/16 x 47 7/16 x 2 3/4 in.); unframed: 89.8 x 105.5 cm (35 3/8 x 41 9/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Leonard C. Hanna Jr. Fund, 1989.52\n\nWithin “Landscape and Nature”, under “水”: River, waterfall and shore figures create time; the waterline sets the rhythm.", "note_html": "卡德伊德里斯山与马多克河，1769年。欧洲。油画；Framed: 105.5 x 120.5 x 7 cm (41 9/16 x 47 7/16 x 2 3/4 in.); Unframed: 89.8 x 105.5 cm (35 3/8 x 41 9/16 in.)。\n\n让河流、瀑布与岸边人物共同构成时间感，水线就是画面的节拍。"}, "cle-2018-174-1770": {"note": "异样头巾男子头像素描，1770年。南亚。蛋彩；Miniature: 22.6 x 16.5 cm (8 7/8 x 6 1/2 in.)。\n\n保留修改与犹豫的痕迹，让创作过程进入成品。", "note_en": "Drawing of a Man’s Head with an Unusual Turban, c. 1780. Northwestern India, Rajasthan, Rajput Kingdom of Kishangarh. Gum tempera and gold on paper; miniature: 22.6 x 16.5 cm (8 7/8 x 6 1/2 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Purchase and partial gift from the Catherine and Ralph Benkaim Collection; Severance and Greta Millikin Purchase Fund, 2018.174\n\nWithin “Material and Technique”, under “素描”: Corrections and hesitation remain visible; process enters the finished work.", "note_html": "异样头巾男子头像素描，1770年。南亚。蛋彩；Miniature: 22.6 x 16.5 cm (8 7/8 x 6 1/2 in.)。\n\n保留修改与犹豫的痕迹，让创作过程进入成品。"}, "cle-1941-566-1770": {"note": "甘比尔先生肖像，1770年。欧洲。素描；Framed: 7.9 x 6.9 cm (3 1/8 x 2 11/16 in.); Unframed: 5.8 x 2.8 cm (2 5/16 x 1 1/8 in.)。\n\n不只看像不像，更看服饰、姿态与目光如何制造身份。", "note_en": "Portrait of Mr. Gambier, c. 1776. John I Smart (British, 1741–1811). Graphite and wash on laid paper; framed: 7.9 x 6.9 cm (3 1/8 x 2 11/16 in.); unframed: 5.8 x 2.8 cm (2 5/16 x 1 1/8 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, The Edward B. Greene Collection, 1941.566\n\nWithin “Portrait and Self”, under “肖像”: Not only likeness: dress, pose and gaze manufacture identity.", "note_html": "甘比尔先生肖像，1770年。欧洲。素描；Framed: 7.9 x 6.9 cm (3 1/8 x 2 11/16 in.); Unframed: 5.8 x 2.8 cm (2 5/16 x 1 1/8 in.)。\n\n不只看像不像，更看服饰、姿态与目光如何制造身份。"}, "cle-1986-63-1775": {"note": "康格拉王桑萨尔·昌德与廷臣，1775年。南亚。蛋彩；Overall: 24.2 x 21.6 cm (9 1/2 x 8 1/2 in.)。\n\n以礼仪、队列与身体距离，画出权力如何被日常表演。", "note_en": "Raja Sansar Chand of Kangra and courtiers, c. 1783. Northern India, Pahari kingdoms. Gum tempera and gold on paper; overall: 24.2 x 21.6 cm (9 1/2 x 8 1/2 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of Clara Taplin Rankin, 1986.63\n\nWithin “Portrait and Self”, under “宫廷人物”: Ceremony, rank and bodily distance show power performed as everyday life.", "note_html": "康格拉王桑萨尔·昌德与廷臣，1775年。南亚。蛋彩；Overall: 24.2 x 21.6 cm (9 1/2 x 8 1/2 in.)。\n\n以礼仪、队列与身体距离，画出权力如何被日常表演。"}, "wellcome-v0044822-1777": {"note": "《塔纳岛男子像》，1777年。大洋洲。铜版画；版画；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「大洋洲」区域页：《塔纳岛男子像》以1777年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。", "note_en": "Lettering: Man of the island of Tanna ; drawn from nature by W. Hodges ; engrav'd by J. Basire ... Bears number: XXVI.\n\nBuilds the regional page for Oceania: A man from the island of Tanna, head and shoulders. Engraving by J. Basire after W. Hodges, 1 February 1777. enters at 1777 with a verifiable date and medium.", "note_html": "《塔纳岛男子像》，1777年。大洋洲。铜版画；版画；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「大洋洲」区域页：《塔纳岛男子像》以1777年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。"}, "cle-1984-59-1777": {"note": "岩树景观与溪堰，1777年。欧洲。油画；Framed: 89.5 x 110 x 8 cm (35 1/4 x 43 5/16 x 3 1/8 in.); Unframed: 70.5 x 91 cm (27 3/4 x 35 13/16 in.)。\n\n以山体、路径与雾气组织观看，山不是背景，而是叙事的主体。", "note_en": "Rocky, Wooded Landscape with a Dell and Weir, c. 1782–1783. Thomas Gainsborough (British, 1727–1788). Oil on canvas; framed: 89.5 x 110 x 8 cm (35 1/4 x 43 5/16 x 3 1/8 in.); unframed: 70.5 x 91 cm (27 3/4 x 35 13/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Mr. and Mrs. William H. Marlatt Fund, 1984.59\n\nWithin “Landscape and Nature”, under “山”: Organises looking through mass, path and mist; the mountain is the subject, not the backdrop.", "note_html": "岩树景观与溪堰，1777年。欧洲。油画；Framed: 89.5 x 110 x 8 cm (35 1/4 x 43 5/16 x 3 1/8 in.); Unframed: 70.5 x 91 cm (27 3/4 x 35 13/16 in.)。\n\n以山体、路径与雾气组织观看，山不是背景，而是叙事的主体。"}, "wellcome-v0044828-1777": {"note": "《库克船队遇见的少年奥赫迪迪》，1777年。大洋洲。铜版画；版画；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「大洋洲」区域页：《库克船队遇见的少年奥赫迪迪》以1777年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。", "note_en": "Lettering: O-Hedidee ; drawn from nature by W. Hodges ; engrav'd by J. Caldwall ... Bears number: XXXV.\n\nBuilds the regional page for Oceania: A young boy called O-Hedidee encountered by Cook on his second voyage. Engraving by J. Caldwall after W. Hodges, 1 February 1777. enters at 1777 with a verifiable date and medium.", "note_html": "《库克船队遇见的少年奥赫迪迪》，1777年。大洋洲。铜版画；版画；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「大洋洲」区域页：《库克船队遇见的少年奥赫迪迪》以1777年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。"}, "wellcome-v0044841-1777": {"note": "《新西兰毛利男子像》，1777年。大洋洲。铜版画；版画；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「大洋洲」区域页：《新西兰毛利男子像》以1777年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。", "note_en": "Lettering: Man of New Zealand ; drawn from nature by W. Hodges ; engrav'd by Michel. Bears number: LV.\n\nBuilds the regional page for Oceania: A man from New Zealand (Maori ?) with tattoos on his face, encountered by Cook on his second voyage, 1772-1775. Engraving by Michel after W. Hodges, 1 February 1777. enters at 1777 with a verifiable date and medium.", "note_html": "《新西兰毛利男子像》，1777年。大洋洲。铜版画；版画；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「大洋洲」区域页：《新西兰毛利男子像》以1777年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。"}, "wellcome-v0044832-1777": {"note": "《汤加独木舟》，1777年。大洋洲。铜版画；版画；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「大洋洲」区域页：《汤加独木舟》以1777年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。", "note_en": "Lettering: Boats of the Friendly isles ; drawn from nature by W. Hodges ; engrav'd by W. Watts. Bears number: XLII.\n\nBuilds the regional page for Oceania: Boats fromTonga (Polynesia), encountered by Cook on his second voyage, 1772-1775. Engraving by W. Watts after W. Hodges, 1 February 1777. enters at 1777 with a verifiable date and medium.", "note_html": "《汤加独木舟》，1777年。大洋洲。铜版画；版画；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「大洋洲」区域页：《汤加独木舟》以1777年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。"}, "david-young-woman-turban-1780": {"note": "c. 1780，法国 巴黎。雅克-路易·大卫的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。", "note_en": "c. 1780, Europe. 雅克-路易·大卫; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1952.542. This is a painting (oil painting).", "note_html": "c. 1780，法国 巴黎。雅克-路易·大卫的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。"}, "fragonard-boy-red-cloak-1780": {"note": "1780s，法国 巴黎。让-奥诺雷·弗拉戈纳尔的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。", "note_en": "1780s, Europe. 让-奥诺雷·弗拉戈纳尔; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1942.49. This is a painting (oil painting).", "note_html": "1780s，法国 巴黎。让-奥诺雷·弗拉戈纳尔的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。"}, "david-oath-of-horatii-1784": {"note": "《霍拉提兄弟的誓言》把罗马历史中的一个瞬间变成了舞台剧。三个兄弟肩并肩站在父亲面前，手臂伸向剑；父亲举起三把剑，背后是拱门和阴影。右侧，女人们一起倒下，母亲和姐妹低下头，知道战争会让她们失去兄弟或丈夫。\n\n大卫用垂直的柱子、硬朗的轮廓和几乎无笔触的画面，把新古典主义的“美德”变成了几何形状。男性的身体是直线，女性的身体是曲线；誓言和悲伤在画布的两侧被区分开来。", "note_en": "Oath of the Horatii turns a moment of Roman history into theatre. Three brothers stand shoulder to shoulder before their father, arms extended towards the swords; the father raises the three blades, an archway and shadow behind him. On the right, the women collapse together, mother and sisters bowing their heads, knowing the war will cost them brothers or husbands.\n\nDavid uses vertical columns, hard contours and a nearly brushless surface to turn Neoclassical \"virtue\" into geometry. Male bodies are straight lines, female bodies curves; oath and grief are divided between the two sides of the canvas.", "note_html": "《霍拉提兄弟的誓言》把罗马历史中的一个瞬间变成了舞台剧。三个兄弟肩并肩站在父亲面前，手臂伸向剑；父亲举起三把剑，背后是拱门和阴影。右侧，女人们一起倒下，母亲和姐妹低下头，知道战争会让她们失去兄弟或丈夫。\n\n大卫用垂直的柱子、硬朗的轮廓和几乎无笔触的画面，把新古典主义的“美德”变成了几何形状。男性的身体是直线，女性的身体是曲线；誓言和悲伤在画布的两侧被区分开来。"}, "cle-1969-35-1785": {"note": "拉达梳妆，1785年。南亚。蛋彩；Image: 25 x 17 cm (9 13/16 x 6 11/16 in.); Overall: 29.7 x 20.3 cm (11 11/16 x 8 in.)。\n\n从衣褶、发型与身体姿态，读出性别、阶层与时代。", "note_en": "Radha's hair being dressed, c. 1790–1800. Northern India, Pahari kingdoms. Gum tempera with touches of color on paper; image: 25 x 17 cm (9 13/16 x 6 11/16 in.); overall: 29.7 x 20.3 cm (11 11/16 x 8 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Edward L. Whittemore Fund, 1969.35\n\nWithin “Portrait and Self”, under “身体与服饰”: Fold, hair and posture reveal gender, class and period.", "note_html": "拉达梳妆，1785年。南亚。蛋彩；Image: 25 x 17 cm (9 13/16 x 6 11/16 in.); Overall: 29.7 x 20.3 cm (11 11/16 x 8 in.)。\n\n从衣褶、发型与身体姿态，读出性别、阶层与时代。"}, "cle-1973-104-1785": {"note": "王族情侣观雨（《十二月令》），1785年。南亚。蛋彩；Image: 13 x 9 cm (5 1/8 x 3 9/16 in.); Overall: 20.7 x 15.2 cm (8 1/8 x 6 in.)。\n\n用时钟、月份与雨季，把抽象时间落到日常动作上。", "note_en": "Royal lovers watching rain clouds: The month of Bhadon, from a Barahmasa, c. 1790. Northern India, Pahari kingdoms. Gum tempera, ink, and gold on paper; image: 13 x 9 cm (5 1/8 x 3 9/16 in.); overall: 20.7 x 15.2 cm (8 1/8 x 6 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Purchase from the J. H. Wade Fund, 1973.104\n\nWithin “City and Everyday Life”, under “时间与日常”: Clocks, months and rain turn abstract time into everyday action.", "note_html": "王族情侣观雨（《十二月令》），1785年。南亚。蛋彩；Image: 13 x 9 cm (5 1/8 x 3 9/16 in.); Overall: 20.7 x 15.2 cm (8 1/8 x 6 in.)。\n\n用时钟、月份与雨季，把抽象时间落到日常动作上。"}, "cle-1933-453-1785": {"note": "黑天着女装庆洒红节，1785年。南亚。蛋彩；Overall: 19 x 27.4 cm (7 1/2 x 10 13/16 in.)。\n\n让短暂的热闹进入图像，节庆既是娱乐，也是社会秩序的排练。", "note_en": "Krishna being dressed in women’s clothes for the spring festival Holi, c. 1790. Northern India, Pahari kingdoms. Ink and gum tempera on paper; overall: 19 x 27.4 cm (7 1/2 x 10 13/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Edward L. Whittemore Fund, 1933.453\n\nWithin “City and Everyday Life”, under “节庆”: A brief festivity enters the image; celebration is also a rehearsal of social order.", "note_html": "黑天着女装庆洒红节，1785年。南亚。蛋彩；Overall: 19 x 27.4 cm (7 1/2 x 10 13/16 in.)。\n\n让短暂的热闹进入图像，节庆既是娱乐，也是社会秩序的排练。"}, "cle-1921-322-1787": {"note": "市川团十郎五世扮行旅武士，1787年。东亚。绘画；Sheet: 29.9 x 14.4 cm (11 3/4 x 5 11/16 in.)。\n\n追踪摹本、复制与传教路线，看图像如何换手、换语境。", "note_en": "Ichikawa Danjuro V as a Travelling Warrior, late 1780s. Katsukawa Shunkō (Japanese, 1743–1812). Color woodblock print; sheet: 29.9 x 14.4 cm (11 3/4 x 5 11/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift from J. H. Wade, 1921.322\n\nWithin “Word and Looking”, under “图像如何旅行”: Follows copies, replicas and missions to see images change hands and contexts.", "note_html": "市川团十郎五世扮行旅武士，1787年。东亚。绘画；Sheet: 29.9 x 14.4 cm (11 3/4 x 5 11/16 in.)。\n\n追踪摹本、复制与传教路线，看图像如何换手、换语境。"}, "cle-1985-71-2-1788": {"note": "卢仝与侍者，1788年。中国。纸本水墨；Sheet: 29 x 18.4 cm (11 7/16 x 7 1/4 in.)。\n\n把侍者、工匠与路人放回画面中心，追问谁被记录、谁被省略。", "note_en": " (雑畫圖冊): Lu Tong and Servant, 1788. Min Zhen (Chinese, 1730–after 1788). Album leaf, ink on paper; sheet: 29 x 18.4 cm (11 7/16 x 7 1/4 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, John L. Severance Fund, 1985.71.2\n\nWithin “Portrait and Self”, under “无名者”: Puts servants, artisans and passers-by at the centre, asking who is recorded and who is omitted.", "note_html": "卢仝与侍者，1788年。中国。纸本水墨；Sheet: 29 x 18.4 cm (11 7/16 x 7 1/4 in.)。\n\n把侍者、工匠与路人放回画面中心，追问谁被记录、谁被省略。"}, "cle-1980-188-1-1788": {"note": "山市晴岚（《潇湘八景》），1788年。东亚。纸本设色；Painting: 29.6 x 49.2 cm (11 5/8 x 19 3/8 in.); Mounted: 128.7 x 61.5 cm (50 11/16 x 24 3/16 in.)。\n\n用货物、叫卖与人群，把交换变成可见的城市节奏。", "note_en": "Mountain Market in Clearing Mist, from Eight Views of Xiao-Xiang (瀟湘八景の内　山市晴嵐図), 1788. Tani Bunchō (Japanese, 1763–1841). Album leaf remounted as a hanging scroll; ink and color on paper; painting: 29.6 x 49.2 cm (11 5/8 x 19 3/8 in.); mounted: 128.7 x 61.5 cm (50 11/16 x 24 3/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Andrew R. and Martha Holden Jennings Fund, 1980.188.1\n\nWithin “City and Everyday Life”, under “市场”: Goods, calls and crowds turn exchange into the visible rhythm of the city.", "note_html": "山市晴岚（《潇湘八景》），1788年。东亚。纸本设色；Painting: 29.6 x 49.2 cm (11 5/8 x 19 3/8 in.); Mounted: 128.7 x 61.5 cm (50 11/16 x 24 3/16 in.)。\n\n用货物、叫卖与人群，把交换变成可见的城市节奏。"}, "albertina-488586-1789": {"note": "《埃梅奥岛塔卢港湾》，1789年。大洋洲。铜版画；版画；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「大洋洲」区域页：《埃梅奥岛塔卢港湾》以1789年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。", "note_en": "View of the Harbour of Taloo, in the Island of Eimeo, 1789. Oceania. engraving; print; dimensions not recorded.\n\nBuilds the regional page for Oceania: View of the Harbour of Taloo, in the Island of Eimeo enters at 1789 with a verifiable date and medium.", "note_html": "《埃梅奥岛塔卢港湾》，1789年。大洋洲。铜版画；版画；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「大洋洲」区域页：《埃梅奥岛塔卢港湾》以1789年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。"}, "albertina-488585-1789": {"note": "《奥海特佩哈首领瓦海阿多阿》，1789年。大洋洲。铜版画；版画；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「大洋洲」区域页：《奥海特佩哈首领瓦海阿多阿》以1789年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。", "note_en": "Waheiadooa, Chief of Oheitepeha, 1789. Oceania. engraving; print; dimensions not recorded.\n\nBuilds the regional page for Oceania: Waheiadooa, Chief of Oheitepeha enters at 1789 with a verifiable date and medium.", "note_html": "《奥海特佩哈首领瓦海阿多阿》，1789年。大洋洲。铜版画；版画；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「大洋洲」区域页：《奥海特佩哈首领瓦海阿多阿》以1789年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。"}, "cle-1916-1150-1790": {"note": "浅草绘马堂休憩女子图，1790年。东亚。纸本设色；Sheet: 39.4 x 25.4 cm (15 1/2 x 10 in.)。\n\n从刀线、墨色与复制，看图像如何离开手稿进入流通。", "note_en": "Print from Women Resting in the Votive Picture Hall at Asakusa, early 1790s. Chōbunsai Eishi (Japanese, 1756–1829). Woodblock print from a triptych; ink and color on paper; sheet: 39.4 x 25.4 cm (15 1/2 x 10 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of Mr. and Mrs. J. H. Wade, 1916.1150\n\nWithin “Word and Looking”, under “印刷与版画”: Knife line, ink and replication show how images leave the manuscript and circulate.", "note_html": "浅草绘马堂休憩女子图，1790年。东亚。纸本设色；Sheet: 39.4 x 25.4 cm (15 1/2 x 10 in.)。\n\n从刀线、墨色与复制，看图像如何离开手稿进入流通。"}, "albertina-488581-1791": {"note": "《友好群岛的舟船》，1791年。大洋洲。铜版画；版画；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「大洋洲」区域页：《友好群岛的舟船》以1791年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。", "note_en": "Boats of the Friendly Islands, 1791. Oceania. engraving; print; dimensions not recorded.\n\nBuilds the regional page for Oceania: Boats of the Friendly Islands enters at 1791 with a verifiable date and medium.", "note_html": "《友好群岛的舟船》，1791年。大洋洲。铜版画；版画；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「大洋洲」区域页：《友好群岛的舟船》以1791年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。"}, "albertina-488584-1791": {"note": "《塔希提奥海特佩哈湾》，1791年。大洋洲。铜版画；版画；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「大洋洲」区域页：《塔希提奥海特佩哈湾》以1791年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。", "note_en": "A View in Oheitepeha Bay, in the Island of Otaheite, 1791. Oceania. engraving; print; dimensions not recorded.\n\nBuilds the regional page for Oceania: A View in Oheitepeha Bay, in the Island of Otaheite enters at 1791 with a verifiable date and medium.", "note_html": "《塔希提奥海特佩哈湾》，1791年。大洋洲。铜版画；版画；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「大洋洲」区域页：《塔希提奥海特佩哈湾》以1791年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。"}, "cle-1921-345-1791": {"note": "巳时（《少女时钟》），1791年。东亚。绘画；Sheet: 36.2 x 23.2 cm (14 1/4 x 9 1/8 in.)。\n\n用时钟、月份与雨季，把抽象时间落到日常动作上。", "note_en": "The Hour of the Snake (from the series A Clock for Young Women), c. 1796. Kitagawa Utamaro (Japanese, c. 1754–1806). Color woodblock print; sheet: 36.2 x 23.2 cm (14 1/4 x 9 1/8 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift from J. H. Wade, 1921.345\n\nWithin “City and Everyday Life”, under “时间与日常”: Clocks, months and rain turn abstract time into everyday action.", "note_html": "巳时（《少女时钟》），1791年。东亚。绘画；Sheet: 36.2 x 23.2 cm (14 1/4 x 9 1/8 in.)。\n\n用时钟、月份与雨季，把抽象时间落到日常动作上。"}, "cle-1916-1152-1792": {"note": "隅田川新大桥游船图，1792年。东亚。纸本设色；Sheet: 39.1 x 26.2 cm (15 3/8 x 10 5/16 in.)。\n\n从刀线、墨色与复制，看图像如何离开手稿进入流通。", "note_en": "Print from Pleasure Boats on the Sumida River beneath Shin-Ōhashi Bridge, c. 1792. Chōbunsai Eishi (Japanese, 1756–1829). Wooblock print from a pentaptych; ink and color on paper; sheet: 39.1 x 26.2 cm (15 3/8 x 10 5/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of Mr. and Mrs. J. H. Wade, 1916.1152\n\nWithin “Word and Looking”, under “印刷与版画”: Knife line, ink and replication show how images leave the manuscript and circulate.", "note_html": "隅田川新大桥游船图，1792年。东亚。纸本设色；Sheet: 39.1 x 26.2 cm (15 3/8 x 10 5/16 in.)。\n\n从刀线、墨色与复制，看图像如何离开手稿进入流通。"}, "cle-1916-1153-1792": {"note": "隅田川新大桥游船图（最左幅），1792年。东亚。纸本设色；Sheet: 39 x 25.6 cm (15 3/8 x 10 1/16 in.)。\n\n从刀线、墨色与复制，看图像如何离开手稿进入流通。", "note_en": "Leftmost Print from Pleasure Boats on the Sumida River beneath Shin-Ōhashi Bridge, c. 1792. Chōbunsai Eishi (Japanese, 1756–1829). Woodblock print from a pentaptych; ink and color on paper; sheet: 39 x 25.6 cm (15 3/8 x 10 1/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of Mr. and Mrs. J. H. Wade, 1916.1153\n\nWithin “Word and Looking”, under “印刷与版画”: Knife line, ink and replication show how images leave the manuscript and circulate.", "note_html": "隅田川新大桥游船图（最左幅），1792年。东亚。纸本设色；Sheet: 39 x 25.6 cm (15 3/8 x 10 1/16 in.)。\n\n从刀线、墨色与复制，看图像如何离开手稿进入流通。"}, "utamaro-three-beauties-1793": {"note": "《三位美人》是喜多川歌磨的大头画（大头画）的代表作。画中三位著名女性并排而立：玉屋的富士本丰姬、浪屋喜多，以及高岛大久。如她们的面容、发型、和服花纹与目光各不相同；背景使用云母粉，使深色背景闪闪发光，衬托出她们的面庞。\n\n歌磨画的不是地位，而是名气：这些女性被城市所关注、讨论和注视。大头画的形式将肖像放大至半身，使观者不得不与她们对视，也让浮世绘从叙事转向一种现代的明星形象。", "note_en": "Three Beauties of the Present Day is the representative work of Kitagawa Utamaro's ōkubi-e (large-head pictures). Three celebrated women are placed side by side: Tomimoto Toyohina of the Tamaya, Naniwaya Kita, and Takashima Ohisa. Their faces, hairstyles, robe patterns and glances differ; mica powder in the background makes a shimmering dark ground from which the faces emerge.\n\nUtamaro paints not status but fame itself: women who are consumed, discussed and looked at by the city. The large-head format enlarges the portrait to half-length, forcing the viewer to meet their eyes, and turns ukiyo-e from narrative toward a modern kind of star image.", "note_html": "《三位美人》是喜多川歌磨的大头画（大头画）的代表作。画中三位著名女性并排而立：玉屋的富士本丰姬、浪屋喜多，以及高岛大久。如她们的面容、发型、和服花纹与目光各不相同；背景使用云母粉，使深色背景闪闪发光，衬托出她们的面庞。\n\n歌磨画的不是地位，而是名气：这些女性被城市所关注、讨论和注视。大头画的形式将肖像放大至半身，使观者不得不与她们对视，也让浮世绘从叙事转向一种现代的明星形象。"}, "david-death-of-marat-1793": {"note": "《马拉之死》把一位被暗杀的政治家变成了烈士。马拉躺在浴缸里死去，身体沿着对角线滑落，右手仍握着羽毛笔，左手拿着写有请愿人名字的请愿书；木块上放着墨水瓶、文件和一把刀。背景是一片空荡的黑暗，没有街道，也没有刺客。\n\n大卫省略了现场的血腥和混乱，只留下一个安静的躯体，看起来几乎像宗教圣像。这是革命宣传的典范：它不报道事实，而是制造一个值得相信的形象。", "note_en": "The Death of Marat turns an assassinated politician into a martyr. Marat lies dead in his bath, body sliding along the diagonal, quill still in his right hand, a petition with a supplicant's name in his left; on the wooden block sit inkwell, papers and a knife. The background is a blank dark field, with no street and no assassin.\n\nDavid omits the blood and chaos of the scene, leaving only a quiet body that reads almost like an icon. It is the model of revolutionary propaganda: it does not report facts, it manufactures an image worth believing in.", "note_html": "《马拉之死》把一位被暗杀的政治家变成了烈士。马拉躺在浴缸里死去，身体沿着对角线滑落，右手仍握着羽毛笔，左手拿着写有请愿人名字的请愿书；木块上放着墨水瓶、文件和一把刀。背景是一片空荡的黑暗，没有街道，也没有刺客。\n\n大卫省略了现场的血腥和混乱，只留下一个安静的躯体，看起来几乎像宗教圣像。这是革命宣传的典范：它不报道事实，而是制造一个值得相信的形象。"}, "cle-1941-552-1795": {"note": "凯瑟琳·克莱门斯与子，1795年。欧洲。手抄本；Framed: 9 x 7.3 cm (3 9/16 x 2 7/8 in.); Sight: 8 x 6.1 cm (3 1/8 x 2 3/8 in.)。\n\n以亲子关系组织画面，儿童不是缩小的大人，而是独立角色。", "note_en": "Portrait of Catherine Clemens and Her Son, John Marcus Clemens, c. 1800. Richard Cosway (British, 1742–1821). Watercolor on ivory in a gold and split pearl frame; framed: 9 x 7.3 cm (3 9/16 x 2 7/8 in.); sight: 8 x 6.1 cm (3 1/8 x 2 3/8 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, The Edward B. Greene Collection, 1941.552\n\nWithin “Portrait and Self”, under “家庭与儿童”: Parent and child organise the picture; children are independent roles, not small adults.", "note_html": "凯瑟琳·克莱门斯与子，1795年。欧洲。手抄本；Framed: 9 x 7.3 cm (3 9/16 x 2 7/8 in.); Sight: 8 x 6.1 cm (3 1/8 x 2 3/8 in.)。\n\n以亲子关系组织画面，儿童不是缩小的大人，而是独立角色。"}, "cbl-thi-1314-1795": {"note": "《巴利经藏与帕玛莱故事：抄本插图》，1795年。东南亚。纸本、墨与颜料；写本；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「东南亚」区域页：《巴利经藏与帕玛莱故事：抄本插图》以1795年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。", "note_en": "Thai folding book (samut khoi) containing extracts from the Pali canon (Tipitaka) and Story of Phra Malai, the text illustrated with scenes from the jataka tales and the life of the Buddha, with ink, colours and gold on paper, dating to 1795. Side 1 is comprised of openings 1-40 while side 2 contains openings 41-79.\n\nBuilds the regional page for Southeast Asia: Extracts from the Pali canon (Tipitaka) and Story of Phra Malai enters at 1795 with a verifiable date and medium.", "note_html": "《巴利经藏与帕玛莱故事：抄本插图》，1795年。东南亚。纸本、墨与颜料；写本；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「东南亚」区域页：《巴利经藏与帕玛莱故事：抄本插图》以1795年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。"}, "cle-1989-340-1795": {"note": "拉达与黑天庆贺洒红节，1795年。南亚。蛋彩；Overall: 26.4 x 18.4 cm (10 3/8 x 7 1/4 in.); with borders: 32.8 x 24.5 cm (12 15/16 x 9 5/8 in.)。\n\n把神圣形象放回具体信仰：先看脸、手势与光环，再读教义。", "note_en": "Radha and Hindu God Krishna celebrating the festival Holi, c. 1800–1810. Northern India, Pahari kingdoms. Gum tempera, ink, and gold on paper; overall: 26.4 x 18.4 cm (10 3/8 x 7 1/4 in.); with borders: 32.8 x 24.5 cm (12 15/16 x 9 5/8 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Bequest of Mrs. Severance A. Millikin, 1989.340\n\nWithin “Faith and Image”, under “神圣人物”: Puts sacred figures back into a specific faith: face, gesture and halo first, doctrine second.", "note_html": "拉达与黑天庆贺洒红节，1795年。南亚。蛋彩；Overall: 26.4 x 18.4 cm (10 3/8 x 7 1/4 in.); with borders: 32.8 x 24.5 cm (12 15/16 x 9 5/8 in.)。\n\n把神圣形象放回具体信仰：先看脸、手势与光环，再读教义。"}, "cle-1992-84-1795": {"note": "行旅武士歇脚农舍，1795年。南亚。蛋彩；Overall: 25.8 x 35.6 cm (10 3/16 x 14 in.)。\n\n追踪摹本、复制与传教路线，看图像如何换手、换语境。", "note_en": "Traveling Warriors Stopping at a Farm, c. 1800. India, Rajasthan, Jodhpur school, early 19th Century. Gum tempera and ink on paper; overall: 25.8 x 35.6 cm (10 3/16 x 14 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Seventy-fifth anniversary gift of Dr. Norman Zaworski, 1992.84\n\nWithin “Word and Looking”, under “图像如何旅行”: Follows copies, replicas and missions to see images change hands and contexts.", "note_html": "行旅武士歇脚农舍，1795年。南亚。蛋彩；Overall: 25.8 x 35.6 cm (10 3/16 x 14 in.)。\n\n追踪摹本、复制与传教路线，看图像如何换手、换语境。"}, "cle-1987-161-1795": {"note": "黑天与长者交谈，1795年。南亚。蛋彩；Overall: 20.3 x 30.5 cm (8 x 12 in.)。\n\n把神圣形象放回具体信仰：先看脸、手势与光环，再读教义。", "note_en": "Hindu God Krishna Talking to Elders, c. 1800. India, Rajasthan, Kishangarh school, early 19th Century. Gum tempera and ink on paper; overall: 20.3 x 30.5 cm (8 x 12 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Anonymous Gift, 1987.161\n\nWithin “Faith and Image”, under “神圣人物”: Puts sacred figures back into a specific faith: face, gesture and halo first, doctrine second.", "note_html": "黑天与长者交谈，1795年。南亚。蛋彩；Overall: 20.3 x 30.5 cm (8 x 12 in.)。\n\n把神圣形象放回具体信仰：先看脸、手势与光环，再读教义。"}, "cle-1942-1151-1796": {"note": "苏珊·科伦·托尔斯肖像，1796年。北美。手抄本；Framed: 8 x 6.6 cm (3 1/8 x 2 5/8 in.); Unframed: 7.1 x 5.6 cm (2 13/16 x 2 3/16 in.)。\n\n不只看像不像，更看服饰、姿态与目光如何制造身份。", "note_en": "Portrait of Susan Coren Towers, 1796. James Peale (American, born The Thirteen Colonies, 1749–1831). Watercolor on ivory; framed: 8 x 6.6 cm (3 1/8 x 2 5/8 in.); unframed: 7.1 x 5.6 cm (2 13/16 x 2 3/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, The Edward B. Greene Collection, 1942.1151\n\nWithin “Portrait and Self”, under “肖像”: Not only likeness: dress, pose and gaze manufacture identity.", "note_html": "苏珊·科伦·托尔斯肖像，1796年。北美。手抄本；Framed: 8 x 6.6 cm (3 1/8 x 2 5/8 in.); Unframed: 7.1 x 5.6 cm (2 13/16 x 2 3/16 in.)。\n\n不只看像不像，更看服饰、姿态与目光如何制造身份。"}, "cbl-thi-1310-1797": {"note": "《巴利经藏与帕玛莱故事：抄本插图（二）》，1797年。东南亚。纸本、墨与颜料；写本；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「东南亚」区域页：《巴利经藏与帕玛莱故事：抄本插图（二）》以1797年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。", "note_en": "Thai folding book (samut khoi) containing extracts from the Pali canon (Tipitaka) and Story of Phra Malai, the text illustrated with scenes from the jataka tales and scenes of corpse meditation, with ink, colours and gold on paper, dating to 1797. Side 1 is comprised of openings 1-48 while side 2 contains openings 49-96.\n\nBuilds the regional page for Southeast Asia: Extracts from the Pali canon (Tipitaka) and Story of Phra Malai enters at 1797 with a verifiable date and medium.", "note_html": "《巴利经藏与帕玛莱故事：抄本插图（二）》，1797年。东南亚。纸本、墨与颜料；写本；馆藏未著录尺寸。\n\n补足「东南亚」区域页：《巴利经藏与帕玛莱故事：抄本插图（二）》以1797年入列，给出一条可核对的时段与材料。"}, "meynier-apollo-urania-1798": {"note": "梅尼耶为图卢兹宅邸绘制的五联画之一；阿波罗与掌天文的缪斯乌剌尼亚并置，把光、诗与天文知识连在一起。\n\n在「山水与自然」的「天文」线索里，把天文女神与太阳神放在同一画面：观测星空也是一种神圣秩序。", "note_en": "1798, Europe. 夏尔·梅尼耶; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 2003.6.3. This is a painting (布面油画).", "note_html": "梅尼耶为图卢兹宅邸绘制的五联画之一；阿波罗与掌天文的缪斯乌剌尼亚并置，把光、诗与天文知识连在一起。\n\n在「山水与自然」的「天文」线索里，把天文女神与太阳神放在同一画面：观测星空也是一种神圣秩序。"}, "cle-2003-6-3-1798": {"note": "阿波罗与乌拉尼亚，1798年。欧洲。油画；Overall: 275 x 235 cm (108 1/4 x 92 1/2 in.)。\n\n让光源、金底与反射参与叙事，光不是效果，而是意义。", "note_en": "Apollo, God of Light, Eloquence, Poetry, and the Fine Arts with Urania, Muse of Astronomy, 1798. Charles Meynier (French, 1768–1832). Oil on canvas; overall: 275 x 235 cm (108 1/4 x 92 1/2 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Severance and Greta Millikin Purchase Fund, 2003.6.3\n\nWithin “Material and Technique”, under “光与材料”: Source, gold ground and reflection narrate; light is meaning, not effect.", "note_html": "阿波罗与乌拉尼亚，1798年。欧洲。油画；Overall: 275 x 235 cm (108 1/4 x 92 1/2 in.)。\n\n让光源、金底与反射参与叙事，光不是效果，而是意义。"}, "goya-third-of-may-1814": {"note": "《五月三日》记录了拿破仑军队在马德里对平民的夜间处决。画面左侧，一排士兵举起火枪，背对观众；画面右侧，一些被处决者已经倒下，另一些用手遮住脸，而中央一个穿白衬衫的男子张开双臂，直视枪口。他身后的灯笼把黑暗变成了舞台。\n\n戈雅画的不是什么英雄的胜利，而是恐惧、鲜血和无法抵抗的躯体。白衣男子的光线像基督一般照在身上，但他并非神性，只是一个即将死亡的人。这幅画常被认为是现代战争形象的开端：不再是将军，而是被杀的人。", "note_en": "The Third of May 1808 records a night execution of civilians by Napoleon's troops in Madrid. On the left, a rank of soldiers raises muskets, backs to the viewer; on the right, some of the condemned have already fallen, others cover their faces, and at the centre a man in a white shirt throws his arms wide and looks straight into the guns. A lantern behind him turns the darkness into a stage.\n\nGoya paints not the triumph of heroes but fear, blood and bodies that cannot resist. The man in white is lit like a Christ, yet he is not divine, only a person about to die. The picture is often taken as the beginning of the modern image of war: no longer generals, but the killed.", "note_html": "《五月三日》记录了拿破仑军队在马德里对平民的夜间处决。画面左侧，一排士兵举起火枪，背对观众；画面右侧，一些被处决者已经倒下，另一些用手遮住脸，而中央一个穿白衬衫的男子张开双臂，直视枪口。他身后的灯笼把黑暗变成了舞台。\n\n戈雅画的不是什么英雄的胜利，而是恐惧、鲜血和无法抵抗的躯体。白衣男子的光线像基督一般照在身上，但他并非神性，只是一个即将死亡的人。这幅画常被认为是现代战争形象的开端：不再是将军，而是被杀的人。"}, "ingres-grande-odalisque-1814": {"note": "《大宫女》展示了一位女子半躺在长沙发上。她背对着我们，头回过肩看，蓝色头巾和金色布料包裹着身体；孔雀羽扇、水烟和帷幕填满了封闭的室内空间。她的脊柱被拉长，右腿多了一个关节，身体的曲线挑战了人体解剖学。\n\nIngres并不在意解剖的准确性；他追求的是连续的线条和光滑的肌肤。这幅画将“东方”想象成一个懒散、可观赏的空间，并将新古典主义的线条推进到抽象的边界。", "note_en": "La Grande Odalisque shows a concubine reclining on a divan. Her back is turned, her head over her shoulder, blue turban and gold fabric enclosing the body; a peacock fan, hookah and drapery fill a closed interior. Her spine is elongated, the right leg gains an extra joint, and the curve of the body defies anatomy.\n\nIngres does not care about anatomical correctness; he wants continuous line and smooth skin. The painting imagines \"the Orient\" as a languid, viewable space, and pushes Neoclassical line to the edge of abstraction.", "note_html": "《大宫女》展示了一位女子半躺在长沙发上。她背对着我们，头回过肩看，蓝色头巾和金色布料包裹着身体；孔雀羽扇、水烟和帷幕填满了封闭的室内空间。她的脊柱被拉长，右腿多了一个关节，身体的曲线挑战了人体解剖学。\n\nIngres并不在意解剖的准确性；他追求的是连续的线条和光滑的肌肤。这幅画将“东方”想象成一个懒散、可观赏的空间，并将新古典主义的线条推进到抽象的边界。"}, "auto-d49e9fd0": {"note": "《橙与书》静物》是拉斐尔·皮尔约1815年的美国静物画作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“橙与书》静物”为题，属于美国的绘画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。", "note_en": "1815, Cross-regional. 拉斐尔·皮尔; source: Wikimedia Commons, catalog no. File:Still life with orange and book-raphaelle peale.JPG. This is a painting.", "note_html": "《橙与书》静物》是拉斐尔·皮尔约1815年的美国静物画作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“橙与书》静物”为题，属于美国的绘画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。"}, "david-cupid-psyche-1817": {"note": "1817，法国 巴黎。雅克-路易·大卫的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。", "note_en": "1817, Europe. 雅克-路易·大卫; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1962.37. This is a painting (oil on canvas).", "note_html": "1817，法国 巴黎。雅克-路易·大卫的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。"}, "friedrich-wanderer-1818": {"note": "《迷雾海上的漫步者》把一个男人放在岩石高峰上，他背对我们，面对翻腾的迷雾海。他穿着深绿色外套，拄着拐杖，头发被风吹起；远处的山峰像岛屿或未知的边界一样从雾中升起。下方是深谷，上方是苍白的天空。弗里德里希用“背影人物”让观者与画中的人物一起凝视。这个男人既不是英雄也不是游客，而是在无限面前失去尺度感的人。浪漫主义的崇高正是这种混合了宏大与不安的感觉。", "note_en": "Wanderer above the Sea of Fog places a man on a rocky summit, his back to us, facing a churning sea of mist. He wears a dark green coat, leans on a cane, hair blown by wind; distant peaks rise through the fog like islands or unknown borders. Below is a deep valley, above a pale sky.\n\nFriedrich uses the Rückenfigur to make the viewer gaze with the figure in the painting. This man is neither hero nor tourist but someone who loses his sense of scale before the infinite. The Romantic sublime is exactly this grandeur mixed with unease.", "note_html": "《迷雾海上的漫步者》把一个男人放在岩石高峰上，他背对我们，面对翻腾的迷雾海。他穿着深绿色外套，拄着拐杖，头发被风吹起；远处的山峰像岛屿或未知的边界一样从雾中升起。下方是深谷，上方是苍白的天空。弗里德里希用“背影人物”让观者与画中的人物一起凝视。这个男人既不是英雄也不是游客，而是在无限面前失去尺度感的人。浪漫主义的崇高正是这种混合了宏大与不安的感觉。"}, "goya-saturn-1820": {"note": "《萨图恩吞食自己的儿子》是戈雅黑色画作中最令人震惊的一幅。萨图恩看起来像个疯狂的老头，眼睛瞪大，嘴巴张开，双手紧握着一个已经被啃掉头和胳膊的小尸体。背景是黑色的，只有肉体和白布捕捉到光线。\n\n晚年的戈雅把自己关在索尔多庄园里，把这些作品直接画在墙上。它们既不是接受委托也不是为展览而作，更像是一个人在与恐惧斗争的私人记录。神话在这里失去了寓意，只剩下暴力本身。", "note_en": "Saturn Devouring His Son is the most appalling of Goya's Black Paintings. Saturn appears as a mad old man, eyes staring, mouth wide, both hands gripping a small body whose head and arm have already been bitten away. The background is black; only flesh and white cloth catch the light.\n\nIn his late years Goya shut himself in the Quinta del Sordo and painted these works directly onto the walls. They were neither commissions nor exhibition pieces, more like a private record of a man fighting fear. Myth loses its allegory here and leaves only violence itself.", "note_html": "《萨图恩吞食自己的儿子》是戈雅黑色画作中最令人震惊的一幅。萨图恩看起来像个疯狂的老头，眼睛瞪大，嘴巴张开，双手紧握着一个已经被啃掉头和胳膊的小尸体。背景是黑色的，只有肉体和白布捕捉到光线。\n\n晚年的戈雅把自己关在索尔多庄园里，把这些作品直接画在墙上。它们既不是接受委托也不是为展览而作，更像是一个人在与恐惧斗争的私人记录。神话在这里失去了寓意，只剩下暴力本身。"}, "auto-78b2a883": {"note": "《女史箴图》是现存最早的中国绢本人物长卷之一，通常被认为是东晋顾恺之的原作、唐代摹本。画卷根据张华《女史箴》的十二段箴文绘制，现存九段：有冯媛挡熊、班姬辞辇，也有宫中女子对镜梳妆、围坐交谈的日常场景。人物衣带飘举，线条细而不断，像春蚕吐丝。\n\n画面没有透视，也没有阴影，却用线条的节奏、人物之间的距离和空白来组织叙事。它既是道德教科书，也是一部宫廷女性生活的图像史。1900年庚子事变后流入英国，现藏大英博物馆。", "note_en": "1820, Cross-regional. Unknown; source: Wikimedia Commons, catalog no. File:The School Room - Anon-c1820-70027.jpg. This is a drawing.", "note_html": "《女史箴图》是现存最早的中国绢本人物长卷之一，通常被认为是东晋顾恺之的原作、唐代摹本。画卷根据张华《女史箴》的十二段箴文绘制，现存九段：有冯媛挡熊、班姬辞辇，也有宫中女子对镜梳妆、围坐交谈的日常场景。人物衣带飘举，线条细而不断，像春蚕吐丝。\n\n画面没有透视，也没有阴影，却用线条的节奏、人物之间的距离和空白来组织叙事。它既是道德教科书，也是一部宫廷女性生活的图像史。1900年庚子事变后流入英国，现藏大英博物馆。"}, "constable-hay-wain-1821": {"note": "《干草车》展示了一条浅河、一辆正在过河的干草车和一座农舍。左边是树木投下的阴影；右边天空突然开阔，云被吹散；车停在河中间，马儿在喝水，远处是萨福克的田野。\n\n康斯特布尔坚持户外作画，把英国的天气看作不断变化的状态，而不是背景。那座农舍是威利·洛特的小屋，他从小就认识这个地方。这种对当地土地的固执依恋，让风景画第一次具备了日常的分量。", "note_en": "The Hay Wain shows a shallow river, a hay wagon crossing it, and a farmhouse. Trees cast shadow on the left; on the right the sky suddenly opens, clouds blown apart; the wagon stands midstream, horses drinking, Suffolk fields beyond.\n\nConstable insisted on painting outdoors, treating English weather as a changing condition rather than a backdrop. The farmhouse is Willy Lott's cottage, a place he had known since childhood. This stubborn attachment to local ground gave landscape painting everyday weight for the first time.", "note_html": "《干草车》展示了一条浅河、一辆正在过河的干草车和一座农舍。左边是树木投下的阴影；右边天空突然开阔，云被吹散；车停在河中间，马儿在喝水，远处是萨福克的田野。\n\n康斯特布尔坚持户外作画，把英国的天气看作不断变化的状态，而不是背景。那座农舍是威利·洛特的小屋，他从小就认识这个地方。这种对当地土地的固执依恋，让风景画第一次具备了日常的分量。"}, "delacroix-liberty-1830": {"note": "《自由引导人民》将1830年七月革命的路障变成了神话。自由女神站在中央，半裸着，右手举起三色旗，左手握着火枪，大踏步踩过尸体。她周围有戴高顶礼帽的市民、拿着手枪的青年、跪在地上的工人；背景是巴黎的屋顶和浓烟。\n\n德拉克洛瓦描绘革命时，不是井然有序的示威，而是混乱、血腥的进攻。三色旗是画面里最亮的颜色，就像一座灯塔，把人群吸引过去。这幅画后来成为法国共和国的象征之一。", "note_en": "Liberty Leading the People turns the barricades of the July Revolution of 1830 into myth. Liberty stands half-naked at the centre, the tricolour raised in her right hand, a musket in her left, striding over bodies. Around her are a bourgeois in a top hat, a youth with pistols, a worker kneeling on the ground; Paris rooftops and smoke behind.\n\nDelacroix paints the revolution not as an orderly demonstration but as a chaotic, bloody advance. The tricolour is the brightest colour in the picture, a lighthouse drawing the crowd towards it. The painting later became one of the symbols of the French Republic.", "note_html": "《自由引导人民》将1830年七月革命的路障变成了神话。自由女神站在中央，半裸着，右手举起三色旗，左手握着火枪，大踏步踩过尸体。她周围有戴高顶礼帽的市民、拿着手枪的青年、跪在地上的工人；背景是巴黎的屋顶和浓烟。\n\n德拉克洛瓦描绘革命时，不是井然有序的示威，而是混乱、血腥的进攻。三色旗是画面里最亮的颜色，就像一座灯塔，把人群吸引过去。这幅画后来成为法国共和国的象征之一。"}, "hokusai-south-wind-clear-sky-1831": {"note": "early 1830s，日本 江户。葛饰北斋的版画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。这是一件版画作品，线条与印痕记录了图像被复制的路径。", "note_en": "early 1830s, East Asia. 葛饰北斋; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1930.189. This is a print (版画（彩色木刻）).", "note_html": "early 1830s，日本 江户。葛饰北斋的版画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。这是一件版画作品，线条与印痕记录了图像被复制的路径。"}, "hokusai-great-wave-1831": {"note": "《神奈川冲浪里》是葛饰北斋《富岳三十六景》中最著名的版画。一股巨大的海浪占据了画面：浪尖像爪子一样张开，三艘运输船被推到下面，船夫们低身躲避；远处的富士山几乎只是一个三角形，静静地停在浪的尽头。\n\n北斋用不同层次的普鲁士蓝印制海浪，从深靛蓝到浅白色，把海水切割成透明的刀锋。他在同一幅作品中展现了瞬间的暴力和永恒的宁静：浪会打下来，而富士山不会。", "note_en": "The Great Wave off Kanagawa is the most famous print from Hokusai's Thirty-Six Views of Mount Fuji. An enormous wave dominates the sheet: its crest opens like talons, three transport boats are pushed beneath it, boatmen crouching low; far away Mount Fuji is almost only a triangle, resting quietly at the end of the wave.\n\nHokusai printed the wave in layers of Prussian blue, from deep indigo to pale white, cutting the sea into translucent blades. He puts the violence of an instant and eternal stillness in one composition: the wave will fall, Fuji will not.", "note_html": "《神奈川冲浪里》是葛饰北斋《富岳三十六景》中最著名的版画。一股巨大的海浪占据了画面：浪尖像爪子一样张开，三艘运输船被推到下面，船夫们低身躲避；远处的富士山几乎只是一个三角形，静静地停在浪的尽头。\n\n北斋用不同层次的普鲁士蓝印制海浪，从深靛蓝到浅白色，把海水切割成透明的刀锋。他在同一幅作品中展现了瞬间的暴力和永恒的宁静：浪会打下来，而富士山不会。"}, "hiroshige-shono-driving-rain-1833": {"note": "1833，日本 东海道。歌川广重的版画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。这是一件版画作品，线条与印痕记录了图像被复制的路径。", "note_en": "1833, East Asia. 歌川广重; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1948.306. This is a print (版画（彩色木刻）).", "note_html": "1833，日本 东海道。歌川广重的版画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。这是一件版画作品，线条与印痕记录了图像被复制的路径。"}, "turner-burning-houses-1835": {"note": "1835，英国 伦敦。约瑟夫·马洛德·威廉·透纳的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。", "note_en": "1835, Europe. 约瑟夫·马洛德·威廉·透纳; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1942.647. This is a painting (oil on canvas).", "note_html": "1835，英国 伦敦。约瑟夫·马洛德·威廉·透纳的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。"}, "ingres-antiochus-stratonice-1838": {"note": "c. 1838，法国 巴黎。让-奥古斯特-多米尼克·安格尔的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。", "note_en": "c. 1838, Europe. 让-奥古斯特-多米尼克·安格尔; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1966.13. This is a painting (油画（亚麻布）).", "note_html": "c. 1838，法国 巴黎。让-奥古斯特-多米尼克·安格尔的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。"}, "turner-fighting-temeraire-1839": {"note": "《战斗的特梅莱尔号》描绘了一艘老战舰的最后航程。一艘拖船冒着黑烟，拖着白色的特梅莱尔号驶向拆船厂；夕阳西下，天空从金色逐渐变成深红色，水面像熔化的镜子。桅杆已不在，船身看起来空旷而巨大。\n\n特纳将工业与怀旧置于同一光线下：蒸汽拖船属于新时代，帆船则属于正在消逝的英国海上力量。美和哀悼在这里是同一个姿态，这也是这幅画成为英国最受喜爱的画作之一的原因。", "note_en": "The Fighting Temeraire depicts the last voyage of an old warship. A tug belches black smoke as it hauls the white Temeraire towards the breaker's yard; the sun sets in the west, sky moving from gold to deep red, water like a molten mirror. The masts are gone, and the hull looks empty and enormous.\n\nTurner puts industry and nostalgia into the same light: the steam tug belongs to the new age, the sailing ship to a vanishing British sea power. Beauty and mourning are the same gesture here, which is why the picture became one of Britain's best-loved paintings.", "note_html": "《战斗的特梅莱尔号》描绘了一艘老战舰的最后航程。一艘拖船冒着黑烟，拖着白色的特梅莱尔号驶向拆船厂；夕阳西下，天空从金色逐渐变成深红色，水面像熔化的镜子。桅杆已不在，船身看起来空旷而巨大。\n\n特纳将工业与怀旧置于同一光线下：蒸汽拖船属于新时代，帆船则属于正在消逝的英国海上力量。美和哀悼在这里是同一个姿态，这也是这幅画成为英国最受喜爱的画作之一的原因。"}, "aivazovsky-ninth-wave-1850": {"note": "《第九波》描绘了风暴过后的黎明。海面上依然被巨浪撕裂；六个幸存者抓住浪尖上的一块残骸；天空从深蓝逐渐转为金橙色，阳光穿透了云层。中央的海浪像一堵透明的墙，几乎要吞没那些人。\n\n艾瓦佐夫斯基并未亲眼见过这场特定的风暴，但他画出了水的透明感、泡沫和折射，令人信服。他创作了数千幅海景画，其中这幅最为人引用：在一幅画里展现了大自然的力量和人类的渺小。", "note_en": "The Ninth Wave shows dawn after a storm. The sea is still torn by huge waves; six survivors cling to a piece of wreckage on the crest; the sky moves from deep blue to orange-gold as sunlight breaks through cloud. The central wave rises like a transparent wall, almost swallowing the figures.\n\nAivazovsky had not witnessed this particular storm, yet he paints the transparency, foam and refraction of water with extraordinary conviction. He produced thousands of seascapes; this is the most quoted: nature's power and human smallness in one breath.", "note_html": "《第九波》描绘了风暴过后的黎明。海面上依然被巨浪撕裂；六个幸存者抓住浪尖上的一块残骸；天空从深蓝逐渐转为金橙色，阳光穿透了云层。中央的海浪像一堵透明的墙，几乎要吞没那些人。\n\n艾瓦佐夫斯基并未亲眼见过这场特定的风暴，但他画出了水的透明感、泡沫和折射，令人信服。他创作了数千幅海景画，其中这幅最为人引用：在一幅画里展现了大自然的力量和人类的渺小。"}, "auto-d713ad77": {"note": "《十九世纪英国学校教室》是佚名画家约1850年的风俗画作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“十九世纪英国学校教室”为题，属于英国的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。", "note_en": "1850, Europe. Unknown; source: Wikimedia Commons, catalog no. File:Classroom 19th century English School.jpg. This is a painting (oil painting).", "note_html": "《十九世纪英国学校教室》是佚名画家约1850年的风俗画作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“十九世纪英国学校教室”为题，属于英国的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。"}, "courbet-painters-studio-1855": {"note": "《画家的工作室》的副标题是“一个真正的寓言，总结了我七年的艺术和道德生活”。在画面中央，库尔贝坐在画架前画风景画，旁边有裸体模特和一个男孩。右边是他的朋友和支持者——波德莱尔、普鲁东、尚弗勒里等；左边是日常生活中的普通人：工人、农民、乞丐、一位寡妇。库尔贝把“社会”搬进了画室，把艺术创作和政治立场放在同一个空间里。这既是对学院派的挑战，也是现实主义宣言：画家不画神话，而是画他眼中的人。", "note_en": "The Painter's Studio carries the subtitle \"A real allegory summing up seven years of my artistic and moral life.\" At the centre, Courbet sits at his easel painting a landscape, a nude model and a boy beside him. On the right are his friends and supporters — Baudelaire, Proudhon, Champfleury and others; on the left, ordinary people from daily life: workers, peasants, beggars, a widow.\n\nCourbet moves \"society\" into the studio and puts artistic production and political stance in the same room. It is both a challenge to the Academy and a Realist manifesto: the painter does not paint myth, but the people he sees.", "note_html": "《画家的工作室》的副标题是“一个真正的寓言，总结了我七年的艺术和道德生活”。在画面中央，库尔贝坐在画架前画风景画，旁边有裸体模特和一个男孩。右边是他的朋友和支持者——波德莱尔、普鲁东、尚弗勒里等；左边是日常生活中的普通人：工人、农民、乞丐、一位寡妇。库尔贝把“社会”搬进了画室，把艺术创作和政治立场放在同一个空间里。这既是对学院派的挑战，也是现实主义宣言：画家不画神话，而是画他眼中的人。"}, "hiroshige-sudden-shower-1857": {"note": "《大桥与安宅的骤雨》描绘了一个木桥横跨隅田川的景象，在暴雨中行人匆匆而过：有人撑伞，有人缩着肩膀，有人干脆淋湿。雨水被画成密集的斜线；河流、屋顶和远岸被压平为灰蓝色的轮廓。\n\n广重没有画暴风雨的中心，而是描绘雨点打在人们身上的瞬间。这样的斜线节奏吸引了梵高，他用油画临摹了这幅版画，把雨画成厚厚的颜料笔触。", "note_en": "Sudden Shower over Shin-Ōhashi Bridge and Atake shows a wooden bridge over the Sumida River as a rainstorm drives pedestrians across it: some open umbrellas, some hunch their shoulders, some simply get wet. Rain is cut as dense diagonal lines; river, roofs and the far bank are flattened into grey-blue silhouettes.\n\nHiroshige does not paint the storm's centre but the moment rain lands on people. That rhythm of diagonals fascinated Van Gogh, who copied the print in oil, turning the rain into thick strokes of paint.", "note_html": "《大桥与安宅的骤雨》描绘了一个木桥横跨隅田川的景象，在暴雨中行人匆匆而过：有人撑伞，有人缩着肩膀，有人干脆淋湿。雨水被画成密集的斜线；河流、屋顶和远岸被压平为灰蓝色的轮廓。\n\n广重没有画暴风雨的中心，而是描绘雨点打在人们身上的瞬间。这样的斜线节奏吸引了梵高，他用油画临摹了这幅版画，把雨画成厚厚的颜料笔触。"}, "millet-the-gleaners-1857": {"note": "《拾穗者》展示了三个农妇在收割后弯腰捡拾散落的谷粒。她们的身体几乎折成直角，手触地面；她们身后是干草堆、收割工人和淡金色的天空。画面没有故事，只有反复的劳作和沉重的地平线。\n\n米勒赋予了他那个时代最不被重视的劳动以宏大的规模：三个形象就像低矮的雕塑，沉默、稳固，不需要同情。当时的保守评论家看作这是危险的宣言，因为它赋予了贫困以尊严和份量。", "note_en": "The Gleaners shows three peasant women bending to pick up scattered grain after the harvest. Their bodies fold almost to the right angle, hands reaching the ground; behind them stand haystacks, harvesters and a pale gold sky. There is no story, only repeated labour and a heavy horizon.\n\nMillet gives the least regarded work of his time a monumental scale: three figures like low sculptures, silent, solid, asking for no pity. Conservative critics read it as a dangerous manifesto when it was shown, because it gave poverty dignity and volume.", "note_html": "《拾穗者》展示了三个农妇在收割后弯腰捡拾散落的谷粒。她们的身体几乎折成直角，手触地面；她们身后是干草堆、收割工人和淡金色的天空。画面没有故事，只有反复的劳作和沉重的地平线。\n\n米勒赋予了他那个时代最不被重视的劳动以宏大的规模：三个形象就像低矮的雕塑，沉默、稳固，不需要同情。当时的保守评论家看作这是危险的宣言，因为它赋予了贫困以尊严和份量。"}, "manet-olympia-1863": {"note": "《奥林匹亚》用19世纪巴黎的现实取代了提香式的躺卧裸女。奥林匹亚穿着拖鞋和黑丝带躺在床上，直视观者；她身后，一名黑人女仆手捧花束，一只黑猫站在她脚边，尾巴竖起。床、花束和披肩的描绘平直直接，没有古典的柔和感。\n\n这幅画在1865年沙龙展引起了轰动：问题不在于裸体，而在于她的目光。她不再是被观看的对象，而是会回望的人。马奈的平涂和强烈的黑白对比打破了自文艺复兴以来统治裸体画的观赏规则。", "note_en": "Olympia replaces the Titianesque reclining nude with the reality of nineteenth-century Paris. Olympia lies on a bed in slippers and a black ribbon, looking directly at the viewer; behind her a black maid holds flowers, and a black cat stands at her feet, tail up. Bed, bouquet and shawl are painted flatly and directly, without classical softness.\n\nThe painting caused a scandal at the 1865 Salon: the problem was not nudity but her gaze. She is no longer an object to be looked at but someone who looks back. Manet's flat paint and hard black-white contrasts break the viewing contract that had governed the nude since the Renaissance.", "note_html": "《奥林匹亚》用19世纪巴黎的现实取代了提香式的躺卧裸女。奥林匹亚穿着拖鞋和黑丝带躺在床上，直视观者；她身后，一名黑人女仆手捧花束，一只黑猫站在她脚边，尾巴竖起。床、花束和披肩的描绘平直直接，没有古典的柔和感。\n\n这幅画在1865年沙龙展引起了轰动：问题不在于裸体，而在于她的目光。她不再是被观看的对象，而是会回望的人。马奈的平涂和强烈的黑白对比打破了自文艺复兴以来统治裸体画的观赏规则。"}, "manet-dejeuner-sur-herbe-1863": {"note": "《草地上的午餐》把一个裸体女人和两个完全穿着的男人放在巴黎郊外的草地上。女人坐在左边，膝盖弯起，目光直视画外；男人们在聊天，似乎毫不在意。另一名女子在后面的溪边弯腰。光透过树叶洒下，人物看起来像是贴在同一个平面上。\n\n马奈借鉴了乔尔乔内《田园音乐会》的构图，但去掉了神话和田园诗意。裸体不再是女神，只是一个在午餐的巴黎女性；这种莫名其妙的并置使这幅画成为现代艺术最早的丑闻之一。", "note_en": "Le Déjeuner sur l'herbe places a nude woman and two fully dressed men on grass outside Paris. The woman sits at the left, knees drawn up, looking straight out of the picture; the men talk, apparently unconcerned. Another woman bends by the stream behind. Light falls through leaves, and the figures seem pasted onto a single plane.\n\nManet borrows the composition of Giorgione's Pastoral Concert but removes myth and idyll. The nude is no longer a goddess, only a Parisian woman at lunch; this unexplained juxtaposition made the painting one of the first scandals of modern art.", "note_html": "《草地上的午餐》把一个裸体女人和两个完全穿着的男人放在巴黎郊外的草地上。女人坐在左边，膝盖弯起，目光直视画外；男人们在聊天，似乎毫不在意。另一名女子在后面的溪边弯腰。光透过树叶洒下，人物看起来像是贴在同一个平面上。\n\n马奈借鉴了乔尔乔内《田园音乐会》的构图，但去掉了神话和田园诗意。裸体不再是女神，只是一个在午餐的巴黎女性；这种莫名其妙的并置使这幅画成为现代艺术最早的丑闻之一。"}, "auto-9afb2e56": {"note": "《女史箴图》是现存最早的中国绢本人物长卷之一，通常被认为是东晋顾恺之的原作、唐代摹本。画卷根据张华《女史箴》的十二段箴文绘制，现存九段：有冯媛挡熊、班姬辞辇，也有宫中女子对镜梳妆、围坐交谈的日常场景。人物衣带飘举，线条细而不断，像春蚕吐丝。\n\n画面没有透视，也没有阴影，却用线条的节奏、人物之间的距离和空白来组织叙事。它既是道德教科书，也是一部宫廷女性生活的图像史。1900年庚子事变后流入英国，现藏大英博物馆。", "note_en": "1865, Cross-regional. 威廉·莱布尔; source: Wikimedia Commons, catalog no. File:Portrait of an old woman LACMA 83.1.1354c.jpg. This is a print.", "note_html": "《女史箴图》是现存最早的中国绢本人物长卷之一，通常被认为是东晋顾恺之的原作、唐代摹本。画卷根据张华《女史箴》的十二段箴文绘制，现存九段：有冯媛挡熊、班姬辞辇，也有宫中女子对镜梳妆、围坐交谈的日常场景。人物衣带飘举，线条细而不断，像春蚕吐丝。\n\n画面没有透视，也没有阴影，却用线条的节奏、人物之间的距离和空白来组织叙事。它既是道德教科书，也是一部宫廷女性生活的图像史。1900年庚子事变后流入英国，现藏大英博物馆。"}, "monet-red-kerchief-1870": {"note": "c. 1868–73，法国。克劳德·莫奈的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。", "note_en": "c. 1868–73, Europe. 克劳德·莫奈; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1958.39. This is a painting (oil on canvas).", "note_html": "c. 1868–73，法国。克劳德·莫奈的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。"}, "whistler-arrangement-grey-black-1871": {"note": "《灰与黑的安排》第一号展示了一位老妇人侧身坐着，脚下放着一只脚凳；她穿着黑色连衣裙和白色帽子，背景是灰色的墙和几幅装裱的画作。画中几乎没有故事，只有垂直和水平的线条以及黑色和灰色的层次。\n\n惠斯勒坚持用音乐式的标题，拒绝让这幅画被解读为“母亲”或“肖像”。他想要一种安排：色彩、形状和情绪像乐谱一样构成。这种唯美主义态度后来影响了抽象艺术对绘画本身的关注。", "note_en": "Arrangement in Grey and Black No. 1 shows an elderly woman seated in profile, a footstool at her feet; she wears a black dress and white cap, against a grey wall and a few framed prints. There is almost no story, only vertical and horizontal lines and a scale of black and grey.\n\nWhistler insisted on musical titles and refused to let the picture be read as \"mother\" or \"portrait.\" He wanted an arrangement: colour, shape and mood composed like a score. This Aestheticist attitude later shaped abstract art's attention to painting itself.", "note_html": "《灰与黑的安排》第一号展示了一位老妇人侧身坐着，脚下放着一只脚凳；她穿着黑色连衣裙和白色帽子，背景是灰色的墙和几幅装裱的画作。画中几乎没有故事，只有垂直和水平的线条以及黑色和灰色的层次。\n\n惠斯勒坚持用音乐式的标题，拒绝让这幅画被解读为“母亲”或“肖像”。他想要一种安排：色彩、形状和情绪像乐谱一样构成。这种唯美主义态度后来影响了抽象艺术对绘画本身的关注。"}, "monet-impression-sunrise-1872": {"note": "《印象·日出》展示了勒阿弗尔港的黎明。太阳是一个橘红色的小点；薄雾把水面分成灰蓝色和浅紫色；远处的吊车、烟囱和桅杆都模糊不清，而前景中一只小船用几笔短刷划破水面。\n\n莫奈不画轮廓，他记录的是某一瞬间空气中的光。评论家路易·勒鲁瓦借用这个标题来讽刺这些画家为“印象派”，这个名字最终被画家们接受。现代绘画的名字就这样因为误解而产生了。", "note_en": "Impression, Sunrise shows dawn in the port of Le Havre. The sun is an orange-red dot; mist divides the water into grey-blue and pale violet; cranes, chimneys and masts blur in the distance, while a small boat cuts the surface in the foreground with a few short strokes.\n\nMonet does not draw outlines; he records light in the air at a particular moment. The critic Louis Leroy borrowed the title to mock these painters as \"Impressionists,\" and the name was taken up by the group. Modern painting acquired its name through a misreading.", "note_html": "《印象·日出》展示了勒阿弗尔港的黎明。太阳是一个橘红色的小点；薄雾把水面分成灰蓝色和浅紫色；远处的吊车、烟囱和桅杆都模糊不清，而前景中一只小船用几笔短刷划破水面。\n\n莫奈不画轮廓，他记录的是某一瞬间空气中的光。评论家路易·勒鲁瓦借用这个标题来讽刺这些画家为“印象派”，这个名字最终被画家们接受。现代绘画的名字就这样因为误解而产生了。"}, "morisot-the-cradle-1872": {"note": "《摇篮》展示了画家的妹妹埃德玛坐在婴儿床旁，通过纱帘看着熟睡的宝宝。她用左臂支撑着头，右手放在婴儿床边；面纱像薄雾一样覆盖在孩子的脸上。灰色、浅蓝色和粉色为主，轮廓几乎消失。\n\n莫里索是印象派中最重要的女性，她画的不是公共空间的景象，而是家庭的宁静内部。观看的姿态温柔，但也略显疲惫和恍惚。", "note_en": "The Cradle shows the painter's sister Edma seated beside a cot, watching her sleeping baby through a gauze curtain. Her left arm supports her head, her right hand rests on the cot's edge; the veil lies over the child's face like mist. Greys, pale blues and pinks dominate, and outlines are almost absent.\n\nMorisot was the most important woman in the Impressionist group, and she painted not the spectacle of public space but the quiet interior of the family. The pose of watching is tender, but also a little tired and absent.", "note_html": "《摇篮》展示了画家的妹妹埃德玛坐在婴儿床旁，通过纱帘看着熟睡的宝宝。她用左臂支撑着头，右手放在婴儿床边；面纱像薄雾一样覆盖在孩子的脸上。灰色、浅蓝色和粉色为主，轮廓几乎消失。\n\n莫里索是印象派中最重要的女性，她画的不是公共空间的景象，而是家庭的宁静内部。观看的姿态温柔，但也略显疲惫和恍惚。"}, "repin-barge-haulers-1873": {"note": "《伏尔加河上的驳船拉夫》展示了一支由十一人组成的队伍沿河拉绳，身体前倾，双脚陷入沙中。前面一位老人目视前方；他身后的一位年轻人试图抬起头。宽阔的河流、远处的小船和炽热的天空在他们身后展开。\n\n作为学生的列宾曾沿伏尔加河旅行，并在看到这些拉夫后开始创作这幅画。他把俄罗斯的贫困和坚韧转化为一种影像。", "note_en": "Barge Haulers on the Volga shows a team of eleven men hauling a rope along the river, bodies leaning forward, feet sunk in sand. At the front an old man stares ahead; behind him a younger man tries to lift his head. The broad river, a distant boat and a hot sky lie behind them.\n\nAs a student Repin travelled the Volga and began the picture after seeing the haulers. He turns Russian poverty and endurance into a physical epic: no heroes, only people joined by a rope.", "note_html": "《伏尔加河上的驳船拉夫》展示了一支由十一人组成的队伍沿河拉绳，身体前倾，双脚陷入沙中。前面一位老人目视前方；他身后的一位年轻人试图抬起头。宽阔的河流、远处的小船和炽热的天空在他们身后展开。\n\n作为学生的列宾曾沿伏尔加河旅行，并在看到这些拉夫后开始创作这幅画。他把俄罗斯的贫困和坚韧转化为一种影像。"}, "degas-dance-class-1874": {"note": "《舞蹈课》展示了巴黎歌剧院芭蕾舞的排练室。中央，一位年长的芭蕾舞导师靠着一根长杖，指导一群穿着白色芭蕾舞裙的女孩；有些在认真听讲，有些在挠背、整理肩带或者发呆。对角线划分了整个房间，镜子、钢琴和地板又把空间向后推。\n\n德加并不追求舞台上的完美，而是展现排练中的疲惫、等待和小动作。他受英格尔风格素描训练，用类似粉彩的色彩和不对称的构图，把幕后世界变成现代绘画的真正主题。", "note_en": "The Dance Class shows a rehearsal room of the Paris Opéra ballet. At the centre an elderly ballet master leans on a long staff, addressing a group of girls in white tutus; some listen, others scratch their backs, adjust a shoulder strap or drift off. A diagonal cuts the room, and mirror, piano and floor push the space back.\n\nDegas does not seek stage perfection but the fatigue, waiting and small gestures of rehearsal. Trained in Ingresque drawing, he uses pastel-like colour and asymmetric composition to make the backstage the proper subject of modern painting.", "note_html": "《舞蹈课》展示了巴黎歌剧院芭蕾舞的排练室。中央，一位年长的芭蕾舞导师靠着一根长杖，指导一群穿着白色芭蕾舞裙的女孩；有些在认真听讲，有些在挠背、整理肩带或者发呆。对角线划分了整个房间，镜子、钢琴和地板又把空间向后推。\n\n德加并不追求舞台上的完美，而是展现排练中的疲惫、等待和小动作。他受英格尔风格素描训练，用类似粉彩的色彩和不对称的构图，把幕后世界变成现代绘画的真正主题。"}, "renoir-bal-moulin-galette-1876": {"note": "《加莱特磨坊的舞会》描绘了蒙马特高地上一场夏天的露天舞会。人群在树影和阳光间穿梭；前景的桌旁有人坐着聊天，而舞者则在中心旋转。树叶将光线分割成片，洒落在衣服、帽子和脸上。\n\n雷诺阿画的不是孤立的人物，而是人群之间的空气：笑声、汗水、香水、烟草和阴影混合在一起。这既是印象派画作中最欢乐的一幅，也是十九世纪巴黎休闲生活的视觉记录。", "note_en": "Bal du moulin de la Galette shows a summer dance in the open air on the Montmartre hill. Crowds move between tree shadow and sunlight; at a table in the foreground people sit and talk, while dancers turn at the centre. Leaves cut the light into fragments that fall across clothes, hats and faces.\n\nRenoir paints not isolated figures but the air between people: laughter, sweat, perfume, tobacco and shade mixed together. It is both the most joyful of Impressionist paintings and a visual record of nineteenth-century Parisian leisure.", "note_html": "《加莱特磨坊的舞会》描绘了蒙马特高地上一场夏天的露天舞会。人群在树影和阳光间穿梭；前景的桌旁有人坐着聊天，而舞者则在中心旋转。树叶将光线分割成片，洒落在衣服、帽子和脸上。\n\n雷诺阿画的不是孤立的人物，而是人群之间的空气：笑声、汗水、香水、烟草和阴影混合在一起。这既是印象派画作中最欢乐的一幅，也是十九世纪巴黎休闲生活的视觉记录。"}, "manet-bar-folies-bergere-1882": {"note": "《福乐喜剧酒吧》展示了巴黎音乐厅的最后一夜。一个酒吧女侍站在柜台后，双手放在大理石台面上，胸前别着一朵花；她面前摆着酒杯、酒瓶和一盘橘子。她身后的镜子反射出整个大厅：吊灯、观众、包厢，以及一个正和她交谈的男人——这也是观众实际上所处的位置。\n\n马奈画的反射并不完全正确，透视也略有偏差。酒吧女侍的表情空洞，既不欢迎也不拒绝。整幅画成为现代城市生活的标志性形象：人群、光线、消费，以及一个无法接近的人。", "note_en": "A Bar at the Folies-Bergère shows the last night of a Paris music hall. A barmaid stands behind the counter, both hands resting on the marble, a flower at her breast; glasses, bottles and a plate of oranges are arranged in front of her. The mirror behind her reflects the whole hall: chandeliers, audience, boxes, and a man speaking to her — the place where the viewer actually stands.\n\nManet paints the reflection not quite correctly and lets the perspective slip. The barmaid's expression is blank, neither welcoming nor refusing. The picture becomes a defining image of modern city life: crowd, light, consumption, and a person who cannot be reached.", "note_html": "《福乐喜剧酒吧》展示了巴黎音乐厅的最后一夜。一个酒吧女侍站在柜台后，双手放在大理石台面上，胸前别着一朵花；她面前摆着酒杯、酒瓶和一盘橘子。她身后的镜子反射出整个大厅：吊灯、观众、包厢，以及一个正和她交谈的男人——这也是观众实际上所处的位置。\n\n马奈画的反射并不完全正确，透视也略有偏差。酒吧女侍的表情空洞，既不欢迎也不拒绝。整幅画成为现代城市生活的标志性形象：人群、光线、消费，以及一个无法接近的人。"}, "boecklin-isle-of-the-dead-1883": {"note": "《死之岛》展示了一个漂浮在海上的墓地：一个被黑色柏树覆盖的岩石岛屿，垂直升起的悬崖；一只小船靠近码头，船上站着一个穿白衣的人，船首放着一口棺材。天空灰蓝沉重，水面几乎静止。\n\n伯克林并没有画特定的地中海岛屿；他把死亡变成了一种空间——一个既无法抵达也无法离开的岛屿。它被无数次模仿和改编，并影响了二十世纪梦境和电影的视觉形象。", "note_en": "Isle of the Dead shows a cemetery floating on the sea: a rocky island covered with dark cypresses, cliffs rising vertically; a small boat approaches the landing, a figure in white standing aboard, a coffin at the bow. The sky is a heavy grey-blue, the water almost still.\n\nBöcklin does not paint a specific Mediterranean island; he turns death into a space — an island that can be neither reached nor left. It was copied and adapted endlessly, and shaped twentieth-century images of dream and film.", "note_html": "《死之岛》展示了一个漂浮在海上的墓地：一个被黑色柏树覆盖的岩石岛屿，垂直升起的悬崖；一只小船靠近码头，船上站着一个穿白衣的人，船首放着一口棺材。天空灰蓝沉重，水面几乎静止。\n\n伯克林并没有画特定的地中海岛屿；他把死亡变成了一种空间——一个既无法抵达也无法离开的岛屿。它被无数次模仿和改编，并影响了二十世纪梦境和电影的视觉形象。"}, "wenban-railroad-station-1883": {"note": "温班以蚀刻记录火车站内部：蒸汽、行李、等待的人和建筑结构共同构成工业时代的入口。\n\n在「城市与日常」的「铁路」线索里，站台、屋顶与人群，让“出发”变成可被反复观看的城市空间。", "note_en": "1883, North America. 西昂·朗利·温班; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1920.154. This is a print (蚀刻版画).", "note_html": "温班以蚀刻记录火车站内部：蒸汽、行李、等待的人和建筑结构共同构成工业时代的入口。\n\n在「城市与日常」的「铁路」线索里，站台、屋顶与人群，让“出发”变成可被反复观看的城市空间。"}, "sargent-madame-x-1884": {"note": "《X女士》描绘的是维珍妮·阿梅莉·阿韦尼奥·戈特罗，一位著名的巴黎美女。她侧身站立，一只手搭在桌子上，头向后仰，露出一张苍白的脸和鼻子；她黑色缎面礼服的肩带滑落，肌肤与布料形成冷峻的对比。这幅画在1884年的沙龙展引起了轰动：不是因为裸露，而是因为姿态太自傲、太不受控制。萨金特后来重新画了肩带，但这种挑衅感并没有消失。它仍然是19世纪末“新女性”最尖锐的肖像之一。", "note_en": "Madame X portrays Virginie Amélie Avegno Gautreau, a celebrated Parisian beauty. She stands in profile, one hand resting on a table, her head thrown back to reveal a pale face and nose; the strap of her black satin dress has slipped, skin and fabric set in cold contrast.\n\nThe picture caused a scandal at the 1884 Salon: not for nudity but for a posture too proud, too ungovernable. Sargent later repainted the strap, yet the provocation did not disappear. It remains one of the sharpest portraits of the late-nineteenth-century \"new woman.\"", "note_html": "《X女士》描绘的是维珍妮·阿梅莉·阿韦尼奥·戈特罗，一位著名的巴黎美女。她侧身站立，一只手搭在桌子上，头向后仰，露出一张苍白的脸和鼻子；她黑色缎面礼服的肩带滑落，肌肤与布料形成冷峻的对比。这幅画在1884年的沙龙展引起了轰动：不是因为裸露，而是因为姿态太自傲、太不受控制。萨金特后来重新画了肩带，但这种挑衅感并没有消失。它仍然是19世纪末“新女性”最尖锐的肖像之一。"}, "auto-0d3092e4": {"note": "《女史箴图》是现存最早的中国绢本人物长卷之一，通常被认为是东晋顾恺之的原作、唐代摹本。画卷根据张华《女史箴》的十二段箴文绘制，现存九段：有冯媛挡熊、班姬辞辇，也有宫中女子对镜梳妆、围坐交谈的日常场景。人物衣带飘举，线条细而不断，像春蚕吐丝。\n\n画面没有透视，也没有阴影，却用线条的节奏、人物之间的距离和空白来组织叙事。它既是道德教科书，也是一部宫廷女性生活的图像史。1900年庚子事变后流入英国，现藏大英博物馆。", "note_en": "1884, Cross-regional. 安德斯·佐恩; source: Wikimedia Commons, catalog no. File:Anders Zorn - Grandmother III 1884 - Bukowskis lot no. 534975.jpg. This is a print.", "note_html": "《女史箴图》是现存最早的中国绢本人物长卷之一，通常被认为是东晋顾恺之的原作、唐代摹本。画卷根据张华《女史箴》的十二段箴文绘制，现存九段：有冯媛挡熊、班姬辞辇，也有宫中女子对镜梳妆、围坐交谈的日常场景。人物衣带飘举，线条细而不断，像春蚕吐丝。\n\n画面没有透视，也没有阴影，却用线条的节奏、人物之间的距离和空白来组织叙事。它既是道德教科书，也是一部宫廷女性生活的图像史。1900年庚子事变后流入英国，现藏大英博物馆。"}, "auto-e13d5cd2": {"note": "《里约港》是乔瓦尼·巴蒂斯塔·卡斯塔涅托约1884年的印象主义作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“里约港”为题，属于巴西的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。", "note_en": "1884, Latin America. 乔瓦尼·巴蒂斯塔·卡斯塔涅托; source: Wikimedia Commons, catalog no. File:Giovanni Battista Castagneto - Porto do Rio de Janeiro, 1884.jpg. This is a painting (oil painting).", "note_html": "《里约港》是乔瓦尼·巴蒂斯塔·卡斯塔涅托约1884年的印象主义作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“里约港”为题，属于巴西的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。"}, "auto-ba3dba36": {"note": "《里约港（其二）》是乔瓦尼·巴蒂斯塔·卡斯塔涅托约1884年的印象主义作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“里约港（其二）”为题，属于巴西的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。", "note_en": "1884, Latin America. 乔瓦尼·巴蒂斯塔·卡斯塔涅托; source: Wikimedia Commons, catalog no. File:Giovanni Battista Castagneto - Porto do Rio de Janeiro (2).jpg. This is a painting (oil painting).", "note_html": "《里约港（其二）》是乔瓦尼·巴蒂斯塔·卡斯塔涅托约1884年的印象主义作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“里约港（其二）”为题，属于巴西的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。"}, "auto-723f2014": {"note": "《里约热内卢罗德里戈湖》是尼古拉·法基内蒂约1884年的学院派风景作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“里约热内卢罗德里戈湖”为题，属于巴西的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。", "note_en": "1884, Latin America. 尼古拉·法基内蒂; source: Wikimedia Commons, catalog no. File:Nicola Facchinetti - Lagoa Rodrigo de Freitas, Rio de Janeiro, ca. 1884.jpg. This is a painting (oil painting).", "note_html": "《里约热内卢罗德里戈湖》是尼古拉·法基内蒂约1884年的学院派风景作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“里约热内卢罗德里戈湖”为题，属于巴西的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。"}, "auto-ad61b00e": {"note": "《里约全景习作：蛇岛》是维克托·梅雷莱斯约1885年的学院派作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“里约全景习作：蛇岛”为题，属于巴西的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。", "note_en": "1885, Latin America. 维克托·梅雷莱斯; source: Wikimedia Commons, catalog no. File:Victor Meirelles - Estudo para Panorama do Rio de Janeiro - Ilha das Cobras e Morro de Santo Antônio - c. 1885.jpg. This is a painting (oil painting).", "note_html": "《里约全景习作：蛇岛》是维克托·梅雷莱斯约1885年的学院派作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“里约全景习作：蛇岛”为题，属于巴西的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。"}, "seurat-grande-jatte-1886": {"note": "《拉格朗德岛的一个星期天》展示了塞纳河边的公园：人们坐在草地上，撑着阳伞，遛狗，划船，所有人都像暂停动作的剪影。画面由无数小色点组成；远看是统一的绿色和蓝色，近看则是橙色、紫色和黄色的小颗粒。人物被简化为纵横的块状，连影子都像用尺子量过一样。\n\n苏拉将色彩科学、光学理论和古典构图融合到一幅画中。它延续了印象派对光线的兴趣，却又与印象派的“瞬间感”相反：这里的一切都是静止且可计算的，是现代城市生活的一个样本。", "note_en": "A Sunday on La Grande Jatte shows a park beside the Seine: people sit on grass, hold parasols, walk dogs, row boats, all like silhouettes paused mid-motion. The surface is built from countless small dots of colour; from a distance they read as unified green and blue, up close as grains of orange, violet and yellow. Figures are reduced to vertical and horizontal blocks, even shadows measured as if by ruler.\n\nSeurat brings colour science, optical theory and classical composition into one picture. It extends Impressionism's interest in light and contradicts its \"instant\": everything here is still and calculable, a specimen of modern city life.", "note_html": "《拉格朗德岛的一个星期天》展示了塞纳河边的公园：人们坐在草地上，撑着阳伞，遛狗，划船，所有人都像暂停动作的剪影。画面由无数小色点组成；远看是统一的绿色和蓝色，近看则是橙色、紫色和黄色的小颗粒。人物被简化为纵横的块状，连影子都像用尺子量过一样。\n\n苏拉将色彩科学、光学理论和古典构图融合到一幅画中。它延续了印象派对光线的兴趣，却又与印象派的“瞬间感”相反：这里的一切都是静止且可计算的，是现代城市生活的一个样本。"}, "auto-aed4a918": {"note": "《黑海海岸沉船》是伊凡·艾瓦佐夫斯基约1887年的浪漫主义作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“黑海海岸沉船”为题，属于黑海的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。", "note_en": "1887, Cross-regional. 伊凡·艾瓦佐夫斯基; source: Wikimedia Commons, catalog no. File:Ivan Konstantinovich Aivazovsky - Shipwreck off the Black Sea Coast.jpg. This is a painting (oil painting).", "note_html": "《黑海海岸沉船》是伊凡·艾瓦佐夫斯基约1887年的浪漫主义作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“黑海海岸沉船”为题，属于黑海的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。"}, "van-gogh-sunflowers-1888": {"note": "《向日葵》展示了阿尔勒黄色房子里的一个花瓶。花朵从明亮的金色到焦棕色不等，花瓣烫焦；背景是一片同样明亮的黄色，花瓶下方只有一条青绿色的线。颜料厚重，几乎从画布上凸起。\n\n梵高计划这组作品是为了在高更到来时装饰黄色房子。对他来说，黄色不是一种颜色，而是一种温度，一种友谊的承诺，以及几乎宗教般的光。", "note_en": "Sunflowers shows a vase in the Yellow House at Arles. The flower heads move from bright gold to burnt brown, petals singed; the background is a field of the same luminous yellow, with only a line of green-blue below the vase. Paint is thick, almost standing off the canvas.\n\nVan Gogh planned this series to decorate the Yellow House for Gauguin's arrival. For him yellow was not a colour but a temperature, a promise of friendship, and an almost religious light.", "note_html": "《向日葵》展示了阿尔勒黄色房子里的一个花瓶。花朵从明亮的金色到焦棕色不等，花瓣烫焦；背景是一片同样明亮的黄色，花瓶下方只有一条青绿色的线。颜料厚重，几乎从画布上凸起。\n\n梵高计划这组作品是为了在高更到来时装饰黄色房子。对他来说，黄色不是一种颜色，而是一种温度，一种友谊的承诺，以及几乎宗教般的光。"}, "trouillebert-elevated-railway-vincennes-1888": {"note": "1888 年巴黎万塞讷大道的高架铁路施工现场。铁路既是速度，也是城市必须重新安排的日常空间。\n\n在「城市与日常」的「铁路」线索里，把铁路建设从工程图纸拉回街道：桥墩、围栏、行人同时进入画面。", "note_en": "1888, Europe. 保罗·德西雷·特鲁耶贝尔; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1980.289. This is a painting (布面油画).", "note_html": "1888 年巴黎万塞讷大道的高架铁路施工现场。铁路既是速度，也是城市必须重新安排的日常空间。\n\n在「城市与日常」的「铁路」线索里，把铁路建设从工程图纸拉回街道：桥墩、围栏、行人同时进入画面。"}, "van-gogh-starry-night-1889": {"note": "《星月夜》是在圣雷米的精神病院创作的。天空像漩涡一样旋转，星星像火球般燃烧，月亮在右侧升起；前景的一棵柏树像黑色火焰一样升起；下面是一个宁静的村庄，教堂的尖塔指向远方。\n\n梵高并不是仅凭记忆绘制这片天空；他把窗外的景色与想象和内心的波动结合在一起。厚重、明显的笔触让画面既有运动感又有静止感：世界在转动，而观者固定在窗前。", "note_en": "The Starry Night was painted at the asylum in Saint-Rémy. The sky becomes a swirling vortex, stars burning like fireballs, the moon rising at the right; a cypress in the foreground rises like a black flame; below lies a quiet village, its church spire pointing into the distance.\n\nVan Gogh did not paint this sky from memory alone; he mixed the view from his window with imagination and inner turbulence. The thick, visible strokes give the picture both motion and stasis: the world turns, while the viewer is fixed at the window.", "note_html": "《星月夜》是在圣雷米的精神病院创作的。天空像漩涡一样旋转，星星像火球般燃烧，月亮在右侧升起；前景的一棵柏树像黑色火焰一样升起；下面是一个宁静的村庄，教堂的尖塔指向远方。\n\n梵高并不是仅凭记忆绘制这片天空；他把窗外的景色与想象和内心的波动结合在一起。厚重、明显的笔触让画面既有运动感又有静止感：世界在转动，而观者固定在窗前。"}, "auto-dd7aafa6": {"note": "《女史箴图》是现存最早的中国绢本人物长卷之一，通常被认为是东晋顾恺之的原作、唐代摹本。画卷根据张华《女史箴》的十二段箴文绘制，现存九段：有冯媛挡熊、班姬辞辇，也有宫中女子对镜梳妆、围坐交谈的日常场景。人物衣带飘举，线条细而不断，像春蚕吐丝。\n\n画面没有透视，也没有阴影，却用线条的节奏、人物之间的距离和空白来组织叙事。它既是道德教科书，也是一部宫廷女性生活的图像史。1900年庚子事变后流入英国，现藏大英博物馆。", "note_en": "1890, West Asia & North Africa. 马里乌斯·鲍尔; source: Wikimedia Commons, catalog no. File:Marius Bauer.'A Street in Cairo'.Etching on paper,28.5cm х 23.1cm.jpg. This is a print.", "note_html": "《女史箴图》是现存最早的中国绢本人物长卷之一，通常被认为是东晋顾恺之的原作、唐代摹本。画卷根据张华《女史箴》的十二段箴文绘制，现存九段：有冯媛挡熊、班姬辞辇，也有宫中女子对镜梳妆、围坐交谈的日常场景。人物衣带飘举，线条细而不断，像春蚕吐丝。\n\n画面没有透视，也没有阴影，却用线条的节奏、人物之间的距离和空白来组织叙事。它既是道德教科书，也是一部宫廷女性生活的图像史。1900年庚子事变后流入英国，现藏大英博物馆。"}, "munch-the-scream-1893": {"note": "《呐喊》展示了奥斯陆峡湾旁的一座桥。中央人物捂着耳朵，嘴巴张开，脸扭曲得像骷髅一样；在他身后，天空呈现橙红色的条纹，水是深蓝色的，两个人影朝远处走去。栏杆在画面中划出一条斜线，仿佛观者也被推向前去。\n\n在日记中，蒙克描述自己听到了“来自大自然的巨大、无限的尖叫”。这并不是一个人在尖叫，而是环境对一个人施加的压力。这幅画成为现代焦虑的普遍象征，被无数次模仿和恶搞，但仍然很有冲击力。", "note_en": "The Scream shows a bridge beside the Oslo fjord. The central figure covers his ears, mouth open, face twisted like a skull; behind him the sky turns in orange-red bands, water is deep blue, and two dark figures walk away. The railing cuts a diagonal out of the picture, as if the viewer were being pushed forward too.\n\nIn his diary Munch described hearing \"a great, infinite scream from nature.\" It is not a person screaming so much as an environment pressing on one person. The image became the universal sign of modern anxiety, copied and parodied countless times, and still effective.", "note_html": "《呐喊》展示了奥斯陆峡湾旁的一座桥。中央人物捂着耳朵，嘴巴张开，脸扭曲得像骷髅一样；在他身后，天空呈现橙红色的条纹，水是深蓝色的，两个人影朝远处走去。栏杆在画面中划出一条斜线，仿佛观者也被推向前去。\n\n在日记中，蒙克描述自己听到了“来自大自然的巨大、无限的尖叫”。这并不是一个人在尖叫，而是环境对一个人施加的压力。这幅画成为现代焦虑的普遍象征，被无数次模仿和恶搞，但仍然很有冲击力。"}, "moreau-jupiter-semele-1895": {"note": "《朱庇特与塞墨勒》展示了凡人塞墨勒要求看到神以真实形态的瞬间。朱庇特坐在中央的宝座上，一条巨蛇盘在胸前，周围环绕着层层金色装饰和神祇；塞墨勒斜卧在前景，她的身体已经被神圣之光穿透，几乎在溶解。莫罗将神话描绘成一个象征的宫殿：色彩如搪瓷，线条似珠宝，没有深度，只有无尽的装饰。这里的象征主义不是讲故事；画面本身成为一个迷宫，眼睛可以一次又一次地进入。", "note_en": "Jupiter and Semele shows the moment the mortal Semele asks to see the god in his true form. Jupiter sits on a throne at the centre, a great serpent coiled at his breast, surrounded by tiers of gold ornament and deities; Semele reclines in the foreground, her body already pierced by divine light, almost dissolving.\n\nMoreau paints myth as a palace of symbols: colour like enamel, line like jewellery, no depth, only endless ornament. Symbolism here is not storytelling; the image itself becomes a labyrinth the eye can enter again and again.", "note_html": "《朱庇特与塞墨勒》展示了凡人塞墨勒要求看到神以真实形态的瞬间。朱庇特坐在中央的宝座上，一条巨蛇盘在胸前，周围环绕着层层金色装饰和神祇；塞墨勒斜卧在前景，她的身体已经被神圣之光穿透，几乎在溶解。莫罗将神话描绘成一个象征的宫殿：色彩如搪瓷，线条似珠宝，没有深度，只有无尽的装饰。这里的象征主义不是讲故事；画面本身成为一个迷宫，眼睛可以一次又一次地进入。"}, "auto-e80436fe": {"note": "《暴风雨早晨的沉船》是伊凡·艾瓦佐夫斯基约1895年的浪漫主义作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“暴风雨早晨的沉船”为题，属于黑海的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。", "note_en": "1895, Cross-regional. 伊凡·艾瓦佐夫斯基; source: Wikimedia Commons, catalog no. File:Ivan Konstantinovich Aivazovsky - Shipwreck on a Stormy Morning, 1895.jpg. This is a painting (oil painting).", "note_html": "《暴风雨早晨的沉船》是伊凡·艾瓦佐夫斯基约1895年的浪漫主义作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“暴风雨早晨的沉船”为题，属于黑海的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。"}, "munch-evening-melancholy-1896": {"note": "1896，挪威 奥斯陆。爱德华·蒙克的版画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。这是一件版画作品，线条与印痕记录了图像被复制的路径。", "note_en": "1896, Europe. 爱德华·蒙克; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1959.82. This is a print (版画（手工上色木刻）).", "note_html": "1896，挪威 奥斯陆。爱德华·蒙克的版画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。这是一件版画作品，线条与印痕记录了图像被复制的路径。"}, "whistler-charing-cross-bridge-1896": {"note": "惠斯勒的石版画把查令十字铁路桥压缩为河面上的一道深色水平线，铁路因此进入城市景观。\n\n在「城市与日常」的「铁路」线索里，把铁路桥当作泰晤士河上的黑色剪影，工程结构同时是城市风景。", "note_en": "1896, Europe. 詹姆斯·麦克尼尔·惠斯勒; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1924.5. This is a print (lithograph).", "note_html": "惠斯勒的石版画把查令十字铁路桥压缩为河面上的一道深色水平线，铁路因此进入城市景观。\n\n在「城市与日常」的「铁路」线索里，把铁路桥当作泰晤士河上的黑色剪影，工程结构同时是城市风景。"}, "pissarro-rue-saint-lazare-1897": {"note": "毕沙罗 1890 年代的石版画系列之一，用快速线条记录圣拉扎尔车站周边的人流与街景。\n\n在「城市与日常」的「铁路」线索里，铁路车站周边的街道，是印象派观察城市速度的入口。", "note_en": "1897, Europe. 卡米耶·毕沙罗; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1987.80. This is a print (lithograph).", "note_html": "毕沙罗 1890 年代的石版画系列之一，用快速线条记录圣拉扎尔车站周边的人流与街景。\n\n在「城市与日常」的「铁路」线索里，铁路车站周边的街道，是印象派观察城市速度的入口。"}, "pissarro-boulevard-montmartre-night-1897": {"note": "《蒙马特大街夜景》是皮萨罗的一系列作品之一，他从巴黎一家酒店的窗口俯视街道。大街斜向右延伸，路灯将湿漉漉的柏油路照成金色的线条；马车、行人和商店橱窗被压缩成短短的笔触。天空深蓝，建筑物是黑色的剪影。\n\n晚年的皮萨罗遭受眼疾困扰，但在这组城市题材作品中找到了新的自由：他不再画乡村风景，而是描绘现代城市的节奏与光影。印象派的“瞬间”变成了大都市的夜脉动。", "note_en": "The Boulevard Montmartre at Night is one of a series Pissarro painted looking down on the street from a Paris hotel window. The boulevard runs diagonally away to the right, streetlamps turning wet asphalt into lines of gold; carriages, pedestrians and shop windows are compressed into short strokes. The sky is deep blue, the buildings black silhouettes.\n\nPissarro was troubled by eye disease in his late years, yet found a new freedom in this urban series: he no longer painted the countryside but the rhythm and light of the modern city. The Impressionist \"instant\" becomes the night pulse of a metropolis.", "note_html": "《蒙马特大街夜景》是皮萨罗的一系列作品之一，他从巴黎一家酒店的窗口俯视街道。大街斜向右延伸，路灯将湿漉漉的柏油路照成金色的线条；马车、行人和商店橱窗被压缩成短短的笔触。天空深蓝，建筑物是黑色的剪影。\n\n晚年的皮萨罗遭受眼疾困扰，但在这组城市题材作品中找到了新的自由：他不再画乡村风景，而是描绘现代城市的节奏与光影。印象派的“瞬间”变成了大都市的夜脉动。"}, "gauguin-where-do-we-come-from-1898": {"note": "《我们从何处来？我们是谁？我们向何处去？》是高更塔希提时期最大的画作。画面的构图是从右向左阅读的——婴儿、女人、老人——就像一个无字的创世纪。中央人物伸手去拿水果，周围是蓝色和绿色的阴影；背后是大海、山脉和神龛。画名刻在左下角，就像墙上的墓志铭。\n\n高更并不是在讲一个具体的故事，而是用身体、色彩和符号拼凑出三个问题。他把殖民地的“他处”变成一个哲学空间，并把自己的焦虑隐藏在那些静止、几乎像雕塑的形象里。", "note_en": "Where Do We Come From? What Are We? Where Are We Going? is Gauguin's largest painting from his Tahiti years. The composition reads from right to left — infant, woman, old person — like a genesis without words. A central figure reaches for fruit, surrounded by blue and green shadow; sea, mountains and a shrine lie behind. The title is inscribed at the lower left like an epitaph on a wall.\n\nGauguin is not telling a specific story but assembling three questions from bodies, colour and symbol. He turns the colonial \"elsewhere\" into a philosophical space, and hides his own anxiety inside those still, almost sculptural figures.", "note_html": "《我们从何处来？我们是谁？我们向何处去？》是高更塔希提时期最大的画作。画面的构图是从右向左阅读的——婴儿、女人、老人——就像一个无字的创世纪。中央人物伸手去拿水果，周围是蓝色和绿色的阴影；背后是大海、山脉和神龛。画名刻在左下角，就像墙上的墓志铭。\n\n高更并不是在讲一个具体的故事，而是用身体、色彩和符号拼凑出三个问题。他把殖民地的“他处”变成一个哲学空间，并把自己的焦虑隐藏在那些静止、几乎像雕塑的形象里。"}, "cezanne-the-brook-1898": {"note": "塞尚把溪流、岩石和树处理成同一套笔触；水不是倒影，而是另一组倾斜的色块。", "note_en": "c. 1895–1900, Europe. 保罗·塞尚; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1958.2. This is a painting (oil painting).", "note_html": "塞尚把溪流、岩石和树处理成同一套笔触；水不是倒影，而是另一组倾斜的色块。"}, "oerder-still-life-1900": {"note": "奥尔德1900年的静物把器物摆成一座小型舞台；桌面的反光比物件本身更先被看见。", "note_en": "1900, Sub-Saharan Africa. 弗兰斯·奥尔德; source: Wikimedia Commons, catalog no. Frans Oerder - Still-life - Google Art Project.jpg. This is a painting (oil painting).", "note_html": "奥尔德1900年的静物把器物摆成一座小型舞台；桌面的反光比物件本身更先被看见。"}, "auto-62ae36e0": {"note": "《从克洛夫街高处看开普敦》是海因里希·赫尔曼约1900年的殖民地地形水彩作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“从克洛夫街高处看开普敦”为题，属于开普敦的水彩传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。", "note_en": "1900, Sub-Saharan Africa. 海因里希·赫尔曼; source: Wikimedia Commons, catalog no. File:Heinrich Hermann - Cape Town from the Top of Kloof Street - Google Art Project.jpg. This is a painting (watercolour).", "note_html": "《从克洛夫街高处看开普敦》是海因里希·赫尔曼约1900年的殖民地地形水彩作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“从克洛夫街高处看开普敦”为题，属于开普敦的水彩传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。"}, "auto-580fb4aa": {"note": "《列夫·托尔斯泰肖像》是伊万·卡扎科夫约1900年的现实主义作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“列夫·托尔斯泰肖像”为题，属于俄国的绘画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。", "note_en": "1900, Europe. 伊万·卡扎科夫; source: Wikimedia Commons, catalog no. File:Leo Tolstoy by I.S.Kazakov (1900, Odessa).jpg. This is a painting.", "note_html": "《列夫·托尔斯泰肖像》是伊万·卡扎科夫约1900年的现实主义作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“列夫·托尔斯泰肖像”为题，属于俄国的绘画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。"}, "auto-27bcc7d5": {"note": "《咖啡壶静物》是卡米耶·毕沙罗约1900年的印象主义作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“咖啡壶静物”为题，属于法国的绘画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。", "note_en": "1900, Europe. 卡米耶·毕沙罗; source: Wikimedia Commons, catalog no. File:Camille Pissarro, Still Life with a Coffeepot, 1900, ЗКРсэ-527, Hermitage Museum.jpg. This is a painting.", "note_html": "《咖啡壶静物》是卡米耶·毕沙罗约1900年的印象主义作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“咖啡壶静物”为题，属于法国的绘画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。"}, "auto-9fd3fc18": {"note": "《女史箴图》是现存最早的中国绢本人物长卷之一，通常被认为是东晋顾恺之的原作、唐代摹本。画卷根据张华《女史箴》的十二段箴文绘制，现存九段：有冯媛挡熊、班姬辞辇，也有宫中女子对镜梳妆、围坐交谈的日常场景。人物衣带飘举，线条细而不断，像春蚕吐丝。\n\n画面没有透视，也没有阴影，却用线条的节奏、人物之间的距离和空白来组织叙事。它既是道德教科书，也是一部宫廷女性生活的图像史。1900年庚子事变后流入英国，现藏大英博物馆。", "note_en": "1900, Oceania. 安德斯·佐恩; source: Wikimedia Commons, catalog no. File:Anders Zorn - Billy Mason 1900 - Museum of New Zealand 1971-0012-48.jpg. This is a print.", "note_html": "《女史箴图》是现存最早的中国绢本人物长卷之一，通常被认为是东晋顾恺之的原作、唐代摹本。画卷根据张华《女史箴》的十二段箴文绘制，现存九段：有冯媛挡熊、班姬辞辇，也有宫中女子对镜梳妆、围坐交谈的日常场景。人物衣带飘举，线条细而不断，像春蚕吐丝。\n\n画面没有透视，也没有阴影，却用线条的节奏、人物之间的距离和空白来组织叙事。它既是道德教科书，也是一部宫廷女性生活的图像史。1900年庚子事变后流入英国，现藏大英博物馆。"}, "auto-58575fef": {"note": "《湄公河上的“安南号”》是维尔赫尔姆·阿内森约1900年的海洋画作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“湄公河上的“安南号””为题，属于越南的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。", "note_en": "1900, Southeast Asia. 维尔赫尔姆·阿内森; source: Wikimedia Commons, catalog no. File:Vilhelm Arnesen - Dampskibet Annam på Mekongfloden ved Saigon - 1900.png. This is a painting (oil painting).", "note_html": "《湄公河上的“安南号”》是维尔赫尔姆·阿内森约1900年的海洋画作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“湄公河上的“安南号””为题，属于越南的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。"}, "auto-2df8ce6f": {"note": "《男孩肖像》是乔治·本杰明·卢克斯约1900年的垃圾箱画派作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“男孩肖像”为题，属于美国的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。", "note_en": "1900, Cross-regional. 乔治·本杰明·卢克斯; source: Wikimedia Commons, catalog no. File:Portrait of a Boy, by George Benjamin Luks.png. This is a painting (oil painting).", "note_html": "《男孩肖像》是乔治·本杰明·卢克斯约1900年的垃圾箱画派作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“男孩肖像”为题，属于美国的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。"}, "auto-256d170f": {"note": "《葡萄静物》是伊迪丝·怀特约1900年的美国静物画作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“葡萄静物”为题，属于美国的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。", "note_en": "1900, Cross-regional. 伊迪丝·怀特; source: Wikimedia Commons, catalog no. File:Edith White Still life with grapes 1900.jpg. This is a painting (oil painting).", "note_html": "《葡萄静物》是伊迪丝·怀特约1900年的美国静物画作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“葡萄静物”为题，属于美国的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。"}, "auto-91d0ab3b": {"note": "《锡兰海域》是维尔赫尔姆·阿内森约1900年的海洋画作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“锡兰海域”为题，属于锡兰的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。", "note_en": "1900, South Asia. 维尔赫尔姆·阿内森; source: Wikimedia Commons, catalog no. File:Vilhelm Arnesen - Under Ceylon - 1900.png. This is a painting (oil painting).", "note_html": "《锡兰海域》是维尔赫尔姆·阿内森约1900年的海洋画作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“锡兰海域”为题，属于锡兰的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。"}, "cezanne-mont-sainte-victoire-1904": {"note": "圣维克多山是塞尚晚年反复描绘的主题。这座山被分解成平行的笔触——赭色、灰绿色、浅蓝色——像石块一样，也像呼吸一样；前景的树木和田野没有清晰的边界，只有推进和后退的色块。天空和山共享同一色调尺度；空间不是通过透视构建的，而是通过色彩的温度和笔触的方向来塑造的。\n\n塞尚同一个景色画了几十次，不是为了记录风景，而是为了找到结构。他把绘画从“看到的东西”转向“视觉如何被组织”，这是立体主义将要采纳的一步。", "note_en": "Mont Sainte-Victoire was a motif Cézanne returned to again and again in his late years. The mountain is broken into parallel strokes — ochre, grey-green, pale blue — like masonry and like breathing; trees and fields in the foreground have no clear edges, only blocks of colour advancing and receding. Sky and mountain share one scale of tones; space is built not by perspective but by temperature of colour and direction of stroke.\n\nCézanne painted the same view dozens of times, not to record landscape but to find structure. He moved painting from \"what is seen\" to \"how seeing is organised,\" a step that Cubism would take up.", "note_html": "圣维克多山是塞尚晚年反复描绘的主题。这座山被分解成平行的笔触——赭色、灰绿色、浅蓝色——像石块一样，也像呼吸一样；前景的树木和田野没有清晰的边界，只有推进和后退的色块。天空和山共享同一色调尺度；空间不是通过透视构建的，而是通过色彩的温度和笔触的方向来塑造的。\n\n塞尚同一个景色画了几十次，不是为了记录风景，而是为了找到结构。他把绘画从“看到的东西”转向“视觉如何被组织”，这是立体主义将要采纳的一步。"}, "redon-vase-flowers-1905": {"note": "1905年前后，雷东把花瓶放在画面中央，花瓣的边缘几乎融进背景；象征主义把可见的花当成不可见情绪的外壳。", "note_en": "c. 1905, Europe. 奥迪隆·雷东; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1935.233. This is a painting (oil painting).", "note_html": "1905年前后，雷东把花瓶放在画面中央，花瓣的边缘几乎融进背景；象征主义把可见的花当成不可见情绪的外壳。"}, "klimt-the-kiss-1908": {"note": "《吻》展示了两个人物跪在花草繁茂的草地边缘：男人俯身靠向女人，她的脸朝上，闭着眼睛。他们的身体被一件巨大的金色斗篷包裹，斗篷上覆盖着圆形、矩形和眼睛形状；男人的衣服是黑白条纹的，女人的衣服则点缀着彩色圆点。背景是闪烁的金色场面，既像马赛克又像夜空。\n\n克里姆特将维也纳分离派的装饰推到极限：爱不仅是叙事，而是一种被包围的存在状态。金箔让画作减轻了重量，并将这对情侣从现实中提升到永恒的图案中。", "note_en": "The Kiss shows two figures kneeling at the edge of a flower meadow: the man bends over the woman, her face tilted up, eyes closed. Their bodies are wrapped in a vast gold cloak covered with circles, rectangles and eye-like shapes; his garment is striped black and white, hers patterned with coloured dots. The background is a shimmering gold field, mosaic and night sky at once.\n\nKlimt pushes Vienna Secession ornament to its limit: love is not a narrative but a state of being enclosed. Gold leaf removes weight from the picture and lifts the couple out of reality into an eternal pattern.", "note_html": "《吻》展示了两个人物跪在花草繁茂的草地边缘：男人俯身靠向女人，她的脸朝上，闭着眼睛。他们的身体被一件巨大的金色斗篷包裹，斗篷上覆盖着圆形、矩形和眼睛形状；男人的衣服是黑白条纹的，女人的衣服则点缀着彩色圆点。背景是闪烁的金色场面，既像马赛克又像夜空。\n\n克里姆特将维也纳分离派的装饰推到极限：爱不仅是叙事，而是一种被包围的存在状态。金箔让画作减轻了重量，并将这对情侣从现实中提升到永恒的图案中。"}, "kamisaka-chrysanthemum-boy-1909": {"note": "神坂雪佳为《百世界之花》画的菊童，线条和图案几乎同等重要；这是1909年的设计性绘画。", "note_en": "1909, East Asia. 神坂雪佳; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1989.85.20. This is a drawing.", "note_html": "神坂雪佳为《百世界之花》画的菊童，线条和图案几乎同等重要；这是1909年的设计性绘画。"}, "kirchner-wrestlers-circus-1909": {"note": "1909，德国 柏林。恩斯特·路德维希·基尔希纳的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。", "note_en": "1909, Europe. 恩斯特·路德维希·基尔希纳; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1966.49. This is a painting (oil on canvas).", "note_html": "1909，德国 柏林。恩斯特·路德维希·基尔希纳的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。"}, "posada-calavera-catrina-1910": {"note": "卡特里娜戴着一顶夸张的帽子，骷髅的脸被画成盛装女子的脸；死亡在这里被化装成社会身份。", "note_en": "c. 1910, Latin America. 何塞·瓜达卢佩·波萨达; source: Wikimedia Commons, catalog no. Posada2.Catrina.jpeg. This is a print.", "note_html": "卡特里娜戴着一顶夸张的帽子，骷髅的脸被画成盛装女子的脸；死亡在这里被化装成社会身份。"}, "posada-jesus-negrete-1910": {"note": "波萨达把一桩刑事案件画成大众印刷品：人物、动作和标题一起制造“轰动”，新闻与图像在这里没有分界。", "note_en": "c. 1910, Latin America. 何塞·瓜达卢佩·波萨达; source: Wikimedia Commons, catalog no. José Guadalupe Posada - The very Sensational Plot of Jesús Negrete, a.k.a., The Tiger of Santa Julia - Google Art Project.jpg. This is a print.", "note_html": "波萨达把一桩刑事案件画成大众印刷品：人物、动作和标题一起制造“轰动”，新闻与图像在这里没有分界。"}, "posada-frivolous-frog-1910": {"note": "波萨达的木刻把青蛙画成穿礼服的角色；动物、衣冠和人的姿态被压进同一条黑白轮廓。", "note_en": "before 1913, Latin America. 何塞·瓜达卢佩·波萨达; source: Wikimedia Commons, catalog no. The Frivolous Frog by José Guadalupe Posada, woodcut, Honolulu Museum of Art.jpg. This is a print.", "note_html": "波萨达的木刻把青蛙画成穿礼服的角色；动物、衣冠和人的姿态被压进同一条黑白轮廓。"}, "delaunay-eiffel-tower-1911": {"note": "德拉纳伊把埃菲尔铁塔变成了一根旋转的彩色柱子。铁质结构被分解成红棕色、橙色和灰蓝色的面；云层以环形爆开，周围的公寓楼向铁塔倾斜。他没有使用立体主义的单色分析；颜色本身就创造了空间——暖色面向前推进，冷色面后退，铁质格子在其中若隐若现。\n\n1911年的巴黎是一个充满飞机、海报、地铁和电灯的城市。这幅画让“同时性”变成了视觉体验：你无法一次看到整座铁塔，只能同时感受到它的几个面。", "note_en": "Delaunay turns the Eiffel Tower into a rotating column of colour. The iron structure is broken into red-brown, orange and grey-blue facets; clouds burst in rings, and the surrounding apartment blocks tilt toward the tower. He does not use the monochrome analysis of Cubism; colour itself creates space — warm planes advance, cool planes recede, and the iron lattice appears and disappears between them.\n\nParis in 1911 was a city of aeroplanes, posters, the Metro and electric light. The painting turns 'simultaneity' into visual experience: you cannot see the tower all at once, only feel several of its faces at the same time.", "note_html": "德拉纳伊把埃菲尔铁塔变成了一根旋转的彩色柱子。铁质结构被分解成红棕色、橙色和灰蓝色的面；云层以环形爆开，周围的公寓楼向铁塔倾斜。他没有使用立体主义的单色分析；颜色本身就创造了空间——暖色面向前推进，冷色面后退，铁质格子在其中若隐若现。\n\n1911年的巴黎是一个充满飞机、海报、地铁和电灯的城市。这幅画让“同时性”变成了视觉体验：你无法一次看到整座铁塔，只能同时感受到它的几个面。"}, "schiele-self-portrait-1912": {"note": "《带中国灯笼植物的自画像》展示了席勒本人：瘦削的身体，肩膀耸起，头微微倾斜，眼睛睁大；右手扭在胸前，手指像小树枝。右侧挂着一株中国灯笼植物，橙色的花萼像小灯笼。背景是空白的，几乎没有空间感。\n\n席勒将自画像变成了一种生理和心理的展露：身体不舒适，表情警觉，就像被看见的动物。那紧绷的线条是维也纳表现主义最锐利的边缘。", "note_en": "Self-Portrait with Chinese Lantern Plant shows Schiele himself: thin body, shoulders raised, head tilted, eyes wide; his right hand twisted across his chest, fingers like twigs. At the right hangs a Chinese lantern plant, its orange calyces like small lamps. The background is blank, with almost no space.\n\nSchiele makes the self-portrait a physiological and psychological exposure: the body uncomfortable, the expression alert, like an animal that has been seen. That taut line is the sharpest edge of Viennese Expressionism.", "note_html": "《带中国灯笼植物的自画像》展示了席勒本人：瘦削的身体，肩膀耸起，头微微倾斜，眼睛睁大；右手扭在胸前，手指像小树枝。右侧挂着一株中国灯笼植物，橙色的花萼像小灯笼。背景是空白的，几乎没有空间感。\n\n席勒将自画像变成了一种生理和心理的展露：身体不舒适，表情警觉，就像被看见的动物。那紧绷的线条是维也纳表现主义最锐利的边缘。"}, "gris-portrait-of-picasso-1912": {"note": "1912年，胡安·格里斯画了他朋友圈里最著名的肖像：毕加索。面部被切成不同的面，从正面、侧面和顶部同时呈现；灰蓝色、赭色和冷白色被压成几乎单色的和弦。格里斯不仅仅是在“打破”毕加索；他是以几何方式重建表情——眼睛像两道斜坡，鼻子是折叠的线条，手像一张纸。\n\n背景中的对角线与衣领的三角形相互交错，把肖像变成了建筑。这标志着分析立体主义从拆解物体转向构建画面，同时格里斯也不再仅仅是追随者。", "note_en": "In 1912 Juan Gris painted the most famous portrait of his circle: Picasso. The face is cut into facets, front, side and top view appearing at once; grey-blue, ochre and cool white are pressed into an almost monochrome chord. Gris does not simply 'break' Picasso; he rebuilds the expression geometrically — eyes as two slopes, the nose a folded line, the hand a sheet of paper.\n\nDiagonals in the background interlock with the triangles of the collar, turning the portrait into architecture. It marks Analytical Cubism moving from dismantling objects to constructing a picture, and Gris becoming more than a follower.", "note_html": "1912年，胡安·格里斯画了他朋友圈里最著名的肖像：毕加索。面部被切成不同的面，从正面、侧面和顶部同时呈现；灰蓝色、赭色和冷白色被压成几乎单色的和弦。格里斯不仅仅是在“打破”毕加索；他是以几何方式重建表情——眼睛像两道斜坡，鼻子是折叠的线条，手像一张纸。\n\n背景中的对角线与衣领的三角形相互交错，把肖像变成了建筑。这标志着分析立体主义从拆解物体转向构建画面，同时格里斯也不再仅仅是追随者。"}, "yoshimura-howling-wolf-1912": {"note": "1912年的绢本挂轴，狼站在雪谷里抬头长啸；日本画把动物的动势压进留白和雾。", "note_en": "1912, East Asia. 吉村凤龙; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1989.474. This is a painting.", "note_html": "1912年的绢本挂轴，狼站在雪谷里抬头长啸；日本画把动物的动势压进留白和雾。"}, "kandinsky-composition-vii-1913": {"note": "《构图 VII》是康定斯基抽象画的巅峰之作。画中没有可辨认的物体，只有巨大的色块、弧线、黑色线条和密集的旋转笔触；中心像一次爆炸，边缘则像碎片被吸引进来。颜色相互碰撞；红、蓝、黄、绿在同一空间中争论又和解。\n\n康定斯基把绘画比作音乐：不是描述世界，而是直接作用于感情。他为这幅画做了数十幅研究，最终呈现为一次视觉盛宴，其中末日与重生同时发生。", "note_en": "Composition VII is the summit of Kandinsky's abstract painting. There are no recognisable objects, only enormous colour masses, arcs, black lines and dense strokes in rotation; the centre reads as an explosion, the edges as fragments being drawn in. Colours push against one another; red, blue, yellow and green argue and reconcile in the same space.\n\nKandinsky compared painting to music: not describing the world but acting directly on feeling. He made dozens of studies for this picture, and what remains is a visual event in which apocalypse and rebirth happen at once.", "note_html": "《构图 VII》是康定斯基抽象画的巅峰之作。画中没有可辨认的物体，只有巨大的色块、弧线、黑色线条和密集的旋转笔触；中心像一次爆炸，边缘则像碎片被吸引进来。颜色相互碰撞；红、蓝、黄、绿在同一空间中争论又和解。\n\n康定斯基把绘画比作音乐：不是描述世界，而是直接作用于感情。他为这幅画做了数十幅研究，最终呈现为一次视觉盛宴，其中末日与重生同时发生。"}, "kirchner-street-berlin-1913": {"note": "柏林街头展示了两条交叉的城市街道。前景中两位穿着时尚黑色衣服、戴着夸张帽子的女性，她们的脸被简化为尖锐、几乎像面具的三角形；街道被切成对角线，行人像风中纸片般弯曲。\n\n基尔希纳将城市的刺激、速度和不安转化为视觉张力：酸粉色、绿色和黑色，短促而尖锐的笔触。表现主义并不在意街道是否正确；它在意的是城市在身体中产生的震动。", "note_en": "Street, Berlin shows two intersecting city streets. In the foreground two women in fashionable black clothes and exaggerated hats, their faces reduced to sharp, almost mask-like triangles; the street is cut into diagonals, pedestrians bent like paper figures in wind.\n\nKirchner turns urban stimulus, speed and unease into visual tension: acid pink, green and black, short and sharp strokes. Expressionism does not care whether the street is correct; it cares about the vibration the city produces in the body.", "note_html": "柏林街头展示了两条交叉的城市街道。前景中两位穿着时尚黑色衣服、戴着夸张帽子的女性，她们的脸被简化为尖锐、几乎像面具的三角形；街道被切成对角线，行人像风中纸片般弯曲。\n\n基尔希纳将城市的刺激、速度和不安转化为视觉张力：酸粉色、绿色和黑色，短促而尖锐的笔触。表现主义并不在意街道是否正确；它在意的是城市在身体中产生的震动。"}, "malevich-black-square-1915": {"note": "《黑方块》并不是描绘一个具体的物体，而是一种姿态：一个黑色的四边形在白色的背景上，边缘不完全笔直，笔触隐约可见。马列维奇在1915年的“0.10”展览中把它挂在角落里，就像一尊圣像一样，让观众在原本应有神圣画像的位置上看到“空白”。它宣告了至上主义的诞生：绘画不再模仿自然或讲述故事，而是回归最基本的形状和颜色。黑方块不是终点，而是一扇门——在它那端，是白色、空白的画布。", "note_en": "Black Square does not depict an object but a gesture: a black quadrilateral on a white ground, its edges not quite straight, the brushwork faintly visible. Malevich hung it in the corner of the 1915 \"0.10\" exhibition like an icon, so that viewers encountered \"nothing\" where a holy image would normally stand.\n\nIt announced Suprematism: painting no longer imitates nature or tells stories but returns to the elementary form and colour. The black square is not an end but a door — beyond it lie the white, empty canvases.", "note_html": "《黑方块》并不是描绘一个具体的物体，而是一种姿态：一个黑色的四边形在白色的背景上，边缘不完全笔直，笔触隐约可见。马列维奇在1915年的“0.10”展览中把它挂在角落里，就像一尊圣像一样，让观众在原本应有神圣画像的位置上看到“空白”。它宣告了至上主义的诞生：绘画不再模仿自然或讲述故事，而是回归最基本的形状和颜色。黑方块不是终点，而是一扇门——在它那端，是白色、空白的画布。"}, "schiele-portrait-child-1916": {"note": "1916，奥地利 维也纳。埃贡·席勒的素描，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。这是一件纸本素描，笔触和留白比完成度更直接。", "note_en": "1916, Europe. 埃贡·席勒; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1964.285. This is a drawing (素描（水粉、水彩、石墨）).", "note_html": "1916，奥地利 维也纳。埃贡·席勒的素描，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。这是一件纸本素描，笔触和留白比完成度更直接。"}, "wenning-rhodes-memorial-1916": {"note": "温宁画的是开普敦桌山下的罗得斯纪念堂；建筑被山体压住，石阶和树影把视线一级级带上去。", "note_en": "1916, Sub-Saharan Africa. 皮特·温宁; source: Wikimedia Commons, catalog no. Pieter Wenning - Rhodes Memorial - Google Art Project.jpg. This is a painting (oil painting).", "note_html": "温宁画的是开普敦桌山下的罗得斯纪念堂；建筑被山体压住，石阶和树影把视线一级级带上去。"}, "kirchner-mountain-landscape-1918": {"note": "1918/19，瑞士 达沃斯。恩斯特·路德维希·基尔希纳的素描，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。这是一件纸本素描，笔触和留白比完成度更直接。", "note_en": "1918/19, Europe. 恩斯特·路德维希·基尔希纳; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1963.86. This is a drawing (素描（石墨、毛笔、墨）).", "note_html": "1918/19，瑞士 达沃斯。恩斯特·路德维希·基尔希纳的素描，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。这是一件纸本素描，笔触和留白比完成度更直接。"}, "sheeler-church-street-el-1920": {"note": "希勒从电影《曼哈顿》的画面出发，把百老汇、华尔街与教堂街高架铁路简化为明暗和形状的节奏。\n\n在「城市与日常」的「铁路」线索里，用精确主义的几何切面，把高架铁路和摩天楼压成同一套城市节奏。", "note_en": "1920, North America. 查尔斯·希勒; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1977.43. This is a painting (布面油画).", "note_html": "希勒从电影《曼哈顿》的画面出发，把百老汇、华尔街与教堂街高架铁路简化为明暗和形状的节奏。\n\n在「城市与日常」的「铁路」线索里，用精确主义的几何切面，把高架铁路和摩天楼压成同一套城市节奏。"}, "auto-f2dad429": {"note": "《柏林夜间街景》是莱塞·乌里约1920年的印象主义作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“柏林夜间街景”为题，属于柏林的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。", "note_en": "1920, Europe. 莱塞·乌里; source: Wikimedia Commons, catalog no. File:Lesser Ury - Nächtliche Strassenszene, Berlin (1920).jpg. This is a painting (oil painting).", "note_html": "《柏林夜间街景》是莱塞·乌里约1920年的印象主义作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“柏林夜间街景”为题，属于柏林的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。"}, "auto-505fc4ea": {"note": "《老人肖像》是伊万·扎博塔约1920年的现实主义作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“老人肖像”为题，属于斯拉夫的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。", "note_en": "1920, Cross-regional. 伊万·扎博塔; source: Wikimedia Commons, catalog no. File:Ivan Žabota - Portret starca.jpg. This is a painting (oil painting).", "note_html": "《老人肖像》是伊万·扎博塔约1920年的现实主义作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“老人肖像”为题，属于斯拉夫的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。"}, "auto-c6739d13": {"note": "《柯克卡迪港的渔船》是约翰·汉密尔顿·格拉斯约1925年的海洋画作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“柯克卡迪港的渔船”为题，属于苏格兰的水彩传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。", "note_en": "1925, Europe. 约翰·汉密尔顿·格拉斯; source: Wikimedia Commons, catalog no. File:Kirkcaldy fishing boat in harbour.jpg. This is a painting (watercolour).", "note_html": "《柯克卡迪港的渔船》是约翰·汉密尔顿·格拉斯约1925年的海洋画作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“柯克卡迪港的渔船”为题，属于苏格兰的水彩传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。"}, "mondrian-composition-red-yellow-blue-1927": {"note": "黑色线把画面切成不等大的矩形，红黄蓝只占少数面积；蒙德里安用最少的颜色测试平衡。", "note_en": "1927, Europe. 皮特·蒙德里安; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1967.215. This is a painting (oil painting).", "note_html": "黑色线把画面切成不等大的矩形，红黄蓝只占少数面积；蒙德里安用最少的颜色测试平衡。"}, "xu-beihong-tianheng-five-hundred-1930": {"note": "1930年，徐悲鸿把田横与五百士的故事画成油画；人物群像在画面右侧排开，海与天把决绝留在空白里。", "note_en": "1930, China. 徐悲鸿; source: Wikimedia Commons, catalog no. Xu beihong Painting Tianheng's five hundreds heroes.jpg. This is a painting (oil painting).", "note_html": "1930年，徐悲鸿把田横与五百士的故事画成油画；人物群像在画面右侧排开，海与天把决绝留在空白里。"}, "mondrian-composition-red-blue-yellow-1930": {"note": "蒙德里安的《红、蓝、黄构图》只包含黑色线条、白色背景和三个基础色平面。一个大红色矩形占据主导位置；蓝色位于左下角，一个小黄位于右下角；黑色线条不对称移动，这里厚、那里细，追求平衡而不是形成网格。\n\n蒙德里安称这种关系为新造型主义：水平和垂直代表宇宙的两种基本力量，原色代表纯净能量，白色代表空间。没有故事，但画作需要长时间凝视：每次注意力的转移，颜色的重量都会改变。", "note_en": "Mondrian's *Composition with Red, Blue and Yellow* contains only black lines, white ground and three primary planes. A large red rectangle dominates; blue sits at lower left, a small yellow at lower right; the black lines move asymmetrically, thicker here, thinner there, seeking balance rather than executing a grid.\n\nMondrian called this relationship Neo-Plasticism: horizontal and vertical stand for the two basic forces of the universe, primary colours for pure energy, white for space. There is no story, yet the painting asks for prolonged looking: with every shift of attention, the weight of the colours changes.", "note_html": "蒙德里安的《红、蓝、黄构图》只包含黑色线条、白色背景和三个基础色平面。一个大红色矩形占据主导位置；蓝色位于左下角，一个小黄位于右下角；黑色线条不对称移动，这里厚、那里细，追求平衡而不是形成网格。\n\n蒙德里安称这种关系为新造型主义：水平和垂直代表宇宙的两种基本力量，原色代表纯净能量，白色代表空间。没有故事，但画作需要长时间凝视：每次注意力的转移，颜色的重量都会改变。"}, "wood-american-gothic-1930": {"note": "《美国哥特式》展示了一位父亲和女儿站在爱荷华州一栋白色木屋前。男人穿着黑色外套，戴着眼镜，手里拿着一把干草叉；女人稍微站在他身后，围裙上有图案，头发梳得很紧。房子的尖形窗户是木匠哥特式的，看起来像一座小教堂。\n\n格兰特·伍德把中西部的本地人物变成了几乎宗教般的肖像：严肃、封闭，又带着一种防御性的尊严。这幅画成了美国画作里最容易被误解的作品——有人看到坚忍不拔，有人看到压抑，两种解读都成立。", "note_en": "American Gothic shows a father and daughter standing before a white timber house in Iowa. The man wears a black coat and glasses, a pitchfork in his hand; the woman stands slightly behind him, her apron patterned, her hair pulled tight. The pointed window of the house is Carpenter Gothic, like a small church.\n\nGrant Wood turns a Midwestern local type into an almost religious portrait: severe, closed, with a defensive dignity. It became the most misread of American paintings — some see endurance, others repression, and both readings hold.", "note_html": "《美国哥特式》展示了一位父亲和女儿站在爱荷华州一栋白色木屋前。男人穿着黑色外套，戴着眼镜，手里拿着一把干草叉；女人稍微站在他身后，围裙上有图案，头发梳得很紧。房子的尖形窗户是木匠哥特式的，看起来像一座小教堂。\n\n格兰特·伍德把中西部的本地人物变成了几乎宗教般的肖像：严肃、封闭，又带着一种防御性的尊严。这幅画成了美国画作里最容易被误解的作品——有人看到坚忍不拔，有人看到压抑，两种解读都成立。"}, "bone-weymouth-victory-day-1946": {"note": "博恩作为二战官方战争艺术家，记录胜利一周年时威茅斯湾的海滩人群：彩旗、泳装、拥挤与松弛。\n\n在「城市与日常」的「战后」线索里，战争结束后的海滩人群，让“胜利”落回普通人的一天。", "note_en": "1946, Europe. 缪尔黑德·博恩; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 1954.772. This is a drawing (水彩、石墨、钢笔与墨水).", "note_html": "博恩作为二战官方战争艺术家，记录胜利一周年时威茅斯湾的海滩人群：彩旗、泳装、拥挤与松弛。\n\n在「城市与日常」的「战后」线索里，战争结束后的海滩人群，让“胜利”落回普通人的一天。"}, "beckmann-perseus-last-duty-1949": {"note": "贝克曼在二战与核威胁之后重写珀耳修斯神话：英雄穿着女装，周围是神话中并不存在的屠杀，胜利被变成控诉。\n\n在「人物与自我」的「战后」线索里，战后神话不是胜利叙事，而是对屠杀、暴力和英雄形象的拆解。", "note_en": "1949, Europe. 马克斯·贝克曼; source: Cleveland Museum of Art, catalog no. 2013.7. This is a painting (布面油画).", "note_html": "贝克曼在二战与核威胁之后重写珀耳修斯神话：英雄穿着女装，周围是神话中并不存在的屠杀，胜利被变成控诉。\n\n在「人物与自我」的「战后」线索里，战后神话不是胜利叙事，而是对屠杀、暴力和英雄形象的拆解。"}, "heijnsbroek-frame-2003": {"note": "2003 年的纸本水粉。黑、灰、绿、黄被组织成一块倾斜的框，画面既不指向具体风景，也不完全脱离地景。\n\n在「材料与技法」的「开放许可」线索里，把颜色压进一个像窗框的缺口：抽象画仍然在处理“看出去”和“被围住”的空间。", "note_en": "2003, Europe. 丰斯·海恩斯布鲁克; source: Wikimedia Commons / 艺术家自发布. This is a painting (纸本水粉).", "note_html": "2003 年的纸本水粉。黑、灰、绿、黄被组织成一块倾斜的框，画面既不指向具体风景，也不完全脱离地景。\n\n在「材料与技法」的「开放许可」线索里，把颜色压进一个像窗框的缺口：抽象画仍然在处理“看出去”和“被围住”的空间。"}, "heijnsbroek-crosslings-3-2004": {"note": "2004 年的纸本水粉。粗笔触在留白上交叉、覆盖、让位，标题里的“crosslings”指的不是图案，而是笔触之间的关系。\n\n在「材料与技法」的「开放许可」线索里，红、蓝、黑、黄的笔画互相穿越，像数字图层被重新压回纸面。", "note_en": "2004, Europe. 丰斯·海恩斯布鲁克; source: Wikimedia Commons / 艺术家自发布. This is a painting (纸本水粉).", "note_html": "2004 年的纸本水粉。粗笔触在留白上交叉、覆盖、让位，标题里的“crosslings”指的不是图案，而是笔触之间的关系。\n\n在「材料与技法」的「开放许可」线索里，红、蓝、黑、黄的笔画互相穿越，像数字图层被重新压回纸面。"}};
